{"columns":["comment_id","issue_key","issue_project_key","comment_author_email","comment_author_name","comment_body","comment_created_at_ts"],"row_count":10000,"rows":[["3848837","DSR-4199","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-29T11:06:08.892Z"],["3848839","DSR-4051","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Post to verification-support [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C06BQ7T6L4F/p1769684759360239]","2026-01-29T11:06:29.656Z"],["3848840","WD-22664","WD","kristinliis.ratto@bolt.eu","Kristin-Liis Rätto","Thank you!","2026-01-29T11:06:59.339Z"],["3848841","PFI-840202","PFI","sabina@bolt.eu","Sabina Kljenak","[^8_T1_1.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-29T11:07:12.467Z"],["3848842","PFI-840202","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T11:07:14.525Z"],["3848844","LSS-62153","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:63fdee79feb4b150c57651b4] Please could you upload the docs as Google Docs?  When I download these docs currently they aren’t in a format I can properly review or amend. Thanks","2026-01-29T11:07:48.715Z"],["3848848","WFM-10207","WFM","george.uibo@bolt.eu","George Uibo","Hey WFM team, reviewed and confirmed that roles are correct/added. Could you kindly handle the case, thank you.","2026-01-29T11:08:30.732Z"],["3848851","GROWTH-740","GROWTH","juan.felipe@bolt.eu","Juan Felipe González","*Update*\n\nDue to the overlap with Product Development, we have consulted with both the Product and Data Science teams to ensure we avoid duplicated work.\n\n*Action Required:* @Horatiu.kraus, we are waiting for a prioritization and resourcing decision from your side. We need to confirm if there is an opportunity to allocate time to this project (even if limited) or if it should be explicitly deprioritized.\n\n*Proposed Next Steps:* Based on your decision, we see three potential paths:\n\n* *Scenario A:* If Homescreen/Search capacity allows, we align on scope and timing with @Lucas.colucci.\n* *Scenario B:* If that is not feasible, we explore alignment with @Pedro.sousa on the Stores initiative to find a shared path.\n* *Scenario C:* As a fallback, we proceed with @Mikhail.korolev’s suggestion to source resources from the merchant side or another external team.\n\nDiscussion [HERE|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r1g_rs5DgnDvF287t6-GTygTPkuDRDhLILq6kbUMnwE/edit?tab=t.0]\n\nDiscussion in [#tmp-eater-dish-item-recommendation-feature|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0A9ZNE35T2]","2026-01-29T11:09:14.124Z"],["3848852","CSDA-296","CSDA","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Hi [~accountid:5d3d9afd7e09400be06bcb30]and[~accountid:557058:67e15ba9-0972-4bf7-9e81-826e62fc001b]!\n\nCould you please let me know if your request has been fulfilled and whether we can close the ticket?\n\nIf you need any further changes in the future, feel free to create a separate ticket 🙂","2026-01-29T11:09:20.735Z"],["3848853","FC-416","FC","mirjam.arrak@bolt.eu","Mirjam Arrak","Postponed to Q2 actuals.\nFP&A would eventually want to see the actuals and budget under Rides Local Ops CC with BL Car. Currently, both budget and actuals are under Workplace CC. Allocation rule would take Driver walk-in spend categories and change CC to Rides Local Ops. \nNeed to wait until Pigment team can make this allocation possible in Pigment (budget) as well.\n\n!image-20260129-110611.png|width=467,alt=\"image-20260129-110611.png\"!","2026-01-29T11:09:27.222Z"],["3848854","CSDT-976","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Next steps:\n\n* 20 random samples reviewed here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1td8sKRKt1axueEB1a2TF3ZD1h8EaAb5M7zW9wIFLeL4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1td8sKRKt1axueEB1a2TF3ZD1h8EaAb5M7zW9wIFLeL4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] \n* Issues to be fixed\n** If Alfred probes for information and user never replies, this should be a resolved case ✅ \n** Cases where user didn’t reply to webform, should be a resolved cases\n** Cases with NULL TRT are automatically considered as fcr = false. Need to include null TRT for now. There is a bigger problem with TRT metric that needs to be addressed separately from the FCR topic. ✅ ","2026-01-29T11:09:38.249Z"],["3848858","L10N-30951","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30824](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30824)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:10:29.125Z"],["3848859","PAW-15254","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sergey-seleznev\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162293\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-29 11:11:00 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-29T11:11:04.019Z"],["3848860","MM-924","MM","maksym.hayduk@bolt.eu","Maksym Haiduk","Some ideas on the UI.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 12.09.23.png|width=405,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 12.09.23.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 12.09.32.png|width=307,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 12.09.32.png\"!","2026-01-29T11:11:12.192Z"],["3848861","PAW-15253","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @xenJ\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162423\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-29 11:11:17 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-29T11:11:17.814Z"],["3848862","DSR-4201","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-29T11:11:24.595Z"],["3848863","LSS-61887","LSS","aleksejs.batenko@bolt.eu","Aleksejs Batenko","Hello, \n\nUnfortunately, we had to replace one vehicle due to accident last moment. Attached I am adding Annex we have to sign with same people. Please adjust wording if needed and send for signing. Thanks in advance!\n\n[^United Motors Annex 2.docx]\n\n","2026-01-29T11:11:34.126Z"],["3848864","LSS-55517","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] the comments have now been resolved. \n\nPlease share the final agreement once cleaned up. Thanks!","2026-01-29T11:11:44.324Z"],["3848865","LSS-61765","LSS","eleanora.maruma@bolt.eu","Eleanora Maruma","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Can we now proceed with the signature?","2026-01-29T11:11:50.193Z"],["3848866","LSS-58622","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hey [~accountid:6166d4c799b4b8006a26023e] - nice to e-meet you 🙂 \n\nI’ve reviewed the initiative and I am OK for you to test in African & International Markets (/)  I say this as we are not collecting any data and are in-fact supporting Driver transparency of their CCTV installations. We are also not making any significant decisions based on profiling we may be doing. \n\nCheers,","2026-01-29T11:12:27.366Z"],["3848869","CNT-526","CNT","piers.mcewan@bolt.eu","Piers McEwan","hi [~accountid:712020:778f9851-345e-4997-bb18-8183eae5cf90] added the edits directly to the Q1-26 Poe Version in each document. \n\nYou’ll have probably seen but i updated wording to make it more generic than for just restaurants, and trimmed the copy in some places. \n\nMessage if you have any questions. ","2026-01-29T11:12:41.566Z"],["3848870","LSS-62385","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}\nReviewed and provided a green-light in the Parent ticket (/) \n{panel}","2026-01-29T11:12:57.059Z"],["3848871","GROWTH-428","GROWTH","juan.felipe@bolt.eu","Juan Felipe González","*Update*\n\n[~accountid:712020:e5acc025-eb4f-4200-b35a-d085235e4bf2] already deployed the mart, and we validated they are working properly, we run 2 experiments, once for out of the app (Braze) and in-apps. \n\n*Next steps*\n\nOnce he is back from holidays, he will push the commit to the experimentation platform, creating the Metrics files. ","2026-01-29T11:13:09.304Z"],["3848876","PFI-840204","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThanks for the ticket! While we get to your request, please make sure to check Configuration Requests Guide (https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/sQUQDAE) to see if you have added everything we need to the ticket, in order to make the process faster and more convenient! \n\nPlease note that, in this queue, we are handling requests related to fee calculators, base fee calculators, invoice issuers, commission changes, invoice layout changes.. etc.\n\nThank you! ","2026-01-29T11:13:55.673Z"],["3848877","PFI-840204","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋 \nThank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! Looks like this ticket needs approval - [~accountId:5b35d0887072062f71e6578f] please approve this ticket in order to continue.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-29T11:13:57.530Z"],["3848879","WFM-10180","WFM","vania.goncalves@bolt-outsource.eu","Vânia Gonçalves","Hello [~accountid:712020:74b4c3fb-6caf-4d5d-b7f8-c2ea38318e58] there is not a special agreement. we usually request classic backlog to senior agents, especially for Social Media agents since they’re able to help with the backlog faster with classic backlog.","2026-01-29T11:14:41.244Z"],["3848883","PFI-840174","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, reissued the invoice","2026-01-29T11:16:21.993Z"],["3848888","PAW-15180","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-alerting, pint-product-observability-and-incident-response-platform, pint-capability-observability\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-29T11:17:17.238Z"],["3848890","PAW-15328","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-admin-panel, pint-product-admin-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-29T11:17:24.143Z"],["3848893","LSS-62106","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","[~accountid:712020:282008bf-7f03-4058-8bec-43f7e5a44ace] thank you for the update!\nI have reviewed and [updated PoA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-QipeNsB1bdbrB2XpkFCc4ehk_QYg2Q-/edit], please have a look and confirm that the content and the translation is accurate, thanks 🙏 ","2026-01-29T11:17:36.547Z"],["3848894","RS-1941","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Hey [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab] , \n\nI noticed that in the one pager the disclaimer needs to be added \n\n**Where direct renewable electricity procurement isn’t possible on the local market, Bolt purchases Energy Attribute Certificates (EACs) for equivalent consumption.*\n\nafter saying ‘_Bolt uses_ _100% renewable electricity from 2025 across Bolt-controlled offices, warehouses, charging docks, and Bolt Market premises.’_\n\nAs a result of the UOKiK investigation, this disclaimer has to always be paired with the renewable energy claim. \n\nPlease make sure this is replicated across the materials. ","2026-01-29T11:17:37.608Z"],["3848895","WFM-10178","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:61442edbe057c6006a4f0f1d]!\r\n\r\nQueue removed.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-29T11:17:44.892Z"],["3848896","LSS-62386","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","[^CZ20260129-001 VO-Link - Bolt Drive CZ.docx.pdf] _(361 kB)_","2026-01-29T11:17:50.876Z"],["3848901","PFI-838135","PFI","karolis.kasarauskas@bolt-outsource.eu","Karolis Kasarauskas","Asked for them to provide us with the link. ","2026-01-29T11:19:16.125Z"],["3848902","LSS-62171","LSS","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","Hi [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] [~accountid:712020:652fd966-97db-4de3-b20d-d6644848128c] , the document is called a Local File. It is a summary of the activities of the local entity and the transfer pricing policies applied accordingly. We need to sign the document due to specific rules in Cyprus. \n\nThe document consists of a main body and various appendices. The appendices include the intra-group agreements which are signed and dated. \n\nI would propose that if it works on your side we sign all the pages in the main body which are pages 1-21 and leave the appendices unsigned.","2026-01-29T11:20:30.095Z"],["3848903","CNT-526","CNT","anniecel.malabanan@bolt.eu","Anniecel Malabanan","Hi [~accountid:5f7722df25fbdf006846d56d], yes I got the notification. I’ll have a look through and will reach out to you if needed.  Thanks a lot!","2026-01-29T11:20:55.788Z"],["3848904","PFI-840212","PFI","mehdi.hameer@bolt.eu","Mehdi Hameer","!WhatsApp Image 2026-01-29 at 2.13.08 PM.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T11:21:16.070Z"],["3848906","PFI-840174","PFI","alina.stepovikova@bolt-outsource.eu","Alina Stepovikova","Hey! Thank you! Does he receive it to his email right away?","2026-01-29T11:21:25.533Z"],["3848907","PAR-3866","PAR","ahmed.farghaly@bolt.eu","Ahmed Farghaly","[~accountid:712020:fc7ada41-3f9c-4d74-95f1-90300ecbe201]  let’s log it as an error ","2026-01-29T11:21:51.148Z"],["3848908","BP-12754","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] I’d like to work on this in the next sprint. Thanks for the ping!","2026-01-29T11:21:53.539Z"],["3848910","LSS-62387","LSS","razvan.scheopea@bolt.eu","Răzvan-Alexandru Scheopea","[^Oradea propunere marketing_draft.docx] _(13.87 MB)_","2026-01-29T11:22:11.252Z"],["3848911","RF-212","RF","afua.tutuwaa@bolt.eu","Afua Tutuwaa-Ampofo","Exclude Germany, Thailand, Nigeria, and Ghana from consolidation. \n","2026-01-29T11:22:19.218Z"],["3848915","WFM-10167","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:637b2101de5cdaba3a6714bd]!\r\n\r\nQueues assigned.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-29T11:23:09.982Z"],["3848916","L10N-30955","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:13.836Z"],["3848917","L10N-30956","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:14.815Z"],["3848918","L10N-30963","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:19.181Z"],["3848919","L10N-30964","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:19.222Z"],["3848920","L10N-30966","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:19.450Z"],["3848921","L10N-30967","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:20.968Z"],["3848922","L10N-30970","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:22.543Z"],["3848923","L10N-30972","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussion