ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:25.339Z"],["3848926","L10N-30980","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:26.761Z"],["3848927","L10N-30982","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:27.820Z"],["3848928","L10N-30984","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-30953](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-30953)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T11:23:28.283Z"],["3848929","WEB-10005","WEB","burak.ozdemir@bolt.eu","Burak Özdemir","[~accountid:712020:2bb94136-b4e4-463e-a0f6-8be773ff520f] I am resolving this task, since it was content sync related and we know the issue, and it’ll be addressed separately.","2026-01-29T11:23:29.323Z"],["3848930","SREDESK-7475","SREDESK","kateryna.kolomiiets@bolt.eu","Kateryna Kolomiiets","Hi!\nI am still waiting for access to jfrog.\n\nSorry.\nWe can close the ticket for now - I will open a new one when I will have access to jfrog\n\n","2026-01-29T11:23:47.179Z"],["3848932","WEB-10005","WEB","samuel.oyekeye@bolt.eu","Samuel Oluseyi Oyekeye","[~accountid:620102dfeaf9e200707370ef] Assigned to you then","2026-01-29T11:24:10.469Z"],["3848933","LSS-60422","LSS","eimantas.balciunas@bolt.eu","Eimantas Balčiūnas","lets close this ticket. ","2026-01-29T11:24:12.034Z"],["3848935","TAXP-1150","TAXP","wenjing.zhang@bolt.eu","Grace Wenjing Zhang","[~accountid:5f23e5f5170ffc0023d69786] [~accountid:5eda5d0647291b0b8608735a] [~accountid:608e5558f0db1300698c69d4] [~accountid:607d9ec5a41c7a007832afa1] [~accountid:712020:3c92a0f8-cf5a-446c-a2f4-4f4460994d1b] based on the discussion we had yesterday, moving forward to collect “View“ requests from the team, here is the [work file|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ZOBypixPtON50ww_KsHegNXsWARQfWkDFfSFQ_LZXHY/edit?gid=1049450906#gid=1049450906] for the requests, please ask the teams to fill in the file if they need some customised views.\nFor *tax leads*, please fill in your requests in “Other“ category.","2026-01-29T11:24:31.673Z"],["3848936","PFI-839781","PFI","martyna.puksmyte@bolt.eu","Martyna Pukšmytė","please review the case APAP ","2026-01-29T11:24:47.329Z"],["3848938","PFI-840174","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","I believe we don’t send email with each reissue, better to send the PDF and download from Admin. Though I believe invoice should be available in app","2026-01-29T11:25:15.779Z"],["3848941","DO-5835","DO","maximilian.linek@bolt.eu","Maximilian Linek","Thanx. I raised a ticket there.","2026-01-29T11:25:44.115Z"],["3848942","WD-22725","WD","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","Hello, all done!","2026-01-29T11:26:00.939Z"],["3848943","RDS-1166","RDS","nami.salimi@bolt.eu","Nami Salimi","Not in our team scope and hence we won’t work on this \n\ncc [~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] ","2026-01-29T11:26:15.760Z"],["3848944","LSS-61105","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] as I have never delt with the claims in the UK and not familiar with the process, could you help me with this one?","2026-01-29T11:26:24.828Z"],["3848945","WD-22707","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Closed request as per the requester’s instructions","2026-01-29T11:27:22.505Z"],["3848946","EBIKE1-227","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:624b3bdf8678e900705d9004] Alright, I missed the descriptions in the original post, sorry.\n\nIt would make sense to make these tests. Where did You exactly find these from?","2026-01-29T11:27:22.651Z"],["3848947","PFI-839781","PFI","martyna.puksmyte@bolt.eu","Martyna Pukšmytė","Hi, [~accountid:5f23da64170ffc0023d64119] maybe you could help to get this case reviewed ASAP, since the user is waiting for weeks and misleading communication has been provided by us to him, also he is sharing this on social meadia\n\n","2026-01-29T11:27:33.698Z"],["3848948","BDB-1531","BDB","filipa.ferrao@bolt.eu","Filipa Salgueiro Ferrão","Hey [~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] one last final adjustment and apologies for only spotting it now. On the wall decor - wall 2 - Big wall2-1 and Big wall2-3 the headlines should have a . at the end. If the middle one didn’t have it we would let it be but since the middle one does it look more coherent that way. So it should be:\n\n*Bolt_Lisbon-airport_Big-wall2-1_decor_7000x2500(1-10)*:  Your ride's on the way.\n*Bolt_Lisbon-airport_Big-wall2-3_decor_7000x2500(1-10)*: Next stop: anywhere in Lisbon.\n\nApologies once again I saw that it was the way I’d put it on the media plan. \n\nEverything else is perfect 🙏🏼","2026-01-29T11:27:34.108Z"],["3848950","LSS-59864","LSS","manuel.sanz@bolt.eu","Manuel Gil Sanz","Thanks [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f] . Will do as requested and send you back the contract once is signed by the partner.","2026-01-29T11:28:15.606Z"],["3848952","LSS-62298","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","h3. *Recap of Slack discussion*:\n\n* Requested the team submit a *Privacy Jira ticket* and select *People* as the Vertical/Function, and share the link once created.\n* Confirmed initial scoping points needed for assessment:\n** Scope limited to France-based employees/entities only (no other jurisdictions/entities).\n** Where employee data is involved, outputs should be *aggregated and/or anonymised* (no identifiable individual-level data).\n* *Provided the privacy position*: inspectors’ objectives can generally be met via de-identified/aggregated information (e.g., job mapping, promotions, role changes), and most requested documents should not contain employee personal data.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}\n[~accountid:712020:ad0f28bc-2e04-43b5-8352-a3a48fd3f720] - provided that ALL employee data we provide to the Inspectors is aggregated information/trends/statistics, we are OK (/) \n{panel}\n\nIf you are unsure whether employee data is properly ‘aggregated’ or ‘anonymised’, please reach out to us in [#confidential-privileged-fr-labour-inspection|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0AB1BRDS68]","2026-01-29T11:28:28.426Z"],["3848954","LSS-61416","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","[~accountid:712020:1a3a17cb-2e37-4162-8d95-4d1059255d7e] thank you for your feedback. \n\n\n\ne-mail sent to the Faro Police Department and we received the proper “ofício” today - attached","2026-01-29T11:28:56.807Z"],["3848956","WD-22697","WD","jakub.pniewski@bolt.eu","Jakub Pniewski","I accept the terms \n\n[~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] ","2026-01-29T11:29:22.297Z"],["3848959","WFM-10204","WFM","george.uibo@bolt.eu","George Uibo","Hello! The role has been requested, and changes may take up to 15 minutes to be reflected. Could you clarify which queues this agent needs?","2026-01-29T11:29:50.586Z"],["3848960","CLIENTAPP-38680","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Only UI tests were added","2026-01-29T11:30:38.200Z"],["3848961","BDB-1531","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","[~accountid:712020:ccc99f37-aac9-4dc9-8233-98fd243b145b] \nUsually if we have just one sentence, we don’t use a dot. But I got your point.\n I would ask a copywriter’s help in this case. \n[~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c] We need your advice here. ","2026-01-29T11:30:39.766Z"],["3848962","LSS-61606","LSS","beatrice.krasenko@bolt.eu","Beatričė Krašenko","\n\n[^Bolt_Food_sutartis_Sushi_Lounge.pdf]\n[^BoltFoodContract-Sushi Lounge (Bivylių al.).pdf]\n[^Signed - Sushi lounge (Dominikonų str.) deal 30.11.2023 16_51_18.pdf]\n\nall found signed contracts with the client ","2026-01-29T11:30:46.712Z"],["3848963","GROWTH-447","GROWTH","avishek.raha@bolt.eu","Avishek Raha","Continued in Growth-680.","2026-01-29T11:31:04.570Z"],["3848964","WFM-10209","WFM","cheryl.annum@bolt.eu","Cheryl Odofoley Annum","!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 11.29.07 AM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T11:31:08.781Z"],["3848965","LSS-62387","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-29T11:31:32.585Z"],["3848967","WFM-10204","WFM","george.uibo@bolt.eu","George Uibo","Role requested [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571937]. WFM team, kindly assign the queues once they respond.","2026-01-29T11:32:13.491Z"],["3848968","TAXP-3404","TAXP","maret.ansperimalberg@bolt.eu","Maret Ansperi-Mälberg","# The conversion was registered in the Commercial Register in January and the contribution is therefore declared in the January TSD return due by February 20, 2026.","2026-01-29T11:32:21.531Z"],["3848970","LSS-61416","LSS","sofia.carto@bolt.eu","Sofia Cartó","here ir is: [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OqGi8qU3mHCaM_aQXL6n3cVedUDPl621/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1OqGi8qU3mHCaM_aQXL6n3cVedUDPl621/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T11:32:51.941Z"],["3848972","FDBT-4841","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-29T11:33:39.903Z"],["3848973","LSS-58363","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","!image-20260129-113232.png|width=855,alt=\"image-20260129-113232.png\"!\n\n[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] seems that all is clear from privacy POV, this is also not a DSR. I would let [~accountid:712020:0285a595-6608-4335-9a5a-60b50674c696] handle this from a legal POV and then we can close the ticket:)","2026-01-29T11:33:41.732Z"],["3848976","LSS-62308","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:62ff8d58b582d07a14a96588] \n\nYes, Bolt can subsidise VAT registration costs for selected drivers, and there is no prohibition under UK VAT law on providing financial support for independent contractors’ administrative or professional costs. \n\nThe main risks are worker-status optics if the subsidy appears mandatory or suggests Bolt is directing drivers’ tax decisions, and tax/admin risk if the subsidy is paid as cash or embedded in trip payments. \n\nThese risks are manageable if the subsidy is clearly optional, framed as a one-off contribution to VAT registration administration (not tax advice and not a condition to access work), and structured so that Bolt pays Beamin/Eazitax directly while the driver contracts independently with the provider and remains free to use any VAT advisor. \n\nApplying objective eligibility criteria (e.g. high-volume drivers) and documenting the commercial rationale further reduces risk.\n\nAdding [~accountid:5eda5d0647291b0b8608735a] to share his view from the tax perspective","2026-01-29T11:33:52.617Z"],["3848980","LSS-59991","LSS","juan.fernandez@bolt.eu","Juan Luis Fernández","Hi Alexandros, Bea Leiva flagged this issue to me. I think it is important\nto discuss it with Clerides today, since they have a good relationship with\nAntitrust Authorities.\n\nJuan Luis Fernández\nSenior Public Policy Manager | Spain & Cyprus\n(+34) 634495459\njuan.fernandez@bolt.eu\nblog.bolt.eu <https://bolt.eu/>","2026-01-29T11:34:38.290Z"],["3848982","BDB-1531","BDB","liisi.tamra@bolt.eu","Liisi Tamra","[~accountid:712020:aa01e2da-d94d-4529-a5fb-d7a1a21e0b79] yep, add a dot if these are all on the same wall to look coherent.","2026-01-29T11:35:43.750Z"],["3848983","PFI-831194","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T11:36:08.602Z"],["3848985","PFI-840066","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T11:36:59.057Z"],["3848986","LSS-62207","LSS","tomasz.blachowicz@bolt.eu","Tomasz Blachowicz","Hi All,\n\nCould we have an update on this? I see Alessandro is out-sick, so not sure who is responsible for it; for our project this is priority as it will block us with the cars registration we would like to have on Wednesday-Thursday upcoming week\n\nBest,\n\nTom","2026-01-29T11:37:09.561Z"],["3848987","LSS-62372","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:60ab8fc8efa79d00691a340f] , suggested wording:\n\nImportant information about expired licences (Nottingham)\n\nWhere Bolt holds a physical copy of an expired licence, Nottingham City Council requirements mean it may be held for up to 30 days from the expiry date.\n\nAfter this 30-day period, the licence may be disposed of in line with local authority requirements.\n\nDrivers using the Bolt platform who wish to collect an expired licence can choose to attend the Nottingham hub within this timeframe to do so.","2026-01-29T11:37:20.429Z"],["3848988","PFI-819602","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T11:37:40.347Z"],["3848989","LSS-59991","LSS","alexandros.lamprou@bolt.eu","Alexandros Lamprou","yes, also Clerides will probably need to participate on the hearing on the 11th.  ","2026-01-29T11:37:40.691Z"],["3848990","PFI-819603","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T11:38:41.674Z"],["3848991","LSS-58363","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Thanks for the update [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] , looks like we’ve gone full circle on this case 😌 I’ll keep the ticket open for now.","2026-01-29T11:38:44.771Z"],["3848993","PFI-840041","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T11:39:18.426Z"],["3848996","PFI-840191","PFI","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","Payouts in progress","2026-01-29T11:39:28.824Z"],["3848998","CSXRT-206","CSXRT","darina.toikka@bolt.eu","Darina Toikka","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1763718527454859?thread_ts=1763128949.076899&cid=C064CEL9FKP|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1763718527454859?thread_ts=1763128949.076899&cid=C064CEL9FKP|smart-card]","2026-01-29T11:39:40.303Z"],["3848999","PFI-838237","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-29T11:39:45.960Z"],["3849001","SCM-1209","SCM","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:5e4a421e691b8a0c95c2cdec] is printing a jig to which an IOT can be fixed with a clamp, so it can be powered on & manipulated from where it most regularly fails.","2026-01-29T11:40:20.533Z"],["3849003","PFI-823059","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T11:40:28.135Z"],["3849006","DSR-4203","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-29T11:41:06.620Z"],["3849008","LSS-62308","LSS","lucca.carney@bolt.eu","Lucca Carney","Thanks for confirming [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] 🙏 \n\nWe’ll make sure to enact it along your notes","2026-01-29T11:41:27.238Z"],["3849009","DBRE-8770","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","(affects all prelive jobs, raising the task priority)\n\nCause: [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/blob/fe18e64c09ec8774642121effa079d0054975c63/roles/db_rundeck/files/write-metrics.py#L108|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/blob/fe18e64c09ec8774642121effa079d0054975c63/roles/db_rundeck/files/write-metrics.py#L108].\n\nFor every sending attempt, there are 30 retries, one in 6 seconds, another in 9, then in 14, 21, 30 and so on, so waiting time is >3.5h for _every_ failed metric reporting attempt – and there are many.\n\n# Failing to send the metrics MUST NOT fail the job; metrics are secondary to what the job is about\n# Retrying SHOULD NOT take more than 30 seconds per report, ideally less; proposed: 3 retries – 3, 6, 9.\n# There should be a safety mechanism that terminates the job if it’s running for too long; 3 x average is sensible choice. For example, the job that is expected to run for 1h – should be terminated forcefully in 3h.\n\nUPD.\n\nSREDO guys confirmed that push gateway is using HTTP -> HTTPS redirect since a week ago, and our code has a bug that cannot handle it.\n\nIn {{pushadd_to_gateway}} first parameter is an URL, which should contain the protocol if that is not HTTP: [https://github.com/prometheus/client_python/blob/a8541354519d04852d24688845f1d2d495eef59c/prometheus_client/exposition.py#L665|https://github.com/prometheus/client_python/blob/a8541354519d04852d24688845f1d2d495eef59c/prometheus_client/exposition.py#L665].\n\nWe are using {{pushgateway_host}} as a parameter, and host is _not_ URL.\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/blob/fe18e64c09ec8774642121effa079d0054975c63/roles/db_mysql_prelive/callback_plugins/db_mysql_prelive.py#L46|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/blob/fe18e64c09ec8774642121effa079d0054975c63/roles/db_mysql_prelive/callback_plugins/db_mysql_prelive.py#L46]\n\nThis should be\n\n{noformat}-pushgateway_host = f\"pushgateway.{telemetry_env}.telemetry.boltint.net\"\n+pushgateway_url = f\"https://pushgateway.{telemetry_env}.telemetry.boltint.net\"{noformat}\n\nDon’t just change the value – *rename the variable as well!* Incorrect variable name caused its incorrect usage, and it in turn broke the jobs.","2026-01-29T11:41:28.326Z"],["3849012","LSS-62388","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","[^Outbound Secondment Agreement (Osborne Clarke and Bolt Services UK Limited) August 2025(596878.1) (1).docx (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-29T11:42:07.217Z"],["3849013","DBRE-8633","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","!image-20260129-114205.png|width=958,alt=\"image-20260129-114205.png\"!","2026-01-29T11:42:08.367Z"],["3849016","BP-12586","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:e2c955ca-33bb-4f61-9a12-3b0fb520b3fd] [~accountid:712020:8973d5d2-02e2-4150-b678-3f91914bf467] I checked also, good to go","2026-01-29T11:42:17.179Z"],["3849019","DBRE-8633","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","!image-20260129-114221.png|width=912,alt=\"image-20260129-114221.png\"!","2026-01-29T11:42:23.958Z"],["3849020","PFI-819069","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment located and matched https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/74371138","2026-01-29T11:42:36.691Z"],["3849023","WFM-10202","WFM","klymentii.tkanka@bolt-outsource.eu","Klymentii Tkanka","[~accountid:712020:9c0690de-08a9-41cf-93b1-9184ed368330] The thing is that I am a Team lead and I am asking to enable the backlog list for the agent, because this agent will mentor newbies. Previously, there were no problems with this and the backlog list was always enabled.\n\n","2026-01-29T11:42:58.152Z"],["3849025","DBRE-8633","DBRE","sangsun.bae@bolt.eu","Sangsun Bae","Done","2026-01-29T11:43:12.022Z"],["3849026","PFI-839651","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hello [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0],\n\nAll clear now, thanks! If you user cannot cover the debt - then CS should have the capability to refund the amount to balance to make it 0. And you can apply this for this case. Once done you will be able to archive the account. \n\nBest Regards,\n\nNigar Alizada ","2026-01-29T11:43:17.301Z"],["3849027","WD-22650","WD","kati.pruel@bolt.eu","Kati Pruel","Hi, \n\nPlease create and map this local accounts. \n\n[^FR COA vs LCOA.xlsx]\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-29T11:43:31.525Z"],["3849028","FX-3686","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769687014404139]*{color}:\nHey <@U02JPNNTE4S> soryr for the long response here is activity and earnings data for the driver similar to what is available via Flee Portal. Driver is now in hidden state and is not visible there. The data is for all driver profiles, currently the active one is this [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/4825911] (for the reference 3619005 is partner ID)\n\nLinked files:\n* [Driver_3619005_2022-01-01_2025_01_01_Activity.csv|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ACK1F17U0/driver_3619005_2022-01-01_2025_01_01_activity.csv]\n\n* [Driver_3619005_2022-01-01_2025_01_01_Earnings.csv|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ABQMVBD50/driver_3619005_2022-01-01_2025_01_01_earnings.csv]\n{quote}","2026-01-29T11:43:48.922Z"],["3849030","FX-3686","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769687041641839]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3686 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T11:44:15.681Z"],["3849033","WD-22657","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","NL001 is moved to company hierarchy Region 6,  the permissions to perform tasks like year close and roll-forward is updatedin the way that compnies in Region 6 can not be selected for roll-forward.","2026-01-29T11:45:14.185Z"],["3849035","LSS-62388","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","*LegalOps:* Please can you kindly assist with arranging the signing of the attached 2 documents by Alex Wong. Thank you in advance.\n\n[^Inbound Secondment Agreement (Bolt Services UK Limited and Osborne Clarke) August 2025(596879.1) (1).docx (48c90faf-8e6c-4d19-9616-e6769eef7a48).pdf] [^Outbound Secondment Agreement (Osborne Clarke and Bolt Services UK Limited) August 2025(596878.1) (1).docx (1) (267db5ff-7ca9-4bca-9ee5-d8bc4ac9d829).pdf] ","2026-01-29T11:45:35.224Z"],["3849036","RNTL-30603","RNTL","raunosten.reile@bolt.eu","Rauno-Sten Reile","It still has an error on producing data to Kafka. I reached out to [~accountid:5d8df271090bd70dc49aed3c] to clarify if something has happened on producing data to Kafka during the last 2 weeks period.","2026-01-29T11:45:38.063Z"],["3849037","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Dzmitry Andryienka [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769687157142279]*{color}:\n<@U02QJBWH8G4> please take a look :melting_face:\n{quote}","2026-01-29T11:46:09.361Z"],["3849040","C2-463","C2","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Ilvestments can not do this research at the moment as there are no batteries there :red_cross: \n\nAfter talking to [~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] yesterday I think our best bet is doing the research in Warsaw, as they have around 200 batteries waiting for repairs + we can pull some “good condition” batteries from Warsaw warehouse, which is close-by. That is still a relatively small number of batteries, but it might just be enough to get some understanding.\n\n\n\n[~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] can you please write down exactly how many batteries and from which cities are currently {color:#ff5630}*on hold*{color} in Warsaw? \n\nAnd more importantly - *do we trust them to do this investigation without any FAEs supervising*? I personally trust Eledrive more than Ilvestments, but actually I do not trust either one of them 100%, because they want this work so they might bend the results slightly.. But this is just my opinion.","2026-01-29T11:46:45.879Z"],["3849043","PFI-840229","PFI","ana.pelivanu@bolt-outsource.eu","Ana Pelivanu","[^Confirmare_Tranzactie_26462_19-01-26.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-29T11:47:09.852Z"],["3849047","DELIVERY-1310","DELIVERY","ivan.koscheev@bolt.eu","Ivan Koshcheev","26W5: Ready for roll out. We plan to release it as part of 1.57 Courier App","2026-01-29T11:48:23.902Z"],["3849048","WD-22628","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hey, As discussed: the issues in not in report mapping, but in using Expense account for recording equity/loan elimination differences. Such differences should be recorded on “Equity” type of ledger account, so WD does not take such differences for calculation of Profit/Loss.\n\n[~accountid:712020:b73d65c1-8791-4157-9850-c426365a190b] , waiting for reporting team decision regarding creation of new “equity' type account and using it for recording elimination differences. ","2026-01-29T11:49:35.616Z"],["3849051","DSR-4205","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-29T11:51:20.716Z"],["3849053","DELIVERY-1839","DELIVERY","ivan.koscheev@bolt.eu","Ivan Koshcheev","26W5: we built a prototype and shared with central ops. Waiting for feedback.","2026-01-29T11:51:35.273Z"],["3849058","WFM-10203","WFM","george.uibo@bolt.eu","George Uibo","Hello WFM team! Agents have the necessary market access. Kindly add them to the requested queues.","2026-01-29T11:53:11.934Z"],["3849060","LSS-62388","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Re outbound secondment agreement regarding Sasha Dornan - I amended Clause 15 to reflect that Bolt’s total liability under the indemnity in respect of third party claims relating to Sasha’s acts or omissions is limited to £50,000, as agreed between [~accountid:712020:209f6e12-e421-4fbf-9a9f-60d100117bab] and OC (see email chain here: [^Bolt Mail - Fwd_ Secondment Agreements.pdf] )","2026-01-29T11:53:15.945Z"],["3849066","LSS-61800","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:6073f7ad9361560068adbda1], thank you for creating this ticket.\n\nThe legal risk of enabling this functionality should be low, as the option to add multiple stops constitutes a *minor extension of an existing trip*, not a separate service or a new standalone feature. The core agreement (transporting the passenger from origin to destination) remains unchanged; the passenger is merely allowed to modify the route at their request.\n\n*The key legal requirement is* *price transparency, as already stated in the tracker*. The passenger must be clearly informed in advance that adding a stop will increase the total fare, and *must see the exact additional price or a clear price calculation before confirming the stop*.\n\nIf the UI clearly displays the price increase (e.g. “Add stop +X NOK”) and requires an explicit passenger action to confirm the change, I’d say no separate or additional consent mechanism is required. In that setup, the functionality complies with consumer protection rules on fair and non-misleading commercial practices.\n\nAll in all, the feature can be enabled in Norway provided that, before each additional stop is confirmed, the passenger is clearly shown the price impact and must actively opt in to the change.\n\nIf you have any additional questions, please let me know, thanks 😉 ","2026-01-29T11:54:35.711Z"],["3849070","PFI-825080","PFI","jergus.janosik@bolt-outsource.eu","Jerguš Jánošík","Any update ?","2026-01-29T11:55:11.239Z"],["3849071","WFM-10183","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:a1ad050c-07e1-448a-8770-6d734d26c8ec]!\r\n\r\nQueues assigned.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-29T11:55:35.373Z"],["3849073","LSS-61228","LSS","alexandre.vanderweerden@bolt.eu","Alexandre Victor Vanderweerden","Hello!\nCan you confirm whether the transfer was sent to the rider's account?\nThank you !","2026-01-29T11:55:42.724Z"],["3849078","RCE-400","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769687778771529]*{color}:\nhere are the lists:\n1. Brussels driver missing license region from drivers license\n\nLinked files:\n* [brussels_driver_missing_license_region.csv|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ABMBTR9FX/brussels_driver_missing_license_region.csv]\n{quote}","2026-01-29T11:56:33.039Z"],["3849080","RS-1938","RS","kadi.tamjarv@bolt.eu","Kadi Jette Tamjärv","Capturing our Slack conversation to highlight the agreements and tasks: \n\n{quote}*Until the outcome of the UOKiK case, we won't put out new materials on Sustainability or promote it but, equally, we cannot remove our Sustainability webpage, and all comms on the blog and LinkedIn so those remain publicly accessible.*\n\n*Therefore, when talking to new B4B customers, Sustainability topic needs to be reactive not proactive for the time being.*  Meaning, [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab] we shouldn’t actively promote it, but if a prospect asks, we can discuss it and share the existing assets. {quote}\n\n*Task*: adding a short note about this on relevant Confluence pages [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/A4OYqwE|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/x/A4OYqwE|smart-link] and [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GP/pages/4331044979/5.8.+Sustainability+assessment+self-service|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GP/pages/4331044979/5.8.+Sustainability+assessment+self-service|smart-link] . \n\n[~accountid:712020:81ed6d45-d7b2-45d4-89cd-030f00488538]{color:#ff5630} could you please take on this {color}{color:#ff5630}*task*{color}{color:#ff5630}? {color}\n\nThe pending extra questions from [~accountid:712020:996ce528-b0dc-49e2-89b8-a8b37096b3ab]:\n\n* Are there any country-specific directions we should be aware of e.g. for Poland? [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] *reply: until proceedings conclude, applying the same level of caution globally as described above.* \n* Do you know if we have a deadline for the UOKiK case? I'm asking because now, with our demand gen strategy focusing on T2+ clients sustainability is a big selling point [~accountid:712020:81ed6d45-d7b2-45d4-89cd-030f00488538]{color:#ff5630} could you please find out if we have a deadline?{color}\n\nThanks,\n\nKadi","2026-01-29T11:56:39.843Z"],["3849082","RCE-400","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769687827662609]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-400 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T11:57:20.728Z"],["3849085","RCE-400","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769687823181219]*{color}:\n2. Drivers from Brussels having license region as \"Flanders\", and missing driver pass (or docuement number)\n\nLinked files:\n* [brussels_drivers_having_flemish_license_missing_driver_pass.csv|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ACK3QSGSC/brussels_drivers_having_flemish_license_missing_driver_pass.csv]\n{quote}","2026-01-29T11:57:24.073Z"],["3849088","WD-22585","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","*Note:* When creating direct intercompany supplier invoices, Workday (WD) always uses the default *ship-to address* (which is Tallinn for EE003). This occurs even if a different ship-to address was selected on the original customer invoice.\n\n!SUPPLIER INVOICE.png|width=1173,alt=\"SUPPLIER INVOICE.png\"!\n\n!CUSTOMER INVOICE .png|width=1188,alt=\"CUSTOMER INVOICE .png\"!\n\nThis is a known *Workday system limitation* (see the support explanation below). Consequently, we cannot automatically populate the tax applicability or tax codes for *EE003’s Polish VAT registration*, because the system will always default to the Estonian address for these supplier invoices.\n\n\n\n!image-20260129-115743.png|width=1173,alt=\"image-20260129-115743.png\"!","2026-01-29T11:57:49.529Z"],["3849090","RCE-400","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769687861974139]*{color}:\n3. Drivers from other Flemish cities missing driver pass (or document number in driver pass)\n\nLinked files:\n* [flemish_drivers_without_driver_pass_number.csv|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ACK3ZCGL8/flemish_drivers_without_driver_pass_number.csv]\n{quote}","2026-01-29T11:57:54.860Z"],["3849092","SAI-1262","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","[+rental-micromobility+|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/CNMF5E2D6/p1769077387901619] updated default behavior on their side and made consistent for both subscription types (single, renewable). Now we always refund to original payment method.\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNMF5E2D6/p1769077387901619|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNMF5E2D6/p1769077387901619|smart-card]","2026-01-29T11:58:37.352Z"],["3849093","LSS-59015","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","Hello [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]. We agree with your views. And also considering that the lawyer does not specify which correspondence they want, we believe we should provide only the communications relevant to the suspension, which seem to be the ones dated from August 3 onwards. Would it be possible to extract this ones?\n\nAlso, we prepared the response to the lawyer, according to the guidelines below. English version [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zdJbMHDCPSnIc_AmfZRDgqhOoyviqNtaD1u0LEkyDro/edit?tab=t.bt9003rojr51], for everyone’s visibility.","2026-01-29T11:58:37.899Z"],["3849096","LSS-61932","LSS","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","{quote}Hi [~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a] thank you for the clarification. Does it mean that if a business user selects the “Bolt” category, the ride is still paid by the business client and not by the user from their personal account?{quote}\n\n[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] Yes, unless the business user selects his personal card.","2026-01-29T11:59:02.595Z"],["3849097","LSS-59015","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","[final PT response|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FSi7zhH55lB2Et50Vx1PsTbTLo0tsxGnH3lPapm6HKc/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-29T11:59:13.414Z"],["3849098","ADS-283","ADS","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-29T11:59:18.963Z"],["3849100","LSS-62372","LSS","karolina.wolanska@bolt.eu","Karolina Wolańska","Perfect, thank you","2026-01-29T11:59:23.135Z"],["3849101","LSS-60205","LSS","alexia.matsangou@bolt.eu","Alexia Matsangou","Hello [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] \n\nApologies for the delay in responding. Here are the findings from our review:\n\n* The reporting rider *does not appear to have another account*, nor is there evidence that they had one previously.\n* The disputed ride was *made from the reporting rider’s own account*.\n* The email on the receipt *matches the email of the rider’s account*.\n* The payment was made via *Google Pay*, so we cannot confirm exactly which card was used.\n\nSince the ticket has already been closed, please advise how you would like us to proceed from here.","2026-01-29T11:59:34.668Z"],["3849109","CCM-22326","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey [~accountid:5e343da79029c30ca0bcbe0d]  👋  Hope you are doing alright. 🙂 \n\nWe have another bigger batch for moving to the *external OPS* branch in TalentLMS. Let me know if I should maybe send you an SD for this, or what is the best way. Also, let me know if some of these users need to be permantnely deleted.\n\n[elvet.emali@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:elvet.emali@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+purity.gitonga@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:purity.gitonga@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+clare.glory@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:clare.glory@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+josphat.karanja@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:josphat.karanja@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+ann.kariuki@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:ann.kariuki@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+micheal.makokha@bolt.eu+|mailto:micheal.makokha@bolt.eu]\n\n[+timothy.mulongo@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:timothy.mulongo@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+william.musili@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:william.musili@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+maurene.odongo@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:maurene.odongo@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+james.omweno@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:james.omweno@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[+kevin.wanyonyi@bolt-outsource.eu+|mailto:kevin.wanyonyi@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[brian.eshiwani@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:brian.eshiwani@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[ann.kariuki@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:ann.kariuki@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[ebby.maingi@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:ebby.maingi@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[kennedy.obiero@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:kennedy.obiero@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[millicent.omumamu@bolt.eu|mailto:millicent.omumamu@bolt.eu]\n\n[molly.oticha@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:molly.oticha@bolt-outsource.eu]\n\n[kennedy.maina@bolt-outsource.eu|mailto:kennedy.maina@bolt-outsource.eu]\n","2026-01-29T12:01:24.016Z"],["3849111","DSR-4207","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-29T12:01:34.368Z"],["3849113","PFI-838251","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThis might have happened due to a temporary technical glitch. We have refunded the first attempt that was charged wrongly and the user should receive it within 10 days or more depending on their bank internal processes.","2026-01-29T12:01:54.283Z"],["3849114","RCE-400","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Merili Randmaa [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769688038665309]*{color}:\nThanks <@U02CCN2T2GZ>!\n\nGreatly appreciated :pray:\n{quote}","2026-01-29T12:01:57.902Z"],["3849115","BDRIV-7","BDRIV","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","Latest info from TWS is that they would provide initial information about cells on {{2026-01-30}} .\n\nI also did some “research” to understand what the exact problem with the charging is.\nMy general understanding is that currently, we have problem of battery charging throughput in the high season.\n\nHowever, as the swapping frequency changes in a single city (seasonality, RpV, fleet size change, etc) throughout the year and cities might need different charging “strategies” during different time of the year.\n\nAt the moment, it seems to me that there is no single “simple” charger which could cover all these needs. In my opinion it would make sense, if we have some sort of “smart chargers”.\n\nWhat would be the definition of a “*smart charger*”?\n\n* The biggest upside would be *adjustable charging current* - according to the warehouse needs, You can adjust the charger output to be 3A-12A. This enables flexibility for warehouses to implement different charging strategies throughout the year.\n** At different currents, the charging efficiency varies - higher currents can charge batteries faster, but may provide cost savings in low season if configured for the more efficient working region.\n** Different warehouses have different power capabilities, they could adjust for their available power resource.\n* Charging profiles for different batteries\n** If our newer batteries - EB1, D1, (new battery) are connected to the charger, they can each have charging profile adjusted according to this specific battery.\n*** Charging of some vehicle batteries can be prioritized\n*** Charging profile can be adjusted according to different batteries - we can probably find the quickest or most efficient profiles for each battery on how to charge them.\n* Internet connection \n** We can have actual charging data\n** Warehouses can change charging currents for batteries etc quickly \n** We can discover faulty or dangerous batteries connected to batteries\n** According to warehouse needs, we can update charger firmware to implement different charging strategies etc.\n\nI looked for some reference products online, they are not exactly what we would want but they are very close and give a price estimate.\n\n[Chinese one which would need to be customized a bit|https://www.alibaba.com/product-detail/KP600A-12V-25A-24V-20A-36V_62275773890.html?spm=a2700.shop_plfe.41413.1.1291771dlD5ddA]\n\n[Expensive Western one |https://www.mouser.ee/ProductDetail/MEAN-WELL/NPB-1200-48?qs=Rp5uXu7WBW%2FGZWZwDUFHNA%3D%3D&utm_id=22436682664&utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_marketing_tactic=emeacorp&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=22436694619&gbraid=0AAAAADn_wf2UyaFoS82ea95SBPCjrIxLV&gclid=Cj0KCQiAp-zLBhDkARIsABcYc6sScFhqEt9okq_M2pohxwR3sI84odkzAGre_xNGEeYIX44Lex-fgdsaAr9uEALw_wcB]\n\n\nAs I heard from [~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] , more efficient are powerful chargers were tested in DE, which provided good results (higher battery throughput and electricity cost save by 6%) and justified the investment into the more expensive chargers as they have better ROI compared to the “good old cheap” chargers.\n\nIn this [thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C078RNU1WJJ/p1769598369000099] the Oslo ops Konstantinos Krikelis describes their charging process and says that Oslo is planning to increase their battery charging capacity to support 1000 current chargers (from current 500 chargers). \n\nI would propose to look further into such chargers and ask what the price would be for a charger that could match our needs.\n\nFYI [~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] [~accountid:5f896ba2e357dd006e937e5b] [~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] ","2026-01-29T12:02:01.157Z"],["3849118","PFI-840030","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T12:02:25.052Z"],["3849119","FDBT-4876","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-29T12:02:30.605Z"],["3849120","PFI-838257","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-29T12:02:39.668Z"],["3849127","PFI-835166","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T12:03:47.787Z"],["3849128","RLONE-518","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Due to the regulations in Denmark and that that Bolt has the contractual relationship with the passenger, drivers and fleets cannot independently collect and retain fares as sellers as this would conflict with Danish taxi law.\n\nRead more in detail [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/LSS-57939].","2026-01-29T12:03:55.685Z"],["3849129","ADS-283","ADS","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline failed. Build: https://jenkins.boltint.net/job/PL/job/autocode-baca-autocode/470/","2026-01-29T12:04:17.998Z"],["3849133","LSS-57939","LSS","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Hi Elina,\n\nThanks for getting back and clarifying the collection obligation.","2026-01-29T12:04:42.129Z"],["3849134","LSS-57939","LSS","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Close ticket.","2026-01-29T12:04:51.644Z"],["3849135","LSS-61448","LSS","ab.moula@bolt.eu","AB Moula","Hey [~accountid:608009c6f74b3f006a326795] [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] \n\nI think we should draft a new co-invest contract for this. It’s cleaner. That we have a separate contract for TT/Solis (not that much comes from that), another for TT EVs and now a new one for normal ICE vehicles @ 25k co-invest each. ","2026-01-29T12:05:13.064Z"],["3849138","LSS-62343","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] I have reviewed the agreement and sharing below suggested amendments as I cannot make any amendments in the pdf document.\n\n6.0 Demise\n\nCurrent version\n\n“Premises at First Floor 22 Gas Street Birmingham”\n\nSuggested version\n\n_“Premises at [Ground Floor and/or First Floor – to be confirmed] 22 Gas Street, Birmingham, as shown edged red on the agreed lease plan, including rights for a separate self-contained external entrance.”_\n\nIssue:\n\n* The HoTs refer to _First Floor only_, whereas the premises operate as a walk-in hub and the landlord has agreed to a new external entrance, which implies ground floor access. - [~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] could you please confirm if my assumption is correct?\n\n*Clause 7.0 - Term & Break Clause*\n\nCurrent version\n\n“Mutual break clause option on 28th September 2028… minimum 6 months notice”\n\nSuggested version\n\n“A mutual break option on 28 September 2028, exercisable on not less than six (6) months’ prior written notice, conditional only upon payment of the basic rent up to the break date and giving vacant possession, with no other conditions attached.”\n\n*3. Clause 8.0 – Rent (£82,000 pa)*\n\n[~accountid:712020:714baa0e-ddd0-4776-8064-c5a5d3ae37aa] is 5k going to be paid only once on top of the first year’s rent?\n\n*4. Clause 16.0* \n\nSuggested version\n\n_“The Landlord shall, at its own cost (subject to the agreed rent uplift), carry out and complete the construction of a separate self-contained external entrance to the Premises, within three (3) months of the Tenant committing to the new lease and receipt of all required head lessor and statutory approvals.”_\n\n*5. NEW CLAUSE REQUIRED*  \n\nThere is no remedy if the landlord does not deliver the works.\n\nSuggested clause\n\n_“If the Landlord fails to complete the entrance works within the agreed three-month period (other than due to Tenant delay or force majeure), the Tenant shall be entitled to an appropriate rent suspension until completion, or the right to terminate the agreement without penalty.”_\n\n*6. Clause 10.0* \n\nSuggested version\n\n_“Use as offices and a walk-in driver / customer hub, including ancillary meeting, waiting, welfare, administrative and operational functions.”_\n\n7. Clause 11.0 \n\nSuggested version\n\n_“Full repairing terms subject to a Schedule of Condition, with the Tenant not required to put the Premises into any better state of repair than evidenced therein.”_\n\n* Without a Schedule of Condition, the Tenant could inherit historic disrepair liability.\n\n*8. Tenant Fit-Out & Layout Changes (Missing)*\n\nThere is no express permission for internal works or layout changes.\n\n_“The Tenant may carry out non-structural internal fit-out and layout works, including redecoration, furniture replacement, meeting booths, branding, glazing changes and reconfiguration to separate staff and visitor areas, with landlord’s consent not to be unreasonably withheld or delayed.”_\n\n*9. Reinstatement at Lease End (Missing)*\n\nSuggested clause\n\n_“The Tenant shall not be required to reinstate alterations at lease expiry unless the Landlord gives written notice at least six months prior to lease end specifying the items to be reinstated.”_","2026-01-29T12:06:27.946Z"],["3849139","LSS-60241","LSS","elena-roxana.iordachel@bolt.eu","Elena-Roxana Iordăchel","Hello! Thank you for all the information and guidance.\n\nWe have confirmed that the phone number associated with the account at the time the trip was made in 2023 is different from the user’s current phone number. However, the user did have that phone number until March 2025. No other account has ever been linked to this phone number.\n\nAdditionally, the device connected to the order is not the same device the customer has been using since March 2025.\n\nWe have now contacted the customer again to clarify whether they were the one who created the account in 2020 and whether they owned it during 2023.\n\nUnfortunately, the original case was closed automatically. The previous agent asked the user if they recognized someone named Alina G, which was the previous name on the account (changed in December 2025). As the user did not reply, the case was automatically closed.","2026-01-29T12:06:34.893Z"],["3849140","DPX-3475","DPX","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:610279a2ec92ab00707f6b23] Seems like that fix is working 💪 \nI tried on several Android/iOS devices, ranging from oldest Android we support:\n- Sunmi V2 Pro (7.1.2)\n- OnePlus 8T (14.0)\n- Samsung Galaxy Tab A7 Lite (14.0)\n- Pixel 8 emulator (16.0)\n- iPad 6th gen (17.7.6)\n- iPhone 11 (26.2)\n\nJust need to set reminder to verify the Expo Update patch before next native release.","2026-01-29T12:06:41.475Z"],["3849142","LSS-61323","LSS","ab.moula@bolt.eu","AB Moula","Hey [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] \n\nAs discussed, can we amend this to just 150 vehicles (total) for now, and then can we include non-committal / non-enforceable wording elsewhere that Bolt intends on scaling this initiative with Feenix up to 1,500 cars. \n\nThis wording is important as Feenix’s financiers want comfort that the demand exists on Bolt for these number of vehicles. \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-29T12:06:47.430Z"],["3849143","PFI-813007","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to client 4366840 and the funds were already paid out to them with the rest of their balance [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/228213434|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/228213434]. \nWe would advise against moving the funds in that case.","2026-01-29T12:07:01.910Z"],["3849144","PFI-840241","PFI","igors.ivanovs@bolt-outsource.eu","Igors Ivanovs","!2.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T12:07:02.933Z"],["3849145","RDXENG-4628","RDXENG","talha.tahir@bolt.eu","Talha Tahir","Driver photo is missing from the live activity. Tested in {{CI.220.0}}, response has driver photo url but app doesn’t reflect.\n\n\n{noformat}{\n  \"code\": 0,\n  \"message\": \"OK\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"content_state\": {\n      \"order\": {\n        \"order_handle\": {\n          \"order_id\": 2500060830,\n          \"city_id\": 1,\n          \"order_system\": \"taxi\"\n        },\n        \"view_type\": \"active_order_tipping\",\n        \"driver_id\": 1688352,\n        \"payload\": {\n          \"type\": \"active_order_tipping\",\n          \"title\": \"Dropoff in 1 min\",\n          \"short_title\": \"1 min\",\n          \"subtitle\": \"Add a tip?\",\n          \"watch\": {\n            \"title\": \"Dropoff in\",\n            \"subtitle\": \"1 min\",\n            \"progress\": 0.96\n          },\n          \"buttons\": [\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060830&country=ee&amount=1&index=0&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"€1\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060830&country=ee&amount=3&index=1&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"€3\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060830&country=ee&amount=5&index=2&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"€5\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060830&country=ee&index=3&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"Other\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"config\": {\n            \"should_show_driver_photo\": true\n          },\n          \"driver_avatar_url\": \"'https://taxify-fleet.s3.amazonaws.com/prelive/'root/581/123/1581123_picture_bukOTtgDhs.png\"\n        },\n        \"action\": {\n          \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailing?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060830&country=ee&source=liveactivity\",\n          \"title\": \"Open activity order\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}{noformat}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 12.34.45.png|width=590,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 12.34.45.png\"!","2026-01-29T12:07:20.991Z"],["3849148","FX-3276","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Marily Haidak [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769688470780319]*{color}:\nHey <@U09D62DKH9P>, is there any update?\n{quote}","2026-01-29T12:08:03.496Z"],["3849157","WD-22650","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi, [~accountid:712020:cfea02e5-8522-43c8-9f69-236d8bece552] . Please next time create a separate ticket for such purposes  (this time I did it myself) [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WDFT-3574|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/WDFT-3574|smart-link]  \n\nOtherwise, there is risk that nobody would reply to you. You see this particular ticket is in status “ Waiting for customer” , and I have already provided solution for initial request. ","2026-01-29T12:09:14.528Z"],["3849158","CORA-387","CORA","anneli.tammesson@bolt.eu","Anneli Tammesson","[~accountid:712020:0d04167f-dce4-443a-8156-8acc576e7815] We need to add additional metadata fields to this Looker.\n\nWe have configured extra metadata fields under documents per markets over time. For example in Belgium we have a metadata field called License region. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 14.08.41.png|width=616,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 14.08.41.png\"!","2026-01-29T12:09:18.793Z"],["3849159","DPX-3475","DPX","tanel.koha@bolt.eu","Tanel Koha","[~accountid:60950a25539c14006ae92e40] Quick question - what happens if app is background and restart signal arrives?\n\nIf it’s problematic, I have a solution idea, but not sure yet if it’s an issue.","2026-01-29T12:09:18.168Z"],["3849163","PFI-828672","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Wrong link provided, this payment is already matched to the same client","2026-01-29T12:09:27.998Z"],["3849164","LSS-62247","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348088|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348088|smart-link]  ","2026-01-29T12:09:29.621Z"],["3849166","HS-29326","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hi Chris! \n\nVitality has confirmed Your membership and Your membership number is 1286532294.\n\nVitality has also sent over the information for adding family members and You can find the document [here|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1H-JiJZtlpjOqqjkNNPrS6TFiN5Edei3s/view?usp=sharing]. The password for opening the file is FEx2BL83. \n\nPlease kindly let me know if You wish to proceed with adding dependents to Your plan. \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin\n","2026-01-29T12:10:42.904Z"],["3849167","WDFT-3569","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","HR001 and BG001 are moved to Region 6, Roles of [~accountid:624d3e6a45ece00069cdb4e5] [~accountid:637f4716de5cdaba3a67c532] and [~accountid:712020:2b04881a-4ca8-40cb-9a35-a008b9853ec0]  are updated so they keep access to these compnies. ","2026-01-29T12:10:53.056Z"],["3849168","FX-3276","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769688641133699]*{color}:\nNext 2-3 weeks to be delivered\n{quote}","2026-01-29T12:10:55.980Z"],["3849170","PFI-840147","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hey, as said in Slack, escalated to Fonoa. I’ll let you know as soon as I hear back!","2026-01-29T12:10:58.866Z"],["3849171","PFI-840147","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","[https://fonoasupport.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/requests/27796|https://fonoasupport.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/requests/27796]","2026-01-29T12:11:02.101Z"],["3849175","LSS-61847","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello, [~accountid:712020:950de065-187c-4170-babd-e5aa814bdb19] ! I believe that all details filled in by you are checked and correct. \n\n+*Signing process:*+\n\n* signee: Ahto Kink (PLEASE FILL THE GAPS: \n** THE FILE NAMED: FORMULARZ_PODMIOTU(1): imię i nazwisko osoby upoważnionej: 40 (53) *AHTO KINK* Podpis: 41 (54) {color:#36b37e}_SIGNATURE - WET INK_{color}\n** THE FILE NAMED: FORMULARZ_ZAP(3): Pieczątka Pracodawcy ({color:#36b37e}_COMPANY STAMP_{color}_)_ _____________________ Czytelny podpis osoby umocowanej (czytelne podpisy osób umocowanych) ({color:#36b37e}_SIGNATURE - WET INK OF AHTO KINK_{color})\n* signature form: wet ink\n* files: both files uploaded in the ticket\n* please send the original POA to Bolt Warsaw Office: ul. Prosta 67, 00-838 Warszawa, Polska (Prosta 67 Street, post code: 00-838 Warsaw, Poland) to the attention of [~accountid:712020:950de065-187c-4170-babd-e5aa814bdb19] - [~accountid:712020:950de065-187c-4170-babd-e5aa814bdb19] please share your mobile phone number for DHL tracking. Thank you!","2026-01-29T12:11:39.553Z"],["3849177","PFI-828672","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Correct payment link https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75687773\r\nMatched","2026-01-29T12:11:51.176Z"],["3849179","PFI-840146","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hey, Same as in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-840147|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-840147|smart-link] , escalated to Fonoa and will let you know as soon as I hear back","2026-01-29T12:12:12.495Z"],["3849180","DELIVERY-1298","DELIVERY","cristian.uricec@bolt.eu","Cristian-Dumitru Uricec","We agreed to have a scope out next week. After that, we will evaluate the effort. ","2026-01-29T12:12:18.019Z"],["3849181","LSS-62394","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","[^Feature Coverage Tracker TbT.xlsx] _(39 kB)_","2026-01-29T12:12:35.333Z"],["3849182","LSS-62394","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","[^Bolt Technology OÜ LA-AMD3 05695-03 v1 22 Jan 2026 BL (1).docx]\n\n","2026-01-29T12:12:52.290Z"],["3849185","PFI-833616","PFI","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","[~accountid:62cebed2afe495359d9dc574], could you please proceed with creating the new subtypes?","2026-01-29T12:13:19.893Z"],["3849186","LSS-62386","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348093|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348093|smart-link]  ","2026-01-29T12:13:32.461Z"],["3849187","DPX-3475","DPX","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:610279a2ec92ab00707f6b23] it just looks to reload once the app is brought up again - I don’t see an issue in that tbh. I mean, there is no freeze or anything like that. Just a few-second spinner.","2026-01-29T12:13:40.518Z"],["3849189","LSS-62345","LSS","iva.buric@bolt.eu","Iva Burić","Hi [~accountid:712020:31cea34c-cf90-4827-8bcd-428a9ac6e80d] \n\nNo immediate further action is required unless new evidence or a formal claim is received.\n\nIf the rider escalates to TfL or another regulator, Legal should be notified immediately to manage disclosure.\n\nCase should be tagged internally as a protected characteristic incident for tracking.\n\nIf you think the response needs to be send to the rider, I am sharing below an example:\n\n_Thank you again for reaching out to share your experience with us._\n\n_We understand how upsetting this situation must have been, especially involving your child, and we want you to know that your concerns were treated with the utmost seriousness. We’ve reviewed the report in line with our platform policies and standards, and have taken appropriate steps in response._\n\n_While we aren’t able to share details of any actions taken regarding other individuals, please rest assured that we’ve done everything within our power to address this fairly and responsibly. Our platform does not tolerate any behaviour that goes against our values of respect, inclusion and safety._\n\n_We’re grateful you took the time to bring this to our attention, and we remain committed to improving experiences for all riders and families who use Bolt. If there’s anything else you'd like us to consider, please don’t hesitate to let us know._\n\nh3. ","2026-01-29T12:14:14.076Z"],["3849190","DSR-4043","DSR","oliver.chinyere@bolt.eu","Oliver Chinyere","Complete. Response sent to data subject today: [https://drive.google.com/file/d/14BQJr1BcTGihSDpXW30TPjGYEhs9Szgt/view?usp=drive_link|https://drive.google.com/file/d/14BQJr1BcTGihSDpXW30TPjGYEhs9Szgt/view?usp=drive_link|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T12:14:28.384Z"],["3849192","PFI-840022","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to active client 3600501. \nWe would advise against moving the funds in that case.","2026-01-29T12:14:42.323Z"],["3849193","DRX-28397","DRX","alvar.hansen@bolt.eu","Alvar Hansen","[~accountid:628dd714269a9a0068f2a783] good question. I asked it on comms channel: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY/p1769688873472249|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CND9AL5LY/p1769688873472249|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T12:14:55.485Z"],["3849194","PFI-833616","PFI","nazrin.nasibova@bolt.eu","Nazrin Nasibova","Helloo, thank you for clarification. I’ll update you here once new subtypes has been mapped","2026-01-29T12:15:06.683Z"],["3849195","LSS-61941","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Sveiki [~accountid:712020:7a0eb594-fb3b-4988-9715-b614bae4a6fb], dalinuosi galimu atsakymo keleiviui projektu.\n\n_Sveiki, (vardas),_\n_Apgailestaujame dėl Jūsų patirties ir suprantame, kad susiklosčiusi situacija galėjo sukelti neigiamų emocijų. Taip pat apgailestaujame, jei Jūsų lūkesčiai neatitiko užsakytų paslaugų kokybės._\n\n_Vis dėlto pažymėtina, kad „Bolt“ veikia tik kaip informacinės visuomenės paslaugos teikėjas ir neteikia pavežėjimo paslaugų. Vadovaujantis „Bolt“ Bendrosiomis nuostatomis ir sąlygomis keleiviams, pavežėjimo paslaugas teikia vairuotojai savarankiškai, o kiekvienos kelionės metu sudaroma atskira sutartis tiesiogiai tarp keleivio ir vairuotojo (Bendrųjų sąlygų 2.1, 5.1 p.)._\n\n_Atsižvelgiant į tai, „Bolt“ neprisiima atsakomybės už vairuotojų veiksmus ar dėl jų kilusią žalą ir neturi teisinio pagrindo atlyginti prašomų neturtinių (moralinių) nuostolių (Bendrųjų sąlygų 7.1, 7.6 p.). Ginčai, kylantys dėl galimos žalos ar paslaugos teikimo aplinkybių, sprendžiami tiesiogiai tarp keleivio ir vairuotojo (Bendrųjų sąlygų 2.3 p.)._\n\n_Jeigu manote, kad Jums buvo padaryta žala, turite teisę ją ginti teisės aktų nustatyta tvarka, kreipiantis tiesiogiai į atitinkamus asmenis ar kompetentingas institucijas._\n\n_Dar kartą apgailestaujame dėl susidariusios situacijos ir dėkojame, kad apie ją informavote._\n\n_Pagarbiai_\n\n_Bolt komanda_\n\n","2026-01-29T12:15:12.507Z"],["3849199","FDBT-4876","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments fails on 2026-01-28 02:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task load_items_to_workday failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'ValueError: can not infer schema from empty dataset', 'run_id': 98980227699212, 'task_key': 'load_items_to_workday'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-28T02%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=partner_payout_currency_clearing.partner_payout_currency_clearing_ledger_aggr_to_workday_integration&base_date=2026-01-28T02%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-29T12:15:52.920Z"],["3849200","PFI-840243","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-29T12:15:53.602Z"],["3849203","LSS-62021","LSS","margarita.sargautyte@bolt.eu","Margarita Sargautytė","Hey Beatričė. Thank you for the overview and suggestions. It sounds reas