by RMB 0.3_\n\nPlease confirm how to proceed.\n\n!WXWorkCapture_17683819022185-20260114-091142.png|width=679,alt=\"WXWorkCapture_17683819022185-20260114-091142.png\"!","2026-01-29T12:38:24.422Z"],["3849467","L10N-31050","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T12:38:24.985Z"],["3849468","L10N-31052","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T12:38:25.100Z"],["3849469","L10N-31051","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T12:38:27.082Z"],["3849470","L10N-31053","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T12:38:27.571Z"],["3849471","L10N-31054","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T12:38:28.612Z"],["3849472","L10N-31044","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31027](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31027)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-29T12:38:39.574Z"],["3849475","HS-29542","HS","kristin.reichardt@bolt.eu","Kristin Reichardt","Thank you!","2026-01-29T12:39:02.908Z"],["3849476","LSS-62395","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:5acb064d56d6c72b45183935] , what is the purpose of this cooperation? Will they help you to close some open positions for your team? ","2026-01-29T12:39:09.011Z"],["3849477","DRX-27617","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","[~accountid:63a2c0057cde7bff9d76f16c] can we please check this ticket again.","2026-01-29T12:39:38.265Z"],["3849482","LUX-806","LUX","ashok.fernandez@bolt.eu","Ashok Fernandez","Here is the [live|https://eu.mixpanel.com/project/3668728/view/4167396/app/home] and [prelive|https://eu.mixpanel.com/project/3769708/view/4266784/app/home] mixpanel","2026-01-29T12:40:09.355Z"],["3849483","MLC-4113","MLC","helina.nommik@bolt.eu","Helina Nõmmik","*W5:* \n\nMapped out the Activation/Onboarding flow in Figma, including also in-apps that are currently in Product team’s ownership. Looked into funnels and comms performance. Added findings to the [Scooters, User Onboarding, automated comms improvement plan 2026|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Hn6lnYQz6wIxyI9uuCQiC83ldE9jtD4mTyk_QhCN4UU/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.bggdizuvd5q8]\n\n*Next steps:* Finalise the improvement plan doc, if some data is still missing, add it there.","2026-01-29T12:40:20.624Z"],["3849485","LSS-62020","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:f50af85a-3d8b-4b5c-b19d-ad552b86d158] please find here the signed document. [^Termination Notice_ Bolt Services ZA (Pty) Ltd_Alexander Forbes Financial Services (Pty) Ltd_28.01.26.pdf]  ","2026-01-29T12:40:45.877Z"],["3849487","C2-459","C2","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","I think it is a reasonable thing to do, let’s proceed","2026-01-29T12:40:47.251Z"],["3849488","LSS-61920","LSS","georgia.heathman@bolt.eu","Georgia Heathman","Agree with Emma’s comments above. \n\n\nI’ve just spoken to John Buckley about the external counsel review. Let’s proceed as we will need to use a parking agreement in future schemes most likely, and the cost can be offset against the Liverpool operation. \n\nHowever, [~accountid:712020:3d2dfcb9-5b90-4b13-a4e2-9b7530e3d83f] conscious this shouldn’t impact any work on the warehouse lease so you can put this second to any requirement from EC on the warehouse. And would it be possible to confirm that the cost won’t go above the £2000 + VAT? \n\nI trust your draft and given we have confirmed insurance is in place I think the risk is reduced. \n\nThank you again!","2026-01-29T12:40:50.941Z"],["3849493","PFI-838522","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThere was no refund on this order [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2356962892/307?orderTryId=3035981064|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2356962892/307?orderTryId=3035981064]. Instead, the user was charged partially from their card and 14.3PLN as debt in their Bolt balance. The debt was later paid on these two orders [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2358436504/307?orderTryId=3038384523|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2358436504/307?orderTryId=3038384523] and [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/284462010?cityId=307&showUserTz=false|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/delivery-order/orders/284462010?cityId=307&showUserTz=false].","2026-01-29T12:41:03.027Z"],["3849495","LUX-806","LUX","prasheel.soni@bolt.eu","Prasheel Soni","Do you know which project is this? I'll raise a ticket to IT to get access to it.\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ACKBNUTFS/image.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ACKBNUTFS/image.png|smart-link]","2026-01-29T12:41:58.122Z"],["3849497","LSS-61972","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:616ff0d63e3753006f99a61c] ! This one should be the right version\n\n[^20260121_6 police Bolt atbilde.docx.edoc] ","2026-01-29T12:42:15.534Z"],["3849499","LSS-62255","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Hi [~accountid:712020:52c03b81-3e44-455b-a71d-0e9088f7c7ad] thank you for your question. \n\nIf I remember correctly, we already had a similar issue in PL and it was agreed that it would be better if Bolt Ops, as a parent entity of the local entities, signed the contract. I’m not sure whether Bolt CZ would have a basis to operate and issue receipts/collect payments on behalf of other local entities. Let me double check what was the outcome in PL and get back to you. In any case, I recommend checking this set up with tax, commerce and billing teams.\n\nLooping in [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2], in case you already have similar experiences from other countries - if so, please feel free to comment.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-29T12:42:22.175Z"],["3849503","PFI-839986","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T12:43:13.505Z"],["3849504","PFI-838537","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nKindly check this issue with the Technical Support team as these are card terminal orders and there was no payment link created for them that can help understand the charges.","2026-01-29T12:43:25.688Z"],["3849505","GRWA-1575","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","PR: [link|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15606]","2026-01-29T12:43:40.586Z"],["3849506","LSS-61967","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:616ff0d63e3753006f99a61c] ! There is the proper one\n\n[^20260121_1 police Bolt atbilde.docx.edoc] ","2026-01-29T12:43:44.052Z"],["3849508","GRWA-1576","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","PR: [link|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/pull/15606]","2026-01-29T12:43:46.478Z"],["3849510","GRWA-1561","GRWA","kristian.aditya@bolt.eu","Kristian Aditya","Airflow PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9819|https://github.com/bolteu/airflow-main/pull/9819]","2026-01-29T12:44:12.364Z"],["3849511","RNTL-30789","RNTL","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162470","2026-01-29T12:44:17.997Z"],["3849513","DRX-27723","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","[~accountid:63998434abc764d2ca5f30bc] will you please add more context into the ticket what exactly the issue is?","2026-01-29T12:44:34.149Z"],["3849514","LSS-60756","LSS","angela.noguera@bolt.eu","Angela Noguera","Yes [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , only Ahto’s.\n\nThen the client will proceed to sign.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-29T12:44:45.377Z"],["3849515","SAI-1215","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","[~accountid:712020:f3b3e918-2599-4c21-991c-efa4dcddf08d] can we close this one?","2026-01-29T12:44:46.738Z"],["3849516","PFI-838559","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThis is related to a new feature called re-use preauthorisation. Instead of placing a new hold for every trip, we now *re-use an existing pre-authorization* for a set period.\n\nThis means if you take multiple trips, we use the same hold to cover the cost, so you won't see multiple temporary charges on your statement.\n\nIn this specific case, the charge for a new completed order [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1499366706/79?orderTryId=2849657127|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1499366706/79?orderTryId=2849657127] was simply applied to a pre-authorization from the cancelled order that was already reserved on the card.","2026-01-29T12:44:59.076Z"],["3849517","PFI-838618","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-29T12:45:29.062Z"],["3849519","SAI-1215","SAI","przemyslaw.wiczolek@bolt.eu","Przemysław Wiczołek","Yes, it was be handled by SAI-1419","2026-01-29T12:45:41.228Z"],["3849521","LUX-806","LUX","ashok.fernandez@bolt.eu","Ashok Fernandez","Here's the name of the projects that I can see in Mixpanel, is that what you need?\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ABMLJMT9B/screenshot_2026-01-29_at_13.45.21.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ABMLJMT9B/screenshot_2026-01-29_at_13.45.21.png|smart-link]","2026-01-29T12:45:52.941Z"],["3849522","PFI-838639","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-29T12:45:53.746Z"],["3849523","LUX-806","LUX","prasheel.soni@bolt.eu","Prasheel Soni","Yes, that's what I needed. Thanks :raised_hands:","2026-01-29T12:46:10.228Z"],["3849525","DPX-3475","DPX","tanel.koha@bolt.eu","Tanel Koha","And BTW, thank you so much for taking time out of your PIM schedule to take a peek here 🙇‍♂️  I owe you!","2026-01-29T12:46:24.527Z"],["3849526","LSS-61297","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","All clear regarding the collection process [~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17] , thanks! (/) \n\nRegarding sharing data with NŠA - maybe first we can reach out to them, and liaise on data sharing (means, what we’ll share, on what frequency etc) and explain that we’d like to sign a Memorandum of Understanding or a Data Sharing Agreement? Then, we can see how they react? I want to avoid us spending time on agreement before we know if they’re even open to signing it. Could you start this conversation with them?","2026-01-29T12:46:33.494Z"],["3849528","CSP-463","CSP","henn.runnel@bolt.eu","Henn Runnel","[PRD: Driver Registration Exact Lookup in Beehive|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XYnjIq9i0RK7h-GiGD-HNljxomXHjf6qTXJWVOu1HN0/edit?usp=sharing]","2026-01-29T12:46:41.177Z"],["3849529","DRX-27860","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","[~accountid:63998438f3c3dfd71fe85ae4] please add a test case for this ticket and link with it","2026-01-29T12:46:45.636Z"],["3849530","PFI-813902","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T12:46:52.921Z"],["3849531","LSS-61615","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","*BACKGROUND:*\n\n* In Romania, Bolt (RO) is contracting with Util Deco SRL (RO company)\n* This involves entering into the following agreements:\n** [Partnership Agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/147PiOTXKn-0jxifCuJPfcsL3DjBNlinX/edit]\n*** Purpose of the agreement is to “_ensure the involvement of persons with disabilities in the production of goods or services marketed by the authorized sheltered workshop UtilDeco Group S.R.L_”.\n*** Clause 5 deals with data protection.\n**** Not explicit, but heavily implied that this is an IC relationship.\n**** Data at-issue is name/position/contact details/signature of signatory. Purpose of processing is execution of the agreement.\n**** Clauses are effectively boilerplate, demanding compliance with applicable laws.\n** [Service Agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bdKoJozudUaUop1WVTwpd3Oxi_Tpv9NU/edit]\n*** Governs obligations re delivery of the services.\n*** Clause 18 deals with data protection.\n**** Not explicit, but heavily implied that this is an IC relationship.\n**** Data at-issue is name/position/contact details/signature of signatory. Purpose of processing is execution of the agreement.\n**** Clauses are effectively boilerplate, demanding compliance with applicable laws.\n* In terms of personal data sharing:\n** Partnership Agreement:\n*** Main data exchange is data of signatories. Fine ✅ \n*** Under Clause 5.1, counterparty must provide Bolt (on request) “_with the job description of the person/persons with disabilities_”. Georgiana has confirmed that this will not happen in practice.\n** Service Agreement:\n*** Main data exchange is data of signatories. Fine ✅ \n\n*INTERNAL NOTES:*\n\n* Overall, the only personal data being shared here is one-off and low risk (i.e., signatory data).\n* The terms in each agreement are fine - we do not need any indemnities etc., and the ‘compliance with law’ base is covered. As such, I have no comments ✅ ","2026-01-29T12:47:07.909Z"],["3849533","PFI-839731","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hello [~accountid:712020:fcfa9422-5db7-4665-8051-fb4034f1ddf7],\n\nEC has been disabled for the driver.\n\nCheers,\n\nNiki ","2026-01-29T12:48:51.340Z"],["3849535","LSS-61615","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Thanks [~accountid:712020:7cc5674c-6f47-4631-8bc3-483c4d0c5273] - in which case, it sounds like the only personal data we are sharing here is the data of the signatories, which is low risk. As such, the privacy provisions of both agreements look fine, and I have no comments at this time ✅ \n\nLet me know if anything further is needed from me. I will reassign the ticket to [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] in the meantime.","2026-01-29T12:49:11.021Z"],["3849536","MLC-4073","MLC","helina.nommik@bolt.eu","Helina Nõmmik","*W5:* \n\nStarted rewriting some of the existing content using mix of ChatGPT project I created for this purpose and Poe. As we currently can’t fully to rely on Poe copywriting yet. \n\nDrafted copies for First E-bike ride and Churn: \n\n* [First e-bike ride email & push|https://docs.google.com/document/d/14o1cyZCzSoWM-LxKZd1RNkvspUQ79ei3e0-Udx0Sfms/edit?tab=t.hrqjz5kjkis7]\n* [Churn vol.1 email & push|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-RGE1fE4-4UCW2vkM3qKj8gXWto6LJ68qgKjML2Xma8/edit?tab=t.6drkox6wstxz]\n\n*Next steps:* continue with the copywriting. Next up: Activation stage and remaining Churn comms. ","2026-01-29T12:49:12.138Z"],["3849537","WD-22728","WD","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","So sorry, please cancel I will log a correct one","2026-01-29T12:49:36.852Z"],["3849540","PFI-839971","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to client 6586450 and can be paid back to them with regular payout on Monday or manual payment earlier. \nIs this still necessary to move these funds to their other account?","2026-01-29T12:49:53.654Z"],["3849541","LSS-61328","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] ! any updates here? ","2026-01-29T12:50:11.310Z"],["3849543","PFI-839748","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hello [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8],\n\nEC has been enabled for both drivers. Thank you.\n\nBest Regards,\n\nNigar Alizada ","2026-01-29T12:50:22.339Z"],["3849544","RS-1962","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:5bbde236ee5d7e7580edbb02] , \n\nThank you for escalating the case! Can you please ask the authority to provide an official letter with a valid legal basis? We would be glad to assist once we have the official request, not in an email format. ","2026-01-29T12:50:38.203Z"],["3849545","LSS-61336","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] ! any updates here?","2026-01-29T12:50:47.945Z"],["3849546","DO-5840","DO","kaarel.nummert@bolt.eu","Kaarel Nummert","The table exists and is queryable via Databricks:\n\n{noformat}SELECT count(*)\nFROM sel_customer_support_pii_spark.support_case_communication_channel_updated{noformat}\n\nreturns {{6552}}.","2026-01-29T12:50:48.974Z"],["3849547","LSS-62342","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348128|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348128|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T12:50:57.571Z"],["3849549","SAI-1197","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","won’t do","2026-01-29T12:51:19.917Z"],["3849550","LSS-62342","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] sent out the document for signatures.","2026-01-29T12:51:20.435Z"],["3849552","LSS-61600","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Muhammad Rafi (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:51:42.447Z"],["3849553","PFI-839963","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to client 6586450 and can be paid back to them with regular payout on Monday or manual payment earlier. \nIs this still necessary to move these funds to their other account?","2026-01-29T12:51:44.711Z"],["3849557","LSS-61699","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","\nHey, [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^EE20260116-001 Fleetbrains - Bolt Drive EE.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:52:25.309Z"],["3849559","DPX-3475","DPX","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","[~accountid:610279a2ec92ab00707f6b23] I didn’t notice a problem after the reload in that case. Also the active order appeared so I assume polling is fine as well. Happy to help! 🤝 ","2026-01-29T12:52:34.152Z"],["3849561","LSS-62399","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","[^BM PoA Template S. Staniszewski_20250916.pdf] _(98 kB)_","2026-01-29T12:52:37.795Z"],["3849562","LSS-60074","LSS","ina.steinborn@bolt.eu","Ina Steinborn","Hi [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] ,\n\na deeper look into it would be much appreciated!\n\nWe would like to do it via DTI.\n\nSo from Uber they offer it as a benefit to their fleets and even argue that the insurance gets cheaper. They offer the dashcam Samsara to their fleets for free for a specific amount of time.\n","2026-01-29T12:52:51.341Z"],["3849563","CSDA-296","CSDA","iuliia.vlasenko@bolt.eu","Iuliia Vlasenko","Yes thanks ","2026-01-29T12:53:32.132Z"],["3849565","PFI-839896","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T12:53:42.867Z"],["3849567","LSS-62131","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Bolt Inbank confirmation (Mantvidas Klevečka) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:54:22.163Z"],["3849571","LSS-61580","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hi, [~accountid:712020:5edd7b8a-e535-468c-85fd-63f0b6de01b2] ! While checking information about landlord in the CEIDG register I noticed that on 1.01.2023 he suspended his business activity (it is officially registered in the CEIDG). Please ask the landlord (Wiesław Kietliński) if:\n\n* he runs his business activity in fact - if so, he should reactive his business in the register by changing the CEIDG information; \n* if he does not run his business activity and leases the outlet as a consumer (not an entrepreneur) (in fact this is shady from a legal POV as such activities are qualified as business activities), we need an official declaration of the landlord about the status change. We basically can conclude lease agreements with consumers (the risk of entity status qualification is on the landlord). If this case happens, please contact Tax team [tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu|mailto:tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu] if we are compliant with the tax law.\n* if the outlet was transferred onto another entity, we need to be presented with official declaration about this transfer (including a type of a transfer: sale of all the business or sale of an outlet);\n\nOnce, we confirm his business status, we will be proceeding with next steps accordingly. 😉 \n\n\n\nE-MAIL IN POLISH:\n\n“_W trakcie przygotowywania aneksu umowy zauważyliśmy w rejestrze CEIDG, że z początkiem stycznia 2023 r. zawiesił Pan działalność gospodarczą (w załączeń wydruk informacji z rejestru:_ [^Wydruk.pdf] _). Dla przejrzystości naszej współpracy oraz by móc poprawnie aneksować umowę, chcielibyśmy potwierdzić Pana status działalności i wybrać najbardziej optymalne rozwiązanie:_\n\n# _Jeżeli aktualnie prowadzi Pan działalność gospodarczą, prosilibyśmy o aktywowanie swojej działalności w rejestrze poprzez aktualizację danych w CEIDG (czyli zmianę statusu)_\n# _Jeżeli nie prowadzi Pan już działalności gospodarczej i wynajmuje lokal jako konsument (a nie przedsiębiorca), prosimy o dostarczenie nam Pana  oświadczenia o zmianie statusu._ \n# _Jeżeli lokal został przeniesiony na inny podmiot, prosilibyśmy o dostarczenie Pana oświadczenia dotyczącego tego przeniesienia (w tym rodzaju przeniesienia: sprzedaż całego przedsiębiorstwa lub sprzedaż samego lokalu) wraz z podaniem danych podmiotu przejmującego (co najmniej: nazwa/imię i nazwisko status działalności, NIP)._\n\n_Z góry dziękujemy za szybką odpowiedź!”_","2026-01-29T12:54:46.805Z"],["3849572","MLC-3912","MLC","helina.nommik@bolt.eu","Helina Nõmmik","*W5:* \n\nPlayed around with Poe, tested how well it adjust our copies. Unfortunately, it’s not that good yet. Shared feedback regarding this with Sarah. \n\nKeeping the project temporarily on hold, pending finalisation of the onboarding flow plan. Picking it up again during next sprint (W6-7). \n\n*Next steps:* Continue with the copywriting. ","2026-01-29T12:55:09.246Z"],["3849573","LSS-62093","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^LT20260125-001 Fleetcom - Bolt Drive LT.docx (2).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:55:11.303Z"],["3849576","LSS-58904","LSS","anca.grossu@bolt.eu","Anca-Ioana Grossu","[Here |https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LvdiXN-SaY8MA4hoIMe8KZzBs7_QeCGL/edit]is the TA Bolt Agreement reviewed by the supplier.","2026-01-29T12:55:53.276Z"],["3849577","LSS-62092","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^EE20260125-002 Fleetcom - Bolt Drive EE.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:56:00.756Z"],["3849579","DSR-4211","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-29T12:56:07.948Z"],["3849581","LSS-62091","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^EE20260126-001 EuroBroker - Bolt Drive EE.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:56:40.451Z"],["3849582","PFI-838738","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nHere are the payments:\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3959166188|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3959166188]\n\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3959346139|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/3959346139]","2026-01-29T12:56:41.628Z"],["3849584","LSS-62231","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:5bc4571d505b7a135722281f] , please see the draft agreement: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JQkO7kXePhjaOJ5XO4RwRfxFO0zB6Shp3RKxuy33g50/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.nb1npwqdc0v9|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JQkO7kXePhjaOJ5XO4RwRfxFO0zB6Shp3RKxuy33g50/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.nb1npwqdc0v9|smart-link] \nPlease carefully review it, especially the parts in yellow. Feel free to amend where incorrect in the track change mode. Please also add missing information/dates, and suggest what else could be added to the agreement. \n\nThank you! ","2026-01-29T12:56:55.180Z"],["3849587","PFI-838749","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-29T12:57:21.964Z"],["3849589","LSS-62077","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:6423e317b05b4e3e7dabadb6] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^DE20260121-001 Euro-Broker - Bolt Drive DE.docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:57:26.449Z"],["3849591","WFM-10208","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, should be visible now","2026-01-29T12:57:52.619Z"],["3849593","LSS-62400","LSS","madara.abeliteorola@bolt.eu","Madara Abelite-Orola","[^20260129_3 police Bolt atbilde.docx.pdf] _(71 kB)_","2026-01-29T12:57:58.566Z"],["3849595","LSS-62004","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:9420007a-1e48-4558-a534-5037f6b36792] ! Any updates from the Counterparty here?","2026-01-29T12:58:15.599Z"],["3849598","CBFP-1022","CBFP","ilya.goryachev@bolt.eu","Ilya Goryachev","Reopened the ticket because of not getting [here|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/5debf78ba5bedcb77ef058982a5548701d9d0a43/src/platform/commerce/invoicing_refund/main/table/RefundRequestTable.ts#L153-L187] refunds without payments","2026-01-29T12:58:28.530Z"],["3849600","LSS-61416","LSS","mariana.graca@bolt.eu","Mariana Graça","+*Situation summary:*+\n\n* Upon first contact with the Police, they requested confirmation if one of their Police Officers was a driver registered on our platform, and if he had performed rides in 2025.\n* Bolt ask the Police for a proper request of this information (“ofício”). However, the Police only sent us a simple email, without any indication of the legal basis sustaining the request or any other information.\n* Nevertheless, since the Police already knew the Officer in question was a TVDE driver (they had the number of his TVDE license), Legal did not saw a risk in merely confirming that the officer +was active on our platform+, and in providing general information about the +global number of completed rides in 2025+.\n* The Police followed up, with a request for more detailed information about the dates of such rides.\n* However, it needs to be taken in consideration that *the Police is not requesting this information in the context of an ongoing criminal investigation*. \n* What this means is that the Police is not acting in their capacity/power as entity to investigate crimes (“_OPC - orgão de polícia criminal_”, according to Law n.º 49/2008, of 27 August). *This is just an internal disciplinary matter of their organization*.\n* In this circumstance, +the Police’s legitimacy and legal basis for making such requests are not the same+.\n* Therefore, we once again requested that the Police send us a proper request (“ofíco”), with the indication of the legal basis they understand to be applicable to this specific situation - where they need information not to pursue criminal investigation, but to conduct a disciplinary process of one of their officers.\n* The Police responded and clarified +that the Officer was on medical leave from the Police, between September 30, 2025 and November 06, 2025, and they need to know if, contrary to the requirements of his Police medical leave, he was performing other professional paid activities, incompatible with such situation+.\n* They just want to know +if he performed rides during this period+. They don’t need any other details, like hours worked, earnings, passengers details, routes taken or GPS location data.\n* As legal basis, they quote article 6.º, n.º 1, c), e) of GDPR - “_Processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that at least one of the following applies: c) processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which the controller is subject; d) processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller_”.\n\n+*Local Legal POV and concerns*+\n\n* Although we don’t have any doubts that the Police has the power and legitimacy to carry out disciplinary proceedings of their own officers, the doubt remains, under local law, on their legitimacy to request third parties (individuals or companies) for private/confidential information for this purpose and on Bolt’s obligation to comply and provide such information, when this is done outside the Police’s capacity of crime investigation, as the Police continues to not provide any legal basis on this regard. \n* This assumes special importance in this situation, considering that *the Officer/Driver can* +*suffer disciplinary sanctions from the Police*+ *(termination of employment, suspension, loss of income)* +*due to information provided by Bolt*+ - in this case, *we already confirmed internally that the Officer/Driver performed rides in the indicated time frame, thus in breach of his Police medical leave*.\n* Upon preliminary legal search (local PT law) on this matter, no unequivocal answer was found on wether Bolt is legally obligated to provide the information required, for this purpose and in this context.\n* The main concern is that, *if sanctions like the ones listed above would fall upon the Officer/Driver, he could pursue litigation/claims against Bolt for illegally/improperly disclosing the information that lead to such sanction*.\n\n+Proposed action: Involve privacy team, Seek external counsel+","2026-01-29T12:58:41.281Z"],["3849602","LSS-62003","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt Inbank confirmation (Edgaras Micevičius) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T12:58:49.191Z"],["3849606","PFI-839870","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to client 8116111 and already paid out to them [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/234040788|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/234040788]. \nWe would advise against moving the funds in that case as this would cause debt.","2026-01-29T12:59:43.620Z"],["3849607","PA-581","PA","yichia.wu@bolt.eu","Yi-Chia Wu","* Update the processed to captured rate:\n** It will require 11 EUR countries' volume (ranging from 30-50%) to hit the 4M threshold\n** This routing can be done by changing Adyen’s traffic (checkout is not influenced)","2026-01-29T13:00:19.201Z"],["3849609","PFI-836775","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Apologies for the delay - unfortunately we can’t issue the invoices manually.","2026-01-29T13:00:23.231Z"],["3849613","PFI-839871","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T13:00:42.459Z"],["3849614","LSS-61882","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^Graiske Transport 2026 Bolt Fleet Partnership Agreement .docx (1).pdf]\n[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) (1) (2) (1).pdf]\n[^Fleet portal access agreement template  - 29.10.2025 (2) (1).pdf]\n\nHey, [~accountid:6151832899b4b8006a366830] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.","2026-01-29T13:00:44.755Z"],["3849615","CSDA-291","CSDA","nika.palaguta@bolt.eu","Nika Palaguta","Hi [~accountid:712020:e0838ce1-3087-40a7-b981-ba80de9296f9] ,\n\nI believe it’s a request to us 🙂 \nPlease submit the request through [our form|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2479/group/3831/create/6093]. \nPlease make sure to add a link to a Jira task led by you and COPs safety team for context. \nWe will return to you with questions and ETA.","2026-01-29T13:01:07.341Z"],["3849616","PFI-839764","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Let’s start from the beginning: \n\n# *Rider cash discount*\n#* FOP (Company earnings): *€6,323.29* {color:#bf2600}This is net discount, no vat included{color}\n#* Admin Balance ({{earning_cash_discount_netted}}): *€6,983.75* {color:#bf2600}This is with VAT included{color}\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.16.14.png|width=582,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.16.14.png\"!\n# *Cancellation fee* - {color:#bf2600}Same point as previously{color}\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.16.57.png|width=606,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.16.57.png\"!\n# *Expense reimbursements* - {color:#bf2600}in Admin, if you sum up earning_additional_service and earning_compensation, the amounts match with FOP{color}\n# {{earning_in_app_discount_netted}} -{color:#bf2600} in Admin it’s brought out separately, but there’s a note that this is included in the {color}{{earning_in_app_ride_fee}}. {color:#bf2600}So in FOP it’s part of the 194k in app earnings{color}\n# I’ll get back to you regarding the invoiced amount after checking. 🙂 ","2026-01-29T13:01:36.008Z"],["3849618","LSS-62065","LSS","catalin.jitariu@bolt.eu","Cătălin-Ioan Jitariu","You can send it to be signed. Thank you for the speedy resolvation [~accountid:712020:3d4c87bb-37b3-4ce8-a9b9-7232af464c95] .\n\n","2026-01-29T13:01:53.064Z"],["3849619","PFI-839764","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1769690754784149|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02C2SY0MHT/p1769690754784149|smart-card]","2026-01-29T13:02:04.984Z"],["3849621","LSS-62102","LSS","fidan.kamilova@bolt.eu","Fidan Kamilova","Hi [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e], we had a meeting with the AMAK and they agreed to amend the document. They can remove the parts that are related to apps. Could you please indicate which parts should be adjusted on the file?\n\nAlso you can see the required information from our side (for FIA index) in the following link: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MB6DWBVerxk0tV19zrjNiEG12jXJh-w3C-liVo-HSew/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MB6DWBVerxk0tV19zrjNiEG12jXJh-w3C-liVo-HSew/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n\nThey send the basic information here: [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RHB6P7kjaAFOf7J9y_or_RWG0o9BruTb/view?usp=sharing|https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RHB6P7kjaAFOf7J9y_or_RWG0o9BruTb/view?usp=sharing|smart-link] \nOnce you download it, you should be able to access the hyperlinks in it.\n\nCc: [~accountid:712020:4270191e-b006-439e-a800-5b8e06cf2c60] ","2026-01-29T13:02:19.934Z"],["3849622","LSS-61820","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:b56ff2aa-977c-46da-aee3-72a641fed4cc] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^DE20260119-002 Triasa Iberia - Bolt Drive DE.docx (1) (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T13:02:23.296Z"],["3849625","PFI-831572","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T13:02:47.966Z"],["3849626","LSS-61815","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Clement Obazee (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T13:03:00.126Z"],["3849628","BZNS-521","BZNS","andrea.attard@bolt.eu","Andrea Attard","Few cases:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.48.38.png|width=383,height=673,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.48.38.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.48.06.png|width=319,height=448,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 13.48.06.png\"!","2026-01-29T13:03:24.080Z"],["3849630","PFI-813906","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T13:03:26.812Z"],["3849631","MM-921","MM","kartikeya.sharma@bolt.eu","Kartikeya Sharma","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1939|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1939|smart-link] \nHi, similar ticket with more description.","2026-01-29T13:03:27.761Z"],["3849632","PFI-840204","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","hey,\n\nadded 25% commission rate BFC.","2026-01-29T13:03:30.941Z"],["3849634","WFM-10209","WFM","marcin.porowski@bolt.eu","Marcin Porowski","Hello, We don't know what is causing the issue. We will investigate this. For now added you queues again so tab should work","2026-01-29T13:03:46.489Z"],["3849635","MM-922","MM","kartikeya.sharma@bolt.eu","Kartikeya Sharma","Ticket with more description [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1990|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1990|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T13:04:10.867Z"],["3849637","WFM-10198","WFM","rodolfo.silva@bolt.eu","Rodolfo Bazante da Silva","Request raised here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601882|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601882]\ngabriela.rios already has the CS - Business role\nProfiles: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/503054?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/503054?tab=settings]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/563032?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/563032?tab=settings]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/502888?tab=settings|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/beehive/agents/edit/502888?tab=settings]","2026-01-29T13:04:37.440Z"],["3849638","PFI-813653","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment matched to client https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/73374961 ","2026-01-29T13:05:10.063Z"],["3849639","LSS-61346","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:705c56b5-c931-428e-8282-8c20af89d9c2] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^Fleet Agreement_Atributo Venusiano Lda (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T13:05:37.996Z"],["3849643","LSS-61364","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:602d7a68-8a81-4bea-98bf-acb7026b1a56] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt Werbevereinbarung_ Frankfurt Fleet Marziyeh Mortazavi (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T13:06:50.235Z"],["3849645","LSS-62065","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","Hi [~accountid:614c2821a6f69e006d6166a0] , I have removed highlighted clauses. Final version here: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qKUomw5KgNenlwNAZ_jaxeiFZX4orRhxjP9qoXq1HYU/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qKUomw5KgNenlwNAZ_jaxeiFZX4orRhxjP9qoXq1HYU/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] .\nPlease share name and e-mail address of the counter-party who will be signing the agreement, this info. is needed by our colleagues in Legal Ops.\nStatus changed to: “To be signed“.\nThanks,\n\nAlex","2026-01-29T13:06:53.470Z"],["3849646","FC-937","FC","katti.raudberg@bolt.eu","Katti Raudberg","Correction journal booked: \n\nJR-KZ001-26-000027","2026-01-29T13:07:03.232Z"],["3849647","INT-862","INT","vivekkumar.singh@bolt.eu","Vivek Kumar Singh","* Q1 Go live plan\n* Experiment:\n** 17th Feb: A/B test vs LPCT (no high pref + 5% min discount on premium category)\n*** Cities: Prague and Baku (@charlie.parsons to confirm post defining experiment design)\n*** 2 weeks runtime\n*** Handover to @suzanne.doering for the setup by 4th Feb\n** 24th Feb: A/B test vs LPCT (no high pref + 5% min discount on premium category)\n*** Cities: Paris and JoBurg\n*** 2 weeks runtime\n*** Handover to @suzanne.doering for the setup by 18th Feb\n* Roll out:\n** Prague and Baku by 3rd March\n** Berlin, Warsaw, Lisbon, Accra by 10th March\n** Paris and JoBurg by 17th March","2026-01-29T13:07:25.339Z"],["3849649","WDFT-3569","WDFT","kadri.keskkula@bolt.eu","Kadri Keskküla","[~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] Please do not forget [~accountid:712020:2261816b-1a2b-4b75-b1dc-d5fce431ad15]  She is responsible for BG and please remove [~accountid:712020:2b04881a-4ca8-40cb-9a35-a008b9853ec0] as her last day in Bolt is 06.02. Please add accountant role for HR001 to [~accountid:712020:c6829626-18d0-4d73-9974-74d1569b4bdf] ","2026-01-29T13:07:31.036Z"],["3849650","PFI-839651","PFI","ketter.ots@bolt.eu","Ketter Ots","Hello [~accountid:619df382b43d5b006a0196e7],\n\nThanks for the response, however, this is not the approach we usually take. In the past, the Fraud Team has simply removed the Fraud rule for unpaid orders that prevent archiving or deleting the account.\n\nRefunding would clear the dept and locating the unpaid orders will be time-consuming, but we want the debt to remain after archiving or deleting the account.\n\nThank you,\nKetter","2026-01-29T13:07:44.799Z"],["3849651","EBIKE1-427","EBIKE1","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] Thanks, good find.\n\nI think the drawing is kind of hard to understand without a connection schematic. Maybe we should create a really simple schematic to send out together with the drawing?","2026-01-29T13:07:47.801Z"],["3849652","LSS-56629","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","*_1P vs 3P visibility improvements (_*[+*_Scope and Flow_*+|https://www.figma.com/design/7Td3UtYgdaPz9FLtF9HkHv/-Drive--Multi-Provider-Aggregations?node-id=5090-56676&p=f&t=FmtMH4z1CUOwS3gE-0]*_)._* _Finalised the roll out plan:_ [+_link_+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C09QX0ZG9T3/p1768923237769929] _with the expectation to launch the AB by the end of the week. Agreed with Operations to revisit the pin sorting logic for Lithuania, as the current logic deprioritises Bolt Vehicles._ \n\n* _The logic is currently based on price for a median order per vehicle model. We plan to migrate to average order value to account for long trips._","2026-01-29T13:08:05.819Z"],["3849653","LSS-61490","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:e1a196fa-6ec1-4aad-999f-4f4a3ba54f01] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^MTS 2 - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.docx (1) (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T13:08:09.147Z"],["3849655","PFI-818200","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T13:08:17.494Z"],["384