","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.013Z"],["3849966","L10N-30714","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.009Z"],["3849967","L10N-30715","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.043Z"],["3849968","L10N-30720","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.100Z"],["3849969","L10N-30718","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.106Z"],["3849970","L10N-30721","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.136Z"],["3849971","L10N-30722","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.162Z"],["3849972","L10N-30709","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.332Z"],["3849973","L10N-30716","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.405Z"],["3849974","L10N-30711","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.380Z"],["3849975","L10N-30710","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.531Z"],["3849976","L10N-30707","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.622Z"],["3849977","L10N-30708","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T13:53:18.935Z"],["3849978","LSS-62029","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] [~accountid:60c88e6e8f2cc1006909fcf6] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.\n\n[^2 priedas_Pasiulymo forma Policijos departamentas.adoc] ","2026-01-29T13:54:04.932Z"],["3849982","PFI-840174","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","sure, changed this too","2026-01-29T13:54:45.498Z"],["3849985","DELIVERY-1442","DELIVERY","abhinav.agrawal@bolt.eu","Abhinav Agrawal","26W5: growth analytics team does not have the time to pick up analysis in January (we had aligned with them that they will work on it). Analysis will come in February. Project is completed from our pov, but not marking as done until we have analysis and results.","2026-01-29T13:55:32.620Z"],["3849986","LSS-61766","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] \n\nplease find reviewed NDA [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hVPJbmatWKR6pDpo73WHIqIBJFCO71UP/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hVPJbmatWKR6pDpo73WHIqIBJFCO71UP/edit|smart-link] \n\nwe can’t agree to one clause about main entity *not being liable* for breaches of affiliates. \n\nIf all agreed please ask them  send the agreement to [+ahto.kink@bolt.eu+|mailto:ahto.kink@bolt.eu] and cc [+signing@bolt.eu+|mailto:signing@bolt.eu] (we will not be able to find the request without putting this email in cc)","2026-01-29T13:55:56.116Z"],["3849989","LSS-61798","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[^Memorandum of Incorporation (1).pdf] Hey, [~accountid:62567ec6a872710069210b83] ! Unfortunately I could not find the recent one( Maybe you may refer to the finance team?","2026-01-29T13:58:03.492Z"],["3849992","PFI-840321","PFI","victoria.akinfenwa@bolt-outsource.eu","Victoria Akinfenwa","!Screenshot_2026-01-25-07-25-11-1111111111.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T13:58:31.010Z"],["3849993","PFI-840225","PFI","rares.almas@bolt.eu","Rareș-Tudor Almaș","Hi [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946], thank you for answering so quickly ❤️\nThey have already tried with RO. Still didn’t work.\nYes please! [~accountid:712020:0b672045-ccee-47bd-a209-1bec8346b45c] pretty please give me a contact person who can access SPV.","2026-01-29T13:58:36.284Z"],["3849994","PFI-830015","PFI","viktorija.valinskaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktorija Valinskaitė","any update?\n\n","2026-01-29T13:58:36.305Z"],["3849996","PFI-839971","PFI","arfeef.abdulsata@bolt-outsource.eu","Arfeef Abdulsata","Hi [~accountid:712020:c32c8896-b371-425a-8240-9bcd70c1a45b],\nThank you for looking into this. Upon further review, I noticed that the user’s previous account (6586450) was deactivated just before the amount of 100 THB was transferred to it. Consequently, the user is unable to receive the funds to the new account through the two standard methods mentioned.\n\nWould it be possible to manually transfer this amount to their new account instead?","2026-01-29T13:58:46.795Z"],["3849998","LSS-61586","LSS","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","Can you assist here [~accountid:712020:aea92140-f49c-4c1f-91bd-1dd458c46c39] ?\n\n","2026-01-29T13:59:18.443Z"],["3849999","LSS-61439","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^[M&N Topspeed Delivery LTD] AGREEMENT ON MANDATORY PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT(Fleet Operator – Bolt).docx (1) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T13:59:34.800Z"],["3850000","PFI-839963","PFI","arfeef.abdulsata@bolt-outsource.eu","Arfeef Abdulsata","Hi [~accountid:712020:c32c8896-b371-425a-8240-9bcd70c1a45b],\nThank you for looking into this. Upon further review, I noticed that the user’s previous account (6586450) was deactivated just before the amount of 300 THB was transferred to it. Consequently, the user is unable to receive the funds to the new account through the two standard methods mentioned.\n\nWould it be possible to manually transfer this amount to their new account instead?","2026-01-29T13:59:55.339Z"],["3850003","LSS-61441","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^[Sirelvis Ltd] AGREEMENT ON MANDATORY PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT(Fleet Operator – Bolt).docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T14:00:25.711Z"],["3850004","CRC-2389","CRC","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","[~accountid:712020:01f9c570-25ce-4e6b-9f2b-7623ae57ce30] Any idea how long it takes usually for the team to review?","2026-01-29T14:00:26.185Z"],["3850005","PFI-840202","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","discussed in scope of the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/2004/PFI-840256|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/PFI/queues/custom/2004/PFI-840256|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:00:31.335Z"],["3850006","LSS-62231","LSS","nils.kacars@bolt.eu","Nils Kacars","Thank you, all looks in order! I have added missing info as well as reviewed and added my suggestions. \n\nPlease let me know if when we can send it to Mobire for their review prior to signing.\n\nCheers,","2026-01-29T14:00:40.500Z"],["3850007","LSS-62126","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","Hey [~accountid:712020:5ffceaff-b794-4708-9ea7-396579c12757] any possibility to get this as word or google doc?","2026-01-29T14:00:46.397Z"],["3850009","LSS-61447","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:60536b5060d39e006f7dae01] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^[N.S.NESAS IMPEX] AGREEMENT ON MANDATORY PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT(Fleet Operator – Bolt).docx (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T14:01:37.932Z"],["3850012","LSS-61942","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:5062d8c8-d77c-47a7-8500-37f92fc11d06] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany 2026 - Merih Özbayraktar (2) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T14:03:19.431Z"],["3850013","LSS-62102","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:922e48f4-d266-4712-8041-89b612243bf1], thank you for noting.\n\nBefore we amend the agreement, please clearly and firmly confirm the *scope of services you intend to use with AMAK, are interested in, or are considering.*\n\nWe want to clearly understand the context of the agreement and potential data processing activities that may be introduced in the market.","2026-01-29T14:03:23.304Z"],["3850014","FX-3760","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769695399595919]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3760] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T14:03:43.748Z"],["3850015","FX-3761","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769695408154979]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3761] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T14:03:52.862Z"],["3850016","LSS-62126","LSS","tudor.profir@bolt.eu","Tudor Profir","Hi [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] , as I mentioned in the ticket, they can’t provide a Google Docs / .doc version due to compliance issues supposedly.\n\nI’ve created a Google Docs version based on the PDF, but let’s make sure we keep it internal: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e9hmRE2LqAg0jVIcQAx565DC3V_MRD57PSDwT0C4ZxA/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e9hmRE2LqAg0jVIcQAx565DC3V_MRD57PSDwT0C4ZxA/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:03:56.438Z"],["3850019","FX-3760","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769695447764019]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3760 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T14:04:20.236Z"],["3850020","FX-3761","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769695452663399]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3761 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T14:04:23.446Z"],["3850022","PFI-838396","PFI","warisara.sopa@bolt-outsource.eu","Warisara Sopa","Is it possible to move from [client 7014987 (Hidden profile)|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7014987?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBangkok] to client [8486708 (active profile)|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8486708?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBangkok]?\n\n","2026-01-29T14:04:27.075Z"],["3850023","WFM-10191","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:63e39f9ca5d0c826306d26ed]!\r\n\r\nI have updated the access for Adewale Oyegbade.\r\n\r\nBut, could you please clarify do want me to update the access/rights for the agents mentioned on the screenshot?\r\n\r\nBy checking some names, I saw some of them already have the required rights and some of them seemed to be inactive agents at all.\r\n\r\nWaiting for you reply,\r\nArtur","2026-01-29T14:04:29.736Z"],["3850030","LSS-61496","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:fa93b5fc-de6e-4a2f-a162-f89ec96ec1a5] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^WPL 2025 Residential Licence Template (2).pdf] ","2026-01-29T14:05:37.652Z"],["3850031","LSS-60921","LSS","andy.effiong@bolt.eu","Andy Effiong","[^Bolt Operations NDA (Mutual) (1) (1).pdf]\n\nSigned and executed by both parties","2026-01-29T14:06:02.065Z"],["3850033","LSS-61494","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:9fd45c83-380e-410c-83d8-9f700c4718bd] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^[Accessible Fleet] Bolt - Fleet Partnership Agreement Taiwan - (CN trans)_FINAL.docx (4) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T14:06:31.727Z"],["3850034","RLONE-395","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","We have enabled rematching both for T2 and T3 so that drivers that are on the way or have had a drop-off at CPH Airport get prioritized.","2026-01-29T14:06:31.864Z"],["3850038","PFI-839971","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:06:59.981Z"],["3850039","WEB-5358","WEB","burak.ozdemir@bolt.eu","Burak Özdemir","Rejecting since we’re doing this for Web CMS and Website now.","2026-01-29T14:07:05.727Z"],["3850040","LSS-61085","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:edc5b324-043b-4263-83ea-09673acdfe71] please give access or copy it to Bolt Gdrive, thanks.","2026-01-29T14:07:06.131Z"],["3850041","CSXRD-356","CSXRD","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","[Impact analysis|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LSQVsZjofjn-AfVXJu-4u58nv4xzSyEhv6smZcaau4E/edit?usp=sharing]\n\n[Slack thread|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C037ZN703U0/p1769693339382239] with suggested action steps","2026-01-29T14:07:06.672Z"],["3850042","PFI-840243","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Changed the report generation for this fleet 🙂 ","2026-01-29T14:07:15.421Z"],["3850043","FRAUDOPS-831","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","*CASE 4: WEEKLY PAYOUT REJECTS*\n\nRejected weekly payouts go to manual reviews which brings additional work as well as delays to partner receiving their funds. Let’s check how many of the order funds were secure at the time of payout. \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 16.06.42.png|width=1001,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 16.06.42.png\"!\n\nSo, we stopped around 44 drivers' payouts that covered around 3.4K€ of secure orders. \n\n*This makes 1.1K€ secure funds being stopped monthly and 15 drivers less being affected.* ","2026-01-29T14:07:41.115Z"],["3850044","CSXRD-371","CSXRD","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","Playbook has been updated with the needed info","2026-01-29T14:07:46.841Z"],["3850045","LSS-62399","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ! May you kindly assist?","2026-01-29T14:07:54.214Z"],["3850047","PFI-839963","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:07:59.101Z"],["3850058","LSS-58451","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:c428e4fe-c7e8-428c-98b9-afce638acb45] ! Any updates here?","2026-01-29T14:09:19.874Z"],["3850066","CSXRD-405","CSXRD","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","Waiting for feedback from Ivan","2026-01-29T14:10:12.926Z"],["3850067","RDXENG-2948","RDXENG","nami.salimi@bolt.eu","Nami Salimi","[~accountid:61f1059be4a724006adb49f9] do you think we can close this ticket since we are already working on unified ETA?","2026-01-29T14:10:20.826Z"],["3850069","LSS-61615","LSS","alexandra.mitroi@bolt.eu","Alexandra-Mihaela Mitroi","hi [~accountid:712020:7cc5674c-6f47-4631-8bc3-483c4d0c5273] as all departments have performed their review, and you also performed yours, it is fine to share the reviewed documents with counter-party.\nLet us know how it went!\n\nThanks,\n\nAlex","2026-01-29T14:10:27.090Z"],["3850070","PFI-840327","PFI","matina.mat-adam@bolt-outsource.eu","Matina Mat-Adam","!Messenger_creation_203ECD95-9726-44BD-82D3-DE51135F2228.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T14:10:51.147Z"],["3850071","PFI-838396","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","We can only move the payment of 27 THB, but the client has more balance on the account.\nIf the whole balance needs to be moved, this should be raised to billing team.\n","2026-01-29T14:11:04.518Z"],["3850073","LSS-62216","LSS","victor.stratan@bolt.eu","Victor Stratan","[~accountid:712020:b1700666-82b2-4a86-82f7-550a84f716c8] yes, we are aware of it and we follow the procedure in place when there is a chance for it. However, this is bank KYC and Markus' actual proof of address should be provided. We had similar cases in the past and it worked fine. Could you please check it and help us with it?","2026-01-29T14:11:21.396Z"],["3850074","PRODSEC-719","PRODSEC","pavel.kargin@bolt.eu","Pavel Kargin","Done, should run next Monday. If something fails will reopen ","2026-01-29T14:11:32.010Z"],["3850077","LSS-59845","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348179|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348179|smart-link]  ","2026-01-29T14:11:44.303Z"],["3850078","PFI-838369","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:11:53.170Z"],["3850080","LSS-61689","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5dbc31f21dee710dad3f44ed] ! Yes, the contract has been sent","2026-01-29T14:12:30.884Z"],["3850082","DSR-2322","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","BH cases closed in [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/666565610] and [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/685089883]","2026-01-29T14:12:36.350Z"],["3850083","CCM-22329","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Khatira,\n\nI have reset Sevda’s test. Before the agent takes the next attempt, please make sure to revise with them where to find Data requests macros in Beehive. \n\nThank you! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-29T14:12:37.127Z"],["3850084","DRX-28345","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Please check regarding steps in the ticket","2026-01-29T14:12:39.138Z"],["3850085","C2-466","C2","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","h1. Shipment overview\n\nShipment consisted of 50pcs C2 batteries, 30 Techsum, 20 TWS. All batteries had HW version 11, which means that none of these batteries had water detection functionality.\n\nh2. Sent to service issue overview\n\nBatteries were reported:\n\n* 26pcs - LED indicator issue\n* 12 pcs - female connector issue\n* 4 pcs - hook missing\n* 7 pcs - upper plastic damaged\n* 1 pcs - {color:#ff5630}*error 4 / 2 LEDs*{color}\n\nh2. Error overview\n\nErrors were checked within time period 01.11.2025 - until the day that the battery was last collected. \n\n8 batteries had reported voltage errors:\n*E512 - BMS overvoltage*\nMCST003634002 - Full battery gave error once - {color:#36b37e}*OK*{color}\n*E513 - BMS undervoltage -* \nMCDT001510002 - One cell significantly lower than othersafter swap (4.1 2.6 4.1 4.1 4.1 4.1 4.1 4.1 4.1 4.1)  - {color:#36b37e}*OK*{color}\n*E524 - Vout mismatch (1..4 LEDs) -* {color:#ff5630}*These batteries shouldn’t have been shipped according to the SOP*{color}\nDSM2203110691 - {color:#ff5630}*NOK*{color}\nDSM2201140944 - {color:#ff5630}*NOK*{color}\n*E24596 - Supressed error undervoltage* \nMC9T003603002 - Empty battery, 0% SoC, Battery dropped to 0% from ~20% - {color:#36b37e}*OK*{color}\nDSM2112241326 - Empty battery, 0% SoC - {color:#36b37e}*OK*{color}\nMCGT002956001 - Empty battery, 0% SoC, Battery dropped to 0% from 22% -{color:#36b37e} {color}{color:#36b37e}*OK*{color}\n*E24602 - IoT detects voltage diff 0.2V*\nDSM2202240105 - Empty battery, 0% SoC - {color:#36b37e}*OK*{color}\n\nh2. Cell voltages overview\n\nCell voltage were checked within time period 03.12.2025 - until the day that the battery was last collected, in “Power OFF” state. \n\nThere were 3 batteries with suspiciously high cell voltage differences.\n\nMCST003634002 - delta 700 mV - Cell 1 constantly lower than others. 700mV at 11% SoC. Not considered dangerous, as there weren’t any other abnormalities.\nMCST002741001 - delta 400 mV - Normal, high delta at 0% SoC. Not considered dangerous.\nMCST003571002 - delta 400 mV - Normal, high delta at 0% SoC. Not considered dangerous.\n\nh1. Summary\n\nThe shipment contained *1 battery* (DSM2112221051) that was reported twice as {color:#ff5630}*error 4 / 2 LEDs*{color}*.*\n\nThere were also *2 batteries* (DSM2201140944, DSM2203110691) which had reported {color:#ff5630}*E524*{color} - these batteries should have not been shipped according to the SOP. ","2026-01-29T14:12:49.882Z"],["3850088","LSS-61085","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:edc5b324-043b-4263-83ea-09673acdfe71] thanks, the comment needs your commercial confirmation - please check my comment and confirm.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bCVLbZWrPOYFQKDLeplt8v9cNEFgofcVqiyx7whUSU4/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bCVLbZWrPOYFQKDLeplt8v9cNEFgofcVqiyx7whUSU4/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:13:19.107Z"],["3850089","PFI-839813","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! \n\n# If you need to review supply netting of change supply netting on/off, kindly create a ticket to config changes queue. \n# For which fleets did you expect the invoices and why? ","2026-01-29T14:13:33.177Z"],["3850090","LSS-56382","LSS","vitaliia.hrabova@bolt.eu","Vitaliia Hrabova","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Hey! Partner accepted the last version of the document. Thanks a lot for help ☺️ ","2026-01-29T14:13:41.497Z"],["3850093","PFI-826346","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:14:31.588Z"],["3850097","DRAG101-381","DRAG101","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371] Initial timeline was[ this|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HtMXbmZx_WpIxe34THiDGx5K2KTZ3O6y/edit?gid=1276067954#gid=1276067954] but this is out of date.\n\nThe latest info I have is: _Currently, the drop detection function can work, and debugging the drop height measurement and collision direction judgment is in progress._\n\nI will ask TWS to provide an update timeline and some documentation about current situation.","2026-01-29T14:14:51.971Z"],["3850099","PFI-839651","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hey [~accountid:615c8598a7071000699c8c93] [~accountid:60cdaa478f2cc1006978c4a0] \n\nCould you please check if account can be archived now? \n\nNiki","2026-01-29T14:15:11.821Z"],["3850100","LSS-56382","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:639b104bf134138b5a515e5b] thanks! Please make sure to fill in the date of conclusion, verify the commercial details and the list of stores and then you can proceed to signing.","2026-01-29T14:15:17.612Z"],["3850102","PFI-814308","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:15:22.820Z"],["3850103","LSS-61689","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348180|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348180|smart-link]  ","2026-01-29T14:15:29.699Z"],["3850106","PFI-838349","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:16:11.157Z"],["3850109","LSS-61623","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","I am confirming that the request has been sent","2026-01-29T14:16:27.470Z"],["3850110","FRAUDOPS-831","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","Totals:\n\nCase 1: EC PASS -- *6.5K€* / 100 drivers\n\nCase 2: EC REJECT -- *25.1K*€ / 472 drivers\n\nCase 3: RP PASS -- *4.6K*€ / 148 drivers\n\nCase 4: RP REJECT -- *1.1K€* /  15 drivers\n\n----\n\nHence, we have the opportunity to catch *11.1K€* more problematic orders from *248 drivers* monthly.\n\nAnd cause less friction on related orders worth around *26.2K€* that correlate to *487 drivers* monthly.\n\n*Total, 37.3K€ monthly / 735 drivers affected.* ","2026-01-29T14:16:30.104Z"],["3850111","CCM-22328","CCM","miroslava.solarova@bolt.eu","Miroslava Solárová","Hello Khatira, \n\nI have reset Shahnaz test progress. Before the agent takes the next attempt, please make sure to revise the steps to take if the rider reports that their unsubscribe link doesn't work. \n\nThank you! \n\nMirka 🙂 ","2026-01-29T14:16:48.293Z"],["3850113","FX-3653","FX","pavel.halavan@bolt.eu","Pavel Halavan","Turns out comparison of  a real time  hex based demand to historical demand for the whole city is not useful on the map but will be useful as a total city demand indicator. This will be developed further with the design changes. For now I park all the changes that already done until we get back to the city demand indicator.","2026-01-29T14:16:52.502Z"],["3850115","PFI-744338","PFI","dominika.kusz@bolt-outsource.eu","Dominika Kusz","Can you add the details to the invoice?","2026-01-29T14:17:42.929Z"],["3850116","PFI-744338","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-29T14:17:47.200Z"],["3850117","LSS-58339","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17] - in reaction to your comment in the draft answer document (“_Ernesto Paulausko vardas ir pavardė matomi ant dokumento, kurį pateikė Zavki (auto reg. dokumentas)_“), I need some more context around the document upload. Could you please confirm the following:\n\n# Document type: What exact document was uploaded by Zavki? (e.g. vehicle registration certificate, insurance document, other)\n# Upload flow: Was this document uploaded directly by Zavki via his RH account, *or* via the fleet (Loginesa) interface?\n# Purpose and use: How was the document used operationally?\n#* purely for a visual/manual check of vehicle eligibility, *or*\n#* was any data extracted, parsed, or validated automatically?\n# Data handling scope: Was Ernesto Paulausko’s name merely visible on the document as uploaded, *or* indexed, searchable, or otherwise stored as a separate data field?\n# Linkage: Was Ernesto Paulausko’s name or data linked to any Bolt account, profile, or internal record other than the document attachment itself?\n\nThis clarification is needed so I can ensure that our external response accurately reflects the scope and purpose of any personal data processing linked to the vehicle documentation. As I don’t speak Lithuanian, I would be grateful if you could provide your answers in English 🙏 ","2026-01-29T14:18:05.007Z"],["3850118","LSS-59330","LSS","sevil.hasanli@bolt.eu","Sevil Hasanli","[~accountid:62b1c880566f3e7b0a8f2eb7] Dear Anna, review is completed. Link:[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t4vghWL3IjLIWKSgciLdxuyyp7lm56_3/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1t4vghWL3IjLIWKSgciLdxuyyp7lm56_3/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:18:08.689Z"],["3850119","PFI-838334","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to client 7703500 and has been paid to them [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/235035138|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/235035138]. \nWe would advise against moving the funds in that case as it would cause debt.\n","2026-01-29T14:18:10.103Z"],["3850120","PRF-1907","PRF","marianne.kaarma@bolt.eu","Marianne Kaarma","[~accountid:5c2f512d36647b5b91017d0c] can we use these in Europe only or also in NZ or African countries?","2026-01-29T14:18:18.465Z"],["3850121","WD-22580","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hello! last two are also added to sandbox.  Have you checked previously added ? does they work correctly? ","2026-01-29T14:18:30.159Z"],["3850127","PFI-840204","PFI","mikolaj.wilk@bolt.eu","Mikołaj Wilk","Could you double check if there is company BFC? I see only driver one \n\n!image-20260129-141844.png|width=1255,height=771,alt=\"image-20260129-141844.png\"!\n\n","2026-01-29T14:18:52.136Z"],["3850128","MKP-9953","MKP","vikas.sekhri@bolt.eu","Vikas Attul Sekhri","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1erl-_NaL68T86wFhaqizYloTTiOxQdU0XHEU-LfVQLM/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1erl-_NaL68T86wFhaqizYloTTiOxQdU0XHEU-LfVQLM/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-29T14:18:55.859Z"],["3850129","FRAUDOPS-684","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher"," 🛑 This cases has deprecated itself as bolt_credit is being closed down as a method 🛑 ","2026-01-29T14:19:04.978Z"],["3850131","WD-22580","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Kindly ask to test by EOD Friday , on Saturday all changes to sanbox will be deleted. ","2026-01-29T14:19:13.583Z"],["3850132","PFI-824402","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:19:13.778Z"],["3850133","LSS-61623","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348184|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348184|smart-link]  ","2026-01-29T14:19:17.270Z"],["3850135","PFI-839761","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! It’s marked as client did not pay, hence no invoice. If the client disputes that, please reach out to our fraud team. Thanks! ","2026-01-29T14:20:07.888Z"],["3850137","PFI-839761","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-29T14:20:20.657Z"],["3850139","PFI-839297","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","Hello,  \n\n  \n\nPlease provide feedback   \n\n   \n\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *პატივისცემით*{color}* \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *Sincerely*{color}* \n{color:#0093D3}{color}\n----\n{color:#0093D3}{color}  \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *მზიკო დანელია*{color}**{color:#0093D3} */*{color}*  *{color:#0093D3} *Mziko Danelia*{color}* \n\n{color:#1F497D}ბარათების{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}მენეჯერი{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color} {color:#1F497D}Card Manager{color} \n\n{color:#1F497D}მომხმარებელთა{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}მხარდაჭერის{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}განყოფილება{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color} {color:#1F497D}Customer Support Department{color}{color:#595959}{color}{color:#2F5496}{color} \n\n  \n\n  \n\n *{color:#333399} *Tel:*{color}* {color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 27 27 37 (*4){color} \n\n *{color:#333399} *Fax:*{color}* {color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 77 27 74{color} \n\n[{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}|https://urldefense.com/v3/__http:/www.tbcbank.ge/__;!\\!P1qVsL2A!JjZp3RvKmPyFPpMib2WSUCp6PkWNjFswW63tExjK8iJPWNwDfHIlD8kZT1rjOdXXWJZHtiNk2GquYRKhfMLnN1yk4Lcm6hI$] \n\n  \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T14:20:28.931Z"],["3850141","LSS-62317","LSS","helen.erg@bolt.eu","Helen Erg","Hei, any chance to get the POA signed as shipment is basically in port?","2026-01-29T14:20:57.969Z"],["3850142","DRX-25955","DRX","nurbol.chorobaev@bolt.eu","Nurbol Chorobaev","Release smoke suite is enough to check for regressions","2026-01-29T14:20:58.231Z"],["3850144","PFI-833565","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to client 1661064 and were paid out here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233071936|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233071936]\nWe would advise against moving the funds in that case.","2026-01-29T14:21:06.025Z"],["3850145","LSS-62282","LSS","raivis.busmanis@bolt.eu","Raivis Bušmanis","I have also reviewed the document and we can proceed on Reed’s framework provided they agree a short set of amendments to ensure commercial and compliance alignment. The simplest way to capture this is to include the below additions in the “Special Conditions” box. \n\n*Key amendments requested:*\n\n# *Expenses  (clause 7 (2))* – only if pre-approved in writing.\n# *Payment (clause 8)* – 30 day payment term instead of 14\n# *Liability/indemnities (clause 15)* – Reed remains responsible as employer (wages, statutory deductions, right-to-work/work permits) and indemnifies Bolt for breaches; introduce a sensible liability cap with standard carve-outs.\n# *Right to dispute timesheet (clause 21 and clause 9) -* ability to withhold disputed amounts; no interest on disputed invoices while resolved in good faith; timesheets are evidence but not “conclusive”; need to introduce a dispute window and correction process.\n# *Engaging other party’s personel (clause 26)* - make it mutual\n# *Insurance (clause 20.)* – please clarify Bolt’s insurance obligation. What is considered as adequate insurance?\n# *Confidentiality (clause 27)* – Each party shall keep the other party’s Confidential Information strictly confidential, use it only for performance of the assignment, disclose it only to those who need to know and are bound by equivalent confidentiality obligations, and keep it secure using appropriate technical and organisational measures. On request or at end of assignment, the receiving party shall return or securely destroy Confidential Information (including copies) and certify destruction if requested.\n# *Bolt policies / compliance* – Reed and the Temporary to comply with applicable laws and Bolt workplace / security policies as communicated.\n\nPlease share this with the counterparty for their review.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-29T14:21:10.420Z"],["3850146","RISK2-3039","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","* *Risk Management:*\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"f0d0e7fa-1581-4a27-910b-39a348ce7db3\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Advanced to the Implementation and Design phase with LogicGate, the new GRC Platform - \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Completed the selection of the new GRC tool - LogicGate and progressed to the mid-point of the LogicGate design phase, focusing on replacing manual overhead with a scalable, automated architecture. Key delivery efforts include automating access via Okta/SCIM, and architecting application designs for logging and tracking Enterprise and Operational risks, KRIs, KRI Measurements, Controls and Assets. This implementation serves as the primary bridge to centralising Bolt’s risk & compliance mapping and enhancing data traceability across the group, aiming to support risk-aware decision making and expansion.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Carry-Over\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Budget\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"64a5559c-b116-4e1d-8581-3e567ac14e0c\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Enterprise Risk Reporting\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Set up a structured quarterly reporting format for Risk Owners to provide updates on Bolt’s top seven Enterprise risks. While initially a manual process to ensure data quality, this framework is designed for a seamless transition to automated tracking within LogicGate.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Carry-Over\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Budget\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"aeedf188-4245-4cee-97a6-f2ef43d2b9b7\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Re-established Quarterly GRC Committee and Governance Landing Page\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Restored the quarterly \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Governance, Risk, and Compliance Committee\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/6822035693/Governance+Risk+and+Compliance+Committee\"}},{\"type\":\"underline\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" as the central mechanism for overseeing Bolt’s risk management and regulatory obligations. A dedicated landing page supports defining the Committee’s role in aligning cross-functional efforts and strengthening controls to support ethical business growth.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Delivered\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Budget\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"4ee9ebb7-ac5b-4ebe-8e4b-4ce2fdc4a46a\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Launched and Operationalised Product Prioritisation Procedure\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Developed an end-to-end workflow for Rides Compliance requests, integrating Legal/Public Policy validation with a robust Risk Scoring mechanism to ensure all regulatory changes within Bolt apps are backed by standardised decision-making. \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The procedure\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/6264225949/Product+Prioritisation+Procedure+for+Rides+Compliance+Regulatory+Requests\"}},{\"type\":\"underline\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" formalises a monthly review process involving senior leadership for incoming product changes (specifically driven by regulatory changes/new laws) and a centralised \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Jira Board \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"link\",\"attrs\":{\"href\":\"https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/COMPLIANCE/boards/8091\"}},{\"type\":\"underline\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"for tracking such changes and decisions made.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Delivered\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Budget\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"79a53d90-676e-402b-837c-faec58b0f6cd\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Zycus iRisk Module and Merlin AI Risk Radar Review & Testing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Supported the Procurement team to evaluate Zycus’s Merlin AI Risk Radar and iRisk module capabilities. Supported streamlining the end to end flow from initial intake to risk assessment, and executed User Acceptance Testing (UAT).\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Delivered\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Budget\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n* *Compliance Management:*\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"2fa8563f-c559-46a0-b63b-039aef7421d8\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Standardised Company-Wide Policy Review Process\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Established a formalised review cycle via the GRC Committee to ensure all internal policies are aligned cross-functionally. This ensures that policy updates are no longer siloed but are vetted by key stakeholders to maintain consistency with Bolt’s strategic values.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": \"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Delivered\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Budget\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-29T14:21:12.586Z"],["3850147","FRAUDOPS-831","FRAUDOPS","lise.vaher@bolt.eu","Lise Vaher","RP [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3163049496061636?o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3163049496061636?o=3598988355446810]\n\nEC [https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/111999336508892?o=3598988355446810|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/111999336508892?o=3598988355446810]","2026-01-29T14:21:17.545Z"],["3850149","LSS-62344","LSS","helen.erg@bolt.eu","Helen Erg","Hei, shipment will touchdown in Estonia tomorrow - without POA we can’t import, can we sign it tomorrow latest?","2026-01-29T14:21:21.438Z"],["3850150","WFM-10179","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601887|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601887]","2026-01-29T14:21:24.864Z"],["3850151","CRC-2389","CRC","stanislavs.kulss@bolt.eu","Staņislavs Kuļšs","[~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a], all questions to Commerce team, if there is any update, they will let us know","2026-01-29T14:21:36.224Z"],["3850152","PFI-840016","PFI","kanyanat.singkum@bolt-outsource.eu","Kanyanat Singkum","Understood, please proceed with moving this payment from client 4373430 to 8525655. Thank you for your assistance in this matter.","2026-01-29T14:21:37.959Z"],["3850154","DSR-3919","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] – reassigning to you.\n\nDD: {{2026-02-20}}\n\n\n\nIn ticket details on the right, Sigrid left a G-Drive file with personal data prepared & response letter. She also investigated the reason for suspension (faces don’t match). Driver is asking for a copy of data that led to block. \n\n\n\nI took a quick look and it seems like there are two different persons' documents and selfies linked to the account. Our standard approach is that under GDPR, Users are entitled to copy of their personal data. If there are reasons to believe that the data belongs to third party, we shouldn’t provide it. If we’re unclear on which one of the two persons is the data subject, we may consider refusing to provide all verification data.\n\n\n\nHere’s a previous example response for wording inspo (here we blurred parts of the User’s ID that were tampered – thereby not personal data of the data subject who requested the copy): [https://docs.google.com/document/d/199dzIySSq8Sz-dRKh1bry-OLHvbi3A4qp0cy1CEwKM0/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/199dzIySSq8Sz-dRKh1bry-OLHvbi3A4qp0cy1CEwKM0/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  you can exchange GDPR for “Applicable Data Protection Laws”\n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-29T14:21:46.612Z"],["3850156","LSS-60756","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348186|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348186|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:21:47.614Z"],["3850158","DRX-25955","DRX","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nPlease, check custom pricing confirmation and when going online and overall if it's working as expected","2026-01-29T14:22:14.290Z"],["3850160","AIOT-526","AIOT","tarmo.kuuse@bolt.eu","Tarmo Kuuse","Full restart duration from command {{reboot}} to login prompt\n\n* before (v1.9.1): ~13s, \n* after (v.1.10.0-3): ~13s (maybe few 100-s of ms more)\n\nThis assumes a clean file system. If the file system needs fixing, it will take much more time.","2026-01-29T14:22:33.359Z"],["3850163","PRF-1906","PRF","marianne.kaarma@bolt.eu","Marianne Kaarma","Duplicate","2026-01-29T14:22:43.421Z"],["3850170","PFI-838128","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Sender name matches with the client name. \nThis is not a case of client making a typo in account details, but instead client using their other account details instead.\nPayment is linked to client 7638817 and the funds are covering their debt partially. \nWe would advise against moving the funds in that case and instead creating a final payment request to send them the rest of the amount and close it. ","2026-01-29T14:23:29.021Z"],["3850175","RISK2-3025","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","* *Risk and Compliance Management:*\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"af82aee3-b36b-4bef-9b4a-9fee1219bf74\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Finalise Implementation and Design Phase with LogicGate\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Complete the application design for logging and tracking Enterprise and Operational risks, KRIs, KRI Measurements, Controls, Assets, the Secure Controls Framework (SCF), and Control Self Assessments (CSA). Simultaneously, initiate and conclude the design and implementation phase for Policy and Issues Management to ensure a holistic GRC environment.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": Delivered\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Carry-Over/On-Hold/Off-Track \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Baseline\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside Counsel Budge\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"t: €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"e5b8fd22-23b9-4c67-8989-f97aba5d640f\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"LogicGate Roll out and Launch Planning\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Establish a launch plan for the LogicGate Risk, Compliance, Policy and Issues Management applications, which includes structured communications to risk working groups, platform demonstrations, the execution of the User Acceptance Testing (UAT) cycle and providing support to business users as they are onboarded to LogicGate.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": Delivered\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Carry-Over/On-Hold/Off-Track \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Baseline\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside Counsel Budge\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"t: €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"34087b0e-fe76-47d0-9e57-56f30b213a59\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Transfer the Risk and Safety Data, and Disputes process into LogicGate\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\" - Initiate the transfer of current Cognito Risk & Safety processes, including the Disputes process into LogicGate. This integration aims to eliminate data silos and automate the correlation between safety data and broader enterprise risk profiles.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": Delivered\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Carry-Over/On-Hold/Off-Track \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Baseline\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside Counsel Budge\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"t: €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n* *Risk Management:*\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"ec484a1a-b2a4-4cdb-b1de-ede2294c5c53\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Update Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) Framework \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- Revise the existing ERM framework to align directly with our new LogicGate workflows to ensure that the methodology fully captures the platform’s automated capabilities and reporting structures.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": Delivered\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Carry-Over/On-Hold/Off-Track \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Baseline\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside Counsel Budge\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"t: €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"b4476083-6fda-470e-a047-b54233774ccc\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Automate Enterprise Risk Tracking and Consolidation \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- Transfer of the top company Enterprise risks from manual tracking into LogicGate to automate the consolidation of quarterly updates, and integrate every enterprise risk identified by the Internal Audit team into the platform, creating a single, automated source of truth for Bolt’s strategic risk profile.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": Delivered\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Carry-Over/On-Hold/Off-Track \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Baseline\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside Counsel Budge\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"t: €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"c82fe00c-1672-4fff-a669-0f55fd0b7e0c\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Drive Alignment through Strategic Risk Monitoring \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- Monitoring all LogicGate inputs from business users regarding top Enterprise Risks to ensure data integrity and consistent framework application. This involves providing active oversight of risk treatment decisions for Operational Risks, specifically the choice to accept, transfer, avoid, or reduce risks to guarantee they remain in alignment with Bolt’s overarching risk framework.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": Delivered\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Carry-Over/On-Hold/Off-Track \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Baseline\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside Counsel Budge\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"t: €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}\n\n* *Compliance Management:*\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"center\",\"localId\":\"4a1cd5ed-6c30-4ef8-9c41-ee532f55d063\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":4},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Transfer Policies from Risk and Compliance Management System (RCMS) to LogicGate \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- Begin the transfer of all existing company policies into the LogicGate platform to centralise documentation. This action will transform our policy management into a unified, searchable, and auditable repository.\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Status\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": Delivered\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/Carry-Over/On-Hold/Off-Track \",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Baseline\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": €0k\"}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Outside Counsel Budge\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"t: €0k\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resourcing\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\": X FTE\"}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-29T14:24:10.150Z"],["3850180","PFI-830822","PFI","mariam.maghalashvili@bolt.eu","Mariam Maghalashvili","Hello, thank you for the clarification. However, I am still confused. \n\nYou mentioned that if a fleet is not VAT-liable, the ‘Liable to VAT' box should be unchecked—which it currently is on the fleet’s profile. If we aren't supposed to be charged VAT, why is it still being deducted from the commission invoices from Bolt to the fleet?","2026-01-29T14:24:39.130Z"],["3850181","BDB-1595","BDB","aliis.topssalulaid@bolt.eu","Aliis Tops-Salulaid","[~accountid:60ab71565dc18500701cae80] Check the designs here: [https://www.figma.com/design/t2CC4p7oozZ48RcWpGr2LW/Performance?node-id=22463-1362&t=g670gteq1WLazf4d-1|https://www.figma.com/design/t2CC4p7oozZ48RcWpGr2LW/Performance?node-id=22463-1362&t=g670gteq1WLazf4d-1|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:24:52.822Z"],["3850182","TAXP-934","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","Documents saved in the file [Transfer Pricing|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1prxWHPkkvDeOWwcZ3noEE7Y_dPFztl9J?usp=drive_link]. These are documents with latest figures as of 29th January 2026. Please note that at the current time the YE review fo Bolt Operations OÜ is still open and the transactions may be subject to change.","2026-01-29T14:25:02.547Z"],["3850183","PFI-835061","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment located and matched to client https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/77535788","2026-01-29T14:25:04.767Z"],["3850184","HWMISC-831","HWMISC","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","Made one cable for validation. After validation is successful, I’ll create 3 more and a cable drawing so it could be ordered from Higo - saves time on handiwork.","2026-01-29T14:25:25.867Z"],["3850186","PFI-825554","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:25:40.534Z"],["3850188","WFM-10179","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Hey [~accountid:6119ead1e05b7b006ad35c05] Request has been made, and is now pending approval. I will confirm once permission owners have responded. ","2026-01-29T14:26:07.386Z"],["3850192","PFI-838428","PFI","gabriel.zarza@bolt-outsource.eu","Gabriel Duarte Zarza","Thank you Afiba!","2026-01-29T14:27:14.439Z"],["3850195","BP-13309","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:ab58e2f4-f31f-4230-9a41-30c28c8bd545] Thanks! I checked, my observation:\n- city and postal code is not pre-filled even though it says town correctly in the suggestion.\n- error message at NIP says only Required, but it should be Must be 10 digits\nAll the rest is well done","2026-01-29T14:27:48.023Z"],["3850196","PFI-839304","PFI","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","Bank has released the payout now","2026-01-29T14:28:07.530Z"],["3850197","WD-22296","WD","anna.erin@bolt.eu","Anna Erin","Hi [~accountid:712020:0d3126a8-2815-43c2-bdb3-c600f5679aaf] Proposal for domestic daily allowances looks fine for me. Please proceed with the set-up.","2026-01-29T14:28:08.518Z"],["3850198","WD-22727","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:0d3126a8-2815-43c2-bdb3-c600f5679aaf] ! you can not select manual, because invoices has Kyriba as payment type. ","2026-01-29T14:28:08.727Z"],["3850199","PCI-51","PCI","kristjan.hiis@bolt.eu","Kristjan Hiis","Nothing has changed from the last year, all of the implementation has stayed the same.","2026-01-29T14:28:13.812Z"],["3850203","DSR-3987","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] – reassigning to you.\n\nPlease review the response prepared by Johannes. They are in G-Drive folder linked to the case details on the right. \n\n\n\nReview the data prepared by Johannes on cancelled orders. Keep in mind that We’re always balancing between providing Driver the data they requested but minimizing the possibility of Rider identification. See if there are any columns that need to be redacted.\n\n\n\nAs always, me and Estelle are ready to support if you’d like to discuss the approach. Shout when needed 💚 \n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-29T14:28:36.860Z"],["3850204","CSDA-309","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hey, Jelena and Ana! I am going to share more updates on this topic with you tomorrow as we will know more about the timelines for the agent performance data in new explores. Based on that we can make the decision on how and when to proceed. Will keep you posted! ","2026-01-29T14:28:39.183Z"],["3850205","WEB-9805","WEB","krister.looga@bolt.eu","Krister Looga","Relevant slack thread: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1769695289738699?thread_ts=1766145332.641209&cid=C064CEL9FKP|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C064CEL9FKP/p1769695289738699?thread_ts=1766145332.641209&cid=C064CEL9FKP|smart-link] \n\nIn short we need to extend the comment field to include the following values if they exist:\n\n\n{noformat}illegalContentCategory?: IllegalContentCategory;\nillegalContentSubCategory?: IllegalContentSubCategory;\nillegalContentUrl?: tString;\nrequestType: RequestType;{noformat}\n\n\nAlso stakeholder as requested to change the field ordering in the comment as such:\n\n\n{quote}f the order reflects on the support case in the same way as displayed above, then we can maybe move request_type to the top and then have the sub-categories?{quote}","2026-01-29T14:28:57.442Z"],["3850208","PFI-840336","PFI","monica.acevedo@bolt.eu","Mónica Acevedo","[^Bolt Enero 2026.pdf]","2026-01-29T14:29:55.116Z"],["3850209","BP-13309","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","the Address filled field is blue 🧐 not grey as others. Is it coz it works as search?\n\n\n!1000011380.png|width=240,alt=\"1000011380.png\"!","2026-01-29T14:30:25.319Z"],["3850210","SREDESK-7477","SREDESK","vadim.kravchenko@bolt.eu","Vadim Kravchenko","I need access to internal-tooling 930271537539 to be able to deploy some internal tools","2026-01-29T14:30:26.360Z"],["3850211","DSR-4053","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Block reason in profile Safety:- HB for fraud. DM sent to *Gabriele Della Mea*\nFleet driver- billing details removed \nAcceptance rate / average rating added :done: \nBH call to be checked :loading: \n","2026-01-29T14:30:47.441Z"],["3850212","WFM-10047","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Thanks [~accountid:712020:a4f6dc7f-ea2b-4b6c-87be-3ca7829f155a] what exactly is the agent trying to edit, meaning which field? ","2026-01-29T14:30:51.534Z"],["3850214","LSS-62309","LSS","triin.soonkoster@bolt.eu","Triin Soon-Köster","Approved, will forward it to for translation.","2026-01-29T14:30:56.655Z"],["3850217","BRE-1158","BRE","arseni.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Arseni Anishchanka","I also checked how difficult it will be to rename subscription-invoicing to rental-pass-billing. It requires significant afford and not worse it. In admin service for subscription-invocing will follow previous naming.","2026-01-29T14:31:14.206Z"],["3850218","LSS-61438","LSS","laura.newton@bolt.eu","Laura Newton","Thanks [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf]. Myself and [~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94] will provide in 30 days notice to them in writing once move in date for new office in confirmed to see what costs to expect for collection.","2026-01-29T14:31:18.184Z"],["3850219","DSR-4027","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Hejsan [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] – another one! This one seems as Superman is not real cases. \n\n\n\nPlease review response prepared by Priit. Estelle will provide info about how we approach these cases on our bootcamp tomorrow.\n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-29T14:31:29.597Z"],["3850220","PFI-840225","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","[^RO1526-3946.zip]\n[^RO1525-47592.zip]\n[^RO1525-43010.zip]\n[^RO1525-38562.zip]\n\nShould be all 4 invoices 2 XMLs per invoice since I’m not sure which one will work for them. Let me know which one they will use please (unless they are too pissed off)","2026-01-29T14:31:36.427Z"],["3850221","LSS-61217","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:3628e8e4-2c88-4d47-8c51-14aa1e98735c] ! Maybe [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117] can help there?\n\nSorry I was searching a lot today, but could not find","2026-01-29T14:31:37.435Z"],["3850222","PAW-15266","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @daysleeperx\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162512\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-29 14:32:06 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-29T14:32:06.878Z"],["3850223","WFM-10208","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","Yes, all work now - thank you!","2026-01-29T14:32:08.926Z"],["3850224","BP-13309","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","Also my app and browser is set to dark theme.  Do we not support it atm? Or there’s something off for me?","2026-01-29T14:32:11.785Z"],["3850225","LSS-61331","LSS","alijan.dias@bolt.eu","Alijan Keval","Rejected means it was rejected by the fleet? [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-29T14:32:14.924Z"],["3850228","PFI-840016","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:32:40.559Z"],["3850232","LSS-62145","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*Stickers - sharing overview of what was discussed with Chirag:*\n{panel}\n\n*Gabrielė Kaveckytė* \n\nHey! I think option 2 is better, it has more info. We can advise what text to add to the stickerOption 1 is too minimal - and since our goal is compliance and not prettyness of the sticker I’d say let’s go with 2\n\n*Chirag Yadav*  \n\nOkay for option 2, can you share a copy / text. I am working with Design team to prep these.\n\nAnd English is fine? Or does it need to be in Estonian also?\n\n*Gabrielė Kaveckytė*  \n\n\nHey and apologies for the delay\n\nI think the below text is defensible with AKI + consistent with external counsel's advice, and [hopefully\n\n] realistic for a sticker._Front-facing headline (large, immediately visible)_\n*RECORDING IN PROGRESS*\n_Core information (short, readable)_\n*This vehicle records video data for the development and testing of autonomous driving systems.*\nController identification\n*Data controller:* Bolt Technology OÜ\nAccess to full information\n*Scan the QR code or visit:*\n [bolt.eu/privacy-data-collection|http://bolt.eu/privacy-data-collection]\n\nOptional but advisable additions (if space allows)\n\n* *No audio is recorded*\n* *Faces and licence plates are anonymised*\n\n_These are not strictly required on the sticker, but they are helpful for public trust and reduce complaint risk without overloading the notice._\n\nEnglish is acceptable, especially given the technical nature of the project and Bolt’s existing practice.\n\n\nThat said, *Estonian is strongly advisable* for a public-space project in Tallinn and will be viewed positively by AKI.\nBest practice would be:\n\n* bilingual sticker (ET / EN), or\n* Estonian on the sticker, English on the linked privacy page (or both online).\n\n!image-20260129-143232.png|width=720,alt=\"image-20260129-143232.png\"!\n\nFYI [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] . Once design/copy is ready for our review, it’ll be added to the [Project Document|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LGc3adiyaTnP_tZUAuIwTJ9756ds1SkNRNfeVwFFqW0/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.bd2bmso0s2jd].","2026-01-29T14:33:20.570Z"],["3850234","WFM-10198","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Safety role [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601888|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601888]","2026-01-29T14:33:54.775Z"],["3850237","EBIKE1-366","EBIKE1","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","I have created 2 tasks which are action items from this task and I will mark this task as done","2026-01-29T14:34:08.764Z"],["3850239","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","Hi!\nThanks to the Exploratory View in Queues, we’ve identified an important gap around Business Company cases and prioritization.\nWe’ve observed that a significant number of Business Company cases do not have any priority value assigned. For this user persona, the expected FRT is 30 minutes, and therefore system-level prioritization is critical to consistently meet our speed targets. At the moment, this prioritization is not applied consistently, which puts the FRT at risk.\nWe’ve already updated the Issue Key SLOs to align with the expected FRT targets. However, we’re still concerned about Business Company cases that have no Issue Key at all, as they currently don’t benefit from any prioritization logic despite having a strict speed expectation.\nHere are a few concrete examples we found:\nEmail source with no priority value and no issue key:\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/730409961|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/730409961]\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/659718820|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/659718820]\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/718895443|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/718895443]\n\n*Question:*\nIs there anything we can do on the system side to ensure Business Company cases are prioritized even when no Issue Key is present?","2026-01-29T14:34:15.901Z"],["3850240","BEE-3696","BEE",null,"Slack","[Stanislau Binko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:9687d9a4-446e-4c1f-9bf8-68017b3676b1] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1769673271062219?thread_ts=1769673271.062219&cid=C032D4ZGZR6|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C032D4ZGZR6/p1769673271062219?thread_ts=1769673271.062219&cid=C032D4ZGZR6|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-29T14:34:17.208Z"],["3850241","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","hi :wave: I think we should have SLO configuration for cases _without_ issue keys\n\nit is not exposed in admin - but otherwise I think it should work here / we can update\n\ncouple questions so far:\n1. would user_persona=Business Company be the only criteria needed here / it is the right one and sufficient? or it's more complicated? :sweat_smile: \n2. do we need only _first reply_ SLO updates, or anything about follow-up as well?\n(I'll be able to get back to this in 1-2 hours after couple internal meetings)","2026-01-29T14:34:17.555Z"],["3850242","BEE-3696","BEE","alina.mazurek@bolt.eu","Alina Mazurek","CC: [@laimdota.vilistere|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5d723b3830f82c0c36be5b56] [@jahanzeb.quraishy|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/62c5ae71580f2f55d77073a8]","2026-01-29T14:34:18.826Z"],["3850243","BEE-3696","BEE","alina.mazurek@bolt.eu","Alina Mazurek","One question on this solution, is there a way to add priority value to all Business Company cases instead of adding SLO for cases without issue keys? if not then:\n1. Business company would be the criteria \n2. To be aligned with the configuration done by Laimdota it should be 30/60 ","2026-01-29T14:34:19.485Z"],["3850244","BEE-3696","BEE","laimdota.vilistere@bolt.eu","Laimdota Vilistere","FYI: [@wellington.ngwenya|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5b7beabdb96a5b58cd3e06ef] what we discussed yesterday :point_up:","2026-01-29T14:34:20.498Z"],["3850246","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","{quote}One question on this solution, is there a way to add priority value to all Business Company cases instead of adding SLO for cases without issue keys?{quote}\n\nI think yes, with some side notes - let me explain a bit more:\n\nso {{priority}} is also controlled via similar configuration, but currently we don't have a way to specify it for _only_ cases without issue keys - if we specify it it would be there for _all_ user_persona=Business Company cases (both with and without issue keys) - which might actually be good (and I think that's what you mean in your message, if I get it right?)\n\nbut similar SLO configuration works differently - it would only be sort of a \"fallback\" for user_personal=Business Company cases in scenario when there are _no issue keys_ at all on the case\n\nit's also possible to set both if you prefer (I guess having more \"accurate\" SLO itself could be still valuable from perspective of e.g. metrics - i.e. checking whether that SLO was achieved or not - or maybe smth else)","2026-01-29T14:34:21.134Z"],["3850247","BEE-3696","BEE","alina.mazurek@bolt.eu","Alina Mazurek","Thanks! I think we would choose both solutions as we still might have cases that will be wrongly tagged with incorrect user persona and then changed to business company and then will priority value will be reset?","2026-01-29T14:34:21.726Z"],["3850248","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","{quote}wrongly tagged with incorrect user persona and then changed to business company and then will priority value will be reset?{quote}\n\nI think priority/SLO should be re-calculated in such scenario","2026-01-29T14:34:22.263Z"],["3850249","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","one question still - if you look at this page with current priorities description [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/4872667781/Support+Case+prioritisation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CD/pages/4872667781/Support+Case+prioritisation|smart-link] - between which of them would be the right place for this \"Business Company\" priority value? (as reminder higher value there means more urgent, and absent value is equivalent to 0 - e.g. {{0.1}} priority is higher than {{absent/default}} priority)","2026-01-29T14:34:23.165Z"],["3850250","BEE-3696","BEE","alina.mazurek@bolt.eu","Alina Mazurek","Okay thx, but still maybe for data consistency let's have also same SLO of 30/60 for untagged cases.\nWe are still seeking alignment between stakeholders on prioritization logic internally so I would just like to maintain the same prioritization as described here for the business tier is it possible? It is subject to change in the future but this is the desirable option for now\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ACKCADVT2/screenshot_2026-01-29_at_13.45.16.png|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ACKCADVT2/screenshot_2026-01-29_at_13.45.16.png|smart-link]","2026-01-29T14:34:23.777Z"],["3850251","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","{quote}Okay thx, but still maybe for data consistency let's have also same SLO of 30/60 for untagged cases.{quote}\n\nsure, we can do both :ok_hand:\n\n{quote}the same prioritization as described here for the business tier{quote}\n\nso there are 2 different values involving business tier - would you want this \"user_persona=Business Company\" one to be what exactly - 1.1 / 1.05 / smth else?","2026-01-29T14:34:24.311Z"],["3850252","BEE-3696","BEE","alina.mazurek@bolt.eu","Alina Mazurek","Exactly 1.05 so the lower one","2026-01-29T14:34:33.576Z"],["3850253","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","got it, thank you! I'll proceed with configuration soon then :loading:","2026-01-29T14:34:34.202Z"],["3850254","BEE-3696","BEE","laimdota.vilistere@bolt.eu","Laimdota Vilistere","[@stanislau.binko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:9687d9a4-446e-4c1f-9bf8-68017b3676b1] are you in sync with [@adam.kudybinski|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/5ff4436491bb2e0108d1548d]?\nI send to him prioritisation request and explained all the details where the User group Business Tier should be moved for prioritisation.","2026-01-29T14:34:35.136Z"],["3850255","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","oh thanks, I didn't know about that - I'll check with Adam, also do you by any chance have link to that request somehow?","2026-01-29T14:34:35.721Z"],["3850256","BEE-3696","BEE","stanislau.binko@bolt.eu","Stanislau Binko","also tier=\"business tier\" is not same as user_persona=\"business company\" I think, so I'm unsure how much these two requests would be connected - but definitely worth looking into it still","2026-01-29T14:34:36.345Z"],["3850258","TAXP-934","TAXP","stefan.chirila@bolt.eu","Stefan Chirila","Many thanks[~accountid:712020:df5d990b-4b48-4ec9-aa62-2cab18e07156] ! I’ve uploaded the documents into PwC’s portal and also added the note on the status.","2026-01-29T14:34:57.422Z"],["3850259","LSS-61827","LSS","kristiina.klemm@bolt.eu","Kristiina Klemm","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] please see attached updated OF. Unfortunately we do not have any feedback yet to the privacy part, but have highlighted the topic once more.\n\n[^Order Form with Bolt Technology OÜ (697b6b0f75) (version 1) (1).docx]\n\n","2026-01-29T14:34:59.007Z"],["3850260","PFI-840151","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\nIf you need a _report_, please refer to FleetX (DriverX). If your request concerns an _invoice_, follow these steps:\n\nPlease try:\n* Open the *Client page in Admin*: [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ → The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see to_execute → it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* If you see another _error_ → provide us a link.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the {{Partner Invoices}}) tab\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-29T14:35:02.631Z"],["3850262","LSS-58352","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Hi [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d]  Novitus have clarified on the open points. \n\nKindly review. ","2026-01-29T14:36:18.617Z"],["3850266","DRX-28289","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: nothing to test, just additional analytics added","2026-01-29T14:37:32.493Z"],["3850269","SREDESK-7476","SREDESK","kourosh.tafreshi@bolt.eu","Kourosh Tafreshi","Hello [~accountid:5f770d66021acf0076bbaef1] \n\nWe can create a new bucket {{platform-navigation-sdk}} in the {{taxify-client}} project  via IaC.\n\nJust to set expectations: the existing {{comms-chat-sdk}} bucket was created a long time ago outside of our current Terraform setup, so I can’t literally “copy that bucket,” but I can create similar bucket in a managed way and  a dedicated service account for your GitHub workflows.\n\nA couple of things I need you to confirm:\n\n# Public unauthenticated access for all binaries in this bucket is acceptable and approved from your side (anyone with the link can download) and this needs a coordination with [Cloud Security|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/team/a5e33eb9-f40f-42b3-a18a-46b8d1b94529?ref=jira$&src=issue] ([~accountid:712020:c94f2cba-c25e-4b00-8ef4-2cad9045ee22] [~accountid:60c8cb62b2156100696dc765] [~accountid:5de0e6d8be6c1f0d07202403]) team as well.\n# If you need a specific region/storage class that differs from our standard, let me know.\n# Any lifecycle/retention requirements for older binaries, or is a “keep everything” policy OK for now?","2026-01-29T14:38:13.003Z"],["3850272","DRX-28484","DRX","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-29T14:38:30.084Z"],["3850273","PFI-837593","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, not getting that error, but still no payment can be found for this amount.\nPlease ask the client o check if the funds have not been rejected.\nPossibility due to name mismatch ad the recipient is added as Bolt, but should be BOLT OPERATIONS OU","2026-01-29T14:38:41.166Z"],["3850274","LSS-62242","LSS","liivika.tamm@bolt.eu","Liivika Tamm","Hi [~accountid:6426a5407222b08f3e7400d7] Thank you for raising the ticket!\n\nOverall this is good to go. Just couple of guardrails to keep in mind from our side:\n\n* Use Teams only to send KPMG the reporting documents (don’t use it as a general storage or chat archive).\n* Always keep your own copy of anything you upload/send (access/content may be removed or unrecoverable). \n* Be careful with personal data (employee/customer details): share only what’s necessary and only if cross-border processing/transfer is allowed for that data. \n* Don’t upload third-party materials unless you’re sure Bolt has the rights (to avoid claims/indemnity risk). \n* Keep access secure (don’t share logins, use strong password/MFA; KPMG won’t be liable for unauthorized access issues).\n\nPlease let me know if you need any support with collecting the signatures.","2026-01-29T14:38:51.834Z"],["3850275","LSS-55646","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348194|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348194|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:39:04.955Z"],["3850276","TAXP-3406","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","[^Support Services Update 2021-2023 2025-08-03.pdf]\n\nSupport Services benchmark applicable for Fy2025","2026-01-29T14:39:05.953Z"],["3850277","LSS-62399","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] , Poland is not my market, I believe [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] might help here 🙂 ","2026-01-29T14:39:06.754Z"],["3850280","LSS-61798","LSS","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","No, this needs to be obtained from the local business registry right? Legal should obtain that for us?","2026-01-29T14:39:24.623Z"],["3850281","LSS-62414","LSS","isabella.danso@bolt.eu","Isabella Danso","[^Axtro Capital Technologies 2026 Bolt Fleet Partnership Agreement .docx.pdf] _(477 kB)_\n\n[^Fleet portal access agreement template  - 29.10.2025 (3).pdf] _(131 kB)_\n\n[^BOLT Operations NDA (Mutual) (2).pdf] _(151 kB)_","2026-01-29T14:39:42.946Z"],["3850282","TAXP-3406","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","[^Contract R&D Support Services Update 2021-2023.pdf]\n\nR&D support benchmark applicable for FY2025","2026-01-29T14:39:57.871Z"],["3850283","C2-456","C2","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","Formal incident report from HW team formulated by [~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] & myself - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P4zW-kTcfYNMNZl38OEdFmeT7FQDlsY3YIow1cNLgHM/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P4zW-kTcfYNMNZl38OEdFmeT7FQDlsY3YIow1cNLgHM/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T14:40:21.804Z"],["3850284","PFI-836035","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Looks like they made 2 payments for the same amount. Bot have been allocated to their balance now. \n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75679689|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75679689]\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75679687|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75679687]","2026-01-29T14:40:34.257Z"],["3850285","DSR-4215","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-29T14:41:07.611Z"],["3850290","LSS-55646","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba], sent out the org chart for Ahto’s signature. ","2026-01-29T14:41:45.744Z"],["3850294","FRAUD-5764","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","*PR*\n\n[https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162479|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162479]","2026-01-29T14:42:20.764Z"],["3850296","WD-22666","WD","magnus.vainumae@bolt.eu","Magnus Vainumäe","[~accountid:712020:aea92140-f49c-4c1f-91bd-1dd458c46c39] have the sets for Jan 2026 been run already?","2026-01-29T14:42:35.954Z"],["3850297","PFI-837870","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-29T14:42:36.936Z"],["3850298","RDS-186","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:712020:cd1584a2-01ac-4b9a-961f-699131bc6efd] updated. ","2026-01-29T14:42:53.256Z"],["3850299","LSS-60903","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:5f0436f3b545e20015573888] [~accountid:712020:b1700666-82b2-4a86-82f7-550a84f716c8] ! \n\nI have some doubts regarding my performance on this ticket – could you please advise?","2026-01-29T14:43:28.926Z"],["3850301","TAXP-3406","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","[^2025 LRD benchmarks - Combined results write up.pdf]\n\nLocal distribution benchmark: target OM and Cap. Floor is support services benchmark","2026-01-29T14:44:16.694Z"],["3850303","BD-1995","BD","uladzislau.klimiankou@bolt.eu","Vlad Klimenkov","[~accountid:712020:f947e1ea-6aeb-46b3-b11b-f505b87c552d] \n\nonce extending the vertical endpoint - could you pls also update this method [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/delivery/commerce/delivery_invoicing/main/handler/service/ProviderInfoService.ts#L128|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/develop/src/delivery/commerce/delivery_invoicing/main/handler/service/ProviderInfoService.ts#L128]   to actually start using it? \n\nIt checks only {{provider_company?.id}} now, but with what we’ve discussed it will be `{{provider_company?.id OR provider_company found by vat code match}}\n\nBy doing this it will actually start returning correct data to billing-business","2026-01-29T14:44:28.824Z"],["3850305","PFI-836520","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment link here https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/77085651 \r\nNot sure what else we can help you with in this case as the payment is matched correctly. ","2026-01-29T14:44:32.173Z"],["3850306","BP-13309","BP","kristyna.mertova@bolt.eu","Kristyna Mertova","[~accountid:712020:ab58e2f4-f31f-4230-9a41-30c28c8bd545] how can I check the version for user with some preffiled details? As i am checking in my app in my WP. But do not know how it looks for a person in PL and with some added info already.","2026-01-29T14:44:33.343Z"],["3850313","UXA-2197","UXA",null,"Automation for Jira","*Paweł Żelazko* has updated the *Epic Link* on UXA-2240 so the total Story Points on this Epic has been adjusted to *2.0*.","2026-01-29T14:45:33.519Z"],["3850319","LSS-61798","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","I will reach out to my colleagues and we will find out","2026-01-29T14:47:17.094Z"],["3850320","DRX-28485","DRX",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Afolashakin Ajayi, the issue that you created is not assigned to any component!","2026-01-29T14:47:18.758Z"],["3850322","LSS-61882","LSS","isabella.danso@bolt.eu","Isabella Danso","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432]  Hi,\n\nThis are some portions of the contract that were not signed and filled by the partner which includes the Vehicle Owners Consent section.\n\nDo I need to raise a new ticket for this to be rectified?","2026-01-29T14:47:36.992Z"],["3850323","PFI-838128","PFI","panitan.waranchit@bolt-outsource.eu","Panitan Waranchit","Dear payment team please consider moving the fund with amount of 100 THB from [Driver profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7638817?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBangkok](HB) to [Driver profile|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8295247?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBangkok](Active)","2026-01-29T14:47:44.246Z"],["3850324","DSR-4035","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Heyya [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] – reassigning. \n\n\n\nPlease review response prepared by Sigrid. Go through Bh and see if Driver asked for document copy. If not, it’s enough we explain blocking reason (broadly enough not to reveal internal processes).\n\n\n\nConsider whether an escalation to CSPC > Privacy was necessary in this case based on the BH ticket convo.\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-29T14:47:51.886Z"],["3850327","LSS-62415","LSS","michal.lutek@bolt.eu","Michał Lutek","[^ONPO.pdf] _(412 kB)_\n\n[^Wniosek Zenoriah.pdf] _(2.58 MB)_","2026-01-29T14:48:14.390Z"],["3850329","DRX-28484","DRX","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162524","2026-01-29T14:48:28.996Z"],["3850330","LSS-62399","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Sorry for disturbing, [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] ! ","2026-01-29T14:48:52.611Z"],["3850331","WD-22702","WD","daniil.vlassenko@bolt.eu","Daniil Vlassenko","Hey [~accountid:6411c587f1b529dfa98c0e66], I have created a new account for Samu and sent him the instructions. For Ville, I initiated the password reset and delivered instructions to his email. Please ask the users to sign in and change their passwords.","2026-01-29T14:49:22.397Z"],["3850333","HS-29519","HS","alice.gorobets@bolt.eu","Alice Gorobets","Hi [~accountid:712020:a8e1edd0-63f0-4319-9248-bcee0079bb13] \nYour document is being signed. Once it’s signed, you will receive a copy to your personal email you have added to Workday. Please reopen the ticket and let me know if any corrections are needed. \n\nHope everything goes well for you! \n\nBest\nAlice, Senior People Operations Specialist ","2026-01-29T14:50:07.688Z"],["3850335","DSR-4101","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Another one [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] \n\n\n\nPlease investigate the BH and see if this is a CSPC > Privacy issue – i.e. is this a DSRR or not if Driver is merely asking for reason, not a copy. If you do not deem this as DSRR, please instruct to push back.\n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-29T14:51:03.058Z"],["3850336","LSS-62399","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Thanks [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] and [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432], I will ask [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] for support with this one.","2026-01-29T14:51:06.356Z"],["3850338","TAXP-3406","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","[^License of IP - 2025 write up.pdf]\n[^FY2025 Bolt Operations TP policy implementation.xlsx]\n[^Appendix A (needs to be downloaded to be correctly seen).xlsx]\n\nLicense & Services (Bolt Operations OÜ)","2026-01-29T14:51:33.436Z"],["3850339","BP-13309","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","* city and postal code is not pre-filled even though it says town correctly in the suggestion\nSome BE responses do not contain separate fields for *City* and/or *Postcode* - in this case, we cannot pre-fill them.\nThe full address contains this information, but it’s a plain string that also includes other parts in addition to the city.\n\nI’ve attached two different responses that show this:\n!image-20260129-144745.png|width=1229,alt=\"image-20260129-144745.png\"!\n\n!image-20260129-144642.png|width=1270,alt=\"image-20260129-144642.png\"!","2026-01-29T14:52:00.114Z"],["3850342","PFI-834952","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, I checked we indeed made the payout to the C on 2025-07-09 and we can not see any rejections for the funds. \n/PT/FT/ROC/00018524/PY/PAYMENT RETURN- 5135169231/BN/Valerii Didenko/BO/Bolt Operations OU 15,VANA LOUNA TN,TALLINN,10134 TALL/BO3/INN,EE/BI/EE747700771011798106/SCID/SEPA/OA/EUR40,00/AB/LHVBEE22XXX/OB/CITIIE2X\n\nInitial ticket [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-739335|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-739335|smart-link]  ","2026-01-29T14:52:41.996Z"],["3850343","TAXP-3406","TAXP","pedro.yaguezbovio@bolt.eu","Pedro Yaguez Bovio","[^Bolt - FINAL sales and distribution services search write-up (2021 - 2023)_14.08.2025.pdf]\n\nBolt UK: Franchise model for Rides","2026-01-29T14:52:54.410Z"],["3850345","LSS-62295","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:36cbea54-0723-40fc-a8d1-2d4945acece1]! Sure, please make sure you share the NDA here if there are any comments on the NDA from the partner (we’ll review them) or once it needs to be signed. The aim is to make sure we keep track of all the NDAs in the tickets. Thank you! ","2026-01-29T14:53:10.747Z"],["3850347","PFI-840243","PFI","monika.civrag@bolt.eu","Monika Čivrag","Thank you! I have notified the fleet about it 🌞 ","2026-01-29T14:53:25.014Z"],["3850349","LSS-61798","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] ! May you kindly assist there by providing Bolt ZA registration certificate?\n\nThanks a lot!","2026-01-29T14:53:32.695Z"],["3850350","LSS-62412","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi Ping, thanks for the ticket! \nI will check OpenStreet map policies with regards to attribution and IP use. \nIn the meantime, would you mind confirming the following for a better background:\n\n* if you’re aware of any contract signed with OSM / any services we’re paying for with OSM? I checked Spotdraft but was only able to find one agreement with OSM that is not relevant. \n* generally, if we’ve used their map or services before in any of our products and how? \n* and if you’re aware if other competitors are using OSM as part of their services (regardless of product type) \n\nThanks in advance! ","2026-01-29T14:53:38.180Z"],["3850351","DSR-4125","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","Reassigning to [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] \n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-29T14:53:49.581Z"],["3850352","BP-13309","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","* NIP says only Required, but it should be Must be 10 digits\n\nWhen field is empty - it says Required. If you enter at least 1 symbol - it says Must be 10 digits.\nDo you want it to always say Must be 10 digits ?","2026-01-29T14:54:10.514Z"],["3850355","PFI-838394","PFI","warisara.sopa@bolt-outsource.eu","Warisara Sopa","Is it possible to move from [+client 7014987 (Hidden profile)+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7014987?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBangkok] to client [+8486708 (active profile)+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/8486708?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Asia%2FBangkok]?","2026-01-29T14:54:48.653Z"],["3850356","PFI-833620","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-29T14:54:53.221Z"],["3850357","LSS-61765","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] ! This one will be performed on Monday since Ahto is working remotely today and tomorrow","2026-01-29T14:54:53.701Z"],["3850358","LSS-62021","LSS","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Hey, sounds good to start with 1st option and see how it goes before incl. VVTAT. Thank you all.","2026-01-29T14:55:05.497Z"],["3850359","PFI-840344","PFI","sharon.achieng@bolt-outsource.eu","Sharon Achieng","!IMG_4771.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T14:55:37.415Z"],["3850361","PFI-833166","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-29T14:55:50.038Z"],["3850362","DRX-28340","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Technical fix, would be covered by regular release circle tests","2026-01-29T14:55:56.175Z"],["3850363","WD-22730","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Hi Ewa,\n\nThis is to confirm that the additional days have been added to the Polish holiday calendar as per your indications.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions.\n\nMany thanks,\n\nMihut","2026-01-29T14:56:16.526Z"],["3850368","LUX-806","LUX","marek.pagel@bolt.eu","Marek Pagel","sent you invite","2026-01-29T14:56:42.308Z"],["3850369","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","2mm EPDM sheet rubber has arrived\n\n!08f3220dfd283e74a1d5909c918dd73a-20260129-141240.jpg|width=157,alt=\"08f3220dfd283e74a1d5909c918dd73a-20260129-141240.jpg\"!\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"0f71b68d-83ce-4a1c-b14c-2cb532d53279\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":10},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Sheet rubber version\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Front flap clearance: 50mm\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The material is flexible and silent when riding.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"A 50mm front clearance poses no risk thanks to the material's flexibility over high bumps or curbstones.\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"In warehouses, bikes usually move on the rear wheel because the front wheel is locked by a hublock.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The flap allows the bike to move forward only.\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Moving backward is not possible.\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"},{\"type\":\"textColor\",\"attrs\":{\"color\":\"#ff5630\"}}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Wide areas on the left and right sides reduce protection by causing water drops to bounce back to the front side.\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"bulletList\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"listItem\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"It provides maximum front protection while keeping the rider's legs dry during maneuvers.\"}]}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":175,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-135037.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-135037.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":640,\"width\":640}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":142,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-141112.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-141112.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1478,\"width\":1478}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":223,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"86ae7d59decd63581311c09fc42ae4d9-20260129-134757.jpg\",\"alt\":\"86ae7d59decd63581311c09fc42ae4d9-20260129-134757.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":143,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"10987258c267ded48c9dec0aa9d140e4-20260129-135203.jpg\",\"alt\":\"10987258c267ded48c9dec0aa9d140e4-20260129-135203.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":143,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"a7f7af8ac37313fa5deb33d7db0ead8e-20260129-135218.jpg\",\"alt\":\"a7f7af8ac37313fa5deb33d7db0ead8e-20260129-135218.jpg\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":567,\"width\":567}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":121,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-142515.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-142515.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1067,\"width\":1067}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":122,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-142718.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-142718.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1056,\"width\":1056}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":2},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":174,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-143627.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-143627.png\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1418,\"width\":1418}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"f88cf59e7abbb3986ae2124addc1bd37.mp4\",\"alt\":\"f88cf59e7abbb3986ae2124addc1bd37.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":960,\"width\":544}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"6d7ff88b0a9c10f64e67927024c1a347.mp4\",\"alt\":\"6d7ff88b0a9c10f64e67927024c1a347.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"7ffdd2c166a83b58e3ac3916afbe9f14.mp4\",\"alt\":\"7ffdd2c166a83b58e3ac3916afbe9f14.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":960,\"width\":544}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"47e25e515414e8c17ca060eb61a78d5b.mp4\",\"alt\":\"47e25e515414e8c17ca060eb61a78d5b.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":320,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"618ce2952099532807c2e210b4c94285.mp4\",\"alt\":\"618ce2952099532807c2e210b4c94285.mp4\",\"collection\":\"\",\"height\":1280,\"width\":720}}]}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-29T14:57:03.795Z"],["3850371","DSR-4079","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","Sent a DM to Andrii Kovalov regarding the fraud block and new opportunity by verification team ","2026-01-29T14:57:03.698Z"],["3850373","BP-13309","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] please check if you have the latest version of the app. I had a similar issue before the update.","2026-01-29T14:57:05.881Z"],["3850374","PFI-838128","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Matched","2026-01-29T14:57:13.797Z"],["3850376","CSDA-313","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Thank you for raising a request to our team!\nWe review all new project requests every Monday morning. We'll update you once the request is reviewed and internally assigned.","2026-01-29T14:57:47.995Z"],["3850377","LSS-62416","LSS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","[^Vertrag Autoproff.docx.pdf] _(453 kB)_","2026-01-29T14:58:04.699Z"],["3850379","PFI-838394","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T14:58:30.529Z"],["3850380","WFM-10196","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Hello [~accountid:6156a567c5388b00694080f3] Please provide detail overview on what task/workflows you will be working on. \n\nOps Outsource (compliance)-  Why do you need this role? \n\nBeehive Driver Reactivation Agent - there are several variation to this role, detail exactly which one you need. \n\nOutsource CS - Rides, Outsource CS - Team Lead - these are CS roles and will not be given for OPS agents. ","2026-01-29T14:58:38.550Z"],["3850384","CSCC-67","CSCC","margarita.hobo@bolt.eu","Margarita Hobo","The training was completed by all  SCC specialists. ","2026-01-29T14:59:05.886Z"],["3850385","RDS-1471","RDS","vivaksha.singh@bolt.eu","Vivaksha Singh","[~accountid:5fca4c37cbead5006998a665] : While analytics, product and design are doing their research, could you estimate the effort for developing / integrating below 3 filters.\n1. Area preferences\n2. Earnings/hour\n\n# Integrating driver destination with smart accept. \n\nFYI [~accountid:712020:9db8be0f-eb61-4ebc-bac7-a9563c14e4b0]  [~accountid:620e7f2eef2bd5006aead114] [~accountid:712020:d88f5976-1e33-47f5-acb2-a9c422493f69] ","2026-01-29T14:59:09.406Z"],["3850386","PFI-832870","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-29T14:59:34.831Z"],["3850388","BP-13309","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] Dark theme is only supported in latest version of iOS if i’m not mistaken and is not supported on Android version.\nHere is a screenshot from live iOS version 219.0\n\n!IMG_0272.PNG|width=335,alt=\"IMG_0272.PNG\"!\n\nAbout the blue it’s usually an indication of picking from autofill (on iOS and macOS), have not seen it on my devices. But have seen it on RB login on the mac. Heres an example:\n\n!Screen Recording 2026-01-29 at 16.49.48.mov|width=584,alt=\"Screen Recording 2026-01-29 at 16.49.48.mov\"!\n\nRegarding city and postal code not being filled in please see post “Known limitation” in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13322|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BP-13322|smart-link] . In short the search we use (not ours) sometimes returns the city name in the description but doesn’t return it as a separate parameter so we cannot use it to fill the field.","2026-01-29T14:59:57.391Z"],["3850389","FPD-1503","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","h1. How Organic Model Error Affects Optimization\n\nh2. Context\n\nIn addition to uncertainty in incremental models, *errors in the organic models* (search sessions and online hours) can materially distort the results of the supply–demand spend optimization.\n\nThe key reason is that the *online hours per search session ratio (OH / SS)* is the primary driver of predicted conversion rates (both S2O and O2F). Any systematic bias in either organic SS or OH propagates directly into conversion estimates and, ultimately, into *finished orders and GMV uplift*.\n\nAs a result, even if incremental response curves are well specified, *organic model error alone can meaningfully overstate or understate the expected gains from reallocation*.\n\nThis analysis isolates and explains that effect.\n\n----\n\nh2. Simulation\n\nTo study the impact of organic model error on optimization outcomes, we generate a controlled simulation that mirrors the structure of the production models.\n\nh3. Base assumptions\n\n* We select baseline organic values for:\n** *Search Sessions (SS)*\n** *Online Hours (OH)*\n* The baseline *OH / SS ratio* is chosen to be close to observed real-world values.\n* A fixed *net spend* is assumed, with demand and supply spend varying inversely.\n\nh3. Incremental response\n\nFor a given demand/supply split:\n\n* Incremental SS, OH, and S2O are estimated using *diminishing returns curves* consistent with the production model formulation.\n* Incremental effects are *stronger on the demand side* (SS and S2O) than on the supply side (OH), reflecting empirical behavior.\n\nh3. Conversion modeling\n\n* *Organic S2O* and *total O2F* are estimated as *deterministic functions of the OH / SS ratio*.\n* We assume a linear relationship:\nhigher OH / SS → higher conversion\n* This ensures that marketplace balance directly controls conversion outcomes.\n\nh3. Base (“true world”) scenario\n\nWe assume:\n\n* perfect predictive accuracy,\n* organic + incremental estimates equal the true values.\n\nStarting from a *balanced baseline* (10% demand / 10% supply), we then:\n\n* shift demand up and supply down (or vice versa) in *0.5pp steps*,\n* recompute all metrics at each split,\n* calculate *finished orders uplift relative to the baseline*.\n\nThis produces the “true” optimization curve.\n\n----\n\nh2. Baseline Optimization Results\n\nThe baseline optimization (no organic error) shows:\n\n* Finished orders uplift peaking at *just above 2%*.\n* The optimal allocation shifts *toward demand spend*, driven primarily by:\n** higher incremental sessions,\n** incremental lift in S2O conversion.\n\nAt the optimum:\n\n* *Total SS increases materially*,\n* *Total OH decreases modestly*,\n* the *OH / SS ratio declines*.\n\nThis decline in OH / SS:\n\n* lowers organic S2O and O2F,\n* but is more than offset by incremental S2O gains,\n* resulting in a net positive uplift.\n\nThis regime is *conversion-sensitive*: changes in marketplace balance strongly affect outcomes.\n\n!image-20260129-132144.png|width=798,alt=\"image-20260129-132144.png\"!\n\n!image-20260129-132209.png|width=798,alt=\"image-20260129-132209.png\"!\n\n!image-20260129-132219.png|width=794,alt=\"image-20260129-132219.png\"!\n\n----\n\nh2. Introducing Organic Model Error\n\nWe now introduce *systematic organic forecast errors*:\n\n* SS error ∈ [−25%, +25%]\n* OH error ∈ [−25%, +25%]\n\nErrors are applied *one metric at a time*, holding all others constant, and the full optimization is rerun under each error scenario.\n\nh2. Results\n\nh3. Effect of Search Sessions (SS) Error\n\nThe overall *shape of the optimization curve remains stable*, but the *magnitude of uplift changes substantially*.\n\nAt the optimal allocation:\n\n* *−25% SS error* → estimated uplift drops to *~1.7%*\n* *0% SS error* → baseline uplift of *~2.8%*\n* *+25% SS error* → estimated uplift increases to *~3.7%*\n\nThis asymmetry arises because:\n\n* SS error affects finished orders *both through volume and through the OH / SS ratio*,\n* under-forecasting SS inflates the ratio disproportionately,\n* over-forecasting SS suppresses the ratio more gently.\n\nAs a result, *SS error produces a non-linear, asymmetric distortion* of the optimization signal.\n\n!image-20260129-132309.png|width=794,alt=\"image-20260129-132309.png\"!\n\nh3. Effect of Online Hours (OH) Error\n\nOH error shows a *more linear but equally material impact*:\n\nAt the optimal allocation:\n\n* *−25% OH error* → estimated uplift increases to *~3.9%*\n* *0% OH error* → baseline uplift of *~2.8%*\n* *+25% OH error* → estimated uplift falls to *~1.9%*\n\nUnlike SS error:\n\n* OH error does *not* directly change volume,\n* it affects finished orders almost entirely through *conversion via OH / SS*.\n\nBecause the conversion functions are monotonic in the ratio:\n\n* OH error propagates nearly linearly into finished orders.\n\n!image-20260129-132334.png|width=796,alt=\"image-20260129-132334.png\"!\n\nThe plots show that SS and OH errors distort optimization *in opposite directions*:\n\n* Increasing SS (or under-estimating OH) worsens marketplace balance.\n* Increasing OH (or under-estimating SS) improves marketplace balance.\n\nThe key distinction:\n\n* *SS error affects both volume and conversion*,\n* *OH error affects conversion only*.\n\nThis explains:\n\n* the non-linear curvature seen in SS-error plots,\n* the near-linear behavior under OH error.\n\n!image-20260129-132354.png|width=1157,alt=\"image-20260129-132354.png\"!\n\n----\n\nh2. Conclusion\n\nErrors in organic search sessions and online hours forecasts have a *first-order impact* on supply–demand optimization results.\n\nKey takeaways:\n\n# *Optimization curves are shape-stable but magnitude-fragile*\nErrors do not change the qualitative direction of the optimal split, but they can *materially over- or under-estimate uplift*.\n# *SS and OH errors behave fundamentally differently*\n#* SS error introduces *non-linear, asymmetric distortion*.\n#* OH error propagates *linearly through conversion*.\n# *Marketplace balance (OH / SS) is the critical transmission channel*\nAny bias in organic forecasts that alters this ratio directly affects conversion and finished orders.\n# *Optimization should be gated by organic model confidence*\nIn markets where SS or OH forecasts are unstable or biased, optimization outputs should be treated with caution or not used at all.\n\nIn short, *incremental modeling accuracy is not sufficient*: without reliable organic baselines, optimization can confidently point in the right direction while being *numerically wrong by a large margin*.","2026-01-29T15:00:11.750Z"],["3850393","BP-13309","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","* the Address filled field is blue 🧐 not grey as others\n\nThis one is very weird - all fields are grey for me. [~accountid:712020:e2c955ca-33bb-4f61-9a12-3b0fb520b3fd] I think all are grey for you as well?","2026-01-29T15:01:11.547Z"],["3850395","PFI-837455","PFI","lola.idowu@bolt.eu","Lolade Alexia Idowu","[~accountid:712020:8bcb68bd-f8da-4da1-8320-2536f6bb0c0c]  - can you provide guidance here?  Thanks!","2026-01-29T15:01:37.432Z"],["3850397","WFM-10185","WFM","ksenia.romanenko@bolt.eu","Ksenia Romanenko","Hello team! Please assign same agents who is working on Rentals Q","2026-01-29T15:01:51.615Z"],["3850398","BP-13309","BP","raman.zhyshkevich@bolt.eu","Raman Zhyshkevich","[~accountid:712020:f7f7320d-7e3a-4389-8726-f082352b7487] [~accountid:712020:e2c955ca-33bb-4f61-9a12-3b0fb520b3fd] let’s move to Slack 🙏 ","2026-01-29T15:01:53.048Z"],["3850399","LSS-61217","LSS","magdalena.kowara@bolt.eu","Magdalena Kowara","Zip Lok from tax team should be able to help","2026-01-29T15:02:10.304Z"],["3850400","LSS-62415","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:5c454c27-a98f-4408-979d-0831728f5d07] ! Please specify delivery details.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-29T15:02:12.973Z"],["3850402","PFI-830581","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Matched","2026-01-29T15:02:37.108Z"],["3850404","LUX-806","LUX","marek.pagel@bolt.eu","Marek Pagel","we don’t have 404 metrics. But I’m at least pretty sure I know where the problem is, even if not yet sure “why”","2026-01-29T15:02:46.491Z"],["3850407","LSS-59845","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Sentry Order Form for Bolt 09012025 (3) (1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T15:03:28.165Z"],["3850411","LSS-60715","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hi, [~accountid:712020:89527d4a-ea9c-40dc-b6fd-9e0779096af2] ! Are you sure that cluase 3.2 and 3.3 of SK GTC are revised in the Special Terms? I don’t recognize any changes of such clauses in [the Special Terms. |https://docs.google.com/document/d/10Gd0vAQZwK3AQIMzpZUFv0YA0VO2A252/edit] If these clause are still up to change, could you please advise?","2026-01-29T15:03:39.511Z"],["3850412","PFI-830043","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-29T15:03:40.529Z"],["3850413","WFM-10205","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601889|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601889]","2026-01-29T15:03:44.203Z"],["3850414","LSS-62288","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348213|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348213|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T15:03:48.170Z"],["3850415","LSS-61902","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","Looked at the purchase order, yup all good you can just sign!\n\nit doesn’t auto-renew, so once the trial is done, no money will automatically be charged.","2026-01-29T15:04:00.649Z"],["3850417","WFM-10205","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Hey [~accountid:712020:3f31dc69-91e1-47bc-9187-ba7e6205feae] Access has been requested and is pending approval. Should be completed by tomorrow morning. I will confirm once done. ","2026-01-29T15:04:21.842Z"],["3850419","BZNS-471","BZNS","edvardsjanis.recickis@bolt.eu","Edvards Jānis Rečickis","[~accountid:5f23e228bedd1000153843ae] Emails are unblocked and live","2026-01-29T15:04:45.717Z"],["3850420","LSS-58352","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","[~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] thank you, reviewed. Please note that there are still some open comments that should be clarified by you and/or [~accountid:712020:62d2d09a-02e2-437d-abbd-86f5be2b5737]. I tagged you in the document.","2026-01-29T15:04:57.108Z"],["3850421","LSS-58622","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:6166d4c799b4b8006a26023e] let me know if all is clear and if you need any further support or have any questions 🙏 ","2026-01-29T15:05:04.211Z"],["3850427","PFI-834221","PFI","anna.zaritska@bolt.eu","Anna Zaritska","Hey! \n\nI have one more wrongly matched payment from this provider. \n\n* Sum 3670.17 UAH\n* Date 26 Jan 2026\n* Payment [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/78443641?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn] \n\nPlease import it to *provider ID 81633*, along with the four payments I submitted earlier.\n\nThanks\n\n","2026-01-29T15:06:00.019Z"],["3850429","DRX-28486","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Bug inside the Driver App|:large_green_circle: Low impact|:android-classic: Android Driver App|DA.126.0\n\n*Driver/Order ids*\n\n*Appearance time*\n26/01/2025\n\n*Description*\nDriver: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3328246?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%[…]ffset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/3328246?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FTallinn]\n\nDriver tries to upload a document into the Support chat in Bolt Driver app. After that, the app closes/reboots (see screen recording).\n\n*From:* *@user-UDQ0ZU37T*","2026-01-29T15:06:28.379Z"],["3850430","DRX-28486","DRX",null,"Slack","[Uladzimir Akulovich|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/604aad6403ceda0069bec100] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF1SLTZ/p1769695341287519?thread_ts=1769695341.287519&cid=CSFF1SLTZ|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CSFF1SLTZ/p1769695341287519?thread_ts=1769695341.287519&cid=CSFF1SLTZ|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-29T15:06:29.659Z"],["3850431","DRX-28486","DRX","maria.temmo@bolt.eu","Maria Temmo","*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ABN71RRHB/chatissue.mp4|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ABN71RRHB/chatissue.mp4|smart-link]","2026-01-29T15:06:30.134Z"],["3850432","DRX-28486","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","[@fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63998438f3c3dfd71fe85ae4] tagging you since you're on-duty QA Engineer. Do we have Xiaomi Redmi 14C in our pool?","2026-01-29T15:06:31.568Z"],["3850433","DRX-28486","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","I had checked on OPPO Reno 15, Android 15 using DA.128.0 and I can upload to the chat view on {{Prelive}}\n\nI'll check if there is a Xiaomi and run the sequence\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AC4MDJF8R/file_upload.mp4|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0AC4MDJF8R/file_upload.mp4|smart-link]","2026-01-29T15:06:32.325Z"],["3850434","DRX-28486","DRX","fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi@bolt.eu","Fiyinfoluwa Daniel Akinrimisi","[@uladzimir.akulovich|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/604aad6403ceda0069bec100] we dont seem to have a Xiaomi 14C but a Xiaomi 15, Android 16 .\n\nTesting on DA.126.0 and DA.128.0, the user is able to upload a media file\n\nThese are {{Prelive}} release buids\n\n*Attachments*\n\n* [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ABS0E9L1G/mobizen_20260129_163957.mp4|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/files/U786847FW/F0ABS0E9L1G/mobizen_20260129_163957.mp4|smart-link]","2026-01-29T15:06:33.150Z"],["3850435","DRX-28486","DRX","uladzimir.akulovich@bolt.eu","Uladzimir Akulovich","Thanks [@fiyinfoluwa.akinrimisi|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63998438f3c3dfd71fe85ae4]! I'm taking a look and will find out how we can fix it","2026-01-29T15:06:33.734Z"],["3850437","LSS-28796","LSS","anna.hultengard@bolt.eu","Anna Hultengård","Hi, as mentioned on Slack, the law firm has now received information from the Swedish Enforcement Authority that the case with M Lager is closed, meaning that the full funds should have been paid. We did not receive a payment confirmation or similar (as requested by Emelie) but perhaps we can check if we received the funds internally? If we have not received the funds, I will revert to the law firm.","2026-01-29T15:07:42.071Z"],["3850440","PFI-840174","PFI","adam.zabrotski@bolt-outsource.eu","Adam Zabrotski","The driver asked whether it’s possible to change this ride as well? Thanks!\n[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-carsharing/orders/edit/global/33486483|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/rentals-carsharing/orders/edit/global/33486483]","2026-01-29T15:08:30.671Z"],["3850441","LSS-28796","LSS","anna.hultengard@bolt.eu","Anna Hultengård","[^Redovisning av avslutat mål.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-29T15:08:36.577Z"],["3850444","PTWS-2134","PTWS","octavian.todor@bolt.eu","Octavian Todor","For some reason, they cannot see one of the columns (Estonians)\n\n!image-20260129-150412.png|width=534,alt=\"image-20260129-150412.png\"!\n\nThis shows up for me and for Steve and Mihut. I checked all the permissions for the Global Mobility Team (Unconstrained) and Global Mobility Team (Relocation) in which Liis is, but I cannot find anything that would cause this. I added Trended Workers data source permissions for the group and it did not help. Estonians, Relocatees and Local Foreigners fields are all based of an CF EE which checks the TF condition for the worker’s relocation tags:\n\n# If relocation tags = permit check/permit exchange → local foreigners\n# If relocation tags = not empty and they contain anything else except for permit check/permit exchange → Relocatees\n# If relocation tags = empty → Estonians\n\nGlobal Mobility Team has access to the relocation tags CF, as well as to the EE CF I created and the source field it uses.\n\nI scheduled the report to run weekly and export an xls as a workaround for now and I will keep looking into this, but for the time being they will have access to the data on a weekly basis via xls export.","2026-01-29T15:09:02.878Z"],["3850446","LSS-62403","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jIZgH3tKdncr6LUxUCHozt8-klDIZdpf/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jIZgH3tKdncr6LUxUCHozt8-klDIZdpf/edit|smart-link] \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i2dhamHslkBf4haq5xoHbGaatxJ2lWQg/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1i2dhamHslkBf4haq5xoHbGaatxJ2lWQg/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T15:09:14.736Z"],["3850447","LSS-62260","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Vollmacht_(1).pdf] ","2026-01-29T15:09:19.830Z"],["3850449","CSDT-978","CSDT","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Refund deductions metrics:\n\n* [notebook|https://bolt-common.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/4068087815930389]\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01A7SKE5C1/p1769596363486779|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01A7SKE5C1/p1769596363486779|smart-link]  - thread to confirm how to map balance_entry_id <> refund_id\n* [https://fivetran.com/dashboard/connections/sensory_furnished/status?groupId=deafness_embarking&service=google_sheets&syncChartPeriod=1 Day|https://fivetran.com/dashboard/connections/sensory_furnished/status?groupId=deafness_embarking&service=google_sheets&syncChartPeriod=1%20Day] - connector for manual refund deductions; {{fivetran_boltfood_order_refund_deduction_manual_spark.order_refund_deduction_manual}} - access limited\n* [https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/delivery/models/intermediate/core/invoice/int_invoice_records_provider_billing/int_invoice_records_provider_billing.sql|https://github.com/bolteu/dbt/blob/main/delivery/models/intermediate/core/invoice/int_invoice_records_provider_billing/int_invoice_records_provider_billing.sql|smart-link]  - delivery uses sum_eur not amount_eur (with VAT)\n* [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01A7SKE5C1/p1750321669026529|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01A7SKE5C1/p1750321669026529|smart-link]  - thread to confirm tables and dimensions to use to get provider refund deductions (asked in June 2025)\n\n\n\nQuestions to discuss with Kevin & Boris:\n\n* it is not possible to map manual refund deductions with refunds; we can either have the data on automatic deductions related to specific refunds or just the sum of refund deductions per order → aggregated by country\n* for automatic deductions, it is possible to add following dimensions for each refund:\n** {{is_automatic_delivery_order_provider_refund_deduction}}\n** {{deduction_balance_entry_id}} ({{balance_entry_id}} in {{core_models_spark.fact_billing_core_balance_provider}})\n** {{deduction_event_ts_utc}}\n** {{deduction_amount}} (or {{deduction_sum}} - without VAT)\n** {{deduction_amount_eur}}(or {{deduction_sum_eur}} - without VAT)\n** {{provider_id}}","2026-01-29T15:10:02.674Z"],["3850450","LSS-62415","LSS","michal.lutek@bolt.eu","Michał Lutek","Hi, you can send it to the office. ","2026-01-29T15:10:08.452Z"],["3850451","LSS-47219","LSS","aleksandra.tretiak@bolt.eu","Aleksandra Tretiak","Hey, [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ! Please find the signed document(s) attached.[^Bolt_Operations_OÜ_AINT_Appnext_Amendment_22122025.docx.pdf] ","2026-01-29T15:10:10.314Z"],["3850453","DSR-4079","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[+driver account+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/6537780?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw] - during the registration process, the account was blocked due to missing correct selfie verification.\nThe fleet and the driver, being aware of this, intentionally made a new registration of the person with new details, so that it would not be possible to find the suspended account.\nTherefore, the account was permanently suspended — due to intentional avoidance of the blocked account and creation of a duplicate with new details.","2026-01-29T15:10:44.005Z"],["3850457","WD-22683","WD","dieulinh.tran@bolt.eu","Diệu Linh Tran","I accept the terms","2026-01-29T15:12:00.033Z"],["3850461","LSS-62231","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Could be sent out. Thank you! ","2026-01-29T15:12:56.359Z"],["3850463","LSS-62149","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","Hi [~accountid:712020:282008bf-7f03-4058-8bec-43f7e5a44ace] , I’ll be having a look at this! I see that the urgency is set to medium, is there any specific date it needs to be done by? Thanks!","2026-01-29T15:13:01.112Z"],["3850468","CCM-22301","CCM","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","Thank you [~accountid:616ec4e2f6da6a006a877eed] ! \n\n\nI’ll start moving the questions into TalentLMS and am aiming to have this completed by the end of this week or the beginning of next week. I’ve also requested commenter access to the document, in case any questions come up along the way.\n\nJust to double-check - the target audience for this exercise is outsourced TP agents only, correct? I’m asking because we haven’t moved BPOs to the Bolt Learning Hub yet, so the MKA would live in TalentLMS for now.","2026-01-29T15:14:44.412Z"],["3850469","LSS-62417","LSS","lisette.suik@bolt.eu","Lisette Suik","From a strictly legal standpoint, notifying merchants in advance that a control group is used might be a good idea. While I agree that there’s nothing in the T&Cs stating that the discount will be applied to 100% of users (not sure about the partner portal copy, though), there is also nothing that explicitly says we can include a control group. So, legally speaking, there’s room to argue either way.\nThe reason I think notification could still make sense is mainly *merchant relationship management*: to avoid merchants finding out themselves and feeling disappointed that this wasn’t shared proactively.\nAnother approach would be to handle this on a case-by-case basis — i.e. if a merchant asks why not all users receive the discount, we explain that a small control group is used for measurement purposes, and if they strongly object, we could fix this (assuming it’s technically possible to exclude them).","2026-01-29T15:14:50.430Z"],["3850470","LSS-62418","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nMonika Čivrag has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-29T15:14:52.946Z"],["3850471","PFI-840151","PFI","annika.helimets@bolt.eu","Annika Helimets","Solved","2026-01-29T15:14:55.175Z"],["3850472","PFI-840151","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-29T15:14:58.870Z"],["3850473","DSR-4141","DSR","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","[~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] ran out of ideas how to explain that I’m reassigning. \n\n\n\nAs always, check if it’s a DSAR and review the responses if it is. I’m 1 convo away. \n\n\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] ","2026-01-29T15:15:12.860Z"],["3850474","TAXP-3385","TAXP","tiiu.albin@bolt.eu","Tiiu Albin","[~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] Thanks [~accountid:614ae82ed747e80075f8baa5] ! As regards the comments in the email, I would suggest we provide responses at a very high level, essentially acknowledging their recommendations. Is that ok? ","2026-01-29T15:15:17.985Z"],["3850476","WD-22718","WD","adam.kudybinski@bolt.eu","Adam Kudybiński","I didn’t know there was this other Workday entry point. It seems to work. Thank you","2026-01-29T15:15:24.967Z"],["3850480","HS-29323","HS","villem.vilipere@bolt.eu","Villem Vilipere","Hi, \n\nSpoke to Giovanna on Slack, we can close the ticket. \n\nKind Regards,\n\nVillem ","2026-01-29T15:17:16.287Z"],["3850485","LSS-62252","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] - from a privacy perspective, my main concern is sharing only the minimal data required with the API partner to resolve the issue and ensuring any data shared with the business customer in the incident serves a clear purpose.\n\nHappy to discuss any further questions. My understanding is that riders via RideBooker are also considered Bolt’s customers, as they receive Bolt Business T&Cs via SMS when ordering a ride.\n\nCC [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] ","2026-01-29T15:18:01.158Z"],["3850487","HS-29235","HS","villem.vilipere@bolt.eu","Villem Vilipere","Hi [~accountid:6271326a2db3080070241cfa] \n\nJust checking do we have any update on this request? \n\nKind Regards, \n\nVillem ","2026-01-29T15:18:39.010Z"],["3850488","DRX-28352","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Please test options which was mentioned in the ticket description","2026-01-29T15:18:49.225Z"],["3850490","LSS-62337","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348224|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348224|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T15:19:34.208Z"],["3850491","LSS-62337","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] sent out the document for signature.","2026-01-29T15:19:54.434Z"],["3850492","LSS-62390","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Thanks [~accountid:712020:dc5a9fc0-ec62-423d-a2f8-435f02007669], as mentioned on Slack, it is a business decision. from legal POV, it would be more efficient not to introduce the interim POBOX address, but have it changed straight to the new address, especially if this is not the problem for the landlord and the workplace team will pick up the correspondence on a regular basis - please ensure that this is taken care of.\n\nI will also start the process of updating the commercial register for the CZ entity. In case there is any change in the planned effective date of the address change, please let me know. Thank you!","2026-01-29T15:20:22.783Z"],["3850493","EBIKE1-227","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] I used LLM to see what are its proposal, most of them were same as we already are doing. This different salt test caught my eye and these ‘'load-tests’'. I checked the salt test, it quiet nice and sever test. ","2026-01-29T15:20:30.928Z"],["3850495","MP-3575","MP","mirkamal.gasimov@bolt.eu","Mirkamal Gasimov","Jira mcp success :done: ","2026-01-29T15:21:24.594Z"],["3850496","LSS-62419","LSS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","[^NDA Avrios.pdf] _(198 kB)_","2026-01-29T15:21:57.886Z"],["3850497","HS-29326","HS","christopher.free@bolt.eu","Chris Free","Thank you Marilin - yes please, lets go and add them to my plan! \n\n\n\nChris ","2026-01-29T15:22:08.405Z"],["3850498","PAW-15272","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-29T15:23:04.791Z"],["3850499","CEBF-1703","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[Tested|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aFzWv1PrZH4vQlgRo2zo-xEmqZp9cQH6c_Zr136zQKQ/edit?usp=sharing] with a bug.","2026-01-29T15:24:16.172Z"],["3850500","PRV-1031","PRV","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Legacy update:*\n\n# Web team confirmed its alignment in December;\n# Last pending step is to add the guidelines to the Privacy Confluence Space.\n\nTBC in Q1 2026. Medium priority.","2026-01-29T15:24:36.165Z"],["3850501","PFI-840354","PFI","sera.teng@bolt.eu","Sera Teng","!image1.jpeg.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T15:24:56.026Z"],["3850502","PFI-840354","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T15:24:58.276Z"],["3850503","RNP-242","RNP","tanel.koha@bolt.eu","Tanel Koha","Hi [~accountid:62e147f78cc02d0b34bd89a4] - the restart blocker should be cleared now!\n\nNotes for pre-release testing (let’s make sure they are covered somewhere/somehow):\n\n*What happens when Expo Updates patch arrives to device? Will it freeze?*\n\nWhen can you continue with this 😄? (We are sorry that it has been blocked for so long.)","2026-01-29T15:25:35.618Z"],["3850505","CORA-303","CORA","sanaullah.khan@bolt.eu","Sana-Ullah Khan","[~accountid:61fa31cd1c9bb000727c6e01] For now it is not needed. If the need arises again i will create another ticket. ","2026-01-29T15:26:30.437Z"],["3850506","TAXP-3385","TAXP","alejandro.sanz@bolt.eu","Alejandro Sanz","[~accountid:61b9ad7c2900b00071da0b68] , fine for me 🙂 ","2026-01-29T15:26:37.091Z"],["3850507","DSR-4015","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","From safety side the block is permanent. Too many different reports and ratings. \nThey counted the grouping [Driver Operating In Fraudulent Manner]. There are several from 2023 until 2025.  [1st report|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1287102246/18?orderTryId=1890332864] and [7th report|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1368717966/396?orderTryId=2174040345]","2026-01-29T15:26:54.051Z"],["3850515","HS-28790","HS","anna.tiurina@bolt.eu","Anna Tiurina","Hey Miina,\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nCould you please clarify for which year the 6 vacation days were allocated - 2025 or 2026?","2026-01-29T15:28:57.468Z"],["3850517","PFI-831891","PFI","daniels.smirnovs@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniels Smirnovs","Any updates?\n\n","2026-01-29T15:30:37.696Z"],["3850518","DSR-3351","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC, please send the following message to the driver along with the image:\n\n{quote}Dear [name],\n\nThank you for your follow-up.\n\nAs requested, we are providing records from our systems confirming that you provided consent for the sharing of a limited set of your personal data with our partner, Eternis.\n\nThese records show that you actively confirmed your consent on two occasions, on 25 April 2025 and 13 May 2025, via the Bolt app. The processing was carried out on the basis of your consent, in accordance with the applicable data protection framework. No personal data was shared prior to your consent being recorded.\n\nIf you no longer wish for your data to be used for this purpose, you may withdraw your consent at any time via your app settings or by contacting Customer Support. Withdrawal of consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal.\n\nBased on the above and the information already provided, we consider this aspect of your data subject access request to have been addressed in full.\n\nIf you believe there is any materially new information relevant to your request, please let us know.\n\nSincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}\n\n!Silviu Ionut Ghinea_Consent.png|width=622,alt=\"Silviu Ionut Ghinea_Consent.png\"!","2026-01-29T15:31:02.263Z"],["3850519","MKP-9949","MKP","andre.tamm@bolt.eu","Andre Tamm","Right, I had a go at this and created a draft PR with most of the changes. I think the only thing missing is adding brand to the call to {{/adminPanel/order/decline}} on the Admin Panel side. Will let you own actually releasing this as it touches quite a lot of your stuff - [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162400|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162400]. (Or alternatively if [@artem.markov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:786a23a6-5409-4cc1-9e53-e525f53a4332] wants to take over feel free)","2026-01-29T15:32:17.827Z"],["3850520","LSS-58697","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Hi [~accountid:5e0f07ab9a4b780d990e9fb9] thank you. Since we received many ticket connected with Bolt Drive incidents and/or fines within the last months, we would like to resolve these issues systematically. We aim to prepare a playbook for the Bolt Drive team with the description of relevant procedures, FAQ and draft messages. [~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] will take care of it.","2026-01-29T15:32:32.238Z"],["3850521","DRAG-668","DRAG","janeli.takk@bolt.eu","Janeli Takk","New version of Dragon battery repair SOP is ready for review. \n\n[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] Could you please review?","2026-01-29T15:33:12.347Z"],["3850522","PFI-840362","PFI","foyinsolami.daniels@bolt-outsource.eu","Foyinsolami Daniels","!{EB216FC7-39DC-4B8A-873B-5F4F4DA214C1}-20260129-153314.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T15:33:25.942Z"],["3850526","CSXRD-367","CSXRD","david.tomes@bolt.eu","David Tomeš","[No luck so far|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C091MT50SG0/p1769587209442149], as there is no bandwidth or will to support partner markets in forecasting.\n\n I will take this to Ivan in March and will build forecasting logic from scratch with UAE and Georgia CS teams","2026-01-29T15:34:01.943Z"],["3850527","C2-466","C2","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[~accountid:712020:7636318d-11ba-448e-8ae7-b935370c0640] Very good & comprehensive report, thanks [~accountid:712020:7636318d-11ba-448e-8ae7-b935370c0640] !","2026-01-29T15:34:12.468Z"],["3850530","LSS-62382","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:ad0f28bc-2e04-43b5-8352-a3a48fd3f720] , thank you for submitting this ticket. \n\nWe have collected the documents requested to the extent that we have access to them from within our legal scope. \n\nIn the attached zip file, you will find the following documents: \n\n*(3) General and legal documents → Kbis + UBO Register* [if you need any specific documents, please specify]\n\n*(4) Legal and functional organization chart of the Group*\n\n*(6) Latest updated articles of association*\n\n*(8) Management agreement and contracts with Group companies*\n\n*(9) + (10) Minutes and Resolutions submitted to General Meetings and draft resolutions, subject to availability*\n\n*(13) Statutory auditors’ reports*\n\n\n\nWith regards to the remaining corporate documents, please raise a ticket [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/47/group/159/create/742] to the Legal Ops team : \n\n*(1) Legal and operational organization chart of the company (Bolt Services France SARL)*\n\n*(2) Presentation of the strategic plan to the supervisory and oversight body and minutes of the meeting*\n\n*(5) Share capital structure of the company*\n\n*(7) Company governance and steering committees*\n\n*(11) Minutes and documents presented to the governance and supervisory body over the last three financial years (business monitoring, strategy, investments, partnerships, etc.)*\n\n\nFor the documents below, I think you should raise a ticket [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2446/group/3798/create/5761] to the Group Reporting and Financial Compliance team: \n\n*(12) Management report to the General Meeting*\n\n*(14) Details of items used to calculate employee profit-sharing (tax profit adjustments, RSP calculation elements) and profit-sharing agreement*\n\n*(15) Details of items used to calculate incentive schemes and incentive agreement*\n\n*(16) Details of items used in the calculation of the CSE subsidy*\n\n*(17) In the event of tax or social security audits: inventory and monitoring of ongoing and/or notified tax and social reassessments*\n\n\n\nAttachment: [^Documents Requested by Chartered Accountant-20260129T162329Z-3-001.zip] \n\n\n\nHappy to discuss further if you have any questions. \n\nThank you !\n\ncc. [~accountid:712020:b3dbddb5-16a8-4ad6-9138-80fbe6e695a9] \n\n","2026-01-29T15:34:51.883Z"],["3850531","C2-465","C2","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1B6fgyoR1caJswWUU3ANOVIVuA-yIobwvsui6CrQ4DlE/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1B6fgyoR1caJswWUU3ANOVIVuA-yIobwvsui6CrQ4DlE/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link]  - HW team formal investigation report from myself & [~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] ","2026-01-29T15:34:54.571Z"],["3850535","C2-465","C2","mihkel.klementsov@bolt.eu","Mihkel Klementsov","Waiting also for LOPS to ask recycling partner to identify all remaining batteries which can be identified so we can be more definitive about which battery was the root cause.","2026-01-29T15:35:35.873Z"],["3850538","CSCC-66","CSCC","margarita.hobo@bolt.eu","Margarita Hobo","The results were communicated in slack channel. Only 36 people completed the course. Here is the list with the results so far: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dlRe_jWG-8qXBMMNbvdo_G4i8YPB9P5OWS6XO7Om7Hw/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dlRe_jWG-8qXBMMNbvdo_G4i8YPB9P5OWS6XO7Om7Hw/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T15:36:55.470Z"],["3850539","FIS-4227","FIS","pavel.permenov@bolt.eu","Pavel Permenov","According to [Confluence|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/4022206963/Partner+Integrations+-+Adeopos], Adeopos doesn’t provide fiscalized pdfs, so the flow returns the error in Slovenia. In Croatia, the same flow returns a QR code. Need to either remove logging, or change the pdf request flow","2026-01-29T15:37:43.018Z"],["3850540","FIS-4227","FIS","pavel.permenov@bolt.eu","Pavel Permenov","[Slovenia|https://kibana-logs.elasticsearch.boltint.net/app/r/s/0ULKz]\n\n!image-20260129-153744.png|width=635,alt=\"image-20260129-153744.png\"!","2026-01-29T15:37:54.110Z"],["3850542","L10N-30903","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.071Z"],["3850543","L10N-30885","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.070Z"],["3850544","L10N-30891","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.119Z"],["3850545","L10N-30888","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.229Z"],["3850546","L10N-30892","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.276Z"],["3850547","L10N-30883","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.296Z"],["3850548","L10N-30900","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.306Z"],["3850549","L10N-30882","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.330Z"],["3850550","L10N-30884","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T15:38:05.349Z"],["3850551","L10N-30899","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","This task was recently updated.","2026-01-29T