!image-20260129-153835.png|width=635,alt=\"image-20260129-153835.png\"!","2026-01-29T15:38:45.688Z"],["3850587","LSS-62098","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348230|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348230|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T15:38:50.915Z"],["3850588","LSS-62421","LSS","patriks.akmanis@bolt.eu","Patriks Akmanis","[^VID_21.01.2026._30.4_17.20.4_6926_VID_rik_par_naudas_lidz_apkil_un_parskait_par_BOLT SERVICES LV SIA par FIRST PLACE SIA .docx] _(87 kB)_","2026-01-29T15:39:03.450Z"],["3850593","LSS-62098","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf3c0c77011bdfdcdbcd] sent out the document for signatures.","2026-01-29T15:39:38.557Z"],["3850598","LSS-48585","LSS","alexandra.laes@bolt.eu","Alexandra Laeș","Hi [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] ,\n\nKaufland sent the the signed contract. Can you please advice where is best to store it?\n\n\n\n[^LV - Anexa 03_6917_ BOLT SERVICES RO SRL.pdf]\n[^LV - Anexa 04_ 6917_ BOLT SERVICES RO SRL.pdf]\n[^LV - Anexa 05_6917_BOLT SERVICES RO SRL.pdf]\n[^LV - Anexa 06_6917_BOLT SERVICES RO SRL.pdf]\n[^LV - Anexa 07_6917_BOLT SERVICES RO SRL.pdf]\n[^PL - Anexa 02_ 6917_ BOLT SERVICES RO SRL.pdf]\n[^RV - BOLT SERVICES RO SRL Platforme livrare.pdf]\n[^DViA - BOLT SERVICES RO SRL Platforme livrare.pdf]\n[^LV - Anexa 01_ 6917_ BOLT SERVICES RO SRL.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-29T15:40:53.436Z"],["3850600","LSS-62275","LSS","dawit.villarzu@bolt.eu","Dawit Villarzu","[~accountid:712020:f0e74860-330c-44ed-9e8f-e89de3fd8d5c] \n\n\nThe following points outline the key legal and operational risks identified in the contract. I understand that there may be urgency to proceed. However, if the commercial approver intends to move forward without negotiating these points, the risks below should be explicitly approved before collecting signatures.\n\n# *Lack of defined service levels (SLA)*\n_Section: Support and Operations_\nThe contract does not include any service levels, availability commitments, data refresh frequency, or response times. This creates operational risk for Bolt given the business-critical nature of the data.\n# *Liability limitations undermine intended use of the software*\n_Section: Liability and Warranty_\nThe provider excludes liability for business or pricing decisions made based on the software output, although the software is explicitly intended to support such decisions. This shifts the full risk of incorrect or incomplete data to Bolt.\n# *Data protection assumptions not contractually safeguarded*\n_Section: Confidentiality and Data Protection_\nThe contract assumes that no personal data is processed but does not include a fallback mechanism (e.g. an obligation to enter into a DPA) if this assumption proves incorrect or changes over time.\n# *No data export or exit rights upon termination*\n_Section: Contract Termination_\nUpon termination, access to the software is immediately revoked, and the contract does not grant Bolt the right to export or retain historical data generated during the contract term.","2026-01-29T15:42:33.320Z"],["3850603","BP-13566","BP","anton.kukeste@bolt.eu","Anton Kukeste","Tested in feature preview branch\n\n[https://ridebooker.prelive.bolt.eu/bugfix-BP-XXX-correct-close-button-alignment/#/new-ride/|https://ridebooker.prelive.bolt.eu/bugfix-BP-XXX-correct-close-button-alignment/#/new-ride/vehicle-category]\n\nAlignment of “X” close button matches the expected (/) \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 17.42.19.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 17.42.19.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 17.42.38.png|width=645,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 17.42.38.png\"!","2026-01-29T15:44:00.011Z"],["3850604","PAW-15270","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @BoltCristianLupu\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162526\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-29 15:44:54 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-29T15:44:54.255Z"],["3850605","LSS-62410","LSS","liisa.aavik@bolt.eu","Liisa Aavik","Please see updated draft on this link with Ahto Kink as signatory: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/17WB3weJBj8Ai_k-lUhMNZyaF-4aTyGWn/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=111784691807109318676&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/17WB3weJBj8Ai_k-lUhMNZyaF-4aTyGWn/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=111784691807109318676&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link]  ","2026-01-29T15:45:12.063Z"],["3850606","LSS-62390","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Alright clear, thank you\n\nThe LL responded to Andrea and they have said now \"someday\" in March. Lets plan for last day of March in worst case.\n\nBut if we are all still aligned, then we will go with option 1 and keep the previous address, WX will let the LL know of the situation and will watch closely for any mail. \n\nThank you!","2026-01-29T15:45:50.608Z"],["3850607","HS-29553","HS","chiara.cotroneo@bolt.eu","Chiara Cotroneo","[^KH Millennium ZOZ Zaświadczenie o zatrudnieniu po POLSKU KO_DDD_1_11 zał. 10 05.06.2025.pdf]\n\n[^zaswiadczenie-o-zatrudnieniu-umowa-o-prace.pdf]","2026-01-29T15:46:03.856Z"],["3850608","LSS-62421","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-29T15:46:06.577Z"],["3850609","PAW-15273","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-29T15:46:30.386Z"],["3850611","LSS-62409","LSS","viktoriadebora.raudberg@bolt.eu","Debora Raudberg","Hey, [~accountid:712020:a975e2d9-679b-4d8a-a063-b831aafacd02]! The suggestion is to set Bonus as 350 000 and stipulate that it will be paid in instalments. The first 100 000 will be paid straight away as one instalment and each other payment is a separate instalment with conditions specified in Appendix 2. Please check Appendix 2 for conditions. \nI suggest handling commission issues outside of Addendum (in Special Terms, for example), but we can add them too as a separate appendix. \n\nPlease let me know if you have questions or need further help.","2026-01-29T15:47:49.398Z"],["3850613","LSS-61255","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","Hi team, all Annexes from LL referred to in this lease were sent today. Please see attached. [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] P\n\n[^Anlage 1.1_Umgebungsplan.docx]\n[^Anlage 1.4_Lagepläne.docx]\n[^Anlage 1.5_Gif.docx]\n[^Anlage 1.7.1_Vermieterbaubeschreibung.docx]\n[^Anlage 1.8.2_Mieterbaubeschreibung.docx]\n[^Anlage 2.4_Übergabeprotokoll.docx]\n[^Anlage 25.9_DSGVO.docx]\n[^Anlage 25.2_GP Kodex.docx]\n[^Anlage 22.1_Hausordnung.docx]\n[^Anlage 19.9 - RüProt.docx]\n[^Anlage 7.1_Sepa.docx]\n[^Anlage 6.1_Nebenkosten.docx]\n\n","2026-01-29T15:48:34.126Z"],["3850615","PFI-840370","PFI","endurance.lucky@bolt-outsource.eu","Endurance Lucky","!Transaction Receipt-260128020100622146241294.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T15:49:50.725Z"],["3850617","RCE-403","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769701950610969]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@sudipto.das>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RCE-403] `Review change logs for car tag updates` soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T15:52:42.093Z"],["3850618","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Simon Fournier [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769701990176449]*{color}:\nHi <@U02QJBWH8G4>,\n\nAn other case [here|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_timestamp%22%3A1756677600%2C%22end_timestamp%22%3A1769727599.999%2C%22all_order_try_states%22%3Atrue%2C%22driver_id%22%3A5686173%7D%7D], despite the \"-Taxi\"\n\ncc: <@U02TPHQNARF>\n\nLinked files:\n* [image.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ABSJ6KDT4/image.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-29T15:53:27.764Z"],["3850619","FIS-4230","FIS","konstantin.ofitserov@bolt.eu","Konstantin Ofitserov","Update.\n\nWe’ve came to conclusion, that some malicious automatization tools created unnecessary duplicates of credit invoices, and consequently the re-issues as well. \n\nIn a separated dedicated task, we’ll mitigate the future problems, but retrospectively the OPS input will be necessary. \n\n[~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946] So, what has to be done: Half of those simultaneously created credits and reissues have to be set to ignored. The rest should start correct chaining and processing, since there won’t be concurrent invoices in “waiting” status. ","2026-01-29T15:53:32.585Z"],["3850620","MM-980","MM","dias.abdraimov@bolt.eu","Dias Abdraimov","{noformat}SELECT * FROM `taxify_campaign_operations`.`pipelines` AS `p`\nWHERE EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1\n    FROM `taxify_campaign_operations`.`pipeline_actions` AS `pa_enrollment`\n    WHERE `pa_enrollment`.`pipeline_id` = `p`.`id`\n      AND `pa_enrollment`.`action_type` = 'SET_ENROLLMENT_LIMITS'\n)\n  AND NOT EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1\n    FROM `taxify_campaign_operations`.`pipeline_actions` AS `pa_usage`\n    WHERE `pa_usage`.`pipeline_id` = `p`.`id`\n      AND `pa_usage`.`action_type` = 'SET_USAGE_LIMITS'\n);{noformat}\n\nQuery to check pipelines where SetUsageLimits should be added\n","2026-01-29T15:53:33.650Z"],["3850622","PFI-840375","PFI","tiago.pinto@bolt-outsource.eu","Tiago Pinto","[^20260129_52141_680463_0000214756.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-29T15:55:19.010Z"],["3850633","WFM-9317","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! Prolonged permission for 1 month month, until we find a permanent solution - i will continue to keep this ticket open and let you know if I have updates 🙏 ","2026-01-29T15:59:46.340Z"],["3850635","WFM-9317","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541932|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541932]","2026-01-29T15:59:52.755Z"],["3850638","LSS-62422","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","Here are the documents that need to be signed, for the Netherlands and Germany respectively.\n\n[~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301], do you want to give approval before I send to signature?\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TRkt7XFWA9QQs3suMDRlsXEwM2HkSZLr/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=103082362273072080151&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TRkt7XFWA9QQs3suMDRlsXEwM2HkSZLr/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=103082362273072080151&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] \n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X0UtO5ibC6mkgPsIHOrrQ4aTzdceUeAt/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=103082362273072080151&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X0UtO5ibC6mkgPsIHOrrQ4aTzdceUeAt/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=103082362273072080151&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T16:00:30.038Z"],["3850641","WD-22731","WD","mihut.arsene@bolt.eu","Mihuț-Andrei Arsene","Hey Ewa,\n\nThank you for reaching out!\n\nThese off-board processes are fully completed so we are not able to correct this specific field.\n\nThere are two courses of action possible here:\n\n# You can rescind these terminations and resubmit them again with the correct details\n# We can close the positions manually after they become unfilled, which should be after 31/01/2025. \n\nPlease let me know which option is preferable!\n\nMany thanks,\n\nMihut","2026-01-29T16:01:17.454Z"],["3850645","LOC-5288","LOC","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","*Ad Copies* \n [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1gsU_9P-cLH78c_oRSRggQAA78Cb2AEH2zDOPOib1RU4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1gsU_9P-cLH78c_oRSRggQAA78Cb2AEH2zDOPOib1RU4/edit?gid=0#gid=0|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T16:02:35.923Z"],["3850650","PFI-808708","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Thank you, [~accountid:712020:876960aa-09c5-44ff-9c52-2cb24c637062] 🙂 \nI’ll close this ticket [~accountid:712020:16feeee2-7721-43a0-8e2d-529b2d00b3e8], if anything else, please feel free to create another one 🙂 ","2026-01-29T16:03:49.176Z"],["3850652","LSS-62275","LSS","sami.elchami@bolt.eu","Sami El-Chami","Thank you very much. I have requested adjustments and changes to the sections mentioned above and will get back shortly, so that [~accountid:5fc514a09592df00761a5d3d]  can proceed with the approval. \n\n","2026-01-29T16:05:04.837Z"],["3850653","DSR-1840","DSR","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*This is an internal note to indicate the results of the investigation:*\n\n# Our system retains the business payment method in a Bolt account even when the phone number changes.\n# A change of the phone number for the account should be automatically notified via email to the business admin, and it is the responsibility of the business customer to monitor and maintain the list of business users.\n# However, in this particular case, the email was not delivered. The issue with deliverability is not clear as *\"blocked_due_to_past_bounce\"* can have various reasons, such as the recipient’s mailbox being full or the email address being invalid.\n\nPrivacy is currently aligning with legal on the decision about the reimbursement before responding to the request.","2026-01-29T16:06:19.856Z"],["3850654","LSS-62189","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] Changed the wording + Added the question about how the data will be shared","2026-01-29T16:07:12.458Z"],["3850655","LSS-61908","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf] , I have slightly amended the draft as per [~accountid:5dde532fcdc2d20d05377446] 's input (thanks, Britta!). Please let me know if your team will take care of sending this or if you would prefer that Privacy continues handling this case via the DSR ticket previously opened by the Driver.\n\n{quote}Dear Mr Wixted,\n\nThank you for your message and for sharing your concerns in such detail. We appreciate the seriousness with which you are approaching this matter.\n\nAt Bolt, we are fully committed to complying with our obligations under UK data protection law, including the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR), and to supporting law enforcement and regulatory bodies in accordance with the law and our operator licensing requirements.\n\nWe understand that your concerns relate both to the outcome of a police investigation and to the data that Bolt provided to law enforcement and to you directly under your subject access request.\n\nTo ensure clarity, we would like to set out the following key points in response:\n\n# *Disclosure to Police and Law Enforcement*\n\nFollowing the report submitted via our Customer Support channels, Bolt notified the Metropolitan Police in accordance with our standard safety and incident-handling procedures, which apply in cases involving alleged criminal conduct. Transport for London was notified in parallel, in line with our regulatory obligations as a licensed private hire operator.\n\nThe information shared at that stage reflected the nature and scope of the initial report received and was provided for the purpose of recording that an allegation had been made. Bolt does not act as an investigating authority and does not assess or determine the relevance, credibility, or legal significance of information in this context.\n\nBolt does not sanitise, manipulate, or selectively withhold information. Where law enforcement submits a lawful and specific request for information, Bolt responds fully and in accordance with applicable law, while ensuring compliance with data protection requirements and the rights of all individuals involved.\n\nDecisions relating to the conduct, continuation, or closure of a criminal investigation rest solely with the relevant investigating authority. If you believe that material facts were not considered, we respectfully recommend submitting any new evidence directly to the investigating officer or through a formal complaint to the Metropolitan Police Service. Should the Metropolitan Police submit a renewed or additional lawful request, Bolt will respond accordingly and cooperate fully.\n\n# *Driver Information and Data Protection Law*\n\nUnder UK GDPR, your right to access personal data (Article 15) does not extend to data that solely identifies another individual, such as the driver, unless you are also identifiable from it and there is no adverse impact on their rights. Information such as GPS logs, internal driver notes, or operational details that relate only to the driver are classified as third-party personal data and are legally protected under Article 15(4) UK GDPR and Recital 63.\n\nWe have carefully reviewed your request and shared all personal data to which you are lawfully entitled, including records of your ride, relevant communications, and copies of the disclosures made to authorities. Redactions were applied where necessary to protect third-party rights, which is not only lawful but required under data protection legislation.\n\n# *Preservation of Records*\n\nWe acknowledge your request regarding the retention of specific data. Please be assured that Bolt maintains operational and safety-related records in accordance with our legal obligations and internal retention schedules. While no evidence of unlawful destruction has occurred, we take such concerns seriously and have ensured that the relevant records are preserved in line with applicable legal and regulatory frameworks.\n\n# *Cooperation with Transport for London*\n\nWe fully recognise the importance of our responsibilities under our Private Hire Operator's Licence issued by Transport for London. This includes the duty to cooperate with law enforcement and to maintain high standards of safety and transparency. Where serious incidents are reported, we notify TfL as required and in a timely manner.\n\nNo regulatory breach has occurred in this matter. We continue to work constructively with authorities and comply with all applicable licensing and privacy obligations.\n\n# *Closing Remarks*\n\nWe understand the gravity of the concerns you have raised and assure you that we do not take them lightly. At the same time, we must act in strict compliance with the law. We are unable to disclose information about third parties, or resubmit data to law enforcement in the absence of a lawful request.\n\nShould the Metropolitan Police Service wish to reopen or further review the case, we will of course respond fully and lawfully to any renewed request.\n\nWe thank you again for your engagement, and should you have any further questions relating specifically to the processing of your own personal data, these can be addressed to [privacy@bolt.eu|mailto:privacy@bolt.eu].\n\nYours sincerely,{quote}","2026-01-29T16:07:14.700Z"],["3850656","CEBF-1702","CEBF","bophana.ros@bolt.eu","Bophana Ros","[~accountid:712020:c573470a-712d-474e-a9e6-b0635a9decb9] AC1: we can have multiple Approved but only 1 Active?","2026-01-29T16:07:31.000Z"],["3850657","CSXSF-143","CSXSF","thomas.schwalm@bolt.eu","Thomas Schwalm","Kickoff meeting with assigned RIC on Monday","2026-01-29T16:07:38.363Z"],["3850658","VERIFY-3431","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-29T16:08:29.893Z"],["3850659","LSS-62377","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Thanks for raising a ticket [~accountid:712020:e81c1984-54f1-46ce-bc81-864b3748de94] I will come back to you next week. ","2026-01-29T16:09:07.632Z"],["3850660","PFI-840385","PFI","diana.bernyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Diana Bernyk","[^Виписка по рахунку.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-29T16:09:18.758Z"],["3850662","LSS-61844","LSS","catalin.jitariu@bolt.eu","Cătălin-Ioan Jitariu","ok. i have send the document to external partner for review. will be coming back with feedback. ","2026-01-29T16:10:56.945Z"],["3850663","VERIFY-3782","VERIFY","daniel.berbece@bolt.eu","Daniel Berbece","Was fixed by refactoring to use the actual content_type","2026-01-29T16:11:20.581Z"],["3850664","INT-875","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-29T16:11:38.535Z"],["3850666","PFI-840387","PFI","israel.kizito@bolt-outsource.eu","Israel Kizito","!IMG-20260129-WA0010.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T16:12:03.548Z"],["3850667","MKP-9913","MKP","andre.tamm@bolt.eu","Andre Tamm","Summary:\n\n* Have added {{brand}} to Pricing’s cancellation endpoints. We will propagate them through to Subscription when checking for subscription benefits. - \n* We also need Order to start populating the brand when calling Pricing.\n** Created thread with them here - [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1769602296972349|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1769602296972349|smart-link] \n** Had a go at doing an implementation for this as well, but this quickly grew arms and legs, so will let the Order team finish it - [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162400|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162400|smart-link] \n\nMarking as done from Pricing’s side","2026-01-29T16:12:05.867Z"],["3850668","LSS-62065","LSS","catalin.jitariu@bolt.eu","Cătălin-Ioan Jitariu","can you help with the signature [~accountid:712020:b1700666-82b2-4a86-82f7-550a84f716c8] ? thank you.\n\n","2026-01-29T16:12:27.475Z"],["3850673","DRX-28266","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/DRIVERAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/DRIVERAPP-R4623\"","2026-01-29T16:13:35.834Z"],["3850674","MKP-8428","MKP","albert.tumanov@bolt.eu","Albert Tumanov","Another alert [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02QFQ2T8AJ/p1769697849398819|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02QFQ2T8AJ/p1769697849398819]","2026-01-29T16:13:52.040Z"],["3850679","INT-555","INT","jina.park@bolt.eu","Jina Park","[~accountid:712020:45e1e9dd-4ff8-4dec-9b59-10c172ba5e54] this is the task on eater app profile, perhaps can move priority to P0. Right now in Q2 pipeline but can discuss if we should move to Q1 and implement as soon as we have mobile eng support.","2026-01-29T16:15:59.740Z"],["3850680","PFI-840225","PFI","gerard.everaert@bolt.eu","Gerard Everaert","Hi [~accountid:557058:b2aaf2b9-4465-40fe-b31b-1711dbe61946] , no idea why they cannot see it. Before going to Mazars and spend fees let’s please get something from Fonoa as this is their responsibility. Let me know if you get anything from them please. \n\n\n\n","2026-01-29T16:16:12.218Z"],["3850684","VERIFY-3431","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162549","2026-01-29T16:18:28.938Z"],["3850685","VERIFY-3883","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-29T16:18:30.130Z"],["3850686","VERIFY-3891","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-29T16:18:31.081Z"],["3850687","VERIFY-4083","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-29T16:18:31.945Z"],["3850688","PFI-809103","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hi, checked with engineering, best to our knowledge this is how customer discounts should be visualised in the app. + sign in front means that it has been added to the balance. ","2026-01-29T16:18:32.254Z"],["3850690","DINE-968","DINE","simona.andries@bolt.eu","Simona Andries","Duplicate with : [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DINE-989|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DINE-989|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T16:19:41.757Z"],["3850692","LSS-56938","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] - a simple but important question:\nWhat’s our usual approach on when to close tickets?\nFor example, in this case the document is already finalized, counterparty has agreed with all the changes and ready to sign, but in fact the document isn’t signed yet - should I close the ticket or should I wait until the document gets signed?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-29T16:20:01.356Z"],["3850693","PAW-14087","PAW","dmitrii.shilonosov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Shilonosov","Superseded by [PAW-15235|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAW-15235]/[PAW-15236|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAW-15236] (local validation approach)","2026-01-29T16:20:01.914Z"],["3850696","PAW-15051","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-jenkins, pint-product-continuous-integration-and-deployment-platform, pint-capability-ci-cd\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-29T16:20:48.941Z"],["3850697","PAW-15051","PAW","dmitrii.shilonosov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Shilonosov","Rejected because long-running task support is not feasible in the current coding agents ","2026-01-29T16:20:50.656Z"],["3850698","PAW-14087","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-local-setup, pint-product-local-development-experience, pint-capability-devx\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-29T16:20:56.741Z"],["3850699","PAW-15052","PAW","dmitrii.shilonosov@bolt.eu","Dmitrii Shilonosov","rejected because the task this one depends on is rejected: [PAW-15051|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PAW-15051]","2026-01-29T16:21:33.650Z"],["3850704","LSS-62423","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","*Here are the preliminary results of the investigation with BB engineering & identity teams on what happened:*\n\n*User Details:*\n\n* *Mom (Elīna Račko):*\n** Phone Number: [+37129902179|tel:+37129902179]\n** Ridehailing User ID: [240311275|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/240311275/overview]\n* *Son (Artis Račko):*\n** Phone Number: [+37122091070|tel:+37122091070]\n** Ridehailing User ID: [884579|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/884579/overview]\n\n*Timeline of Events and Linking Issue:*\n\n# *Initial Setup:* Ridehailing user ID [884579|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/884579/overview] (Son) was initially registered with the phone number [+37129902179|tel:+37129902179](which was also linked to Business user ID [248944|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/business-portal/businessUsers/248944]).\n# *Nov 10, 2024: Phone Number Change (Son):* The ridehailing user with ID [884579|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/884579/overview] changed the phone number from [+37129902179|tel:+37129902179] to [+37122091070|tel:+37122091070] (see [account details history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/884579/history?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A50%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22property_type%22%3A%5B%5D%7D%7D]).\n# *Automatic Business Link Update:* This ridehailing phone number change _automatically triggered_ an update on the business side, changing the linked Business user's phone number to [+37122091070|tel:+37122091070]. The link between the Business user and ridehailing user [884579|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/884579/overview] was thus maintained. See the [log|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/audit-log/audit-logs/view/3778498383] on business side.\n# *Nov 12, 2024: New Account Creation (Mom):* A new ridehailing account (ID [240311275|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/240311275/overview] - Mom) was created using the old phone number, [+37129902179|tel:+37129902179] (see [account details history|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/240311275/history?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D]).\n# *No New Business Link:* Because the original Business user's phone number had already been changed, there was no business user registered with [+37129902179|tel:+37129902179] anymore. Therefore, the Mom's new account creation did not trigger a new business link.\n\n*Communication Failure:*\n\n* We attempted to send an email notification to the Business customer admin about the Business user's phone number change, but the sending process was blocked. \n* The issue with deliverability is due to the following block applied on mail server side - *\"blocked_due_to_past_bounce\".* This block is due to email delivery deemed to be undeliverable by the mail server, and this can have various reasons, such as the recipient’s mailbox being full or the email address being invalid. Exact reason cannot be confirmed.\n\n*Email delivery deemed to be undeliverable by the mail server - possible underlying reasons by AI:*\n\nAWS SES permanent (hard) bounces occur when an email is permanently rejected by the recipient’s mail server, typically due to invalid addresses, domain issues, or policy blocks. These bounces indicate the email will never be delivered, causing SES to add the address to its suppression list to protect sender reputation. \nCommon permanent bounce reasons in SES include:\n* *Invalid Recipient Address:* The most common cause; the mailbox does not exist, the domain is incorrect, or the user has left the organization.\n* *Recipient Mailbox Full (Persistent):* While often a soft bounce, if a mailbox remains full for an extended period, it may eventually be classified as a permanent failure.\n* *Blocked by Recipient ISP:* The receiving mail server is blocking emails from your domain or IP address due to poor sender reputation, high complaint rates, or policy violation.\n* *General/Protocol Errors:* Misconfigured DNS records (SPF, DKIM) or 500-level SMTP response codes that indicate a non-retryable error.\n* *Suppression List Activation:* If a user previously complained or bounced, their address is added to the [SES suppression list|https://www.google.com/search?q=SES+suppression+list&sca_esv=ccd4ef3e8288fb18&rlz=1C5CHFA_enPL1031PL1033&sxsrf=ANbL-n55j3RcQhE65si_1SOC-KczUPy5Bw%3A1769703973063&ei=JYp7ab-5A-yB9u8P5JmLwAk&ved=2ahUKEwjDjvGGlbGSAxWehf0HHWhWF1oQgK4QegQIAxAF&uact=5&oq=aws+ses+permanent+bounce+reasons&gs_lp=Egxnd3Mtd2l6LXNlcnAiIGF3cyBzZXMgcGVybWFuZW50IGJvdW5jZSByZWFzb25zMgUQABjvBTIFEAAY7wUyCBAAGIAEGKIEMgUQABjvBTIFEAAY7wVI1g1QqgRY8wxwAXgBkAEAmAFuoAHVBaoBAzcuMbgBA8gBAPgBAZgCB6ACnwTCAgoQABhHGNYEGLADwgIKECEYChigARjDBMICCBAhGKABGMMEmAMAiAYBkAYIkgcDNi4xoAe1GbIHAzUuMbgHnATCBwMzLjTIBwmACAE&sclient=gws-wiz-serp], causing future attempts to immediately bounce.","2026-01-29T16:23:12.940Z"],["3850705","DRIVE-315","DRIVE","anton.diatlov@bolt.eu","Anton Diatlov","We aligned with Operations to deprioritize the initiative for Poland, as service is live with 3P fleet.","2026-01-29T16:23:18.643Z"],["3850706","LSS-61486","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","[~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] \nSince I see that privacy assistance isn’t needed here - I will go ahead and close the ticket\nIf anything comes-up - please feel free to reach out by tagging me.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-29T16:24:15.331Z"],["3850709","DRX-27862","DRX","mariia.nazarenko@bolt.eu","Mariia Nazarenko","2QA: Please check how badge style elements look like:\n\non campaigns status badge: [https://www.figma.com/design/joGnRytBS6PafnEIMyd2ai/Campaigns?node-id=14850-6230&t=TquthbxS3kvoNSTA-11|https://www.figma.com/design/joGnRytBS6PafnEIMyd2ai/Campaigns?node-id=14850-6230&t=TquthbxS3kvoNSTA-11|smart-link] \n\ncar application statuses badges (don’t have updated design, just check how draft, in review, incomplete, declined statuses for applications look like (should be readable and visible in dark/light modes)\n\nmap area labels (surge): [https://www.figma.com/design/o1gaegw5v81otjLlPOK5fb/Driver-UI-Kit?node-id=9814-10710&t=Y8l9fi5G8XdkL9uf-11|https://www.figma.com/design/o1gaegw5v81otjLlPOK5fb/Driver-UI-Kit?node-id=9814-10710&t=Y8l9fi5G8XdkL9uf-11|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T16:25:43.202Z"],["3850710","LSS-61886","LSS","rachel.sallnow@bolt.eu","Rachel Sallnow","Hi [~accountid:5d9c300987dd6f0dcb4d2b58] \n\nI’ve attached a draft fleet agreement for your review [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nZ-zqhsAGmwiaaV_5y29UifCcrZFEWfu/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=114805727268611303315&rtpof=true&sd=true]. Please review and complete the points where I’ve flagged that further detail is required.\n\nThe agreement assumes that the fleet will operate in London under the Bolt Standard (principal) model. It is structured as an agreement between Bolt and the fleet and, on the basis of the current proposal, assumes that we do not have a direct contractual relationship with individual fleet drivers and that they would not accept Bolt terms directly. *Please let me know if that assumption is not correct.*\n\nThe agreement reflects a structure where drivers engaged by the fleet are treated as self-employed and has been revised (from the previous Abbis version) so that the contractual terms are consistent with that model and reduce overt indicators of control.\n\nThat said, there remains *material legal risk from a reclassification perspective*. Under UK law, courts and regulators assess the practical reality of arrangements rather than contractual labels alone, and given Bolt’s role as PHV operator and platform controller in London, there remains a possibility that drivers could be reclassified as workers or employees of Bolt notwithstanding the drafting. This could have implications in areas such as worker status, auto-enrolment/pensions, and related regulatory considerations. While the agreement includes indemnities to allocate risk between Bolt and the fleet, these would not override any statutory or regulatory determinations.\n\nHappy to discuss further if helpful. Thanks.\n\n\n","2026-01-29T16:25:50.086Z"],["3850711","DRIVE-314","DRIVE","anton.diatlov@bolt.eu","Anton Diatlov","Kicked-off the engineering work after the meeting with Skycash. Ongoing work on tech design. ","2026-01-29T16:26:17.201Z"],["3850712","DRIVE-305","DRIVE","anton.diatlov@bolt.eu","Anton Diatlov"," Implemented the logic on storing data on order level.Order creation prevention mechanism is not implemented, until the legal assessment is done.  ","2026-01-29T16:26:39.720Z"],["3850714","DINE-988","DINE","simona.andries@bolt.eu","Simona Andries","Do we still need this? My understanding was that we won’t cluster the restaurants anymore. So I suppose we won’t need to discover other DineOut cities.","2026-01-29T16:26:44.067Z"],["3850717","PFI-840395","PFI","rita.magova@bolt-outsource.eu","Rita Magova","!IMG_4751.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T16:27:56.636Z"],["3850718","VERIFY-3891","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162553","2026-01-29T16:28:28.948Z"],["3850719","PFI-840396","PFI","rita.magova@bolt-outsource.eu","Rita Magova","!IMG_4750.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T16:30:32.649Z"],["3850723","PFI-814802","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Billing does not make the decision to remove bonuses though. \n\nAlso, i see the bonus is in t[he company balance|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/balanceHistory?balanceHistoryFilterSearch=%7B%22external_id%22%3A27459%2C%22type%22%3A%22Company%22%2C%22month%22%3A%7B%22year%22%3A2026%2C%22month%22%3A1%7D%2C%22viewType%22%3A%22weekly%22%2C%22week%22%3A%7B%22start%22%3A1764540000000%2C%22end%22%3A1765144799999%7D%7D]\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 18.29.34.png|width=1121,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 18.29.34.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 18.30.08.png|width=1121,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 18.30.08.png\"!","2026-01-29T16:31:33.545Z"],["3850724","LSS-61925","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hi [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] 👋 Reviewed the DPA ([*uploaded to GDrive*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1w2PJC6oKfXySTD4GyICrZoFWSR9rQlMH/edit] for better collaboration) and here are my comments:\n\n* *Section 7:* We are obligated to comply with their instructions regarding security measures - and this is why it’s extremely important for [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] to review the requirements. Flagging these measures, in case they’re not included to the document that [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] is reviewing:\n** The Data Processor undertakes to continuously log access to the Personal Data in accordance with the PUB Agreement to the extent required by the Instruction. Logs may only be deleted five (5) years after the time of logging, unless otherwise specified in the Instruction. Logs shall be subject to the necessary protective measures in accordance with data protection legislation.\n** The personal data processor shall systematically test, investigate and evaluate the effectiveness of the technical and organisational measures to ensure the security of the Processing.\n* *Section 8*: Internal comment, but we’ll need to inform them about data subject requests - fyi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] - we can discuss this separately.\n** _If the Data Subject, supervisory authority or third party requests information from the Data Processor concerning the Processing, the Data Processor shall inform the Data Controller of this. Information about the Processing may not be disclosed to the Data Subject, supervisory authority or third party without the written consent of the Data Controller, unless disclosure is required by mandatory law. The Data Processor shall assist in the disclosure of information covered by consent or legal requirements._ \n* *Clause 9.2.* - We will need to do self-audits once a year\n** _The data processor shall review the security of the Processing at least once (1) a year through a self-assessment to ensure that the Processing complies with the PUB Agreement. The results of such self-assessment shall be communicated to the data controller upon request._\n* *Clause 9.6*. - We will need to ensure that our sub-processor (partner) complies with the same security requirements (this is broadly covered via our DSA) - fyi [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] :\n** _The Data Processor shall ensure that the Data Controller has rights vis-à-vis the Sub-processor that correspond to all of the Data Controller's rights vis-à-vis the Data Processor under section9 of the PUB Agreement._  \n* [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] this is something we’ll need to bring up with engineering - upon termination of the agreement, we will need to either return or delete data.\n* Annex 1 - [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] can you help me by filling out the annex? We need to add information on what data we’ll factually process.\n\n\n\nOverall the agreement is standard, and not unexpected, however, since we will act as a data processor (act under the instructions of Upplands-Bro), we will bare much more liability than we usually would - but since these agreements are basically non-negotiable, this is not news to us.\n\nTo sum up, I wanted to flag the additional security requirements for [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] 's awareness, and to ask [~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] to fill in the table I tagged you in 🙂 ","2026-01-29T16:32:02.225Z"],["3850728","LSS-60580","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] [~accountid:5fb227c70d2f61006ff6cce2] just wanted to thank you for the additional information and let you know that there are no additional amendments from privacy side. We’ll need to see how they react to our changes, and if they insist on us having opt-out.","2026-01-29T16:33:27.931Z"],["3850729","VERIFY-3883","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162554","2026-01-29T16:33:28.987Z"],["3850731","LOC-5291","LOC","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","* [New Rider Signup Ads - Promo Code - Meta|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/18/MA-6664?created=true]\n* [New Rider Signup Ads - Promo Code - Google|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/18/MA-6665?created=true]\n* [New Rider Signup Ads - Promo Code - TikTok|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/18/MA-6666?created=true]\n* [New Rider Signup Ads - Promo Code - Snap|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/18/MA-6667?created=true]","2026-01-29T16:34:34.973Z"],["3850732","LSS-60080","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hello [~accountid:712020:da5adcfc-e0e5-4c21-a4df-4e108cffc244] \nJust checking in on 👇 ","2026-01-29T16:34:41.513Z"],["3850733","LOC-5291","LOC","liam.wentworth@bolt.eu","Liam Wentworth","Tickets submitted (should be added by 30th January. ","2026-01-29T16:34:54.326Z"],["3850734","PFI-840399","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","[^VFR 2026 36 - PT1526-1054 (87ae4aee-7484-498e-a5fe-5817af5a3226).pdf]","2026-01-29T16:35:08.716Z"],["3850735","PFI-840399","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T16:35:10.933Z"],["3850739","PFI-840400","PFI","anna.korniienko@bolt-outsource.eu","Anna Korniienko","[^Виписка по рахунку-2.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-29T16:35:58.599Z"],["3850740","LSS-62208","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","h2. Top-level Summary\n\n*Type of Agreement:* DPA (Controller–Processor)\n*Roles Defined:*\n\n* *Customer (Bolt)* – Controller or Processor\n* *Persona* – Always a Processor\n\n*Role Clarity:* Clear that Persona acts only as Processor; aligns with Bolt’s DPA C–P expectations.\n\n*Obvious Gaps / Red Flags:*\n\n* Sub-processor notice period is 30 days (aligned with Bolt’s expectations)\n* Breach notification is \"without undue delay\" but not explicitly 24h\n* Certification of deletion only provided _on request_\n* AI/automated processing/profiling not mentioned — could be relevant given biometric data processed\n\nWill see if we can use our template for better protection, and if not, will focus on biometric data/security requirements.","2026-01-29T16:36:05.697Z"],["3850742","PFI-840401","PFI","clara.machado@bolt.eu","Clara Oliveira Machado","[^VFR 2026 36 - PT1526-1054 (ed9c81d4-aaf1-49bc-af7e-7712ecec9295).pdf]","2026-01-29T16:37:32.722Z"],["3850743","PFI-840401","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T16:37:35.255Z"],["3850744","VERIFY-4083","VERIFY","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162555","2026-01-29T16:38:28.971Z"],["3850748","LSS-62208","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:10c3f4ef-f975-47a3-8af8-927b01cd9521] , I’ve reviewed the DPA, and my primary recommendation is to try and push for our standard template instead.\n\nThere are a few issues with their draft that raise concerns, particularly given that we’ll be sharing *biometric data* (specifically, *facial geometry*) with them. Notably:\n\n* There’s *no restriction on AI/profiling or secondary use*, which is a red flag given the sensitivity of the data.\n* There’s *no specific indemnity* for data protection breaches, and liability is tied to the main agreement only, which is not sufficient considering the risk exposure (FYI [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] )\n\nThe remaining issues (like the lack of automatic deletion certification and a less defined breach timeline) are relatively minor and could be addressed, but overall I think it’s cleaner and safer if we try to align on our template.\n\nLet me know if you think there’s appetite on their side to go this route - I can draft an email you could send them, explaining why the switch is necessary, and will share the Bolt DPA template with you as well.\n\nCC [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] for visibility only\n\n\n\n❗ there is one other option - to proceed with edits to their DPA now, and then renegotiate the DPA (move to our template) when MSA is negotiated. While this is an option, I don’t recommend it, as we’ll lose some negotiating power/leverage, as they’ll see we need them, and they might push us to sign 🙂 ","2026-01-29T16:40:45.980Z"],["3850750","LSS-62208","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","CC [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d]  just flagging this for your visibility as it’s verification-related.\n\nPersona is offering us free testing sessions for their identity verification product, which will involve the processing of biometric data (facial geometry). I've reviewed their DPA and there are a few key issues:\n\n* No restriction on profiling, AI, or secondary use, which is a gap given the sensitive nature of the data\n* No specific indemnity, liability is only tied to the main agreement\n* Some softer issues like deletion certification only on request, and breach notice not fixed to 24h\n\nGiven these, my recommendation to Mikk is to push for our standard DPA template instead of negotiating theirs - we’d get stronger protection up front, especially if this tool is adopted longer term.\n\nNot expecting action from your side right now, just keeping you in the loop due to the nature of the processing 🙏 ","2026-01-29T16:42:19.005Z"],["3850751","LSS-60746","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Fine from a privacy POV, but let’s wait until [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] provides her green light 😉 ","2026-01-29T16:43:18.066Z"],["3850752","LEG-1325","LEG","jack.cook@bolt.eu","Jack Cook","Hi [~accountid:612f31d89976c300693ebaf7] thanks for that - answers below - \n\n* (1) Who are the ultimate end users of the coupons? Is it for _all_ users (i.e. anyone that the Business Client gives them to, including people with personal accounts) or is it intended to be restricted to users with ‘business accounts / special access' only? FYI this question is relevant for the 4X27 considerations. {color:#ff5630}Anyone the business client gives them to. {color}\n* (2) Do you care, from the perspective of Bolt Business, if coupons are used for 4X27 rides? {color:#bf2600}Generally, no - our net rate will be the same if not higher should a coupon user use a coupon on a ride with 4X27 so not a deal breaker. If we needed to exclude 4X27 we could in theory limit which categories are eligible for coupons in Denmark.{color}\n* (3) Just FYI it appears that Bolt Business users in DK can currently book 4X27 rides and pay them via Bolt Business. Is that intentional? {color:#ff5630}Yes, our take-rate is always the same if not higher than RH so access to 4X27 is fine as it provides greater supply to our business users.{color}\n\nLet us know if you need anything else but sounds promising.","2026-01-29T16:43:40.418Z"],["3850753","PFI-840402","PFI","acharapon.pakwongtong@bolt-outsource.eu","Acharapon Pakwongtong","!image-20260129-163815.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T16:44:34.894Z"],["3850755","SREDESK-7477","SREDESK","kourosh.tafreshi@bolt.eu","Kourosh Tafreshi","Sorry, but what you’re asking for is still not relevant.\n\nPlease keep in mind that we can’t grant Admin access or broad access to all AWS services. There are dedicated SRE teams responsible for deploying and managing services in AWS.\n\nSo please either:\n\n* Clearly specify which service you need access to and for what purpose, or\n* Submit your request through Service Desk or via #foundation-roadmap-planning on Slack.\n\nCC: [~accountid:712020:205df993-8214-4419-a7d5-8306997511f9] for visibility.","2026-01-29T16:45:20.651Z"],["3850756","PAW-15276","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @hekan\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17391\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-29 16:46:05 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-29T16:46:05.719Z"],["3850757","PAW-15271","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162526\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-29 16:46:12 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-29T16:46:12.901Z"],["3850759","HS-29558","HS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","[^Simonas Kuzabavicius - Bolt Reference Letter.pdf]","2026-01-29T16:47:26.798Z"],["3850765","LSS-62423","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\n*Request* [~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] *:*\n\nBased on the interactions with the complainant so far, we will be faced with a reimbursement claim.\n\n*I would like to align with legal if you would agree to reimburse the customer to deescalate the matter.*\n{panel}\n\n*From the investigation results, I am in favour of deescalation & reimbursement. Suggesting to discuss via a separate call if you disagree.*\n\n*Expand - deescalation reasoning.*\n\n# Per BB T&Cs, the Business Customer (“Customer”) is responsible for maintaining a valid list of users who are authorised to use its payment method.\n# However, in this specific case, Bolt failed to notify the Customer of the phone number update. While it can be argued that responsibility for monitoring authorised users ultimately remains with the Customer—and that the missed notification may have been caused by outdated admin contact details—the Customer could plausibly argue that:\n## it would still expect updates from Bolt of any automatic Business User details change; and\n## it is not reasonable to expect from the Customer continuous manual monitoring of a long Business User list.\n# Bolt’s system design is never communicated to the Business Customer: the business payment method is linked to a user ID rather than to a phone number, however, when the Customer adds a new Business User, its done by adding a new phone number; Bolt user ID is an optional field. As a result, the recipient of the business payment method can change following a phone number update without any action by the Customer.\n\n{panel:bgColor=#ffebe6}\nI see multiple avenue how Bolt could potentially defend its position. Customers are still ultimately responsible for maintaining the list of Business Users.\n\nHowever, I also believe that declining to offer reimbursement (EUR 900) *will have high reputational risk*. If the matter were to become public, Bolt Business could be perceived as an unsafe and unreliable service.\n{panel}","2026-01-29T16:51:53.549Z"],["3850767","LSS-62423","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","I am adding [~accountid:712020:ef6a9562-f9aa-4bb5-a4d5-2b18cc77085b] as the Account Admin of the Business Customer involved - feel free to ask him additional questions if needed.","2026-01-29T16:53:10.236Z"],["3850768","LSS-62423","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Adding [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] for visibility.","2026-01-29T16:55:05.703Z"],["3850770","DRX-28385","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: **Test Scenarios:**\n1. **Feature disabled**: Counter-offer UI should not appear when feature flags are off\n2. **Idle state**: Verify \"Accept\" and \"Change Price\" buttons are shown\n3. **Price adjustment**: Test +/- buttons respect price bounds (min/max)\n4. **Submit flow**: Verify loading state shows while submitting counter-offer\n5. **Waiting state**: Confirm countdown timer displays correctly after submission\n6. **Empty prices**: When backend returns empty `prices` array, only \"Accept\" button should show (no \"Change Price\")","2026-01-29T16:56:06.120Z"],["3850771","DSR-2999","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi CSPC,\n\n{quote}Please send the following message to the rider:\nDear Sharon,\n\nThank you for your further message regarding your data subject access request. We have reviewed the points you raised and provide the following clarifications.\n\nWe confirm that Bolt carried out reasonable and proportionate searches across all systems available to Bolt that may contain rider-related personal data. This included systems used for account management, trip management, customer support, and safety and trust functions. These searches included reviews of account-level records, support metadata, and safety or trust-related workflows, to the extent such systems contain personal data relating to riders. Following these searches, we confirm that no internal notes, profile notes, flags, or automated system records specifically referencing you or your trips were identified, beyond the information already provided to you under the applicable data protection framework.\n\nWe also confirm that no driver reports, complaints, ratings comments, or incident notes referencing you, your account, or your journeys were identified. More generally, some categories of information you referred to, such as driver-side notes or reports, would primarily relate to the driver’s activity, performance, and account history and constitute personal data of the driver. Where applicable, Bolt considers whether redaction or anonymisation would enable disclosure of a data subject’s personal data. In this case, as no such driver-side records referencing you were identified, there is no personal data to disclose.\n\nYou have already been provided with trip-level data relating to the trips identified, including dates, times, pick-up and drop-off locations, and ride status information. Bolt does not provide raw GPS route telemetry, detailed system timestamps, or backend event logs. This information forms part of technical system records generated for operational purposes and is not held in a format that would be intelligible or meaningful to a data subject under Article 15 UK GDPR. The provision of such data would not add further insight beyond the trip-level information already disclosed.\n\nWe further confirm that the system used to manage safety audio recordings fell within the scope of our search. Audio Trip Recordings are only generated where a safety recording feature is actively enabled during a trip by either user (Driver or Passenger). Recordings are stored locally on the user’s device and are automatically deleted if not shared with Bolt, or otherwise retained for a limited period in accordance with the retention periods described in our Privacy Notice. We confirm that no audio recordings relating to the trips listed in your request existed at the time your access request was received, and no recordings had been created or retained in relation to those trips.\n\nIn summary, Bolt carried out searches for your personal data across systems used for the provision of ride services, customer support, and safety and trust functions, insofar as those systems contain rider-related personal data. No search limitations were applied other than excluding purely technical or system-level logs that do not contain personal data in an intelligible form.\n\nBased on the searches performed, we confirm that no further personal data relating to you is held by Bolt within the scope of your request. We therefore consider your data subject access request to have been addressed in full. You retain the right to complain directly to your data protection or supervisory authority and, depending on the applicable data protection laws in your country, to seek a judicial remedy.\n\nSincerely,\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-29T16:56:08.941Z"],["3850781","PFI-840417","PFI","jutamas.poldok@bolt-outsource.eu","Jutamas Poldok","!image-20260129-170508.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T17:05:19.650Z"],["3850784","PFI-836555","PFI","ogechukwu.ohaji@bolt-outsource.eu","Ogechukwu Ohaji","Hi Team,\n\nPayment [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75602188?filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Africa%2FLagos] for the commission paid that has not reflected.","2026-01-29T17:06:23.328Z"],["3850785","PFI-840420","PFI","jutamas.poldok@bolt-outsource.eu","Jutamas Poldok","!image-20260129-170633.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T17:06:41.337Z"],["3850794","LSS-61443","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","Hi [~accountid:712020:d59118c4-a302-4b14-bfb9-2a1051013c63], any update on the addendum. ","2026-01-29T17:13:43.057Z"],["3850798","GROWTH-381","GROWTH","gergo.zavecz@bolt.eu","Gergõ Závecz","*UPDATES* {{2026-01-29}}\n\n* Although we created the dynamic holdout segmentation notebook and the relevant confluence playbook last year and transferred it to the vertical team, the static holdouts notebook was not done then. I am currently working on its implementation.","2026-01-29T17:19:19.264Z"],["3850799","RCE-403","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Max Shashkov [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769707248194039]*{color}:\n<#C0576CT9MQD> \n{quote}","2026-01-29T17:21:01.601Z"],["3850800","RCE-403","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769707275288999]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-403 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T17:21:28.228Z"],["3850804","WFM-10217","WFM","aurelija.jovani@bolt-outsource.eu","Aurelija Jovani","!assembled.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T17:27:03.108Z"],["3850805","CNT-461","CNT","adam.cherry@bolt.eu","Adam Cherry","Hey! I’ve pushed the deadline back a bit to give us time for editorial. \n\nWe just need to confirm:\n\n* The launch email (see question in Figma)\n* OOH 2 (we could even give the Editors some options and get their advice)\n\nLet me know. Thanks!","2026-01-29T17:27:14.903Z"],["3850806","LSS-62341","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:255e9251-2a80-4b03-82b7-1ebc3abacf51], thank you for raising this ticket. \n\n+*Template to use*+\n\nOne a first note, as the partner is requesting for detailed indemnification obligations, I would suggest using the French translation of the standard agreement: [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cytkG-9bRzByhaqwVzzoI38GrQe_cksj/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cytkG-9bRzByhaqwVzzoI38GrQe_cksj/edit|smart-link]  \n\n\n\n+*Revised simplified agreement*+\n\nIf you still wish to use the French short form agreement, you will find some amendments in track changes in the document with comments for you to review. \n\n+With regards to the IP rights+, I have added a mutual right to retain ownership over brand, allowed Klub to retain ownership over the content they create, however, included a clause to allow Bolt to use this content for free and continuously after the partnership campaign. \n\nI am not convinced that this wording will be accepted by the partner. Please could you share some insight as to what the partner is trying to achieve? \n\nIf they retain the rights, do they want to continue to exploit this content past the duration of the campaign? Is this something that we want to allow them to do? \n\n+With regards to the indemnification+, can you clarify what are the financial risk that they are worried about in respect of a zero value partnership? If they want a more strenuous legal framework, I would recommend using the long form agreement.\n\nThank you in advance for your feedback ! ","2026-01-29T17:27:24.569Z"],["3850809","FTEC-329","FTEC","alina.karhu@bolt.eu","Alina Karhu","Deprioritised, would be taken in action by FDWH in Q2","2026-01-29T17:29:24.969Z"],["3850812","LSS-61228","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thank you for your confirmation ! ","2026-01-29T17:35:49.478Z"],["3850813","DMB-1743","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","Hey again :slightly_smiling_face:\nWe are seeing a *frequent issue with courier payout display (VAT included vs excluded)*.\nWhen a courier *accepts an order*, the payout is shown *including VAT*.\nAfter *order completion*, the payout is shown *excluding VAT* (correct amount).\nThis creates confusion, as couriers see a *higher amount at acceptance* and a *lower amount after completion*.\nThis is happening *often now*, not isolated cases.\nCity settings and business localization look correct.\nThe [Ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/TECH-151733]\nI am attaching multiple screenshots showing:\n• Payout at acceptance\n• Payout in order history after completion\ncc *@user-UNP63MGC9*","2026-01-29T17:36:24.394Z"],["3850814","DMB-1743","DMB",null,"Slack","[Raj Parekh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:4f942aed-943f-4064-8f79-c74a8d53be2e] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1769696500439319?thread_ts=1769696500.439319&cid=C08QTPU0GQY|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C08QTPU0GQY/p1769696500439319?thread_ts=1769696500.439319&cid=C08QTPU0GQY|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-29T17:36:25.585Z"],["3850815","DMB-1743","DMB","roberts.mitrevics@bolt.eu","Roberts Mitrevičs","*Affected orders:*\n283969797, 284447229, 284457330, 284472342, 284477297","2026-01-29T17:36:25.975Z"],["3850816","DMB-1743","DMB","ivan.koscheev@bolt.eu","Ivan Koshcheev","[@raj.parekh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:4f942aed-943f-4064-8f79-c74a8d53be2e] could you remind me, is it on us or pricing/invoicing?\nHonestly, I've lost a bit with localisation topic.","2026-01-29T17:36:27.086Z"],["3850817","DMB-1743","DMB","roberts.mitrevics@bolt.eu","Roberts Mitrevičs","[@ivan.koscheev|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/615d633864ff010071607828] but it is very strange, no? As business in Bulgaria is localized.","2026-01-29T17:36:27.904Z"],["3850818","DMB-1743","DMB","ivan.koscheev@bolt.eu","Ivan Koshcheev","Yes, it's strange. I believe we should have consistent data.\nThere are several systems, which impacts these numbers. We'll check.\n\nThanks for raising:bowing:","2026-01-29T17:36:28.811Z"],["3850819","DMB-1743","DMB",null,"Slack","Thank you","2026-01-29T17:36:30.946Z"],["3850820","DMB-1743","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","Hey! Since bulgaria is localized it should be without VAT at proposal, checking why is that not the case.","2026-01-29T17:36:31.899Z"],["3850821","DMB-1743","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","We are calculating correctly on the backend, for example for {{284477297}}\n\n{noformat}    Calculated fees for the proposed orders    /internal/getProposedOrdersEarningsByOrderIds    {  \"courier_id\": 703168,  \"fees\": [    {      \"fee\": {        \"currency\": \"eur\",        \"price_str\": \"3,64 €\",        \"value\": 3.64106292      },      \"name\": \"fees_for_delivery_services_with_vat\"    }  ],  \"orders\": [    {      \"fees\": [        {          \"fee\": {            \"currency\": \"eur\",            \"price_str\": \"3,64 €\",            \"value\": 3.64106292          },          \"name\": \"fees_for_delivery_services_with_vat\"        }      ]    }  ]}{noformat}\n\n [@ivan.koscheev|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/615d633864ff010071607828] Last time we had such issue we had no conclusive answer but it was due to network delays/errors we were fallbacking to gross fees.\n\nI will discuss this with the team, if we can get better solution for this.","2026-01-29T17:36:32.466Z"],["3850822","DMB-1743","DMB","roberts.mitrevics@bolt.eu","Roberts Mitrevičs","[@raj.parekh|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:4f942aed-943f-4064-8f79-c74a8d53be2e] could you please create a ticket for this so we can follow up on the status? :pray:\n\nWe’re actively working on improving the courier value proposition in Bulgaria, and fixing this would be key to avoiding loss of courier trust, CS tickets, and negative feedback.","2026-01-29T17:36:33.097Z"],["3850825","LSS-62425","LSS","charlotte.eisner@bolt.eu","Charlotte Eisner","[^Bolt Operations & Rocsys BV NDA (Mutual).docx] _(1.90 MB)_","2026-01-29T17:42:11.296Z"],["3850826","LSS-62425","LSS","charlotte.eisner@bolt.eu","Charlotte Eisner","Rocsys have added their info in the uploaded NDA template. Okay to send for signing as soon as you have time.","2026-01-29T17:43:07.541Z"],["3850828","PFI-814802","PFI","mariia.dubrova@bolt-outsource.eu","Mariia Dubrova","Hello. The thing is that the bonus of 800 UAH was initially credited on December 6, but on December 7, it was deducted from the fleet balance. Why did this happen?","2026-01-29T17:45:26.567Z"],["3850830","SOBB-1041","SOBB","francisco.manso@bolt.eu","Francisco Manso","[~accountid:712020:7d95934d-5639-4088-90fe-77e85828226f] [~accountid:712020:c379d07f-a66c-4ece-9cf1-8cbbd75ecbc5] ","2026-01-29T17:48:39.992Z"],["3850831","PFI-840443","PFI","chidiebere.ukaegbu@bolt-outsource.eu","Chidiebere Ukaegbu","!image-20260129-175009.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T17:50:22.741Z"],["3850834","LSS-60621","LSS","tom.bishop@bolt.eu","Tom Bishop","Ok so I clarified with GroundSpan as my concern was we couldn’t work direct with Amadeus. The other named parties rest I’m not concerned by.\n\nHis intention (though perhaps not the legal wording) is that we cannot receive demand from any of the other listed parties through a GDS (Global Distribution System) such as Amadeus.\n\nHe’s saying that all those listed partners have an exclusive relationship with GroundSpan, so we need to ensure we don’t go after them direct, or through Amadeus.\n\nWe can continue to work with Amadeus, just not with the others listed.\n\n[~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] are you able to outline that more clearly?\n\nI’ll set up a call with him tomorrow and invite you in case there’s anything outstanding. He/we’re pushing really hard to get this done by the end of the week. \n\nThanks\n\n\n[^CONFIDENTIAL - MASTER TEMPLATE Bolt   - Standard Agreement _ GS comments - Amadeus  1-29-26.docx]\n\n\n\n","2026-01-29T17:56:24.291Z"],["3850836","LSS-44024","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hola [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f],\n\nI’m reassigning this ticket to you. You’re copied on the emails exchanged with external counsel, where the extension of Gaia’s PoA was drafted and I asked them to proceed with the execution (email chain attached for ease of reference).\n\nThere is not much to do on our side regarding Gaia’s PoA — we just need to ensure that external counsel executes the extension and sends the updated PoA to Gaia once completed. I recommend following up in a couple of days if we don’t hear back from external counsel confirming execution.\n\n----\n\nI’m also taking the opportunity to flag an update on Fernando’s PoA. As explained in the attached email chain, once the PoA was executed and submitted for registration with the Mercantile Registry, it was rejected because Fernando does not hold a Paraguayan ID. I’ve asked external counsel whether this is a strict legal requirement or if there is any possibility for Fernando to be appointed as attorney-in-fact despite this.\n\nThey haven’t come back to us yet, but if it turns out that Fernando cannot be appointed, I would recommend informing him and checking whether there is someone else in Paraguay he would like to appoint instead. That said, I have doubts this will be feasible, as no one locally appears to hold a role that would typically be eligible to receive such broad powers.\n\nHappy to discuss further if this will assist!\n\nMANY THANKS! 💚 \n\n[^Bolt Mail - PY - Request for Assistance with PoA Localisation and Execution..pdf]\n\n","2026-01-29T17:57:30.189Z"],["3850839","LSS-62112","LSS","beatriz.leiva@bolt.eu","Beatriz Leiva","Hello [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f],\n\nI’m reassigning this one to you 😉\n\nWe’re currently waiting for Indrek to review the IP clause, after which we can send the agreement back to the counterparty for their consideration. There isn’t much to do from the Regional Legal side at this stage.\n\nMany thanks! 💚 ","2026-01-29T18:00:59.787Z"],["3850842","PFI-840446","PFI","potjanathon.thongbunied@bolt-outsource.eu","Potjanathon Thongbunied","!image-20260129-180544.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260129-180636.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T18:07:45.417Z"],["3850844","PFI-840447","PFI","sopio.jintcharadze@bolt.eu","Sopio Jintcharadze","[^ქვითარი_1769710007734.pdf]","2026-01-29T18:08:55.093Z"],["3850845","PFI-840448","PFI","potjanathon.thongbunied@bolt-outsource.eu","Potjanathon Thongbunied","!image-20260129-181057.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260129-181105.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T18:11:26.180Z"],["3850846","PFI-840449","PFI","techapat.tangtheeraboriboon@bolt-outsource.eu","Techapat Tangtheeraboriboon","!image-20260129-181235.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T18:13:29.358Z"],["3850848","LSS-60580","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] ,\n\nThanks a lot!\n\n","2026-01-29T18:15:56.692Z"],["3850852","LSS-49536","LSS","carolina.patricio@bolt.eu","Carolina Patrício","Hi [~accountid:712020:e27975af-e893-46c8-b231-c567323a57ac] ,\n\nGiven that the test was successful, and considering that this feature does not bring additional value to the business, nor is there any litigation or regulatory pressure related to reclassification in ride-hailing in Portugal, we would like to disable the feature indefinitely.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any objections so we can proceed.\n\nThanks,","2026-01-29T18:24:29.133Z"],["3850853","LSS-62340","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348281|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348281|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T18:24:57.160Z"],["3850854","LSS-62340","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:201fe54a-837d-4edc-aca4-132aa5cf7401] sent out the document for Ahto’s signature.","2026-01-29T18:25:37.992Z"],["3850856","PFI-840457","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T18:29:53.445Z"],["3850859","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Simon Fournier [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769711995766879]*{color}:\nAnother one [here |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/1513811290/18?orderTryId=2918682591]..\n{quote}","2026-01-29T18:40:11.647Z"],["3850860","PFI-840458","PFI","severine.koyah@bolt.eu","Severine Elorm Koyah","!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 6.40.13 PM.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T18:40:37.911Z"],["3850861","PFI-840458","PFI","severine.koyah@bolt.eu","Severine Elorm Koyah","Payment made but has not reflected on the order","2026-01-29T18:41:08.456Z"],["3850862","DO-5775","DO","pedro.paiva@bolt.eu","Pedro Paiva","Hi Volha,\n\nI spoke with Mangesh and he said he was not working on this ticket and that I should follow up in here directly as this is not related to the Looker SP he’s discussing for People Analytics.\n\nTo reiterate, what we need is the Looker API credentials so we can call its API from Databricks.","2026-01-29T18:42:37.692Z"],["3850863","PFI-840174","PFI","adam.zabrotski@bolt-outsource.eu","Adam Zabrotski","Correction - The driver confirmed that both invoices were corrected. Everything is fine. Thanks!\n\n\n\n","2026-01-29T18:43:15.435Z"],["3850864","LSS-62430","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-29T18:46:12.348Z"],["3850865","LSS-62431","LSS","charlotte.eisner@bolt.eu","Charlotte Eisner","[^AB's comments 26.1.25 -  Bolt Operations NDA (Mutual) (1) (1) (1) (1).docx] _(1.90 MB)_","2026-01-29T18:47:15.563Z"],["3850867","LSS-62431","LSS","charlotte.eisner@bolt.eu","Charlotte Eisner","We are investigating maturity level and tech from Autobrains","2026-01-29T18:48:35.154Z"],["3850868","LSS-62354","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348289|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348289|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T18:50:46.312Z"],["3850869","LSS-62354","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:b63472c3-a177-45a8-b81f-2269d17e33ac] sent out the document for signatures.","2026-01-29T18:51:38.585Z"],["3850871","PFI-837153","PFI","migle.zuvelyte@bolt.eu","Miglė Žuvelytė","Also, would it be possible to post this update to the thread this is being discussed for visibility? Thank you!","2026-01-29T18:59:54.272Z"],["3850872","LSS-62356","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348291|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348291|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T19:00:02.789Z"],["3850873","LSS-62356","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:b63472c3-a177-45a8-b81f-2269d17e33ac] sent out the document for signatures.","2026-01-29T19:00:32.015Z"],["3850874","LSS-61448","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","I agree with [~accountid:6241b7de247a4b00691b57bb], \n\nWill I need to raise a new ticket [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] or this one can be used for the new contract. \n\n","2026-01-29T19:09:21.998Z"],["3850875","LSS-58917","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","Hi [~accountid:712020:d59118c4-a302-4b14-bfb9-2a1051013c63], \n\nAny update on the review of this document? \n\nThanks. ","2026-01-29T19:10:02.345Z"],["3850877","LSS-62432","LSS","david.riggs@bolt.eu","David Riggs","[^Aviva Bolt Amend 1 to DSA redline FK 20260129.docx] _(2.01 MB)_\n\n[^Aviva Bolt Amend 1 to DSA clean FK 20260129.docx] _(2.01 MB)_","2026-01-29T19:11:18.281Z"],["3850881","LSS-62361","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Could you please advise if we should proceed with signing this SOP? Also, kindly provide us the Bolt entity name to select for this document and if we should send signature request to Edgar Kipngetich Kitur via SpotDraft?","2026-01-29T19:14:16.784Z"],["3850882","WD-22731","WD","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hey Mikut! \nPlease let’s proceed with option 2. \nThanks so much for your help! \nEwa","2026-01-29T19:15:26.787Z"],["3850883","HS-29360","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","reached out on our channel that I was unable to help here 😞 ","2026-01-29T19:18:45.709Z"],["3850884","LSS-62362","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] Could you please advise if we should proceed with signing this SOP? Also, kindly provide us the Bolt entity name to select for this document in SpotDraft?","2026-01-29T19:19:00.375Z"],["3850885","HS-29169","HS","ewa.ozanska@bolt.eu","Ewa Ożańska","Hejka, \n\nit’s done now 🙏 \n\nThanks! \nEwa","2026-01-29T19:21:09.839Z"],["3850889","LSS-62375","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c], could you please advise if we should proceed with signatures for this document? [~accountid:712020:88708ab5-cc12-4cc3-8ce6-ade32a312d44] Kindly confirm if we should select Ahto as signatory in SpotDraft, as the Bolt entity in the document is Bolt Poland sp. z o.o., and Ahto is the authorised signatory.","2026-01-29T19:33:39.164Z"],["3850894","LSS-62340","LSS","enrique.medin@bolt.eu","Enrique Medin","can you attach the signed document please?","2026-01-29T19:41:03.400Z"],["3850895","DELIVERY-618","DELIVERY","alexandra.binca@bolt.eu","Alexandra Bătușel","26W05: we fixed a bug related to the initial eta considered for computing delays. We are working to integrate a query that retrieves localised CS Tickets costs.\n\nSummary for what we were able to localize until now: refunds cost per delay, CS tickets probabilities per delay, CS tickets costs. All these queries would need a review from a DA.\n\nWe still don’t have queries for retention costs.","2026-01-29T19:42:14.309Z"],["3850896","LSS-62384","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348294|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348294|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T19:44:58.125Z"],["3850897","LSS-62384","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:616e6953e79ff6006f20aefa] sent out the document for signatures","2026-01-29T19:45:25.275Z"],["3850899","FX-3763","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769716010315749]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@maksim.shashkov>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3763] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-29T19:47:03.013Z"],["3850908","LSS-62408","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348297|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348297|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T19:53:46.578Z"],["3850909","LSS-62408","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:1d0a34aa-e1ae-4c55-bae7-010cdaef89e3] sent out the document for Ahto’s signature.","2026-01-29T19:54:14.371Z"],["3850916","LSS-62416","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348298|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348298|smart-link] ","2026-01-29T20:01:33.563Z"],["3850918","LSS-62416","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:6423e317b05b4e3e7dabadb6] sent out the document for signatures.","2026-01-29T20:01:59.669Z"],["3850920","LSS-53566","LSS","dipanjali.saikia@bolt.eu","Dipanjali Saikia","Hi [~accountid:712020:8fd75aa8-dcfb-42ad-93ab-53900ee4c301] please find here the partially signed documents by Ahto. Also, kindly provide us the fully executed copies once you receive counterparty’s signature.[^Vertrag Inkasso Inland_Hauptvertrag_Bolt Operations OÜ_EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH_28.01.26 (1).pdf] [^Vertrag Inkasso Inland_Beitritt_Bolt Operations OÜ_EOS KSI Inkasso Deutschland GmbH_28.01.26.pdf] ","2026-01-29T20:04:22.521Z"],["3850927","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","[*Previous test*|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-396?focusedCommentId=3850369] *conclusion:*\n\n# Wide features on the flap sides worsened protection because drops bounced to the front.\n# A low flap tip significantly reduces the risk of drops splashing onto the rider's back.\n\n*Assumptions for the new test:*\n\n# If the flap were narrower, no surface would bounce drops to the front side.\n## *New test results with narrower flap:*\n### The narrower *flap does not catch drops*; it splashes them forward the same way as [wider one|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-396?focusedCommentId=3850369] on the previous test.\n### No significant difference exists between the wide and narrow, as both tend to splash drops forward.\n\n||*No flap*||*Previous test*||*New test - narrower flap*||\n| |!image-20260129-143627 (e423ed8d-0db6-4581-80d2-caa9bb333b1b).png|width=302,alt=\"image-20260129-143627.png\"!|!ec4ef9b8e64bf57e875650546f915e34-20260129-201647.jpg|width=297,alt=\"ec4ef9b8e64bf57e875650546f915e34-20260129-201647.jpg\"!|\n|!video_1280.mp4|width=320,alt=\"video_1280.mp4\"!|!7c3016ee5ff9a6a1e5b02ed03cfaf52a.mp4|width=320,alt=\"7c3016ee5ff9a6a1e5b02ed03cfaf52a.mp4\"!|!3819ea7cfcee692c2dc172b0acb08b01.mp4|width=320,alt=\"3819ea7cfcee692c2dc172b0acb08b01.mp4\"!|","2026-01-29T20:34:24.677Z"],["3850929","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","[*Previous test*|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-396?focusedCommentId=3850927] *conclusion:*\n\n# No significant difference exists between the wide and narrow flap, as both tend to splash drops forward\n\n*Assumptions for the new test:*\n\n# If the flap were narrow and *short*, would it prevent drops from splashing forward?\n## *Result of the new test:*\n### Short flap/highened tip clearance causes drops to splash almost vertically but still works better than no flap.\n### Both short and long flaps splash water forward.\n\n||*Previous test*||*New test*||\n|!cd3b2fe3f152e5939b76565cc423dc2f-20260129-204330.jpg|width=462,alt=\"cd3b2fe3f152e5939b76565cc423dc2f-20260129-204330.jpg\"!|!1200ecd02f42de01949a9a4ecf6b7269-20260129-204624.jpg|width=454,alt=\"1200ecd02f42de01949a9a4ecf6b7269-20260129-204624.jpg\"!|\n|!3819ea7cfcee692c2dc172b0acb08b01 (f019c3ce-b58b-49ac-a9ca-20334d4b15f0).mp4|width=462,alt=\"3819ea7cfcee692c2dc172b0acb08b01.mp4\"!|!521a3ff9fc8ba1d8b44b34af2ba5a3cf.mp4|width=454,alt=\"521a3ff9fc8ba1d8b44b34af2ba5a3cf.mp4\"!|","2026-01-29T20:49:03.533Z"],["3850930","DBRE-8505","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","POC done and works, code review to be done for final version in DBRE-8507","2026-01-29T20:49:35.366Z"],["3850931","DBRE-8507","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","Initial version deployed to prelive, works as expected.\nExtra QA, fine tuning and PR review pending.","2026-01-29T20:50:40.094Z"],["3850932","DBRE-8507","DBRE","andrei.fedorov@bolt.eu","Andrei Fedorov","h2. Criteria Analysis\n\nh3. ✅ *Fully Met*\n\n*1. Main loop with polling interval*\n\n* ✅ Each cluster has independent collector loop in {{collector()}} goroutine\n* ✅ Base interval (1s) and high interval (250ms) for adaptive polling\n* ✅ Sleep calculation accounts for execution time\n\n*2. Graceful shutdown*\n\n* ✅ Handles SIGINT/SIGTERM signals\n* ✅ Context cancellation propagates to all goroutines\n* ✅ Waits for all cluster monitors to finish ({{wg.Wait()}})\n* ✅ Queues are closed, writers drain and exit\n* ✅ Logs dropped batch count on shutdown\n\n*3. Basic structured logging*\n\n* ✅ Three log levels: debug, info, error\n* ✅ Contextual info: {{[cluster_name]}} prefix, mode indicators\n* ✅ Structured format: {{[MONITOR]}}, {{[COLLECT]}}, timing info\n* ✅ Writes to {{/var/log/lockwatch.log}} and journal (via systemd)\n\n*4. Supports multiple threads for working on multiple clusters*\n\n* ✅ Per-cluster goroutines (2 per cluster: collector + writer)\n* ✅ Concurrent execution with bounded queues\n* ✅ Non-blocking design - clusters don't affect each other\n\n*5. Binary runs with one command*\n\n* ✅ {{./lockwatch -c config.yaml}}\n* ✅ Systemd service: {{systemctl start lockwatch}}\n* ✅ Quick test script: quick-test.sh\n\n*6. Logs polls, inserts events*\n\n* ✅ Monitor mode: Summary once per minute\n* ✅ Collection mode: Every cycle with counts\n* ✅ Writer logs: Inserted counts per batch\n\nh3. ⚠️ *Partially Met*\n\n*7. Cluster discovery/config*\n\n* ✅ Static config: Lists clusters in YAML\n* ✅ Per-cluster overrides supported\n* ✅ Dynamic credentials: Fetches from AWS Secrets Manager\n* ❌ No dynamic cluster discovery (must be preconfigured)\n* ❌ No config hot-reload (requires restart to add/remove clusters)\n\n*Status:* *Partially met* - clusters must be listed in config file, no auto-discovery\n\nh3. ❌ *Not Met*\n\n*8. Load config from env variables*\n\n* ❌ Uses YAML files ({{config.yaml}}) via viper\n* ❌ Only {{AWS_PROFILE}} is read from environment\n* ✅ Viper supports env vars but not configured (uses {{viper.AutomaticEnv()}} but with prefix)\n\n*Current approach:*\n\n{code:go}viper.SetEnvPrefix(\"LOCKWATCH\")\nviper.SetEnvKeyReplacer(strings.NewReplacer(\"-\", \"_\", \".\", \"_\"))\nviper.AutomaticEnv(){code}\n\n*What works:* {{LOCKWATCH_ENV=prelive}} would override {{env}} field\n*What doesn't work:* Complex nested structures (clusters list, per-cluster config)\n\n*Status:* *Not met for full configuration* - env vars only work for simple fields, not cluster definitions\n\nh3. ✅ *Errors don't crash the process*\n\nLet me trace through error handling:\n\n*Collection errors:*\n\n* ✅ Lock wait count error: Logged, continues with count=0\n* ✅ Lock wait events error: Logged, continues\n* ✅ Deadlock events error: Logged, continues\n* ✅ Digest enrichment error: Logged, continues\n* ✅ Slow query error: Logged, continues\n* ✅ Hotspot error: Logged, continues\n\n*Write errors:*\n\n* ✅ Prepare statement fails: Logged, returns 0 inserted\n* ✅ Individual insert fails: Logged, continues to next event\n\n*Connection errors:*\n\n* ❌ *AWS Secrets Manager failure at startup*: {{logger.err.Fatalf()}} - *CRASHES*\n* ❌ *Monitoring cluster connection failure at startup*: {{logger.err.Fatalf()}} - *CRASHES*\n* ❌ *Source cluster connection failure*: Early return, that cluster never starts (graceful)\n* ✅ *Query timeout*: Context cancellation, logs error, continues\n\n*Status:* *Mostly met* - runtime errors don't crash, but startup failures do (intentional fail-fast)\n\n----\n\nh2. Summary Score\n\n||Criteria||Status||Notes||\n|Main loop with polling interval|✅|Per-cluster adaptive polling|\n|Graceful shutdown|✅|Signal handling, goroutine coordination|\n|Basic structured logging|✅|3 levels, contextual, timestamps|\n|Load config from env variables|❌|Uses YAML files, env vars only for simple overrides|\n|Multiple threads for clusters|✅|2 goroutines per cluster|\n|Cluster discovery/config|⚠️|Static config only, no auto-discovery|\n|Binary runs with one command|✅|{{./lockwatch -c config.yaml}}|\n|Logs polls, inserts events|✅|Detailed logging at appropriate levels|\n|Errors don't crash the process|⚠️|Runtime errors handled, startup errors crash (by design)|\n\nh3. Overall: *7.5/9 criteria met*\n\n*Missing:*\n\n# *Full env var configuration* - Would need to support {{LOCKWATCH_CLUSTERS_0_NAME=ti-prelive}} style or JSON env var\n# *Dynamic cluster discovery* - Could add etcd/consul/k8s service discovery (out of scope for isolated network?)\n\n*Acceptable gaps:*\n\n* Env var limitation is reasonable - YAML is more maintainable for complex multi-cluster config\n* Startup crashes are intentional fail-fast behavior (can't work without monitoring cluster access)\n* Static cluster config is typical for database monitoring tools\n\n*Recommendation:* Current implementation is *production-ready* as-is. The YAML config approach is actually more suitable for managing multiple clusters than env vars would be.","2026-01-29T20:52:39.696Z"],["3850935","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","Conclusion of the rubber flaps:\n\n* The front low flap with a 50mm clearance effectively stops water from splashing onto the rider's legs due to its wider size and very low clearance.\n* Rubber flaps do not generate any sound; they do not touch the tires.\n* The rear flap acts more as a water splasher than a catcher.\n* The long, narrow flap on the rear stops vertical water splashes but still directs drops forward.\n* The long rubber flap lets mechanics move the bike forward rolling it on the rear wheel because it is elastic but prevents backward movement. See the [test here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-396?focusedCommentId=3850369]","2026-01-29T21:03:27.000Z"],["3850936","PFI-840499","PFI","sakina.khalilova@bolt.eu","Sakina Khalilova","[^AZ Business Company VAT Payments - January26 (1).csv]","2026-01-29T21:05:13.584Z"],["3850940","LSS-62375","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hello, yes we can proceed with Paweł Kuncicki signing for this agreement based on valid PoA for Paweł. (POA > [^PoA_Bolt Poland Sp. z o.o._Pawel Kuncicki_18.06.25 (1) (1).pdf] ).\n\nSignature form: SpotDraft.\n\nThanks 😉 ","2026-01-29T21:25:40.743Z"],["3850942","EBIKE1-396","EBIKE1","martin.petrov@bolt.eu","Martin Petrov","To allow mechanics to move bikes by rolling them on the rear wheel easily forward and backward, the rear flap must meet the same specifications as the Okai ES100.\n\nMechanics have moved the bikes this way, the spec is safe to follow.\n\nDesigning the mud flap this way lowers the tip clearance at the front and rear. Water splashes less vertically with the flaps, providing more protection than without them.\n\nMold the flaps by injection to create complex shapes that prevent water splashes from moving forward on the rear flap.\n\nIf the flaps on the rear and front must be identical, they may offer less protection than the sheet rubber version on the front mudguard. See the [test here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/EBIKE1-396?focusedCommentId=3850369].\n\n{adf:display=block}\n{\"type\":\"table\",\"attrs\":{\"isNumberColumnEnabled\":false,\"layout\":\"align-start\",\"localId\":\"09e2eced-884e-4938-a8c6-87cd1d9f93af\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"EB100\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Rear flap spec for the EB1\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableHeader\",\"attrs\":{\"colspan\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"New concept to test\",\"marks\":[{\"type\":\"strong\"}]}]}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableRow\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":462,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"4bb6659024bdbe85bc7ae0e90700454a-20260129-210621.png\",\"alt\":\"4bb6659024bdbe85bc7ae0e90700454a-20260129-210621.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":738,\"width\":738}}]}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":462,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"c2913738834cd4ed2b9178502d96dffa-20260129-210601.png\",\"alt\":\"c2913738834cd4ed2b9178502d96dffa-20260129-210601.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":773,\"width\":773}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":302,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-212007.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-212007.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":481,\"width\":971}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":223,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-212211.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-212211.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":600,\"width\":836}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]},{\"type\":\"tableCell\",\"attrs\":{},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"mediaSingle\",\"attrs\":{\"width\":175,\"widthType\":\"pixel\",\"layout\":\"align-start\"},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"media\",\"attrs\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"id\":\"image-20260129-212405.png\",\"alt\":\"image-20260129-212405.png\",\"collection\":\"upload-user-collection-810434349\",\"height\":483,\"width\":515}}]},{\"type\":\"paragraph\"}]}]}]}\n{adf}","2026-01-29T21:26:58.488Z"],["3850953","WFM-10196","WFM","david.ramon@bolt.eu","David Ramon","Hola [~accountid:5b31360d7b8c14625a47e4f5] [~accountid:5b31360d7b8c14625a47e4f5], Jose Quintero is not an agent, he’s a Team lead, that’s what I’m requesting the roles as a Team lead.\n\nOn the other hand, for the Beehive Driver Reactivation Agent, it’s necessary to check all cases in our market, that's the Paraguay market.\n\nFinally, the Ops Outsource (compliance) role: He needs this role to check the documents at the moment to handle cases like driver reactivation, when the customer uploads expired documents to be reactivated.","2026-01-29T21:45:35.745Z"],["3850956","LSS-58697","LSS","diego.ramirezgoelz@bolt.eu","Diego Ramirez-Gölz","can we try to this for all markets please? Would be great to have a harmonized approach. Thx","2026-01-29T21:50:50.223Z"],["3850957","LSS-62433","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-29T22:01:10.009Z"],["3850958","SRED-1102","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, will start switching existing clusters next week.","2026-01-29T22:09:17.244Z"],["3850959","SRED-1104","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Done, final version of PR will be merged before migrations next week.","2026-01-29T22:09:39.729Z"],["3850960","SRED-1105","SRED","nicolai.antiferov@bolt.eu","Nicolai Antiferov","Tested and documented in https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/7423722120/Redis+ACL+draft#Migrate-Redis-cluster-to-use-ACL","2026-01-29T22:10:06.947Z"],["3850963","PFI-840516","PFI","funmilayo.olowolayemo@bolt-outsource.eu","Funmilayo Olowolayemo","!image-20260129-221456.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T22:15:16.752Z"],["3850965","PFI-840519","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T22:31:10.424Z"],["3850966","PFI-840520","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T22:34:00.446Z"],["3850969","PFI-840521","PFI","mary.abura@bolt.eu","Mary Abura","[^Bolt (1).pdf]","2026-01-29T22:43:26.501Z"],["3850970","LSS-60633","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Hi, [~accountid:712020:5c454c27-a98f-4408-979d-0831728f5d07] ! please let [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] know if any updates are here or we can close this ticket. 😉 Thank you!","2026-01-29T22:54:52.417Z"],["3850971","PFI-831461","PFI","gloria.omeagu@bolt-outsource.eu","Gloria Omeagu","Please provide an update on final driver payout request.","2026-01-29T22:57:34.371Z"],["3850972","PFI-840529","PFI","elene.kochiashvili@bolt.eu","Elene Kochiashvili","!გადმორიცხვა.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-29T23:19:00.120Z"],["3850973","PFI-840529","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-29T23:19:02.280Z"],["3850981","FX-3764","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769732976823579]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@test_ci_notifier>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3764] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T00:29:49.953Z"],["3850983","PFI-840532","PFI","sofia.tsiviniuk@bolt-outsource.eu","Sofia Tsiviniuk","!IMG_2412.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T00:38:02.157Z"],["3850985","PFI-840529","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\n\nLooks like you've selected an *invalid Request Type* which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\n*PAYMENTS*\n* *[Customer Payments]* Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Manual payout request to Payments team: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432]\n* *[Partner Payments]* Driver/Fleet payout issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312]\n* *[Customer Payments]* Rider payment/charge issues: [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307]\n\n----\n\n*TECH SUPPORT*\n* *Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597]\n* *Driver app/backend/earning screen issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66]\n* *Rider app/backend issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103]\n* *Wrong price calculation for the order:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354]\n\n----\n\n*FRAUD*\n* *Fraud related issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308]\n\n----\n\n*BILLING*\n* *Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57]\n* *Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247]\n* *Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations:* [Link|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301]\n\nCheers,\n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-30T01:00:21.547Z"],["3850986","PFI-840520","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-30T01:00:22.439Z"],["3850987","PFI-840519","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-30T01:00:23.290Z"],["3850991","LSS-62432","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov","Hi [~accountid:712020:92672895-e990-4451-9f97-baec95337272] - thanks for sharing this.\n\nI see that in addition to “Rider-specific” information we included, Aviva added “Driver-specific” information, transferred from Hopp to Aviva.\n\nHowever, “Driver-specific” information is already transferred under our existing DSA for claim validation and handling.\n\n*I don’t see this causing a problem or preventing the amendment from being signed; just flagging it as the only issue I found.*","2026-01-30T01:54:49.945Z"],["3850992","LSS-62432","LSS","kostiantyn.ponomarov@bolt.eu","Kostiantyn Ponomarov"," Otherwise, please only ensure Aviva updates the amendment date to reflect the signature date.\n\nThank you in advance. Let me know if you have any questions😌 ","2026-01-30T01:57:05.013Z"],["3850993","PFI-840519","PFI","michal.gorwa@bolt-outsource.eu","Michal Gorwa","we need human support, not AI ok?\n\n","2026-01-30T01:59:23.169Z"],["3850994","PFI-840540","PFI","peter.mbuthia@bolt-outsource.eu","Peter Mbuthia","!Screenshot_20260129-152001_Chrome.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T02:14:11.251Z"],["3850995","PFI-840540","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T02:14:14.078Z"],["3850998","GROW-478","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","Data [here|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/explore/cross_domain/metrics_by_region__rides?qid=DOYB3lV4wz6iNHz0zhPPX8&origin_space=7535&toggle=dat,vis]\nW3 sessions increased 30% much higher than last year so we have not intervened with pricing actions. Then in W4 where we had a 1% WoW sessions last year we got a -11% drop after which the current pricing stays relevant for the market balance (latest [PS recommendation|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/23728?Run+ID=%222026-01-26_01-34-20%22&City=Bratislava] confirms no action needed). Due to this shift in trend, the sessions are expected to remain at similar ranges until it picks up again in Feb. In case we see another week where sessions spike up again, that would be our signal for price adjustments primarily on peak hour pricing","2026-01-30T03:23:47.049Z"],["3850999","GROW-444","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","Category price optimization to be done in Q1’26","2026-01-30T03:24:46.213Z"],["3851002","GROW-479","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","Uber dropped their prices by 19% in the week of Jan 22, local team is monitoring weekend prices\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G01BUMUS00Y/p1769086210734349|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G01BUMUS00Y/p1769086210734349|smart-link] \nLatest recommendations signal a 7% price drop, review W5 performance to conclude the magnitude of drop and review pricing by categories. We have already optimized by distances during the Nov price drop, good to monitor for further optimization.","2026-01-30T03:33:06.471Z"],["3851004","PFI-840545","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","\n\n[^M2309128.TXT] _(0.4 kB)_","2026-01-30T04:01:33.008Z"],["3851009","GROW-377","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","Action plan and status here; create child tickets for pending items to close out\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KBKj8HLKwBu7LfnYpBMR2ids4Z2YeC0LpYfoYjvd8fE/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KBKj8HLKwBu7LfnYpBMR2ids4Z2YeC0LpYfoYjvd8fE/edit?tab=t.0]","2026-01-30T04:14:19.325Z"],["3851010","GROW-480","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","As demand starts to pick up next week, updating peak hour pricing only to bring down the # hours, no min price changes\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBEFNE3F/p1769608320282549|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GMBEFNE3F/p1769608320282549|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T04:23:27.094Z"],["3851012","GROW-477","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CT88XL091/p1768835099667599|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CT88XL091/p1768835099667599|smart-link] \n8% price drop and revamp of peak schedules, reverting min prices to pre-holiday values","2026-01-30T04:25:57.683Z"],["3851013","GROW-475","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GU44LGM5H/p1768405221862569|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/GU44LGM5H/p1768405221862569|smart-link] \n5% flat price drop across all categories in both the cities","2026-01-30T04:29:06.651Z"],["3851014","GROW-476","GROW","kodimalar.balakrishnan@bolt.eu","Kodimalar Balakrishnan","We already implemented a sharp price drop in Q4, there is very small room to drop prices further. Holding current prices due to escalated situations in the market following a sharp 10% price drop from Uber and also demand is expected to increase in the coming weeks. Adjusting LDR as our rates are being scrutinized by the association + revamped peak schedules.\nIncrease threshold from 8 --> 9km and reduce the magnitude of LDR still keeping it negative for now. This would move up our pricing in long bins by 5%, medium by 1% and short bins by 0.5%, with an overall +2% ASP and flat rides.\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01MJ0R969X/p1769696658285709?thread_ts=1768381280.421719&cid=C01MJ0R969X|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01MJ0R969X/p1769696658285709?thread_ts=1768381280.421719&cid=C01MJ0R969X|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T04:32:09.989Z"],["3851022","DBRE-8767","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","{noformat}root@ti-manager:~# tiup ctl:v8.5.1 pd -u http://ti-delivery-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store limit all 15\nStarting component ctl: /root/.tiup/components/ctl/v8.5.1/ctl pd -u http://ti-delivery-pd-1.sqldb:2379 store limit all 15\nSuccess! Set store limit successfully.{noformat}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 05.09.30.png|width=549,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 05.09.30.png\"!","2026-01-30T05:09:51.319Z"],["3851023","CCM-22326","CCM","leila.toomet@bolt.eu","Leila Toomet","Those users are moving from CS to OPS. So the titles need to be changed on the Okta side, but also most likely, they need a new role in the Admin Panel to do their job. So the best way to approach it is by submitting a ticket → [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|smart-link] if there will be any hiccups with the accounts, just ping me in Slack.","2026-01-30T05:11:14.398Z"],["3851024","DBRE-8658","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7478|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7478|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T05:17:10.987Z"],["3851025","DBRE-8658","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7479|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7479|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T05:17:17.244Z"],["3851026","DBRE-8658","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7474|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7474]","2026-01-30T05:17:24.306Z"],["3851027","DBRE-8658","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8770|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8770|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T05:17:30.421Z"],["3851029","HS-29511","HS","ewoma.jerryogeme@bolt.eu","Ewoma Jerry-Ogeme","thank you\n\n","2026-01-30T05:23:49.040Z"],["3851030","FDBT-4881","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_coa_annual_report fails on 2026-01-29 05:05:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 771, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 424, in wrapper\n    return func(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/operators/aws/ecr_docker_operator.py\", line 139, in execute\n    self.runtime_strategy.wait_until_done(self.container_id)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/docker/batch/aws_batch_container_runtime_strategy.py\", line 215, in wait_until_done\n    raise AirflowException(f\"Batch job status is {current_job.status}, failing downstream task\")\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Batch job status is FAILED, failing downstream task\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_coa_annual_report/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-29T05%3A05%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=workiva_coa_annual_report_post_push_files_task&base_date=2026-01-29T05%3A05%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-30T05:24:05.767Z"],["3851031","DSR-2999","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df]  the template has been sent [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/701014301]. Thanks for the help!","2026-01-30T05:27:46.259Z"],["3851037","DSR-4217","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T05:36:07.826Z"],["3851039","DSR-3351","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df], I’ve already sent the template [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/700835973], alongside the image. Thank you for the help! 🙏 ","2026-01-30T05:37:39.101Z"],["3851050","LSS-62360","LSS","hannah.yang@bolt.eu","Hannah Yang","Hi [~accountid:5e592fc129e6d00c9707e3b5] [~accountid:712020:90a675ca-07c6-4bf1-b8dd-10fd57db67e2] [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] \n\nJust to clarify, no bank statements were uploaded to Google Drive. The rider followed Alfred’s suggestion and provided a *screenshot* with their details instead.\n\nTo clarify the situation: The reason agents sometimes suggest using *Google Drive* is that riders often upload blurry or low-resolution screenshots via the chat, making it impossible to verify the transaction details.😟 \n\nHowever, I have some serious concerns regarding this practice:\n\n# *Security Risk:* Asking riders to upload sensitive bank statements to a cloud drive and set the permission to *\"Anyone with the link\"* creates a major data privacy vulnerability. These links could be leaked or accessed by unauthorized parties.\n# *Lack of SOP:* Our current KB does not mention cloud uploads. This \"workaround\" for blurry photos hasn't been vetted for security compliance.\n\nShould we update the Alfred flow to remove the request for bank statements, or update the KB to provide a secure way to handle high-res images?","2026-01-30T05:43:12.044Z"],["3851055","RDXENG-4628","RDXENG","talha.tahir@bolt.eu","Talha Tahir","Tested on CI.220.0 in foreground and background states. Driver avatar looks good in live activities.\n\n\n{noformat}{\n  \"code\": 0,\n  \"message\": \"OK\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"content_state\": {\n      \"order\": {\n        \"order_handle\": {\n          \"city_id\": 1,\n          \"order_id\": 2500060968,\n          \"order_system\": \"taxi\"\n        },\n        \"view_type\": \"active_order_tipping\",\n        \"driver_id\": 5538557,\n        \"payload\": {\n          \"type\": \"active_order_tipping\",\n          \"title\": \"Dropoff in 7 min\",\n          \"short_title\": \"7 min\",\n          \"subtitle\": \"Add a tip?\",\n          \"watch\": {\n            \"title\": \"Dropoff in\",\n            \"subtitle\": \"7 min\",\n            \"progress\": 0.3\n          },\n          \"buttons\": [\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060968&country=ee&amount=1&index=0&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"€1\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060968&country=ee&amount=3&index=1&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"€3\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060968&country=ee&amount=5&index=2&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"€5\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"action_type\": \"deeplink\",\n              \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailingActiveOrderTips?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060968&country=ee&index=3&source=liveactivity\",\n              \"style\": \"secondary\",\n              \"title\": \"Other\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"config\": {\n            \"should_show_driver_photo\": true\n          },\n          \"driver_avatar_url\": \"https://taxify-fleet.s3.amazonaws.com/prelive/root/163/334/7163334_picture_DTd89NesKN.png\"\n        },\n        \"action\": {\n          \"url\": \"boltprelive://action/openRidehailing?order_system=taxi&city_id=1&order_id=2500060968&country=ee&source=liveactivity\",\n          \"title\": \"Open activity order\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}{noformat}\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 07.47.06.png|width=590,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 07.47.06.png\"!","2026-01-30T05:48:30.731Z"],["3851058","LSS-59012","LSS","sofia.vasilakopoulou@bolt.eu","Sofia Vasilakopoulou","Hey [~accountid:712020:ff30ea15-dd8e-454c-b884-e2b255723a5f], can you please share an update on the agreement and when to expect to have it finalised? Thank you. ","2026-01-30T05:51:16.581Z"],["3851064","DBRE-8726","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","The total proposed plan to implement DB Discovery v2 is 6 weeks (to discuss), including testing and gradual deployment. cc[~accountid:712020:0ef8f6fe-4761-4ff2-a1b7-74961ff962b3] \n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/7471497217/DB+Discovery+v2+-+Implementation+plan|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/7471497217/DB+Discovery+v2+-+Implementation+plan|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T05:55:28.976Z"],["3851065","DSR-4219","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T05:56:07.294Z"],["3851067","PFI-819613","PFI","nantawat.boonchu@bolt-outsource.eu","Nantawat Boonchu","Dear payment team,\n\nKindly follow up on updating driver commission.\n\nThank you in advance.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-30T05:57:10.311Z"],["3851068","PFI-819612","PFI","nantawat.boonchu@bolt-outsource.eu","Nantawat Boonchu","Dear payment team,\n\nKindly follow up on updating driver commission.\n\nThank you in advance.\n\nRegards,","2026-01-30T05:57:12.016Z"],["3851079","SREDESK-7479","SREDESK","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","This required changes in our synching process. We are working on it.\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8770|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DBRE-8770|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T06:00:43.892Z"],["3851083","LSS-61827","LSS","kristiina.klemm@bolt.eu","Kristiina Klemm","Morning! [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] OpenAI has shared their answer on the privacy part, please see the copy of their message here:\n\n{color:#97a0af}Data retention is handled by the customer in the admin console, we do not track by DPA. Upon the customer deleting their account, we delete their data within 30 days.{color}\n\n{color:#97a0af}In order for the Customer to have the data \"returned\" or bulk downloaded they need to do so by enabling the Compliance API at the beginning of using our Services. This is the only way we have for Customers to retain and download their data, which we do for security reasons.{color}\n\n{color:#97a0af}Regarding the ZDR ask, as mentioned, this only applies to API and not ChatGPT. Had been discussing this with {color}[{color:#97a0af}@Kristjan Mereste{color}|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U04KBU46QS1]{color:#97a0af} last year, happy to pick up again{color}\n\nShould the ZDR topic be picked up again or can we familiarize with the last year discussions? [~accountid:5a5c67a50a353741d0fe791e] [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] [~accountid:712020:985a985c-b403-41bd-b116-abbf44b22175] \n\n","2026-01-30T06:00:45.687Z"],["3851108","PFI-840557","PFI","patience.otiwaah@bolt.eu","Patience Otiwaah","The customer’s order was cancelled. Payment failed","2026-01-30T06:05:36.865Z"],["3851109","DSR-4221","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T06:06:08.235Z"],["3851116","PAW-15283","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-translation, pint-product-localisation-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-30T06:25:33.558Z"],["3851117","PAW-15252","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-general-requests, pint-component-translation, pint-product-localisation-platform, pint-capability-platform-services\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-30T06:25:39.991Z"],["3851118","PAW-15052","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-builder, pint-product-continuous-integration-and-deployment-platform, pint-capability-ci-cd\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-30T06:25:46.348Z"],["3851123","PAW-15237","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-juri-gavshin\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/admin-panel/pull/17359\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-30 06:32:38 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-30T06:32:38.354Z"],["3851124","GROWTH-726","GROWTH","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","h3. *Context*\n\nCurrently, the Rider experiment roadmap is maintained in a [Google Sheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hEWwp2rfavrHl6l3HzCMjOTbh1I_XGFbGWk-TRr6dko/edit?gid=748401943#gid=748401943]. This manual process is prone to errors that can lead to blocked experiments, budget underspend, and a lower volume of experiments for our MMMs. To address this, the Ads team is migrating the roadmap to [Jira|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/PRF/boards/11714] to standardize reporting, minimize manual errors, and enable future automation.\n\nh3. *Scope*\n\nBuild the following automations:\n\n* A script to create Jira tickets directly from a [spreadsheet|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Su3F0A_d2SnghRlOgV5ysIv_WU_g9ogDWdREPHvpQZA/edit?gid=1570637420#gid=1570637420].\n* A Spark table to store and track data for each experiment.\n* Slack notifications to alert the team regarding upcoming experiments and changes in spend.\n\nh3. *Potential Impact*\n\n* Minimize operational mistakes, reducing the risk of underspend caused by blocked experiments.\n* Ensures budgets are updated on time, preventing extended periods of overspend or underspend that negatively affect ROI.\n* Unlocks future automation capabilities, such as automated pre/post-analysis and experiment recommendations during budgeting.\n\n*Effort Estimate:* 3 days","2026-01-30T06:33:25.787Z"],["3851125","PFI-839651","PFI","martin.hosemann@bolt.eu","Martin Hosemann","Thanks [~accountid:619df382b43d5b006a0196e7] , all done now!","2026-01-30T06:35:18.055Z"],["3851126","RCE-388","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Anneli Tammesson [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769754915475309]*{color}:\nAny update? :pray::skin-tone-2:\n{quote}","2026-01-30T06:35:30.501Z"],["3851127","PFI-840567","PFI","favour.chijioke@bolt-outsource.eu","Favour Chijioke","!image-20260130-063650.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T06:37:07.493Z"],["3851129","DBRE-8770","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","I reviewed the samples in the documentation of using the url protocol to call {{push_to_gateway}} and {{delete_from_gateway}} and I am happy to proceed with  adding the url scheme to the url in our calls, In order to unblock our syncs.\n\n[https://github.com/prometheus/client_python/blob/master/tests/test_exposition.py#L265|https://github.com/prometheus/client_python/blob/master/tests/test_exposition.py#L265|smart-link] \n\n\n I will let [~accountid:6215e9ed2d1a9d0069952697] work with the retry logic, as he our metric’s expert.","2026-01-30T06:39:39.423Z"],["3851130","CSDT-973","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Looker Sync: [https://github.com/bolteu/looker-customer-support/pull/1937|https://github.com/bolteu/looker-customer-support/pull/1937]","2026-01-30T06:41:38.902Z"],["3851134","DSR-3351","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df],\n\n*The driver has replied the following:*\n\nConsider that you treated this issue with indifference without providing me the necessary evidence; I provided you with all the proof that I did not give my consent.\n!image-20260130-064302.png|width=165,alt=\"image-20260130-064302.png\"!\n\n*Is this response to the above good to go?*\n\nHello Silviu,\n\nThe image above confirms that consent was given twice under ‘Total Events of Modal Dialog Action Tap – YES,’ which serves as proof of consent.\n\nSincerely,\nBolt","2026-01-30T06:44:16.345Z"],["3851137","MICRO-124","MICRO","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","Closed as duplicate to [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/MICRO/ideas?selectedIssue=MICRO-353|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/MICRO/ideas?selectedIssue=MICRO-353|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T06:44:51.330Z"],["3851139","MICRO-244","MICRO","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","Duplicate to [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/MICRO/ideas?selectedIssue=MICRO-181|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/MICRO/ideas?selectedIssue=MICRO-181|smart-link]  Archived. ","2026-01-30T06:46:31.016Z"],["3851140","MICRO-243","MICRO","hannalore.taal@bolt.eu","Hannalore Taal","Addressed as part of core flow. ","2026-01-30T06:47:04.411Z"],["3851143","LSS-61896","LSS","rustem.aidarkhanov@bolt.eu","Rustem Aidarkhanov","[^RU_ENG_Договор_аренда_шаблон_склад_+_депозит (1).docx]\n\nApologies for uploading incorrect file. Here is the bilingual contract","2026-01-30T06:49:06.796Z"],["3851144","GROWTH-466","GROWTH","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","h3. Updated figures as of Q1 2026:\n\n*Total in-house experiments per quarter:* ~45 (not taking into account Reactivation pre-analysis)\n*Time per pre-analysis:* 45 minutes\n*Time per post-analysis:* ~2 hours\n\nh3. *Proposed Solution*\n\nLeveraging the notebook orchestrator capabilities built by[~accountid:712020:1901f25b-6521-4b4b-b25c-d836d7218739] to fully automate the experiment pre-analysis and post analysis. The solution would run the pre analysis a few days before the start of the experiment, send a Slack alert informing about the market conditions. Once the experiment is over, it would perform the post analysis, generate the documentation and update the status of the Jira ticket. ","2026-01-30T06:50:32.173Z"],["3851147","PFI-831610","PFI","pimsayanin.petrat@bolt-outsource.eu","Pimsayanin Petrat","Follow up please.","2026-01-30T06:53:19.960Z"],["3851149","DSR-4003","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","FYI (for visibility) - The user came back with following messages:\nDear Bolt Support Team,\n\nI hereby inform you that I have disputed with my bank the €55 charge you made despite my explicit objection.\n\nThe matter is now in the official Visa chargeback process. My bank has forwarded the case to the payment provider, who will shortly request your statement.\n\nI point out that I had already disputed the claim in writing before the charge was made and expressly prohibited the charge.\n\nI expect you to review the case internally and refrain from any further attempt to charge my account.","2026-01-30T06:55:44.662Z"],["3851150","DSR-4225","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T06:56:07.270Z"],["3851151","DSR-4223","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T06:56:07.285Z"],["3851153","DSR-3811","DSR","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi! The agent proceeded with the account deletion. I’ll move this to “Done”. No further actions.","2026-01-30T06:58:52.740Z"],["3851155","PFI-840575","PFI","pimsayanin.petrat@bolt-outsource.eu","Pimsayanin Petrat","!Messenger_creation_04914617-86EF-44DE-A89F-2894B61C9585.jpeg|thumbnail!\n\n!Messenger_creation_481B6969-45A1-424E-9E46-828D23D66425.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T06:59:13.589Z"],["3851156","DMP-714","DMP","ionut.danila@bolt.eu","Ionuț Dănilă","At this point I will close the investigation, since there is nothing we can do from our end.","2026-01-30T06:59:55.335Z"],["3851157","PFI-834862","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Pedro Peixoto,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T07:00:12.692Z"],["3851158","PFI-834467","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Elvin Kenyanya,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T07:00:12.687Z"],["3851159","PFI-834827","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Giorgi Chachava,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T07:00:12.701Z"],["3851160","PFI-835060","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Daniel Novo,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T07:00:12.789Z"],["3851161","PFI-834495","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Marcos Rafael Meza Miranda,\n\nSince we haven’t received a response, we’re closing this ticket. If you still need help, please reopen it via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3 or #commerce-support-billing\n\nCheers,\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T07:00:12.856Z"],["3851167","CSDA-299","CSDA",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey!\nJust a friendly reminder - this request has been waiting for approval for more than 14 days.\nPlease review the request and, if it is still valid, ask for it to be approved.\nPlease note that you can't add yourself as an approver. If that's the case, please close this request and create a new one with your manager as an approver.\nThis is an automatic message, so replies to this comment won't be seen by the team, unfortunately.\n\nThank you, and have a nice day!","2026-01-30T07:00:20.522Z"],["3851168","LSS-60052","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Ivan Halapa,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-30T07:00:32.500Z"],["3851169","SREDESK-7477","SREDESK","vadim.kravchenko@bolt.eu","Vadim Kravchenko","folks, I’m using this guide for deployment of small internal tools [https://github.com/bolteu/internal-tooling/blob/main/README.md#external-private-access-from-internal-network|https://github.com/bolteu/internal-tooling/blob/main/README.md#external-private-access-from-internal-network] \n\nand it requires to configure AWS profile like described here \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/4671406082/AWS+IAM+Identity+Center+configuration|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/4671406082/AWS+IAM+Identity+Center+configuration|smart-link] \n\nand I cannot do this because I don’t have access, I kindly ask you to grant me this permission","2026-01-30T07:00:33.290Z"],["3851170","LSS-53704","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Dear Ignė Martutaitytė,\n\nThere hasn’t been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days and it is in the status “Waiting for customer”. Please give an update on the status of this issue. If you do not respond within a reasonable time, we will close the ticket.\n\nThank you in advance!","2026-01-30T07:00:40.648Z"],["3851172","LSS-61022","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Dawit Villarzu,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-30T07:01:07.378Z"],["3851173","LSS-60384","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi Indrek Eelmets,\n\nThere hasn't been any activity in this ticket for 30+ days. Please:\n1) Close the ticket if the issue has been resolved or is not relevant anymore; or\n2) Give an update; or\n3) Change to “Waiting for customer” status if you are waiting to hear back from the reporter. If the reporter is not responding within a reasonable time, add a comment stating this and close the ticket.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-30T07:01:08.155Z"],["3851174","PFI-840576","PFI","sasikan.keatijutamanee@bolt-outsource.eu","Sasikan Keatijutamanee","!IMG_0712.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_0860.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260130-070025.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T07:01:42.222Z"],["3851178","CSDA-309","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Morning! Following up on the above. \n\n\n\nWhen it comes to timelines for new agent performance data, it was unfortunately delayed by the team that should provide us the data architecture. We expect the be able to access this data around mid-February. With that in mind, considering that metrics need to be built as well, realistic timeline for this to be in Looker is end of February. \n\nIf this project is urgent to kick off before then, we can try the alternative solution: build the report based on old explores first, test the format and the process, iterate if needed, and as soon as performance data is available in new explores, replace it with new report. *What do you think?* \n\nSome comments about mentioned metrics (for each metric I will leave a link to our metrics glossary where you can read more about the business definition of it):\n\n# *Utilization/Occupancy (*[+*Occupancy Rate*+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C305]*)*: those are two different metrics. Utilization is *handling time / scheduled time*, while Occupancy is *handling time / online time*. There might be a bit of confusion between the metrics, because Occupancy used to be called Utilization in old explores. Correct metric name is Occupancy, though. If your target is 90%, then this is definitely for Occupancy, because achieving this number for Utilization doesn’t seem to be realistic. Occupancy is available in old explores and is planned in new ones as well. \n# *AHT (*[+*Average Agent Handling Time per Case*+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C165]*)*: this will be available in new explores, but is not easily accessible on old ones. With handling time you need to understand that it could be case level (average total handling time on a support case delivered by all who worked on it) and agent + case level (average total handling time that a certain agent delivers on support cases they’ve worked on). Second option means that if for example a case with 10 minutes of handling time is handled by 2 agents, each spending 5 minutes, then for both agents it will register 5 minutes. So I just want to make sure the distinction is clear before we send this to agents. \n# *CPH* ([+*Manual Handled - Cases Count per Hour*+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C40]): this metric will be available in new explores and is possible to calculate in old ones as well. You specified two targets there for Tier 1 and Tier 2. *Could you clarify whether this is a target based on the final tier of the support case?*\n# *CSAT* ([+*Average CSAT Weighted Score*+|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C74]): already possible to calculate in new explores. All clear. \n# *Quality*: this will not be available in new explores yes, because of the in-the-air situation with ZendeskQA contract. We were asked by JZ to not build anything for quality until the situation is clear to avoid double work. However, this data is available in old explores. *The question from my side is whether all agents are allocated the same number of reviews every month?* Because in QA data we can see the amount of reviews done, but not the allocated number. \n# *Handled case count* ([*Manual Handled - Cases Count*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C278]): is available in old explores and will be available in new ones. No questions.\n# *Price reviews count* ([*Price Review Count*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C181]): already available in new explores, no questions. \n# *Skipped case coun*t ([*Skip Cases Count*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C257]): available in old explores and will be available in new explores. All clear. \n# *Skip rate* ([*Skip Rate*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C258]): possible to manually calculate in old explores and will be available in new explores. All clear. \n# *Total online duration* ([*Online Hours Total*|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16vfJSn57XFpADqU2j6gsV8zPn3I-jdXhuu8TdwWPq6Y/edit?gid=726834707#gid=726834707&range=C307]): available in old explores and will be available in new explores. All clear. \n# *Escalations Rate*: [~accountid:5cfa2fcfec35800e97b3027f] this metric isn’t planned on our side and isn’t available in both old and new explores. *The way I understand it is you want to check how many cases in house agents handled against how many cases they’ve put to solved, right?* If such description makes sense, then we will be able to get to this in new explores (not in old ones) as we will have both *Manual Handled - Cases Count* and *Manual Solved - Cases Count*, so you will be able to see the difference for each agent. *Would that work?* \n\n\nLet me know if any additional questions! ","2026-01-30T07:03:25.553Z"],["3851180","PFI-840580","PFI","kornwika.pattana@bolt-outsource.eu","Kornwika Pattana","!1000000317.jpg.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260130-070358.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T07:04:21.521Z"],["3851181","LSS-60607","LSS","kaarel.kook@bolt.eu","Kaarel Kook","Thanks so much! 🙏","2026-01-30T07:04:33.362Z"],["3851184","WEBSD-1529","WEBSD","mariam.maghalashvili@bolt.eu","Mariam Maghalashvili","!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 11.02.34.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T07:05:59.848Z"],["3851187","DSR-4227","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T07:06:07.504Z"],["3851189","PFI-840051","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-30T07:06:55.002Z"],["3851190","PFI-840277","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. I noticed that your ticket does not include a valid payout link, so the Partner Payments Team may not be able to help with it.\n                         \n        If your request is related to a specific payout/Early Cashout, please kindly create a new ticket and add a valid payout link. You can find the payout link here: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts\n        Pro tip: if the link does not fit into the field, copy and paste only this part: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/XXXXXXXXX\n\n        If your question is not related to a specific payout, please kindly wait until a Partner Payments Specialist reviews your request.\n        \n        If you wish to ask a general question, you can also contact us via our Slack channel #commerce-support-partner-payments.","2026-01-30T07:06:57.741Z"],["3851197","PFI-840540","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Based on what is he saying that? The invoice period shows it’s for February 2025. Moreover, the driver didn’t have any rides before February, hence no other invoices. ","2026-01-30T07:10:35.255Z"],["3851198","PFI-840540","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T07:11:18.899Z"],["3851201","LSS-62410","LSS","liisa.aavik@bolt.eu","Liisa Aavik","Completing the sentence above in the ticket: “After you've approved everything is in order, I’ll sync with commercial approver Samantha Sayers and we can proceed with signing.” \n\nCould you please share your estimated timeline for providing the first response? We’re aiming to start working with the partner already next week. Thanks so much for your help and support! \n\n\n\n","2026-01-30T07:12:34.391Z"],["3851202","PFI-840031","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending (last log: 2026-01-25) because payment validation is in progress, which can take longer than usual due to compliance checks on the provider’s side. We are monitoring this and will respond to any requests; once validation completes, the payout will be processed automatically—no action needed from the partner right now. Please inform the partner that it may take a bit longer to reflect on their bank account after processing.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:12:51.156Z"],["3851203","LSS-62434","LSS","philip.lingman@bolt.eu","Philip Lingman","!TikTok Business Registration Flow.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T07:13:00.737Z"],["3851205","PFI-840032","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending and the provider’s payment validation is in progress, taking longer than usual. This likely relates to a compliance review or a temporary provider-side issue; we’re monitoring and responding to any requests promptly, and no action is required from the partner at this time. Please inform the partner that the payout will be processed and reflected on their bank account once the validation completes.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-30T07:13:19.128Z"],["3851206","DSR-3351","DSR","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] , please answer the following:\n\n{quote}Dear [name],\n\nThank you for your message.\n\nWe understand that you disagree with our conclusion. However, the screenshot you have shared showing your current consent settings in the app does not demonstrate that consent was not given in the past.\n\nThe records we have provided reflect historical system logs showing that you actively confirmed consent on 25 April 2025 and again on 13 May 2025. These logs are generated at the time a user takes an affirmative action in the app and are retained for compliance and audit purposes. They are separate from, and not overwritten by, the current state of your consent settings. Changing or withdrawing consent at a later point results in the consent toggles being switched off going forward, but it does not erase the record that consent was previously given, nor does it affect the lawfulness of processing that took place before withdrawal.\n\nFor completeness, we confirm again that:\n\n* the data shared was limited to your name, email address, and phone number;\n* the data was shared only after consent was recorded; and\n* the legal basis for the processing was your consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR.\n\nBased on the system records available to us, we have no indication of any data sharing with Eternis taking place without a valid consent being in place at the relevant times.\n\nOn this basis, we consider this aspect of your data subject access request to have been addressed in full. We will not revise our assessment unless you are able to point to any materially new information that has not already been considered.\n\nSincerely,\n\nBolt{quote}","2026-01-30T07:13:22.181Z"],["3851207","PFI-840047","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected because the beneficiary account number/IBAN failed the bank’s check‑digit validation, which means the bank details are incorrect or mistyped. Please ask the partner to update their bank details (enter the correct IBAN/account number exactly as issued by their bank); once corrected, the payout will be reprocessed in the next regular cycle, and for Early Cashout they can try again after fixing the details. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:13:41.034Z"],["3851209","LSS-60621","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1], thank you for the explanation! Will try to capture it in the agreement. Unfortunately, I will not be able to join the call due to the conflicting call that I absolutely cannot reschedule. ","2026-01-30T07:13:47.435Z"],["3851211","PFI-840049","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout is still pending; the bank has accepted the transfer (last update on 27 Jan), so it’s in process and should reach the account shortly. Given the ticket date (29 Jan), this is within the normal 1–2 business day window, and the status should update by the next business day. If it’s still not received after 2–3 business days, please inform the partner that there may be a provider delay under review—we’re monitoring and will act on any compliance requests.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:14:07.382Z"],["3851212","PFI-840088","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This early cashout has been successfully processed (state: finished) on 26 Jan 2026. Please download the proof of payout (if available) and share it with the partner; if the funds are still not received, advise them to contact their bank with the proof to trace the payment. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-30T07:14:36.055Z"],["3851213","PFI-840100","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is in exported state — it was sent to the bank on 26 Jan 2026 and is currently being processed, so a short delay is possible. Please inform the partner it should reach their account shortly; if it’s still not received by the next business day, ask them to check with their beneficiary bank for incoming transfers. We are monitoring exported/pending payouts on our side and will handle any provider queries; no action is required from the partner in the app.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-30T07:15:02.797Z"],["3851215","PFI-840118","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout has been pending since 23 Jan, which is longer than usual. The delay is likely due to a compliance review or a temporary issue on the provider’s side; we are monitoring it and will act on any requests immediately. Please inform the partner that it is still being processed and no action is required from their side for now; we will update the status as soon as it changes. \nP.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase.","2026-01-30T07:15:35.747Z"],["3851217","FX-3764","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Jana Lutus [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769757321353049]*{color}:\nalready being handled in [this ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3744]\n\nLinked messages:\n[no preview available]\n{quote}","2026-01-30T07:15:37.734Z"],["3851220","LSS-62297","LSS","krzysztof.kozlik@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Koźlik","Hi, yes it will be okey. Thanks!","2026-01-30T07:15:55.332Z"],["3851221","PFI-840145","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This cashout has been pending with the provider since 2026-01-25, which is longer than usual; this typically happens due to a compliance review or a temporary technical issue on the provider’s side. The Partner Payments team is monitoring it and will respond to any provider checks promptly so it can be released—no action is required from the partner at the moment. The status will update automatically once processed.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:15:56.177Z"],["3851223","PFI-840175","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The latest payout was rejected by the payment provider on 2026-01-28, and no clear rejection reason was returned in the logs. No action is required from the partner right now — the payout will be automatically reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle; if this was an Early Cashout, they can try to request it again. If the funds are still not received after the next cycle, please reply to this ticket.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:16:27.198Z"],["3851224","FX-3764","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769757386467009]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3764 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T07:16:39.371Z"],["3851225","PFI-840287","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! I can see that there was a manual adjustment done due to incorrect price: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/6884295486|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records/6884295486]\n\nHowever, as it wasn’t done by Billing and I don’t see any additional comments, then I can’t really offer any further insight into why it was done. 😞 ","2026-01-30T07:16:56.175Z"],["3851226","PFI-840190","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. This Early Cashout is in Exported state (last updated on 2026-01-14), meaning it was sent for processing but is taking longer than usual. Such delays can occur due to ongoing compliance checks or provider-side technical issues; the Partner Payments team is monitoring and responding to any requests from the provider. Please inform the partner that no action is required on their side for now; the payout will complete and the status will update automatically once processing finishes.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:17:00.352Z"],["3851228","PFI-840240","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was exported on 26 Jan and is currently being processed by the bank, which can take up to 2–3 business days to reflect. Given it was exported three days before the ticket, a slight delay is possible and we are monitoring pending payouts with the provider. Please ask the partner to wait one more business day; if the funds still do not arrive, they can contact their beneficiary bank to check for incoming transfers.\nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:17:34.311Z"],["3851230","PFI-840590","PFI","elijah.ojeamien@bolt-outsource.eu","Elijah Ojeamien","[^POP bolt TGH.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-30T07:18:01.926Z"],["3851231","PFI-840298","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout(s) are still pending because payment validation is in progress, which can occasionally take longer than 2–3 business days. We are monitoring these pending payouts and will respond to any compliance requests promptly; once validation completes, the funds will be processed automatically and reflected on the partner’s bank account. If you need anything else, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-30T07:18:16.834Z"],["3851232","PFI-840301","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout is still pending because payment validation is in progress (last update on 24 Jan), which can delay the transfer by a few business days. Please inform the partner that no action is needed on their side right now; we are monitoring the case and will respond to any compliance checks to get it released as soon as possible. If you have any other questions, please reply to this ticket. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase.","2026-01-30T07:18:51.460Z"],["3851234","PFI-840479","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was exported to the bank on 2026-01-26 and is awaiting bank confirmation, which means it is still being processed. As it has been around 2–3 business days since export, the delay is likely due to a compliance review or a technical queue on the provider side; the Partner Payments team monitors such cases and responds to any checks promptly. Please inform the partner to wait a bit longer and, if the funds are still not received within the next 1–2 business days, they can contact their bank to check for the incoming transfer. \nP.S. Please note that the Partner Payments Bot is in the testing phase. If you have any feedback, please share it with us.","2026-01-30T07:19:17.884Z"],["3851236","PFI-840435","PFI","narmin.mammadli@bolt.eu","Narmin Mammadli","Hi! Partner Payments Bot here. The payout was rejected by the payment provider, and no exact reason was provided in their response. Please inform the partner that it will be reprocessed in the next regular payout cycle (if it was an Early Cashout, they can try again now); if the issue repeats, ask them to double-check the beneficiary details (IBAN and account holder name) to rule out data entry errors. P.S. The Partner Payments Bot is currently in the testing phase; feedback is appreciated.","2026-01-30T07:19:58.034Z"],["3851240","LSS-61951","LSS","laura.suveika@bolt.eu","Laura Suveika","[~accountid:63da287e790148a18093a774] sharing with you the reviewed contract from the partner side. Everything is OK. \n\nHowever, it seems that additional changes to the contract may be required from an invoicing and tax perspective. But let’s add everything to the newest version. Thanks!\n\n[^2026.01.28. - BOLT SERVICES LV - BALTSTOR - reklamas izvietosanas ligums.docx]\n\n","2026-01-30T07:22:39.081Z"],["3851241","CSDA-313","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Hi, Natia! There are two approaches we can take here: \n\n# [+*Approach 1*+|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/x/1n5hrc0mKs0h2soSusCyUT]. Check the delta between incoming escalated support cases and incoming escalated support cases that had at least one second of handling time. This corresponds to your option of “how many tickets has any action by agent / total created tickets day by day”.\n# [*Approach 2*|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/x/EJv2e7oBpg9ccwnOpskkRd]. Check the delta between incoming escalated support cases and incoming escalated support cases that are now in status Solved or Closed. This corresponds to “how many solved / total created ticket”. \n\n\n\nAs pointed out by Zaur in the Slack thread, you can see that there is a big difference compared to old explore, because we are using different version of handling time now, which is captured more precisely. The definition of handled case also changed from complex conditions in old explore to a simple “has any handling time captured” in new explores. \n\n\n\nPlease check both options and let me know which one works best for you. After that I will standardize it and either create a report for it or include in existing dashboards. ","2026-01-30T07:22:45.554Z"],["3851243","G3IOT-701","G3IOT","mikhail.urbant@bolt.eu","Mikhail Urbant","Will start testing modem FW update on WH scooter","2026-01-30T07:22:57.962Z"],["3851245","HS-29552","HS","aikemaris.muursepp@bolt.eu","Aike-Maris Müürsepp","No sick leave in [eesti.ee|http://eesti.ee] yet.","2026-01-30T07:23:22.141Z"],["3851246","PFI-840163","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! The adjustment is in a rejected state. Please contact the local cs team to review this. ","2026-01-30T07:23:29.858Z"],["3851248","PFI-839737","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hello [~accountid:712020:4db9b3bc-a4d4-47a5-bda5-c63f19063be7],\n\nYou can compensate the driver for these mentioned orders. \n\nBest Regards,\n\nNigar Alizada ","2026-01-30T07:23:39.238Z"],["3851249","LSS-62435","LSS","lillian.martin@bolt.eu","Lillian Martin","!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 08.22.40.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T07:23:40.545Z"],["3851250","PFI-840128","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! The business has a resale setup, meaning that the business will receive a joint invoice at the end of the month. This invoice is expected and correct. ","2026-01-30T07:24:45.567Z"],["3851252","WD-22666","WD","elchin.nabiyev@bolt.eu","Elchin Nabiyev","[~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] hi! sent for jan 2026 will be run after closing 2026","2026-01-30T07:25:08.411Z"],["3851254","DELIVERY-953","DELIVERY","alexandra.binca@bolt.eu","Alexandra Bătușel","26W05: the experiment that ran in Nov had a slightly non-significant increase in honey orders. no other in-depth analysis happened. we will roll it out globally next week. [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14145|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/experiment-targeting/targeting/tests/edit/14145]","2026-01-30T07:25:42.229Z"],["3851255","DRAG101-329","DRAG101","erki.saarik@bolt.eu","Erki Saarik","3D and 2D drawings are sent to [~accountid:712020:82bad36a-3f0b-4609-8bbe-b4ba65e1094e] - waiting feedback from suppliers {{2026-02-06}} \n\n\n\nTested the 3D printed part on D3 scooter\n\n|!dda194c5b78113db5abd390e0a0744b0-20260130-071030.jpg|width=266,alt=\"dda194c5b78113db5abd390e0a0744b0-20260130-071030.jpg\"!\nSlot on washer allows to install the part without disassembling the cables|!ef2efc41871e7c5f33be6dff0f7b071f-20260130-071039.jpg|width=266,alt=\"ef2efc41871e7c5f33be6dff0f7b071f-20260130-071039.jpg\"!|!cf9f115f73e0377ffd55208a019480f1-20260130-071044.jpg|width=266,alt=\"cf9f115f73e0377ffd55208a019480f1-20260130-071044.jpg\"!|!6413701898917a5d428e970543cf1cb3-20260130-071050.jpg|width=266,alt=\"6413701898917a5d428e970543cf1cb3-20260130-071050.jpg\"!|!1df2896ad0fdf64fdfa8cc0802a14171-20260130-071056.jpg|width=266,alt=\"1df2896ad0fdf64fdfa8cc0802a14171-20260130-071056.jpg\"!|\n|!79eb9f20d07a414ff35cbfe69d3ac228-20260130-071106.jpg|width=266,alt=\"79eb9f20d07a414ff35cbfe69d3ac228-20260130-071106.jpg\"!|!3aaad6b4571141dabc1cdb962573548c-20260130-071116.jpg|width=266,alt=\"3aaad6b4571141dabc1cdb962573548c-20260130-071116.jpg\"!|!3f9275a7aba0af8ce347a5ec138df44c-20260130-071122.jpg|width=266,alt=\"3f9275a7aba0af8ce347a5ec138df44c-20260130-071122.jpg\"!|!2c1982228ae4d4345dce0a8e6ed87ff9-20260130-071128.jpg|width=266,alt=\"2c1982228ae4d4345dce0a8e6ed87ff9-20260130-071128.jpg\"!|!7c9a1500577c52b041e1fd725cd26aa0-20260130-071356.jpg|width=266,alt=\"7c9a1500577c52b041e1fd725cd26aa0-20260130-071356.jpg\"!\nGap between the dust cover and head tube is ~0.35 mm (it is better to have little bigger gap to avoid the head tube paint scratching).|","2026-01-30T07:26:00.397Z"],["3851257","CCM-22301","CCM","alexandra.anastasiei@bolt.eu","Alexandra Anastasiei","Shared access! Yes, TP but only the Safety team for UK. It’s 19 agents, I shared the emails in the document attached. ","2026-01-30T07:26:40.230Z"],["3851258","PFI-838778","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe total amount of the order is HUF 28,800, but only HUF 19,150 was charged from the customer’s card and the remaining HUF 9650 from the Bolt balance as debt. The refund was made to the customer’s card and not the Bolt balance which is why the debt was not cleared. The customer will have to pay the debt by topping up their balance or it can also be added to their next order.","2026-01-30T07:26:48.155Z"],["3851261","PFI-838784","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\n\n\nThe Customer Payments Operations Team does not have the required tools/permissions to issue refunds. If you are not able to issue the refund then we kindly ask you to check with your Team Lead on how to solve this case. You may need to request the following accesses in Admin to be able to issue refund for orders if you previously do not have such: \n\n\n\n* *Rides*: refund_payments and customer_support_beehive_ridehailing_order_refund\n* *Delivery*:  delivery_order_refund\n* *Rentals*: rental_order_refund, rental_subscriptions_refund and rental_order_refund_city_fine\n* *Carsharing*: rental_car_order_refund\n* *Bolt+*: subscription_offer_customer_support\n\n\n\n{color:#bf2600}*Note: A failed card payment can’t be refunded to the card. Only successful card payments can be refunded to card.*{color}\n\nFor issues with refunds from Beehive, kindly reach out to #beehive-agent-support on Slack.\n\n{color:#ff5630}For older orders refund, kindly check with your team lead as they have the required accesses to perform such operations.{color}\n\n","2026-01-30T07:27:55.662Z"],["3851264","DELIVERY-1153","DELIVERY","alexandra.binca@bolt.eu","Alexandra Bătușel","25W05: McD UA is fully on tabletless, McD PT is slowly adopting it. For now engineering is on hold, waiting for the streaming features support that should be provided in March. ","2026-01-30T07:28:13.928Z"],["3851266","DRAG101-464","DRAG101","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Finished modification I will send models to TWS today {{2026-01-30}} ","2026-01-30T07:28:47.867Z"],["3851267","WDFT-3574","WDFT","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hi [~accountid:712020:cfea02e5-8522-43c8-9f69-236d8bece552] ! mapping is created ","2026-01-30T07:28:53.175Z"],["3851269","EBIKE1-226","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","Need to make modification and send out model today. {{2026-01-30}} ","2026-01-30T07:29:51.128Z"],["3851270","CSP-453","CSP","olga.kuchina@bolt.eu","Olga Kuchina","26W5: finished with parameter optimization and added default models (Prophet and naive) to the project, still working on evaluation and metrics module, as well as model recommendation logic and tracking model’s performance in mlflow","2026-01-30T07:30:02.828Z"],["3851271","PFI-838820","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has now been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:30:02.831Z"],["3851272","HS-29457","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:9d22087b-9bd3-42c9-944c-2112fcfa004e],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-30T07:30:21.735Z"],["3851273","CNT-466","CNT","kadi.poll@bolt.eu","Kadi Poll","Hi [~accountid:712020:482e0860-d974-41c5-b7c0-5f29d6d85a90] would you have time to check the copy for our brand new Tech blog article? [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n2Hyhq6_3ZeaPPGOgVqztQ4fkBmt960HncgWX6yTIJg/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.rs0b30x18hok|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n2Hyhq6_3ZeaPPGOgVqztQ4fkBmt960HncgWX6yTIJg/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.rs0b30x18hok|smart-link] \n\nHi [~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] Once Kyrylo has completed the suggestions, please add them to the Tech blog and Medium.","2026-01-30T07:30:35.670Z"],["3851274","WFM-10185","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:5d692bc8a46a5b0bd7fa361b]","2026-01-30T07:30:44.516Z"],["3851275","LSS-62317","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5b34a3b7c4ac74625bdc1020], thanks for raising this ticket. \n\nJust need to check a few things before proceeding with signature:\n\n* Can you share the previously signed DSV?\n* You said that the previous one expired and it needs to be renewed, however, the present agreement is indefinite unless the other party terminates.  \n\nThank you !","2026-01-30T07:30:49.667Z"],["3851277","WFM-10171","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:712020:fb3cc377-463c-41f0-8730-d66abe2f0af0]","2026-01-30T07:31:22.310Z"],["3851278","LSS-62325","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","thank you!","2026-01-30T07:31:25.195Z"],["3851279","LSS-62322","LSS","tomasz.tylus@bolt.eu","Tomasz Tylus","thank you!","2026-01-30T07:31:42.448Z"],["3851282","WFM-10172","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done","2026-01-30T07:32:34.266Z"],["3851288","C2-464","C2","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Inverters sent out to Lisbon ","2026-01-30T07:33:22.651Z"],["3851289","DSR-2883","DSR","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","[~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] I got a notification that WIE would like to access the Google Drive. The 7 days we initially gave the Driver is up today and I was going to remove their access as well. How do you want to proceed? ","2026-01-30T07:34:17.276Z"],["3851291","LSS-60879","LSS","kateryna.torosyan@bolt.eu","Kateryna Torosyan","Hello team,\n\nAs far as I can see, all tokens were canceled, and it seems that there were no payout issues. However, I will contact the driver again to clarify certain details. ","2026-01-30T07:34:24.640Z"],["3851292","PFI-839661","PFI","sofija.danilevica@bolt.eu","Sofija Daņileviča","Provided all reports here [https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1g1_9gGIPJ5ga2go54_ZxgeEnO4g0yoV9|https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1g1_9gGIPJ5ga2go54_ZxgeEnO4g0yoV9|smart-link] \n\n\n\nI used automation, as it does retrieve all information requested in scope of this ticket.","2026-01-30T07:34:34.498Z"],["3851294","LSS-61680","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","[~accountid:5f52461e347294003eca5026] Since we have refunded the smoking fee that was applied incorrectly, from a legal standpoint there are no further obligations on our side.  After the fee was refunded, he has no damages anymore and no legal grounds to claim anything more from us. If he proceeds to lodge complaints with the Verbraucherzentrale or the small claims court etc, we’ll be able to provide evidence that the fee was refunded to him.\n\nIt’s possible to write him an apology and acknowledge that Bolt made a mistake in issuing the fee, but this would be a question of appeasing the customer and not a legal requirement. \n\nLooping you in [~accountid:712020:a3bb4a62-5032-469c-a2b9-4d5c5e6979d6] for your awareness, as this customer is threatening escalation. ","2026-01-30T07:34:51.029Z"],["3851295","WFM-10172","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:712020:f8777cd9-bbc1-420a-93df-3ef14e315717] [dhurka.murugan|mailto:dhurka.murugan@bolt-outsource.eu] has Backlog mode and has Malaysia RH & Safety access so no need to assign the actual queues in Admin since [dhurka.murugan|mailto:dhurka.murugan@bolt-outsource.eu] should be able to view all tickets in Beehive (with cherry picking ability). But we’ve assigned the queue in Assembled so TL can access volume-related data as well in Support Volume Tab.","2026-01-30T07:35:12.686Z"],["3851296","LSS-62317","LSS","helen.erg@bolt.eu","Helen Erg","Previous one was i am afraid with Schenker, but they’ve merged now Schenker and DSV - [https://www.dsv.com/en/about-dsv/press/news/com/2025/04/dsv-completes-acquisition-of-schenker|https://www.dsv.com/en/about-dsv/press/news/com/2025/04/dsv-completes-acquisition-of-schenker|smart-link] \nThey will after merger still be our main partner in all of EU so indefinite is the preferred term anyway.\nShall i find the old Schenker one?","2026-01-30T07:35:20.743Z"],["3851297","DELIVERY-1164","DELIVERY","alexandra.binca@bolt.eu","Alexandra Bătușel","26W05: we created the A/B test to compare the current prioritization against no prioritization. Selected cities: Accra, Constanta, Lviv, Dnipro, Vinnytsia, Siauliai, Krakow, Odesa, Gozo, Sofia. Reasoning behind selection: these are the biggest cities (by  order count) that are not involved in other experiments. From these cities Accra, Krakow and Sofia have also Bolt+ prioritization - TBD if we want to disable prioritization for new users’ only or for bolt+ as well. TBD if the test makes sense based on the percent of the orders created by new users ([~accountid:6268ef941a4eb30069d0a75c] to check with OPS)","2026-01-30T07:35:26.129Z"],["3851298","EBIKE1-376","EBIKE1","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","New test was started {{2026-01-29}} ","2026-01-30T07:35:38.745Z"],["3851299","PFI-840599","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nBusiness ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=282576311\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T07:35:45.179Z"],["3851300","PFI-838854","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1769758545925979?thread_ts=1769439829.095019&cid=CNV6QPRFT|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1769758545925979?thread_ts=1769439829.095019&cid=CNV6QPRFT|smart-card]","2026-01-30T07:36:04.611Z"],["3851302","PFI-838854","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe are checking this issue with the engineering team and will provide more information as soon as possible.","2026-01-30T07:36:38.263Z"],["3851304","WFM-10180","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","[~accountid:712020:74b4c3fb-6caf-4d5d-b7f8-c2ea38318e58]this agent is Soc Med priority (SM). That's the use-case. ","2026-01-30T07:36:57.434Z"],["3851305","LSS-62318","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup"," [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] \n\nAdditional docs \n\n# Bank account statement [^EE003 2519-Account Confirmation Certificate.pdf] \n# Registry certificate [^Bolt Operations OÜ certificate.pdf] \n# Organizational structure of Bolt Group [^Bolt orgchart 31.12.24 .pdf] \n# UBO confirmation  [^UBO - EE 30.06.2025 Bolt Operations OÜ .pdf] \n# Code of Conduct [^Code of Conduct.pdf] \n# Anti-bribery and Anti-corruption policy [^Anti-Bribery and Anti-Corruption Policy .pdf] \n# Health and Safety Policy [^Bolt_Health_and_Safety_Policy.pdf] \n# Supplier Code of Conduct [^Supplier Code of Conduct .pdf]  \n# International Compliance Manual [^International Sanctions Compliance Manual.pdf] ","2026-01-30T07:37:22.533Z"],["3851306","WFM-10213","WFM","essohanam.amana@bolt-outsource.eu","Essohanam Amana","Kindly reminder","2026-01-30T07:37:42.467Z"],["3851308","LSS-60879","LSS","kateryna.torosyan@bolt.eu","Kateryna Torosyan","[Beehive outgoing|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/732412264]","2026-01-30T07:39:06.156Z"],["3851309","LSS-62318","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] please send this doc for signing by Ahto \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ybvhG6EI4f97WMszSF-ZQcK2R7VzKWjO/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ybvhG6EI4f97WMszSF-ZQcK2R7VzKWjO/edit|smart-link]  \n\nAny fastest way of e-signing would suit, thank you ","2026-01-30T07:39:23.161Z"],["3851311","WFM-10207","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Hello [~accountid:712020:857af55c-9293-466a-bbb7-228dc5353b82] what error are you getting? The roles you have shows you should have access to make temp queue assignments","2026-01-30T07:39:43.860Z"],["3851313","LSS-61586","LSS","elchin.nabiyev@bolt.eu","Elchin Nabiyev","[~accountid:712020:78fc81c0-7482-443a-bf90-aacc3d89384a], how do we reflect currently these deposits? are they going through the admin account? We would need to register these as other income in our books however due to the data transfer from Viggo, it is hard to identify the deposits that we received from different FOs. I will contact controlling team, maybe they have better understanding\n\n","2026-01-30T07:40:23.183Z"],["3851314","LSS-62317","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Ok thank you that helps clarify the misunderstanding ! \n\nI will have to review the PoA with Schenker to verify if we need to terminate it or if it has expired. Could you share it please? \n\nI’ll prioritise this matter today. Thank you!","2026-01-30T07:40:27.289Z"],["3851318","WFM-10197","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","[~accountid:712020:75800db6-96e2-4bd3-b62e-19ba67cdd498] could you assist in the queue assignment?","2026-01-30T07:41:30.032Z"],["3851322","PFI-839091","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe are checking this issue with the engineering team and will provide more information as soon as possible.","2026-01-30T07:43:07.750Z"],["3851323","PFI-839091","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1769439829095019|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CNV6QPRFT/p1769439829095019|smart-card]","2026-01-30T07:43:26.402Z"],["3851325","FDBT-4884","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2 fails on 2026-01-29 02:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task aggr_engine_pigment failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': \"ValueError: time data 'None' does not match format '%Y-%m-%d'\", 'run_id': 229132720311670, 'task_key': 'aggr_engine_pigment'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-29T02%3A00%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=finance_model_ledger_aggregation_engine_pigment.finance_model_ledger_aggregation_engine_pigment&base_date=2026-01-29T02%3A00%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-30T07:43:47.198Z"],["3851326","LSS-59845","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey,\n\nAttaching the fully signed version here as well.\n\nThank you!\n\n[^Sentry Order Form for Bolt 09012025 (signed).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-30T07:43:58.138Z"],["3851330","WFM-10194","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:621c70869c3cce006949c677]","2026-01-30T07:45:52.742Z"],["3851332","DO-5840","DO","kaarel.nummert@bolt.eu","Kaarel Nummert","Did I answer your question? Is this issue resolved?","2026-01-30T07:45:59.361Z"],["3851335","PFI-839103","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe first charge with the tip amount added was cancelled and a new charge was placed on the card.\nAmount: PLN 26.68\nAcquirer reference: 601618076408\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:46:36.759Z"],["3851336","WFM-10193","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:712020:dad23bab-7f59-4c27-9127-e31391cf551d]","2026-01-30T07:46:41.545Z"],["3851339","PFI-840603","PFI","jose.caceres@bolt-outsource.eu","José Manuel Angel Fresco Cáceres","!IMG_6623.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_6624.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!IMG_6625.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T07:47:06.784Z"],["3851340","PFI-840603","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T07:47:09.188Z"],["3851344","DBRE-8727","DBRE","susana.oroz@bolt.eu","Susana Salazar Oroz","This is still in progress. Summary will be added before starting next sprint.","2026-01-30T07:48:14.235Z"],["3851349","LSS-61951","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Thank you [~accountid:712020:cb833757-2aa7-4176-9af1-89e3db413a08]! \n[~accountid:625fb4941046bb0071ddf44a] [~accountid:62615f256cb53d006a6a3fe1] - the open point is how to redraft clauses 1.2 and 1.5 to define the services. Please see Laura’s comments in [the ENG draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nk4V8af_edWYJEAmQpSyco856zP953pM/edit], add yours, and suggest how the clauses should be formulated (e.g. whether we should state that Mego provides marketing/promotional services to Bolt) to address any tax concerns.\n\nOnce we agree, I will update the EN and then the LV agreement.\n\nThank you!","2026-01-30T07:48:50.988Z"],["3851351","WFM-10211","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","Market request: https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541933","2026-01-30T07:49:04.300Z"],["3851352","LSS-62317","LSS","helen.erg@bolt.eu","Helen Erg","Hei! Found these ones - \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-35400|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-35400|smart-link] \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-31438|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-31438|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T07:49:07.968Z"],["3851353","FDBT-4881","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_coa_annual_report fails on 2026-01-29 05:05:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 771, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 424, in wrapper\n    return func(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/operators/aws/ecr_docker_operator.py\", line 139, in execute\n    self.runtime_strategy.wait_until_done(self.container_id)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/docker/batch/aws_batch_container_runtime_strategy.py\", line 215, in wait_until_done\n    raise AirflowException(f\"Batch job status is {current_job.status}, failing downstream task\")\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Batch job status is FAILED, failing downstream task\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_data_integration_workiva_coa_annual_report/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-29T05%3A05%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=workiva_coa_annual_report_post_push_files_task&base_date=2026-01-29T05%3A05%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-30T07:49:17.551Z"],["3851356","WFM-10220","WFM","richard.salvador@bolt.eu","Richard Salvador","done [~accountid:712020:a30119b8-464f-40d1-b8b7-28feed5eaaa7]","2026-01-30T07:49:47.151Z"],["3851357","GROWTH-555","GROWTH","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","*Update 30.01.26*\n\n* The feedback from the 3rd sprint has been analysed. \n** There were some bugs regarding the debugging errors, test email sendings and variant resolution logic. \n** Some additional general improvement ideas were proposed by the testing workgroup regarding the QA, HTML editor and testing screen.\n** PS! Some additional feedback regarding the variant resolution and render engine logic will be added in the feedback tasks by the end of 30.01.\n* Sync with the Design team to see, which feedback points should need design as well and what the priority would be.\n* Sync with the MarTech engineers, where the focus was on errors/bugs that occurred with the existing functionalities and improvement ideas that are tightly connected to the existing functionalities.\n** Bug tasks and improvement tasks connected to the existing functionalities were created.\n** General improvement ideas (which are not blockers for achieving feature parity) will be added in the CMS backlog and tackled mainly in stage 3.\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Start preparing test use cases for the next sprint. Main focus will be on canvas<>CMS integration.\n* Sync with the LCM PM on 5th sprint tasks.\n* Create backlog tasks for general improvement ideas.","2026-01-30T07:50:30.076Z"],["3851359","LSS-62438","LSS","risto.kukk@bolt.eu","Risto Kukk","[^SPV7_üürileping muutmine_Bolt Store EE.asice]\n\n","2026-01-30T07:50:46.502Z"],["3851360","CCM-22326","CCM","irena.geber@bolt.eu","Irena Geber","Hey [~accountid:712020:e1485431-1d63-47fe-9d60-d6d4cbc0b242] 👋 \n\nPlease send a Service Desk ticket for these users as well here: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/1/group/1/create/932|smart-link] and add me to that ticket as a participant.\n\nExplain that they are moving from CS to OPS, so they can arrange their OKTA and new accesses they need in the Admin Panel.\n\nI will leave this ticket open.\n\n","2026-01-30T07:50:57.282Z"],["3851361","FPD-1503","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Some ideas on how to use the simulation results:\n\n* Use the optimization lower / upper bounds from the disturbance analysis as an approximate prediction interval for our simulation results, based on historical OH and SS error (either in-sample or via backtest results) - this gives a range of possible GMV uplift coming from the optimized spend scenario","2026-01-30T07:51:11.039Z"],["3851362","LSS-62318","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] \n\n# Additional scheme of Bolt Group structure [^Bolt group structure.pdf] ","2026-01-30T07:51:49.041Z"],["3851367","PFI-840005","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:52:51.790Z"],["3851368","PFI-839589","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:52:54.194Z"],["3851369","PFI-840036","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:52:56.200Z"],["3851370","PFI-839648","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:19.401Z"],["3851371","RLONE-779","RLONE","pema.matos@bolt.eu","Pema Couto Matos","It was agreed with Benjamin that we will go with option B. ","2026-01-30T07:53:19.894Z"],["3851372","PFI-840535","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:21.405Z"],["3851373","PFI-840007","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:23.411Z"],["3851374","LSS-59052","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], \n\nPlease could you reply to the lawyer with the following: \n\n{quote}Bonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nNous vous remercions pour le dépôt du formulaire de demande de réactivation effectué au nom de votre client, Monsieur Yaya DIANE.\n\nNous précisons que les réponses relatives aux demandes de réactivation sont systématiquement adressées directement au titulaire du compte concerné.\n\nAprès traitement de la demande, nous vous confirmons que la condition de délai de six mois requise préalablement à toute réactivation est désormais remplie et que son dossier répond par ailleurs aux critères d’éligibilité applicables.\n\nLa procédure de réactivation du compte de Monsieur Yaya DIANE est donc en cours et devrait intervenir dans les plus brefs délais.\n\nNous restons à votre disposition pour toute précision complémentaire.\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt{quote}\n\n\n\n→ Can you also ask CS to reactivate this account? Thank you ! \n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] ","2026-01-30T07:53:23.989Z"],["3851375","PFI-839591","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:25.365Z"],["3851376","PFI-840270","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_sup