ing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:29.291Z"],["3851378","PFI-839594","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:31.088Z"],["3851379","PFI-839908","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:33.087Z"],["3851380","PFI-839575","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\r\n\r\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\r\n\r\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en\r\n\r\nAdvise the customer to check with their bank to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\r\n\r\nThe reversal can take up to 30 days to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\r\n\r\nThank you,\r\n\r\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:53:35.014Z"],["3851382","LSS-61675","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b],\n\nPlease could you reply to the lawyer with the following:\n\n{quote}Bonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nNous vous remercions pour le dépôt du formulaire de demande de réactivation effectué au nom de votre client, Monsieur Oumar BARRY.\n\nNous précisons que les réponses relatives aux demandes de réactivation sont systématiquement adressées directement au titulaire du compte concerné.\n\nAprès traitement de la demande, nous vous confirmons que la condition de délai de six mois requise préalablement à toute réactivation est désormais remplie et que son dossier répond par ailleurs aux critères d’éligibilité applicables.\n\nLa procédure de réactivation du compte de Monsieur Oumar BARRY est donc en cours et devrait intervenir dans les plus brefs délais.\n\nNous restons à votre disposition pour toute précision complémentaire.\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt{quote}\n\n \n\n→ Can you also ask CS to reactivate this account? Thank you !\n\n\n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] ","2026-01-30T07:54:30.982Z"],["3851385","PFI-840010","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:54:55.589Z"],["3851386","LSS-62360","LSS","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Hey [~accountid:712020:51155f35-611f-4ae4-8802-edf2381a5aaa] \n\n* On the topic of Alfred, [~accountid:712020:90a675ca-07c6-4bf1-b8dd-10fd57db67e2] needs to first find out from  #dev-support-automation-support why Alfred made such a suggestion. I have a feeling Alfred interpreted the case as “I have an unrecognised charge”. In the guidelines for that KB, we ask for such information, as more often it’s not a user but a third party who doesn’t have an account with us. The transactions allow us to locate the acocunt which the payments were made from. \n* We don’t have a KB advising any document uploads to google drives, because it’s not something that should be happening. We shouldn’t have asked for a bank statement at all. The correct process was described by [~accountid:712020:90a675ca-07c6-4bf1-b8dd-10fd57db67e2] above, that we should explain the refund processing time, etc. \n* If we are handling an unrecognised charge case and ask for a bank statement there, that’s okay. If it’s too blurry, we simply need to ask the user to resend it and explain we can’t locate the transactions without a clear statement. \n\n","2026-01-30T07:54:59.720Z"],["3851388","PFI-839745","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-30T07:55:16.068Z"],["3851392","LSS-61672","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b],\n\nPlease could you reply to the lawyer with the following:\n\n{quote}Bonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nNous vous remercions pour le dépôt du formulaire de demande de réactivation effectué au nom de votre client, Monsieur Abdou-El-Azize BAE.\n\nNous précisons que les réponses relatives aux demandes de réactivation sont systématiquement adressées directement au titulaire du compte concerné.\n\nAprès traitement de la demande, nous vous confirmons que la condition de délai de six mois requise préalablement à toute réactivation est désormais remplie et que son dossier répond par ailleurs aux critères d’éligibilité applicables.\n\nLa procédure de réactivation du compte de Monsieur Abdou-El-Azize BAE est donc en cours et devrait intervenir dans les plus brefs délais.\n\nNous restons à votre disposition pour toute précision complémentaire.\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt{quote}\n\n \n\n→ Can you also ask CS to reactivate this account? Thank you !\n\n\n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] ","2026-01-30T07:55:56.574Z"],["3851393","SCM-1129","SCM","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","postponed to 15th of Feb since NB parts are being collected from PL to CWH \nan STK today would get cancelled and re-created","2026-01-30T07:56:25.061Z"],["3851394","LSS-60379","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Slack comment from [~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] (replied via Slack)\n\nYou comment is overall correct, we have not received the controllers we paid repair service cost for to 3B.\nWe have replied to and rejected any invoices we have deemed incorrect (charges for services previously not agreed upon) and requested the partner to reply with the whereabouts our the repaired controllers by December 16th.\nI can forward you the last email I have written to them to which they failed to reply.\nCan we have a call this week to see what can be the further legal actions to force them to give up Bolt's property that they have seized?","2026-01-30T07:56:25.510Z"],["3851396","RCE-388","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769759788753689]*{color}:\nJust started the release. should be done in an hour\n{quote}","2026-01-30T07:56:42.190Z"],["3851397","LSS-62318","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] - please find the signed doc attached 🙂 \n\n[^KYC questionnaire and information letter 2025-01-27 vEN_TDG (1).docx - signed.pdf] ","2026-01-30T07:56:50.071Z"],["3851399","WD-22666","WD","elchin.nabiyev@bolt.eu","Elchin Nabiyev","however, we want the december account certifications to transfer to me","2026-01-30T07:57:36.153Z"],["3851400","PFI-840557","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThere was no charge for this payment. Kindly advise the user to check with their Mobile Money service provider regarding this charge. ","2026-01-30T07:57:39.649Z"],["3851401","LEG-1132","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Email to the external counsel sent on 29 Jan - waiting for their feedback.","2026-01-30T07:57:42.030Z"],["3851403","FDBT-4881","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-30T07:58:19.045Z"],["3851404","LSS-61925","LSS","tarmo.randel@bolt.eu","Tarmo Randel","Thank you Gab for flagging this item - we can not meet the requirement to store log of all data processing activities for 5 years. Administrative activities performed via Admin web application - yes, we store, but not all access (user facing application).\n\n","2026-01-30T07:58:19.775Z"],["3851405","CSDT-973","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Looker sync to be done by Kevin later on today","2026-01-30T07:58:21.086Z"],["3851406","LEG-1327","LEG","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Email to the external counsel sent on 29 Jan - waiting for their feedback.","2026-01-30T07:58:27.105Z"],["3851407","LSS-62208","LSS","mikk.vachtmeister@bolt.eu","Mikk Vachtmeister","Can you share our standard DPA? ","2026-01-30T07:58:54.108Z"],["3851411","HS-29326","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Thank You!\n\nI will let You know once Vitality confirms they have added them to Your plan. \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-30T07:59:04.708Z"],["3851412","LSS-62106","LSS","karl.apsolon@bolt.eu","Karl Apsolon","[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] Looks good, just EE part 9k€ → 30k€ needed. Thanks!","2026-01-30T07:59:16.021Z"],["3851413","PFI-840612","PFI","darren.seruwagi@bolt.eu","Darren Mbigiridde Seruwagi","!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 08.59.02.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T07:59:22.333Z"],["3851415","RDXENG-4683","RDXENG","talha.tahir@bolt.eu","Talha Tahir","Tested add tipping scenario with foreground and background states on CA.195.0 release build. Looks good.\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260130-080840.png|width=1080,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130-080840.png\"!","2026-01-30T07:59:35.556Z"],["3851416","LSS-62318","LSS","aveliis.saluveervutt@bolt.eu","Ave-Liis Saluveer-Vutt","[https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348357?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|https://app.spotdraft.com/contracts/v2/348357?blocked=true&clusterId=EU&workspaceId=31839|smart-link]  ","2026-01-30T07:59:42.589Z"],["3851417","MM-991","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements provided; not enough info for a developer to start.|\n|Clarity|🟡|The summary is understandable, but lack of detail limits clarity.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links to documentation or supporting sources included.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or specs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-30T07:59:56.521Z"],["3851421","CSDT-990","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","[Lage group|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/24041]: Anete Rudzīte: cannot yet do it, need Refund agent event ❌\n\n* Need to add safety boolean from fact_support_case to refunds explore, asked Kevin to do it, because he will do Looker sync today. \n* [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/x/tX1FCvJVSMjZdo9ZqBEdQQ|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/x/tX1FCvJVSMjZdo9ZqBEdQQ] - almost ready query to use","2026-01-30T08:00:57.087Z"],["3851422","LSS-59948","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","ESSENTIALLY: Bolt <> Liki 24 exchange of personal data\n\nLiki 24 <> Pharma onward exchange","2026-01-30T08:01:08.844Z"],["3851423","SCM-804","SCM","federico.levi@bolt.eu","Federico Levi","[~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] hello\nthere is a hickup due to the forecast demand calculations topic we have been discussing on Tuesday\nThe project file is [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1g3fqek9viT2kb_d38Dxwir59f0cZkjKMK6MfN9t-dXo/edit?gid=1284450631#gid=1284450631] (will link it to the ticket as well)\n\nIn the file, I have set calculations for MoM (need to just validate some city names e.g. Antwerp in Workday vs Antwerpen in Admin) - but we discussed to check the WoW too to then identify the more accurate option\n\n\n\nETA postponed to next week","2026-01-30T08:01:36.067Z"],["3851424","BDRIV-7","BDRIV","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","[~accountid:6215e9f275803500683497d5] I agree that more flexibility on the charger current selection, and reporting battery statuses will be useful in the long run, but we must also take into account that we would need to allocate additional resources to creating new infrastructure to (all) warehouses, and ensuring that warehouses know how to use the chargers in a manner that will allow us to reap the benefits (alternatively we would have to automate the charging which would extend the scope of implementing the new infrastructure in warehouses).\n\nWe should know the approximate ROI/benefits of implementing such system before delving deeper into this project. I propose that one way to approach this would be to compare the efficiency and capex cost of: \n\n* Set-value high current (fast) charging in high and low seasons \n\nto \n\n* Dynamic current charging in high and low seasons. ","2026-01-30T08:01:42.819Z"],["3851425","XP-3109","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:61b0698cc75da800725c5dce], \nPlease link the ticket to an epic (so it's visible on the Product Discovery board).","2026-01-30T08:01:48.014Z"],["3851426","XP-3098","XP",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:40cb7816-0b3b-4f87-ae87-8ac607ccf2c0], \nPlease link the ticket to an epic (so it's visible on the Product Discovery board).","2026-01-30T08:01:48.045Z"],["3851427","RCE-388","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Anneli Tammesson [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769760056043659]*{color}:\nLet me know, once done, I´ll start running the pipeline\n{quote}","2026-01-30T08:01:58.447Z"],["3851428","PFI-828373","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, this ticket will be closed. Please follow advice from previous responses and reach out / create new ticket if further help is needed.","2026-01-30T08:02:07.964Z"],["3851429","DSR-4229","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T08:02:07.983Z"],["3851431","C2-463","C2","sander.viitak@bolt.eu","Sander Viitak","[~accountid:5e4658b55a495e0c91a7a011] [~accountid:712020:199c869c-84be-4d6f-9d2d-2a504d806ff1] [~accountid:712020:7636318d-11ba-448e-8ae7-b935370c0640] Will go to Warsaw to check batteries . {{2026-02-03}} ","2026-01-30T08:02:34.635Z"],["3851437","FX-3765","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769760169186229]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3765] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T08:03:33.850Z"],["3851441","PFI-840613","PFI","aleksandra.sheherina@bolt-outsource.eu","Aleksandra Sheherina","[^payment_order_1342037471.pdf.pdf]","2026-01-30T08:04:08.239Z"],["3851442","MM-992","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements provided; insufficient information for a developer to start.|\n|Clarity|🔴|No content in the description; summary alone is not enough for clarity.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links or references to supporting documentation or sources.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description with requirements and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the scope and expected outcome.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or feedback.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-30T08:04:33.939Z"],["3851443","LSS-60535","LSS","toomas.parts@bolt.eu","Toomas-Hendrik Parts","Hey! What is the latest on this?","2026-01-30T08:04:40.613Z"],["3851446","PFI-840613","PFI","aleksandra.sheherina@bolt-outsource.eu","Aleksandra Sheherina","Looks like probably made a payment back to bank account she used to get her payout from. Please let us know if this will be added to balance or returned to her.","2026-01-30T08:04:53.995Z"],["3851447","LSS-62106","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, \n[~accountid:712020:282008bf-7f03-4058-8bec-43f7e5a44ace] thanks! \nTo the Legal Ops team: can we please get a signature for this PoA [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-QipeNsB1bdbrB2XpkFCc4ehk_QYg2Q-/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-QipeNsB1bdbrB2XpkFCc4ehk_QYg2Q-/edit|smart-link]?\n\nThank you!","2026-01-30T08:05:12.738Z"],["3851449","DELIVERY-781","DELIVERY","tudor.suruceanu@bolt.eu","Tudor Suruceanu","26W05: Did a sanity check in Cluj-Napoca, then started a full A/B test in Cluj-Napoca, Valletta, Vilnius, Iasi, Craiova, Prague, Kosice, Brno, Kaunas and Tartu","2026-01-30T08:05:18.712Z"],["3851450","DRX-28415","DRX","ahmed.munir@bolt.eu","Ahmed Munir","Hiding border scenario is also tested from *Order Details Maps* after a fix is made:\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_094837_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_094837_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_094843_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_094843_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_100337_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_100337_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n*Campaigns Map:*\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_095413_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_095413_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_095425_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_095425_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n*Scheduled Rides Detail Screen:*\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_100236_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_100236_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_100145_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_100145_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\n!Screenshot_20260130_100241_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg|width=810,alt=\"Screenshot_20260130_100241_ee.mtakso.driver.internal.prelive.jpg\"!\n\n\n\nVerified","2026-01-30T08:05:43.888Z"],["3851452","PFI-839972","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T08:06:37.214Z"],["3851453","MARTECH3-1574","MARTECH3","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind",":Badger_on_Scooter:  *From Rentals LCM*: We don’t use SMS at all, and there aren’t any plans to use it in the future. Since it’s not relevant for us, I will skip feedback here.","2026-01-30T08:07:00.846Z"],["3851454","LSS-59948","LSS","ema.mlynarcikova@bolt.eu","Ema Mlynarcikova","* -Adjust the consent tickbox – to inform Users their data is shared with Liki24 & Liki24 will share these pharmacies-\n* Liki24 to ensure Pharmacies comply with rules","2026-01-30T08:07:06.805Z"],["3851455","DELIVERY-1173","DELIVERY","tudor.suruceanu@bolt.eu","Tudor Suruceanu","26W05: Completed and started dry-running the Rust implementation globally. We also already switched to only using Rust for Matrix Dispatch in Bucharest. Waiting for more data, to compare performance.","2026-01-30T08:07:14.810Z"],["3851456","PFI-840614","PFI","tatiana.horvathova@bolt-outsource.eu","Tatiana Horváthová","!IMG_4583.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T08:07:28.547Z"],["3851457","PFI-840614","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nDelivery ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1961738486\n","2026-01-30T08:07:30.421Z"],["3851458","FDBT-4884","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2 fails on 2026-01-29 02:00:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task aggr_engine_pigment failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': \"ValueError: time data 'None' does not match format '%Y-%m-%d'\", 'run_id': 1022888791546157, 'task_key': 'aggr_engine_pigment'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-29T02%3A00%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=finance_model_ledger_aggregation_engine_pigment.finance_model_ledger_aggregation_engine_pigment&base_date=2026-01-29T02%3A00%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-30T08:07:53.404Z"],["3851461","CSP-440","CSP","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","26W05:\n\n(/) FAQ pages\n\n:loading: Backend driven icons","2026-01-30T08:09:33.225Z"],["3851464","CSP-389","CSP","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","26W05:\n\n* New tests running without auto submit\n* Next steps agreed upon and rework has started","2026-01-30T08:10:24.074Z"],["3851465","CSP-377","CSP","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","26W05:\n\n* New tests running without auto submit\n* Next steps agreed upon and rework has started","2026-01-30T08:10:27.290Z"],["3851466","CSP-10","CSP","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","26W05:\n\n* New tests running without auto submit\n* Next steps agreed upon and rework has started","2026-01-30T08:10:31.650Z"],["3851467","LSS-61670","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], please could you reply with the following: \n\n\n\nBonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nNous accusons réception de votre email.\n\nAprès examen attentif de la situation de Monsieur Youcef NAJDI, nous vous informons que la demande de réactivation ne peut être acceptée. En effet, le blocage initial du compte, fondé sur plusieurs signalements de passagers pour des comportements inappropriés à caractère sexuel, constitue une violation des conditions contractuelles et porte atteinte à la sécurité des utilisateurs de notre plateforme, ce qui est incompatible avec une remise en service du compte.\n\nConformément au cadre applicable au dialogue social dans le secteur des VTC, nous vous informons que les coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants figurent ci-dessous, si votre client souhaite les contacter.\n\n|[+*Coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants du secteur des VTC*+|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/#h2-2]|\n|*ACIL : Association des Chauffeurs Indépendants Lyonnais*\n* [Site internet |http://www.acilvtclyon.fr/]\n* Coordonnées *:* [acilvtclyon@gmail.com|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/acilvtclyon@gmail.com]|\n|*FO : Force Ouvrière*\n* [Site internet |https://www.force-ouvriere.fr/travailleurs-des-plateformes-avec-fo-pour-gagner-des-droits]\n* Coordonnées *:* [+sg@force-ouvriere.fr+|mailto:sg@force-ouvriere.fr] |\n|h3. *UD - VTC SUD : Union des VTC 06/83*\n* Page [Facebook|https://www.facebook.com/p/UNION-DES-VTC-0683-100088991093162/] \n* Coordonnées :  [+uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com+|mailto:uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com] \n* Représentants :  \n** Houari BEN ALI | 06 01 64 77 79  | [+houari3120@live.fr+|mailto:houari3120@live.fr]  \n** Sabrina SABENA | 07 68 25 41 16 | [+lilisab1930@gmail.com+|mailto:lilisab1930@gmail.com]  \n** Florian RUBELI MAROVELLI | 06 06 44 38 09 | [+florian.rubeli@gmail.com+|mailto:florian.rubeli@gmail.com] |\n|h3. *UNION - Indépendants*\n* [Site internet |https://www.union-independants.fr/]\n* Coordonnées : [contact@union-independants.fr|mailto:contact@union-independants.fr] \n* Représentants : \n** Adel DE SOUSA | [+syndic.occitanie@gmail.com+|mailto:syndic.occitanie@gmail.com]\n** Ali LEMMOUCHI | [+ali197393@hotmail.com+|mailto:ali197393@hotmail.com]\n** Fabian TOSOLINI | [+fabian@union-independants.fr+|mailto:fabian@union-independants.fr]  |\n\nNous restons disponibles pour toute précision utile.\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt\n\n\n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] ","2026-01-30T08:11:08.551Z"],["3851469","PFI-836822","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued, please, find it here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6131434909|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6131434909]","2026-01-30T08:11:31.795Z"],["3851471","LSS-60738","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","Hi team, Pro Bro has decided to update an offer once again, to our benefit and sent a new version of the amendment. Will share a link here, please let me know if we can move ahead with it for signature collection.\n\nHere’s the amendment - [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pN1rKvd6aglQN9ZKv1xVvPRarrRrTljp/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=114882246052216185934&rtpof=true&sd=true|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pN1rKvd6aglQN9ZKv1xVvPRarrRrTljp/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=114882246052216185934&rtpof=true&sd=true|smart-link] \n\nThanks!","2026-01-30T08:12:05.752Z"],["3851477","LSS-58339","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team, [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] [~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17] thank you for your engagement and support 🙏 \n\nJust a gentle reminder that we need to send our response to the lawyer today. Thank you very much.\n\n","2026-01-30T08:13:32.752Z"],["3851480","RDXENG-4220","RDXENG","mustafa.ogun@bolt.eu","Mustafa Ogün Öztürk","We decided to drop that screen for now.","2026-01-30T08:14:15.888Z"],["3851481","XP-2782","XP","andrey.kuzmin@bolt.eu","Andrey Kuzmin","[~accountid:712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] Can be medium","2026-01-30T08:14:20.570Z"],["3851482","PFI-832530","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Reissued","2026-01-30T08:14:20.607Z"],["3851483","CLIENTAPP-38781","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R3020\"","2026-01-30T08:14:34.668Z"],["3851485","CLIENTAPP-38781","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R3021\"","2026-01-30T08:14:51.989Z"],["3851486","RDXENG-4241","RDXENG","mustafa.ogun@bolt.eu","Mustafa Ogün Öztürk","To disable it during the active order, we need BE work.","2026-01-30T08:15:05.783Z"],["3851487","RDXENG-4244","RDXENG","mustafa.ogun@bolt.eu","Mustafa Ogün Öztürk","To disable it during the active order, we need BE work.","2026-01-30T08:15:15.075Z"],["3851488","LSS-61773","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], please could you reply with the following:\n\nBonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nSuite à votre demande concernant Monsieur Nassim ADRAR, nous vous informons que, conformément à nos procédures internes, une période de 6 mois à compter de la date du blocage, le 1er août 2025 dans le cas de Monsieur Nassim ADRAR, doit s’écouler avant que la demande de réactivation puisse être examinée.\n\nNous vous invitons à revenir vers nous à compter du 1 février 2026 pour effectuer la demande de réactivation du compte.\n\nConformément au cadre applicable au dialogue social dans le secteur des VTC, nous vous informons que les coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants figurent ci-dessous, si votre client souhaite les contacter.\n\n|h2. [+*Coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants du secteur des VTC*+|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/#h2-2]|\n|h3. *ACIL : Association des Chauffeurs Indépendants Lyonnais*\n* [Site internet |http://www.acilvtclyon.fr/]\n* Coordonnées *:* [acilvtclyon@gmail.com|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/acilvtclyon@gmail.com]|\n|h3. *FO : Force Ouvrière*\n* [Site internet |https://www.force-ouvriere.fr/travailleurs-des-plateformes-avec-fo-pour-gagner-des-droits]\n* Coordonnées *:* [+sg@force-ouvriere.fr+|mailto:sg@force-ouvriere.fr] |\n|h3. *UD - VTC SUD : Union des VTC 06/83*\n* Page [Facebook|https://www.facebook.com/p/UNION-DES-VTC-0683-100088991093162/] \n* Coordonnées :  [+uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com+|mailto:uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com] \n* Représentants :  \n** Houari BEN ALI | 06 01 64 77 79  | [+houari3120@live.fr+|mailto:houari3120@live.fr]  \n** Sabrina SABENA | 07 68 25 41 16 | [+lilisab1930@gmail.com+|mailto:lilisab1930@gmail.com]  \n** Florian RUBELI MAROVELLI | 06 06 44 38 09 | [+florian.rubeli@gmail.com+|mailto:florian.rubeli@gmail.com] |\n|h3. *UNION - Indépendants*\n* [Site internet |https://www.union-independants.fr/]\n* Coordonnées : [contact@union-independants.fr|mailto:contact@union-independants.fr] \n* Représentants : \n** Adel DE SOUSA | [+syndic.occitanie@gmail.com+|mailto:syndic.occitanie@gmail.com]\n** li LEMMOUCHI | [+ali197393@hotmail.com+|mailto:ali197393@hotmail.com]\n** Fabian TOSOLINI | [+fabian@union-independants.fr+|mailto:fabian@union-independants.fr]  |\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt \n\n\n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] ","2026-01-30T08:15:15.107Z"],["3851489","LSS-62440","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nSigrid Hõbejärv has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-30T08:15:32.443Z"],["3851492","GROWTH-610","GROWTH","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","*Update 30.01.26*\n\n* The Message CMS <> Canvas integration was deployed this week.\n** The message node in canvas now lets you choose a message to send from active CMS templates. This means that we can target users (Rider and Driver domains at the moment) and send Emails and SMSs via Canvases.\n** The end-to-end pipeline is working as originally designed,  where sending respects frequency caps and quiet hours.\n** !Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 10.09.22.png|width=735,height=537,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 10.09.22.png\"!\n* First brief tests have been promising, as correct messages have reached the test user. Needs thorough testing from the testing workgroup with real use cases.\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Safe tests in live Admin Panel with the LCM Testing Workgroup. \n** Have to be careful with the setups (only test with known user IDs) as Email and SMS channels can send real messages.\n* During testing, the following must be taken into account:\n** Functional checks:\n*** Verify the message render logic (correct language, correct personalisation)\n*** Translation behaviour and translation fallback behaviour\n*** Variant resolution behaviour (correct variant based on the user context)\n*** Verify the nodes in Canvas (Delay, Audience Path, Action Path) function correctly.\n** Safety checks:\n*** Confirm frequency caps, quiet hours, recipient selection","2026-01-30T08:16:38.343Z"],["3851493","SUPX-1769","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","Closing and moving to a separate story","2026-01-30T08:16:43.247Z"],["3851494","LSS-62440","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-30T08:16:58.777Z"],["3851495","SUPX-1769","SUPX","christian.kalme@bolt.eu","Christian Kalme","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2369|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2369|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T08:16:58.935Z"],["3851498","IPOPS-21","IPOPS","swapnil.kasar@bolt.eu","Swapnil Kasar","# [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A9H7ZR79U/p1769760654033829|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A9H7ZR79U/p1769760654033829]\n# ","2026-01-30T08:17:29.334Z"],["3851502","LSS-60063","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","Hi [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a], not sure if you’ve seen the email, but Ignitis reached out to us and  said that they will move ahead with the DSA agreement, therefore the meeting has been cancelled. \n\n[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] let me know when we can move ahead with sharing the updated agreement with them 🙂 \n\nThanks team!","2026-01-30T08:18:08.906Z"],["3851503","PFI-840047","PFI","augustas.strimaitis@bolt-outsource.eu","Augustas Strimaitis","Could you please review it again?","2026-01-30T08:18:11.182Z"],["3851504","LSS-61925","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:c0f6fbe7-f5ae-44e2-bb6c-8e5815ace0d9] please take a look at my comments, can we align how much room to negotiate do we have? As [~accountid:5c987f2c0cf73c3215ff6aa7] pointed out, we’re not able to comply with all requirements. ","2026-01-30T08:18:12.169Z"],["3851507","PFI-838649","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThere was a temporary technical issue with the payment service provider which caused the payments to fail. We have now cancelled the payments and for orders that were completed, a balance debt will be created to the user's account and they will be able to pay it with their next order.","2026-01-30T08:18:48.893Z"],["3851508","PFI-840009","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThere was a temporary technical issue with the payment service provider which caused the payments to fail. We have now cancelled the payments and for orders that were completed, a balance debt will be created to the user's account and they will be able to pay it with their next order.","2026-01-30T08:18:51.246Z"],["3851509","PFI-838647","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThere was a temporary technical issue with the payment service provider which caused the payments to fail. We have now cancelled the payments and for orders that were completed, a balance debt will be created to the user's account and they will be able to pay it with their next order.","2026-01-30T08:18:53.278Z"],["3851510","PFI-840018","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThere was a temporary technical issue with the payment service provider which caused the payments to fail. We have now cancelled the payments and for orders that were completed, a balance debt will be created to the user's account and they will be able to pay it with their next order.","2026-01-30T08:18:55.056Z"],["3851511","DSR-3777","DSR","sigrid.hobejarv@bolt.eu","Sigrid Hõbejärv","[~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] We received the below response: \n\nTo the Bolt Data Privacy Team,\n\nYour \"sincere apology\" for the delay is as hollow as the data dump you’ve provided. Do not mistake my patience for ignorance.\n\n​I did not submit a Data Subject Access Request (DSAR) to receive a copy of my own name and phone number—I have those on my ID card. I submitted this request to uncover the specific, granular evidence used to restrict my access to the Bolt platform.\n\nYour response is a calculated failure for the following reasons:\n\n* _​Violation of Section 26(b) (Right to Access):_ You have provided \"supporting documents,\" yet none of them detail the specific \"Partner Level\" logs that triggered my deactivation. Where are the timestamps, the specific trip IDs, and the internal \"Quality\" tags that led to this decision?\n* ​_Profiling & Automated Decisions:_ Under the Kenya Data Protection Act, I have the right to know the logic involved in automated processing. Your system blocked me; I demand the raw data strings and the compliance matrix parameters that flagged my account.\n* ​*Article 47 Defiance: *You mention my right to a \"judicial remedy.\" Rest assured, I am well aware. However, under the Constitution of Kenya, I am entitled to written reasons for administrative action that adversely affects my rights. \"Attached data\" is not a \"reason.\"\n\n_My Final Demand:_ Within 48 hours, you will provide a supplementary disclosure that includes:\n\n* The _exact \"Partner Level\" error logs_ associated with my account.\n* The _specific customer complaints_ (redacted only for names, not substance) and the internal investigation notes that supposedly \"verified\" them.\n* The _audit trail_ of the \"numerous warnings\" Ricky claimed were sent, which are suspiciously missing from your first batch of data.\n\nIf you continue to play this game of \"hide and seek\" with my personal data, I will not \"contact you further\" to \"address concerns.\" I will move directly to the ODPC for an Enforcement Notice and file for special damages at the High Court for the loss of income caused by your technical opacity and procedural unfairness.\n\n​James Kimani Nderu 0735100002","2026-01-30T08:18:56.187Z"],["3851512","PFI-839003","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\r\nThere was a temporary technical issue with the payment service provider which caused the payments to fail. We have now cancelled the payments and for orders that were completed, a balance debt will be created to the user's account and they will be able to pay it with their next order.","2026-01-30T08:18:56.856Z"],["3851513","LSS-61606","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey team, \n[~accountid:60acb13f1155bb006fce252c] could you please share our signed response with the partner? \n[^2026-01-30 atsakymas į pretenziją (Sushi).docx (1).pdf] \n\nThank you all for your help and involvement! ","2026-01-30T08:19:22.684Z"],["3851514","LSS-59351","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], please could you reply with the following:\n\n\n\nBonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nSuite à votre demande concernant Monsieur Ibrahim BAMBA, nous vous informons que, conformément à nos procédures internes, une période de 6 mois à compter de la date du blocage, le 18 septembre 2025 dans le cas de Monsieur Ibrahim BAMBA, doit s’écouler avant que la demande de réactivation puisse être examinée.\n\nNous vous invitons à revenir vers nous à compter du 18 mars 2026 pour effectuer la demande de réactivation du compte.\n\nConformément au cadre applicable au dialogue social dans le secteur des VTC, nous vous informons que les coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants figurent ci-dessous, si votre client souhaite les contacter.\n\n|h2. [+*Coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants du secteur des VTC*+|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/#h2-2]|\n|h3. *ACIL : Association des Chauffeurs Indépendants Lyonnais*\n* [Site internet |http://www.acilvtclyon.fr/]\n* Coordonnées *:* [acilvtclyon@gmail.com|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/acilvtclyon@gmail.com]|\n|h3. *FO : Force Ouvrière*\n* [Site internet |https://www.force-ouvriere.fr/travailleurs-des-plateformes-avec-fo-pour-gagner-des-droits]\n* Coordonnées *:* [+sg@force-ouvriere.fr+|mailto:sg@force-ouvriere.fr] |\n|h3. *UD - VTC SUD : Union des VTC 06/83*\n* Page [Facebook|https://www.facebook.com/p/UNION-DES-VTC-0683-100088991093162/] \n* Coordonnées :  [+uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com+|mailto:uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com] \n* Représentants :  \n** Houari BEN ALI | 06 01 64 77 79  | [+houari3120@live.fr+|mailto:houari3120@live.fr]  \n** Sabrina SABENA | 07 68 25 41 16 | [+lilisab1930@gmail.com+|mailto:lilisab1930@gmail.com]  \n** Florian RUBELI MAROVELLI | 06 06 44 38 09 | [+florian.rubeli@gmail.com+|mailto:florian.rubeli@gmail.com] |\n|h3. *UNION - Indépendants*\n* [Site internet |https://www.union-independants.fr/]\n* Coordonnées : [contact@union-independants.fr|mailto:contact@union-independants.fr] \n* Représentants : \n** Adel DE SOUSA | [+syndic.occitanie@gmail.com+|mailto:syndic.occitanie@gmail.com]\n** li LEMMOUCHI | [+ali197393@hotmail.com+|mailto:ali197393@hotmail.com]\n** Fabian TOSOLINI | [+fabian@union-independants.fr+|mailto:fabian@union-independants.fr]  |\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt\n\n\n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] ","2026-01-30T08:19:23.323Z"],["3851518","TAXP-3405","TAXP","gerard.everaert@bolt.eu","Gerard Everaert","The Romanian tax authority registered a Romanian PE for Bolt Operations OÜ on 11 December 2025. Their arguments are based on the concept of dependent agent, claiming that Bolt Operations OÜ develops its activity in Romania through Bolt Services RO SRL, which we do not agree with. Considering the analysis made by EY and Băncilă, Diaconu și Asociații SPRL regarding their arguments and likelihood of success of Bolt’s judicial challenge, we are not going to make additional in-depth analysis. Bolt Operations OÜ filed an administrative claim against the ex-officio PE registration on 23 January 2026 (attached hereto) and will follow with a judicial claim to suspend the PE registration until the main administrative and judicial claims on the registration itself are resolved. [^23012026-130633- (1).pdf] ","2026-01-30T08:20:44.536Z"],["3851520","DSR-4231","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T08:21:07.881Z"],["3851521","LSS-61689","LSS","anna.selecka@bolt.eu","Anna Selecka","Ōsom, thank you! Please let me know once signed, so once Nina’s back, I can proudly tell her it’s done 😂","2026-01-30T08:21:17.153Z"],["3851522","LSS-59762","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], please could you reply with the following:\n\n \n\nBonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nSuite à votre demande concernant Monsieur Karim DIAKITE, nous vous informons que, conformément à nos procédures internes, une période de 6 mois à compter de la date du blocage, le 11 septembre 2025 dans le cas de Monsieur Karim DIAKITE, doit s’écouler avant que la demande de réactivation puisse être examinée.\n\nNous vous invitons à revenir vers nous à compter du 11 mars 2026 pour effectuer la demande de réactivation du compte.\n\nConformément au cadre applicable au dialogue social dans le secteur des VTC, nous vous informons que les coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants figurent ci-dessous, si votre client souhaite les contacter.\n\n|h2. [+*Coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants du secteur des VTC*+|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/#h2-2]|\n|h3. *ACIL : Association des Chauffeurs Indépendants Lyonnais*\n* [Site internet |http://www.acilvtclyon.fr/]\n* Coordonnées *:* [acilvtclyon@gmail.com|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/acilvtclyon@gmail.com]|\n|h3. *FO : Force Ouvrière*\n* [Site internet |https://www.force-ouvriere.fr/travailleurs-des-plateformes-avec-fo-pour-gagner-des-droits]\n* Coordonnées *:* [+sg@force-ouvriere.fr+|mailto:sg@force-ouvriere.fr] |\n|h3. *UD - VTC SUD : Union des VTC 06/83*\n* Page [Facebook|https://www.facebook.com/p/UNION-DES-VTC-0683-100088991093162/] \n* Coordonnées :  [+uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com+|mailto:uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com] \n* Représentants :  \n** Houari BEN ALI | 06 01 64 77 79  | [+houari3120@live.fr+|mailto:houari3120@live.fr]  \n** Sabrina SABENA | 07 68 25 41 16 | [+lilisab1930@gmail.com+|mailto:lilisab1930@gmail.com]  \n** Florian RUBELI MAROVELLI | 06 06 44 38 09 | [+florian.rubeli@gmail.com+|mailto:florian.rubeli@gmail.com] |\n|h3. *UNION - Indépendants*\n* [Site internet |https://www.union-independants.fr/]\n* Coordonnées : [contact@union-independants.fr|mailto:contact@union-independants.fr] \n* Représentants : \n** Adel DE SOUSA | [+syndic.occitanie@gmail.com+|mailto:syndic.occitanie@gmail.com]\n** li LEMMOUCHI | [+ali197393@hotmail.com+|mailto:ali197393@hotmail.com]\n** Fabian TOSOLINI | [+fabian@union-independants.fr+|mailto:fabian@union-independants.fr]  |\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt\n\n\n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca] ","2026-01-30T08:21:28.384Z"],["3851523","PAW-15286","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-30T08:21:52.409Z"],["3851525","RDXENG-4244","RDXENG","juri.noga@bolt.eu","Juri Noga","[~accountid:6401d565314f508813822b2e] should be available soon [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162562|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162562|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T08:22:10.191Z"],["3851526","PFI-839790","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-30T08:22:13.275Z"],["3851528","L10N-31068","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can f