a.","2026-01-30T08:31:30.989Z"],["3851579","HS-29450","HS","nycole.okili@bolt.eu","Nycole Okili Bibang","Hello,\n\nAs of today, I still have not received my employer certificate.\n\nI am therefore following up on my previous request and remain awaiting its transmission.\n\nThank you in advance for your response.\n\nKind regards,","2026-01-30T08:31:32.733Z"],["3851580","LSS-61676","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], please could you reply with the following:\n\n \n\nBonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nSuite à votre demande concernant Monsieur Pascal KOK, nous vous informons que, conformément à nos procédures internes, une période de 6 mois à compter de la date du blocage, le 14 novembre 2025 dans le cas de Monsieur Pascal KOK, doit s’écouler avant que la demande de réactivation puisse être examinée.\n\nNous vous invitons à revenir vers nous à compter du 14 mai 2026 pour effectuer la demande de réactivation du compte.\n\nConformément au cadre applicable au dialogue social dans le secteur des VTC, nous vous informons que les coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants figurent ci-dessous, si votre client souhaite les contacter.\n\n|h2. [+*Coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants du secteur des VTC*+|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/#h2-2]|\n|h3. *ACIL : Association des Chauffeurs Indépendants Lyonnais*\n* [Site internet |http://www.acilvtclyon.fr/]\n* Coordonnées *:* [acilvtclyon@gmail.com|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/acilvtclyon@gmail.com]|\n|h3. *FO : Force Ouvrière*\n* [Site internet |https://www.force-ouvriere.fr/travailleurs-des-plateformes-avec-fo-pour-gagner-des-droits]\n* Coordonnées *:* [+sg@force-ouvriere.fr+|mailto:sg@force-ouvriere.fr] |\n|h3. *UD - VTC SUD : Union des VTC 06/83*\n* Page [Facebook|https://www.facebook.com/p/UNION-DES-VTC-0683-100088991093162/] \n* Coordonnées :  [+uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com+|mailto:uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com] \n* Représentants :  \n** Houari BEN ALI | 06 01 64 77 79  | [+houari3120@live.fr+|mailto:houari3120@live.fr]  \n** Sabrina SABENA | 07 68 25 41 16 | [+lilisab1930@gmail.com+|mailto:lilisab1930@gmail.com]  \n** Florian RUBELI MAROVELLI | 06 06 44 38 09 | [+florian.rubeli@gmail.com+|mailto:florian.rubeli@gmail.com] |\n|h3. *UNION - Indépendants*\n* [Site internet |https://www.union-independants.fr/]\n* Coordonnées : [contact@union-independants.fr|mailto:contact@union-independants.fr] \n* Représentants : \n** Adel DE SOUSA | [+syndic.occitanie@gmail.com+|mailto:syndic.occitanie@gmail.com]\n** li LEMMOUCHI | [+ali197393@hotmail.com+|mailto:ali197393@hotmail.com]\n** Fabian TOSOLINI | [+fabian@union-independants.fr+|mailto:fabian@union-independants.fr]  |\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt\n\n \n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca]","2026-01-30T08:31:36.058Z"],["3851583","PFI-839900","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will be initiated shortly. Once the refund done, it should reflect in the user’s account within 48 hours. ","2026-01-30T08:31:51.408Z"],["3851584","GROWTH-616","GROWTH","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","*Update 30.01.26*\n\n* Some simpler tests have been made and the test message sending works as expected. The SMS also is integrated to Canvases and first tests have worked with the SMS message channel.\n* On the engineering side we’ve made some UI fixes for content and preview sections (in prelive), so the builder would be user-friendlier.\n** !Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 10.36.27.png|width=1457,height=755,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 10.36.27.png\"!\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Make changes to the content blocks logic - remove channel-specific content block types.\n* Wait for the feedback from the LCM testing workgroup. Make changes to the builder based on feedback.","2026-01-30T08:32:17.382Z"],["3851586","LSS-58339","LSS","lilijana.zaiceva@bolt.eu","Lilijana Zaiceva","Hi [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] let me clarify some of the information.\n\n# *Document type:* it’s a vehicle registration certificate.\n# *Upload flow:* it was uploaded through the fleet owner’s portal. This is a standard practise, as fleet owners register the vehicles to their fleet first, then they register the driver who then gets the vehicle assigned to them. \n# *Purpose and use:* since the document was uploaded via car application, all car applications are checked by the agents to make sure that vehicles match the criteria, such as age; information of seats, fuel type, etc.; and to make sure that the vehicle looks good enough visually (no visual damage). \n# *Data handling scope:* Ernestas name is only there visually. We check the document to make sure the data matches description and the vehicle in the picture, however we don’t store such data as vehicle owner’s name anywhere as drivers often register with vehicles that belong to their friends, family members, etc.\n# *Linkage*: No, there’s no registrations or any sort of information related to Ernestas anywhere else, apart from ir being on this document. \n\nLet me know if there’s anything else that would need to be clarified!","2026-01-30T08:32:37.981Z"],["3851588","PFI-840242","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-30T08:33:28.067Z"],["3851589","PFI-839165","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-30T08:33:42.165Z"],["3851590","PFI-829216","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, I added the right payment link to your request.\nWould this not have been already paid out to them with their weekly payout here [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233448754|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/invoicing-payment/payouts/view/233448754] ?","2026-01-30T08:33:45.106Z"],["3851596","PFI-839818","PFI","iulia.duma@bolt-outsource.eu","Iulia Duma","Hello. I will ask the driver if they can provide more screenshots. Thank you!","2026-01-30T08:35:01.599Z"],["3851598","MTE-1121","MTE","mateusz.sabat@bolt.eu","Mateusz Sabat","[~accountid:5d6e089134b3d20d9777ef90] do we have any list of important events to monitor like in task description?","2026-01-30T08:35:28.482Z"],["3851599","PFI-839143","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment capture has now been successfully sent out again and once completed, the debt will be cleared. If the customer has already paid for the pending payment on their next order, they will be refunded back to the Bolt balance. If the user is unhappy with the Bolt balance refund, kindly check with your team how to help compensate the user, keeping in mind that refunding the user back to their payment method will not cancel the balance refund, meaning they will be refunded twice.","2026-01-30T08:35:44.926Z"],["3851600","BDB-1596","BDB","polina.petuhhova@bolt.eu","Polina Petuhhova","Hey [~accountid:624c636af40798007059caa8] \nVynoteka, KIKA and Bottlery logos are missing. Could you please provide those?\n\nThe rest is here: [https://www.figma.com/design/0DgdnyAcnDJPuHO1vhUCJM/Bolt-Food-digital-campaigns?node-id=19783-12637&t=wrplSbv52wFxGn3l-1|https://www.figma.com/design/0DgdnyAcnDJPuHO1vhUCJM/Bolt-Food-digital-campaigns?node-id=19783-12637&t=wrplSbv52wFxGn3l-1|smart-link] \n\nThank you!","2026-01-30T08:36:04.115Z"],["3851601","LSS-61448","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:608009c6f74b3f006a326795] no need for a new ticket, I will continue on this one. \n\nAligned with this approach as an amendment/addendum to the number of Vehicles would have implications on Solis' lending obligations under the original cooperation agreement. ","2026-01-30T08:36:05.688Z"],["3851602","PFI-839142","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThere was a temporary technical issue with the payment service provider which caused the payments to fail. We have now cancelled the payments and for orders that were completed, a balance debt will be created to the user's account and they will be able to pay it with their next order.","2026-01-30T08:36:07.740Z"],["3851603","PFI-826328","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Based on records I can see that the earning was added to balance: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter={\"order_id\"%3A2310354718%2C\"city_id\"%3A1}&page={\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"limit\"%3A100}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/records?recordFilter=%7B%22order_id%22%3A2310354718%2C%22city_id%22%3A1%7D&page=%7B%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22limit%22%3A100%7D]","2026-01-30T08:36:48.771Z"],["3851604","LSS-62441","LSS","helen.erg@bolt.eu","Helen Erg","[^Maersk LnS Sweden AB_PoA_template_Direct Rep_v2.docx] _(466 kB)_\n\n[^Maersk LnS Norway AS_PoA_Template_Direct Rep_v1.docx] _(464 kB)_","2026-01-30T08:37:07.550Z"],["3851605","DRX-28350","DRX","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","2QA: Nothing to test","2026-01-30T08:37:10.669Z"],["3851607","LSS-62088","LSS","paul.bittan@bolt.eu","Paul Bittan","Hi [~accountid:5d9c300987dd6f0dcb4d2b58] - in answer to you questions:\n\n*PRIVILEGED*\n\n*Can self-employed drivers registered under a fleet submit their own vehicle applications and upload documents, instead of this being done by the fleet owner via the Fleet Portal?*\n\nAll of the following increase employment reclassification risk under the fleet model:\n\n* drivers being self-employed;\n* drivers registering themselves directly rather than via the fleet;\n* Bolt contacting drivers directly rather than through the fleet; and\n* controls sitting at driver level rather than fleet level.\n\nAgainst that backdrop, vehicle onboarding and submission of vehicle documentation should remain a fleet-level process, even where drivers are self-employed and own their vehicles.\n\nUnder the to be new Standard Principal terms, drivers acting on behalf of the fleet under section 14.4, and their acts and omissions are treated as those of the fleet. Bolt therefore contracts with, and relies on, the fleet as the Service Provider in this model. Allowing drivers to submit vehicle applications and documentation directly to Bolt would weaken this B2B framing and increase the risk that Bolt is viewed as onboarding and managing drivers directly, rather than dealing with a genuine fleet intermediary.\n\nThis is a factor commonly relied upon by claimants and tribunals in employment and worker reclassification cases, where the focus is on the reality of the relationship and the degree of individual-level control exercised by the platform. The risk is particularly relevant here because fleet structures are not regarded as reclassification-proof, and we have chosen not to mitigate that exposure through Bolt Boost top-ups to fleets. \n\nThis does not prevent Bolt from requesting or verifying limited driver-level information for access control and compliance purposes. Responsibility for vehicle onboarding and approval should, however, remain with the fleet.\n\n*Are we able to communicate directly with self-employed fleet drivers regarding vehicle documents or their application status?*\n\nOperational communications (including onboarding status, vehicle documentation and application outcomes) should, as a default, take place between Bolt and the fleet, rather than directly with drivers.\n\nDirect Bolt-driver communication should therefore be limited to compliance, access-rights and investigatory matters. Routine driver-level operational communications should be avoided, as they increase the perception of Bolt exercising control at the individual level and dilute the fleet-based contracting model.\n\n*The new T&Cs we’re expecting shortly - are these the updated ones for the Principal model, covering legal entity onboarding and the standard driver relationship?*\n\nYes. The to be new Standard Principal terms applies depending on who the Service Provider is.\n\nWhere Bolt contracts with a fleet, the terms apply at fleet level and govern Bolt’s relationship with that legal entity. Drivers are not parties to that contract and provide services pursuant to their own arrangements with the fleet.\n\nWhere Bolt contracts with an individual driver, the same standard terms apply directly to that individual. The terms do not carry over between different contracting arrangements.\n\n*In case of fleet suspension, should drivers still be presented with different terms, or would the standard T&Cs apply?*\n\nIf a fleet is suspended, Appointed Drivers cannot continue operating under that fleet’s contract for the duration of the suspension. Their right of access to the platform derives solely from the fleet’s relationship with Bolt, and while that relationship is suspended, there is no contractual basis for continued access.\n\nWhere a suspension is temporary, drivers should not be transitioned to individual accounts during the suspension period, as their access rights are expected to be restored if and when the fleet suspension is lifted.\n\nWhere a fleet is permanently suspended or terminated, and a driver wishes to continue operating on the platform, they must onboard separately as an individual Service Provider and accept the Principal terms. This constitutes a new and separate contractual relationship.\n\n*If a driver is self-employed, can we switch them to a private driver account without involving the fleet company (in case the fleet is suspended)?*\n\nWhere a fleet has been permanently suspended or terminated, there is nothing in the Platform Terms that prevents a self-employed driver from contracting directly with Bolt as an individual Service Provider, provided they accept the standard Platform Terms.\n\nThis must be treated as a clean contractual break and a new relationship, not a continuation of the fleet arrangement. During a temporary suspension, drivers should not be transitioned to individual accounts, as their access rights are expected to be reinstated if and when the fleet suspension is lifted.\n\nOutside the context of a permanent suspension or termination, actively facilitating movement from fleet to individual accounts would materially increase reclassification risk and should be avoided.\n\n*Operational note*\n\nGiven the reclassification risk profile of fleet models, it would be sensible for Ops/Product to sense-check the proposed onboarding, document flow and driver communication approach with other Bolt markets that operate fleet models in higher-risk jurisdictions (e.g. French and/or Portuguese Ops - FR is a mixed market (fleet and independent drivers) and PT is only a fleet market (local law requirement)), to ensure consistency and avoid unintended operational divergence.","2026-01-30T08:37:44.195Z"],["3851608","MTE-1121","MTE","anton.hmelnitski@bolt.eu","Anton Hmelnitski","[~accountid:712020:cd383b4c-dce2-4e04-98a6-4398af29ffc2] let’s do only the events in description ","2026-01-30T08:37:51.534Z"],["3851609","L10N-31095","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31067](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31067)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-30T08:37:58.744Z"],["3851610","L10N-31096","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31067](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31067)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-30T08:37:59.176Z"],["3851611","L10N-31098","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31067](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31067)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-30T08:37:59.796Z"],["3851613","HS-29558","HS","kristi.vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Hi Ben! I can send this reference letter out on Monday as it’s internal policy to send out reference letters only after the termination date which in this case is 31.01.2026 - I hope that’s okay.\n\nBest wishes\n\nKristi Liina","2026-01-30T08:38:26.074Z"],["3851614","WFM-10213","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:63627a607d4645af4f03d008]!\r\n\r\nQueue assigned.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T08:38:41.131Z"],["3851615","MARTECH3-1234","MARTECH3","prakhar.saini@bolt.eu","Prakhar Saini","*Update 02/02*\n\nGeneralized the prototype analysis into a [generalized playbook|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JqJOD8wpAOj3xl7ZySVK9n98QlT_ZBd8-odKwPNBfYI/edit?tab=t.pd5ut3m7ulo5#heading=h.f4d8av3xtoxz] and discussed with [~accountid:63f5cbedd6722987749da196] and [~accountid:637dde50fde064eda2edd049] to gather feedback. \n\n*Next Steps*\n\nAddress the feedback received, mainly focusing on the following:\n\n* Make the thought-process going in between the layers clearer, adopting a decision-tree structure.\n* Add all available tools that the LCM specialists can leverage.","2026-01-30T08:39:20.875Z"],["3851616","SCM-832","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","Hey [~accountid:623ace301c7f6a00704940a2] I mark the task as done, as all my research is completed and collected in [this file|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1nqjszBHeECH00t0qFnA5RyfckmHIkHl-0IuPSDeb2Ec/edit?gid=56582663#gid=56582663] already for some time now. If the project will be renewed from the management side, we can reopen this task.","2026-01-30T08:39:36.348Z"],["3851619","PFI-828760","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, have made an exception and we have moved this payment to their balance.","2026-01-30T08:42:18.658Z"],["3851622","HS-29558","HS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","Hello [~accountid:712020:6bc77170-e958-4b44-90fe-43a2fc30553a] that’s totally fine thank you. ","2026-01-30T08:44:04.164Z"],["3851628","PAW-15281","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sage386\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162550\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-30 08:45:31 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-30T08:45:31.543Z"],["3851629","CSDA-309","CSDA","jelena.voitenko@bolt.eu","Jelena Voitenko","Hi-hi!\n\nRegarding the “test” report -  if you are willing to try out - let’s do, we are more than happy! 🙂 Because I think anyway we will spend February adjusting and getting feedback from Leds, so as of March the report will be already perfect and we can just replicate it with the new explore then.\n\n\n\n# Utilisation is not planned in the new explores? With Utilisation, scheduled time is 8 hours as a basis for our agents? Since we don’t use “schedules” for IH team? Or how does it work?\n# Thank you! For agents, we would like to see the case level (average total handling time that a certain agent delivers on support cases they’ve worked on). If it is not possible to be added with the old explores, we can skip it for now and add when it will be available then.\n#  We have some agents (as in Cyprus/Greece) who work as Tier-1 agents, so targets are different for them. It would be great to be able to see 2 lines with this metric - one for Tier-1 cases and one with Tier-2, do you think it is possible?\n# All good\n# All agents per market have the same target every month, but if differs per market. I think in this case we can just place this with the minimum target (as we have min. requirements for all markets). Understandable if in the new report. \n# All good\n# All good\n# All good\n# All good\n# All good\n# Yes, thank you, that works! Because we have agents who just “assist” basically with the ticket and then escalate it back, so it is important for us to see this metric.\n\n\n\n","2026-01-30T08:45:45.670Z"],["3851630","PAW-15256","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sage386\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/160962\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-30 08:45:48 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-30T08:45:49.017Z"],["3851631","PAW-15239","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @sage386\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162337\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-30 08:45:55 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-30T08:45:55.532Z"],["3851634","G3IOT-1214","G3IOT","endrik.salak@bolt.eu","Endrik Salak","[~accountid:5e9a112618b8ed0c0f776390] Assuming that the cut-off voltage for the 5000mAh LG M50LT cell used in the battery is 3.0V, reducing the fully charged voltage level to either 3.9V or 4.0V would result in the following available capacity that can be used:\n\n4.00V: 4167 mAh (~83%)\n\n3.95V: 3958 mAh (~79%)\n\n3.90V: 3750 mAh (75%) ","2026-01-30T08:46:17.708Z"],["3851635","DELIVERY-1164","DELIVERY","mihai.jugariu@bolt.eu","Mihai Jugariu","26W05: Finished design doc [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7155023880/2025+Dec+-+Reduce+pickup+leg+distance+of+Bolt+orders+without+increasing+order+lateness#A%2FB-testing|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/7155023880/2025+Dec+-+Reduce+pickup+leg+distance+of+Bolt+orders+without+increasing+order+lateness#A%2FB-testing|smart-link] and looking to add some statistics for pick-up leg for prioritized users vs average.","2026-01-30T08:47:09.607Z"],["3851636","HS-29493","HS","ingrid.valgejarv@bolt.eu","Ingrid Valgejärv","Waiting on effective date confirmation from the manager","2026-01-30T08:47:24.331Z"],["3851639","PAW-15287","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-30T08:47:57.846Z"],["3851641","GROWTH-617","GROWTH","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","*Update 30.01.26*\n\n* We’ve received extensive feedback on the necessary settings (must-haves, nice-to-haves, not necessarys) for Push notifications (based on Braze functionalities) from the LCM testing workgroup and will include these in the Push notification builder task.\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Adjust the initial task description and start work with the task in the 26Q1S3 (9.02-20.02)","2026-01-30T08:48:59.025Z"],["3851645","LSS-62234","LSS","elina.andrijevska@bolt.eu","Elīna Andrijevska","Hi [~accountid:712020:bc7bca9c-4d13-42b6-9684-04014a47f7aa] ! \nMost of the questions could have been answered based on [the legal questionnaire|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PnuX7Bp17Zz1QInoHVhu4fafPaKWAeXB/edit] we prepared together with the Bech-Bruun law firm before the launch. Thus, there does not appear to be a need to engage external counsel or the authorities. Please take a look at my [comments|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jFxT6N22xeTAcvnVODteUbcV4kPh-_5eqfwhj7DhHIo/edit?tab=t.0] and let me know if the information is sufficient 🙂 ","2026-01-30T08:50:27.430Z"],["3851648","WFM-10212","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:61ea6e9084311c0069465f61]!\r\n\r\nQueues assigned.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T08:50:53.617Z"],["3851649","PFI-835518","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, regarding the original question.\n\nBased on internal data, I see that the invoice for the Order attached has been sent properly. It’s possible to confirm the status of the invoice issuance here: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-fiscalization/fiscalization/invoices/871327917|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-fiscalization/fiscalization/invoices/871327917]","2026-01-30T08:51:11.654Z"],["3851650","LSS-60535","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","Hi [~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9] please find all the documents [here|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/173jMmFcYfPt7AcopZnA9cAMakX0V2_bc] - will be signed by Ahto today.","2026-01-30T08:51:22.255Z"],["3851651","PFI-829328","PFI","pimsayanin.petrat@bolt-outsource.eu","Pimsayanin Petrat","Follow up please.","2026-01-30T08:51:45.935Z"],["3851658","PFI-840642","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T08:53:22.039Z"],["3851659","HS-29517","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Confirming home address ","2026-01-30T08:53:29.418Z"],["3851661","GROWTH-497","GROWTH","sander.nommik@bolt.eu","Sander Nõmmik","*Update 30.01.26*\n\n* The first Identify calls regarding business attributes in the Rider workspace ({{max_tier}}, {{new_tier}}, {{business_users_ride_count}}, {{business_users_order_count}}) have been deployed via Profiling and will reach Rudderstack only when there’s been changes in the values of the attributes. Additionally, these attributes are now available via Profiling and free to use in Admin Panel as well.\n** Looker schedules for these attributes for the Rider workspace have been stopped (as of 27.01).\n\n*Next steps*\n\n* Discover, which attributes should go under the same change.\n* Analyse the initial results of Looker vs Profiling event ingestion numbers for the changes made.","2026-01-30T08:53:32.239Z"],["3851663","LSS-61677","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:712020:6e2a3112-018b-43a3-9d2c-1c0019581fcb], please can I ask your help with this ticket please? \n\nA driver has been blocked and is asking us to reactivate his account. Aba has confirmed that this may be because there is a missing or expired document. Kindly could you verify and confirm?\n\n\n\nThank you ! 🙏 \n\n\n\nDriver: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/5062284?tab=profile&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{}}&tz=Europe%2FParis|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/5062284?tab=profile&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&tz=Europe%2FParis]","2026-01-30T08:54:12.508Z"],["3851664","CSDA-291","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hey hey! [~accountid:712020:fc4dfd71-d965-42cc-8737-ee01e32024dc], thank you ✨ \n\nI will then close this request. But as mentioned, we have tasks in our backlog to enable driver ID/partner ID for refunds and add more data points for support cases related to refunds and compensations for deep dives. Let me know if you have any further questions or comments.\n\nHave a nice weekend ☀️ ","2026-01-30T08:54:18.693Z"],["3851665","LSS-58352","LSS","agata.knapinska@bolt.eu","Agata Knapińska","hey [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d], i just replied on all comments \nadditionaly i git from Novitus anexx for “old” ekasa which i’m attaching here for your review. Please let me know if any questions [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sbZJ_VtXhDPAmLWhML_1NXIqFHQ_spQabvd1Xvbe-WQ/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sbZJ_VtXhDPAmLWhML_1NXIqFHQ_spQabvd1Xvbe-WQ/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link]  ","2026-01-30T08:54:56.383Z"],["3851666","PFI-840287","PFI","ilaria.bufaloni@bolt.eu","Ilaria Bufaloni","Hey [~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] thank you for checking. Do you know who I can ask to/tag for further insights about this case?","2026-01-30T08:55:09.262Z"],["3851667","FX-3766","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769763295487329]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@ernests.rudzitis>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3766] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T08:55:13.322Z"],["3851668","PFI-840644","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T08:55:36.376Z"],["3851670","RS-1986","RS","diana.oidsalu@bolt.eu","Diana Oidsalu","Hello, this is the only thing we sent them for the moment\n\nHello,\n\nWe acknowledge receipt of your inquiry 25PEN2994-BR.27.96.300367-2025 dated January 28, 2026.\n\nAt Bolt, we take the privacy and security of our customers, employees, and independent contractors very seriously. We only share data with law enforcement and other relevant authorities if we are satisfied that the requirements of our third-party data sharing policy have been met.\n\nIn order to identify and locate the requested personal data and to assess the necessity, proportionality, and legality of your request, additional time may be required. We will respond to your inquiry as soon as possible.\n\nIf you have any questions regarding your inquiry, please feel free to contact our support team by replying to this email.\n\nKind regards,\n\nBolt","2026-01-30T08:56:10.803Z"],["3851672","PFI-840630","PFI","yuliia-diana.pikh@bolt-outsource.eu","Yuliia-Diana Pikh","Hello, same issues:\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/732516622|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/732516622]\n\n[https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/732500260|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/732500260]\n\n","2026-01-30T08:56:24.290Z"],["3851673","WFM-10214","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:86fe5543-2da3-4e6f-a318-f35fcc13371b].\r\n\r\nQueue assigned permanently as a Primary.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T08:57:23.576Z"],["3851674","LSS-62361","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:652fd966-97db-4de3-b20d-d6644848128c]  \n\nCorrect entity for Bolt Food in KE is Bolt Operations OÜ. \n\nSignatory should be Ahto Kink. \n\n[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61999|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-61999|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T08:57:28.626Z"],["3851675","LSS-62341","LSS","valentin.descas@bolt.eu","Valentin Descas","Hi [~accountid:712020:d008dcec-6cfe-47e4-83a0-c29522744742],\n\nThank you for the clarifications and for sharing the revised version of the agreement.\n\nOn IP rights, my understanding is that the partner mainly wants to ensure they are the only ones using content that mentions Bolt during the campaign period. From our side, we do not intend to reuse their videos or stories outside of this specific activation.\n\nThe content published on Instagram and TikTok will most likely remain live on their accounts after the campaign, but without any further promotion or active push on their side once the campaign has ended. They do not intend to use the content beyond the campaign period, as it relates to a time-limited offer.\n\nRegarding indemnification, they mentioned that the amount included in the previous agreement felt disproportionate considering this is a value-in-kind partnership with no financial consideration. This clause was included in the previous agreement but does not appear in the simplified version, which should be fine given the nature of this partnership.\n\nLet me know if you’d like me to clarify or discuss any of these points further.\n\nThanks a lot ! ","2026-01-30T08:57:36.893Z"],["3851676","DELIVERY-1159","DELIVERY","sergey.lapin@bolt.eu","Sergey Lapin","26W5: A/B tests are running; the metric indicating share of failed orders tend to decrease (not yet significant). Preliminary analysis of the starvation rate shows it’s general reduction (shared insights in the [slack channel|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07DLPHD5FZ/p1769611904129379?thread_ts=1765552057.302289&cid=C07DLPHD5FZ])","2026-01-30T08:58:36.826Z"],["3851677","INT-86","INT","mate.varadi@bolt.eu","Máté Váradi","26W5\n\n* What moved this week: \n** Finished optimization rewrite [[ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/COP-1937], supporting documents: [changes to optimization framework math|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uBf_alcpmFaSiG08trIcfkfObtluuQkr4TLEzwuw3Nk/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.u6s1zsujkjkz], [simulation results to select between two approaches|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uBf_alcpmFaSiG08trIcfkfObtluuQkr4TLEzwuw3Nk/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.jtjwpb1v8z11], [workaround to have one treatment level per cohort|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uBf_alcpmFaSiG08trIcfkfObtluuQkr4TLEzwuw3Nk/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.17bfesj8evs9]]\n** Ran an analysis to validate our rides requirement definition - checking whether 80th percentile RPH would result in 20% campaign conversion rates on average, as expected. Details can be found [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uBf_alcpmFaSiG08trIcfkfObtluuQkr4TLEzwuw3Nk/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.mmq20e7rqrb]\n** [Experiment|https://docs.google.com/document/d/18E6V9Dn998GNAjMVXPyqoOLYDMRD9l7S8WGLkK3ezB0/edit?tab=t.0] support\n* Next week focus: \n** I am OOO","2026-01-30T08:58:38.350Z"],["3851678","WEBSD-1473","WEBSD","hector.picon@bolt.eu","Héctor Gabriel Alanis Picón","Hi [~accountid:5cbf158a6fbf5a10040d1d63]  👋 \n\nWorking on it but you have some sections up.\n\n[https://bolt.eu/en-sa/driver/guide/|https://bolt.eu/en-sa/driver/guide/|smart-link] \n\n\nRegards,","2026-01-30T08:58:43.785Z"],["3851680","LSS-62416","LSS","ben.strey@bolt.eu","Ben Strey","Hello [~accountid:712020:652fd966-97db-4de3-b20d-d6644848128c] I had to make an adjustment. Please send out this contract version instead. \n\n[^Vertrag Autoproff Updated.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-30T09:00:00.501Z"],["3851681","LSS-60063","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey team,\n[~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8] thanks! I see that we still have one open question in the main agreement. Once it is resolved, please share this agreement and its annexes with Ignitis for their review 🙏 ","2026-01-30T09:00:00.789Z"],["3851682","PFI-840644","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hey there!\nIf you need a _report_, please refer to FleetX (DriverX). If your request concerns an _invoice_, follow these steps:\n\nPlease try:\n* Open the *Client page in Admin*: [link|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-rides/clients?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D].\n* Enter the fleet/driver ID into → {{External ID}} filter field\n* Open the driver/fleet profile\n* Open {{Invoice tasks}} tab\n* If you see _“Invoice sum too small”_ → The invoice was not generated as the driver did not owe any commission to Bolt or the driver had more compensation than owed commission. \n* If you see to_execute → it means that the invoice still needs to be generated. You either look at the invoice for the current month (which does not have an invoice yet because month is still going). If you see that to_execute is for the invoice for multiple months → it means that in the past months it was not generated and will be generated in the end of the month.\n* If you see another _error_ → provide us a link.\n* Invoices for all history of the fleet/driver should be under the {{Partner Invoices}}) tab\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-30T09:00:16.601Z"],["3851683","PFI-840642","PFI","nikolai.rol@bolt.eu","Nikolay Roll","👋 Hi there!\n*Rider needs to change details on invoice*\nTo comply with tax regulations, we are unable to re-issue rider invoices. Please advise the user to ensure that their Personal or Work Profile information is correct and that they select the right Billing Profile _before_ taking a ride, just as they would choose the correct payment method in advance.\n\n*Invoice in Romania is missing a number*\nIf the invoice is missing a number, please mention this in the ticket comments so we can review it manually.\n\n*Where to find the invoice*\nPlease use KB article to find the invoice: https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/360003866399\n\nThank you for submitting the ticket.\n\nBest regards,  \n_Billing Ops AI_\n\nThis an automated message created to help resolving requests using our available knowledge base and tools. In case of any doubts or concerns please leave the comment, and our team will revert shortly. Alternatively, please, ask in *#commerce-support-billing* Slack channel.","2026-01-30T09:00:17.431Z"],["3851685","CSDA-298","CSDA","mariia.cherezova@bolt.eu","Mariia Cherezova","Hi again! Since there was no follow-up for about two weeks, I will close the request. If you have any comments or questions, please write here - and I will reopen it.\n\nHave a nice weekend ✨ ","2026-01-30T09:00:29.215Z"],["3851686","WFM-10215","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:9bdd162b-aea1-4903-ac52-7df6be2941f7]!\r\n\r\nQueue priorities changed.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T09:00:34.168Z"],["3851687","LSS-62442","LSS","devon.diesel@bolt.eu","Devon Diesel","[^Feb.2025-indef_Square de Meeus_SQ.pdf] _(392 kB)_\n\n[^SQ_Belgium_EN_Contract_Terms.pdf] _(97 kB)_\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 10.59.35.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T09:01:10.347Z"],["3851688","WD-22650","WD",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, we haven't heard from you in 7 days.","2026-01-30T09:01:29.609Z"],["3851689","WD-22296","WD",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi, we haven't heard from you in 7 days.","2026-01-30T09:01:29.801Z"],["3851691","DELIVERY-1230","DELIVERY","ionut.danila@bolt.eu","Ionuț Dănilă","26W4: *In Deployment -* Update backend entities to support Unified Distance-Based Ranges for City, Zone, and Merchant Layers:\n\n* The pricing configuration system was extended to support distance-based tiers for both Delivery Fee and Small Order Fee calculations.\n* Support was added for sourcing distance tier definitions from multiple levels, including City, Zone, and Merchant, enabling reuse and consistency across pricing setups.\n* Schema changes were propagated by regenerating all dependent validators and API types, ensuring type safety and alignment across services.\n* This unlocks dynamic distance-based pricing without duplicating distance ranges across configurations. Pricing logic is now more flexible, easier to maintain, and better suited for scalable rollouts and experimentation across cities and zones.","2026-01-30T09:02:57.256Z"],["3851692","SREP-1105","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","Requested bucket, waiting: [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03GMLEA664/p1769597614259199?thread_ts=1768213665.668689&cid=C03GMLEA664|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03GMLEA664/p1769597614259199?thread_ts=1768213665.668689&cid=C03GMLEA664|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T09:02:59.997Z"],["3851696","LSS-60621","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1], I am sorry that I am about to bring unpleasant news but it seems we cannot really agree to what GS is requesting. The adjusted agreement is [*here*|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FCmTHMC4fJFukkz3AtOWWVcBpPXV1ICL/edit].\n\n* In 11.1 GS states that  GS is a software platform for intermediating rides and Bolt is not (whereas we all know Bolt is the operator of the software platform). This is something we cannot agree with.\n* In 11.2 GS wants us to agree that we will not compete with them in terms of rides distribution in the US or in the rest of the world. This is again something we cannot confirm since we are a business that develops software that collects riders' requests for a ride and distributes them to the drivers / fleets. This means we are already competing with GS in that sense. Therefore, this is something we cannot agree with.\n* 11.3 is something we can likely agree to, meaning Bolt *must not use Amadeus directly* *when all three of these are true*:\n*# Bolt already has connectivity with a third-party tool (like Amadeus), *and*\n*# The specific TMC or online tool involved has a *preferred distribution partnership with GS*, *and*\n*# The booking is *for that TMC / online tool*\n* In _those_ cases, Bolt must route the booking *through GS*, even if Amadeus connectivity exists.\n* 11.4 - I have included what we can agree on in accordance with your instructions below. The clause basically says the following now:\n** This clause *only applies to bookings that come from a specific list of partners* (the “GS-Preferred Partners” listed below).\n** When a booking comes from one of those partners, the Vendor agrees to *make a reasonable effort* to process that booking *using GS’s booking tools*.\n** This is *not a strict requirement* and *not exclusive*:\n*** Bolt is *not promising that 100% of those bookings will go through GS*\n*** Bolt is *not required to move business if it’s impractical or infeasible*\n* ADDENDUM - [~accountid:712020:70d80a66-553d-4db2-b50f-6bdb7d3bd7a1] have you checked their adjustments in the addendum? They are all commercial. If you are good with them, then feel free to accept them.\n\nI have adjusted the agreement and reviewed it once again. If the above is good to go, then we may proceed to signing.","2026-01-30T09:03:29.751Z"],["3851697","HS-29508","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Waiting fro Zinc results","2026-01-30T09:03:31.149Z"],["3851698","FDBT-4891","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2 fails on 2026-01-30 08:29:58+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task execute failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 190428347960991, 'task_key': 'execute'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2/grid?dag_run_id=manual__2026-01-30T08%3A29%3A58%2B00%3A00&task_id=finance_model_ledger_aggr_pigment.finance_model_ledger_aggr_pigment&base_date=2026-01-30T08%3A29%3A58.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-30T09:03:32.352Z"],["3851702","PFI-840649","PFI","caroline.safari@bolt-outsource.eu","Caroline Safari","!image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T09:04:46.731Z"],["3851707","DSR-4233","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T09:06:57.645Z"],["3851708","WD-22727","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Solution: \n\nAdding Manual type to Remit-to Connect \n\n!image-20260130-090707.png|width=1425,alt=\"image-20260130-090707.png\"!","2026-01-30T09:07:11.576Z"],["3851711","WD-22296","WD","deepak.chaturvedi@bolt.eu","Deepak Chaturvedi","Hi [~accountid:712020:66d8f4d5-ef7d-4df5-ad8d-55b91c398d6c] ,\n\nPlease set up Daily allowance for domestic travel as per the attached file. For international trip, we will follow the list published by US government as one standard rate  is not possible. \n\nRegards,\n\nDeepak","2026-01-30T09:07:44.470Z"],["3851712","LSS-62317","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi Helen, thanks for sharing - the previous Customs Letters seem quite straightforward - I don’t believe that there should be any issue related to the merger. \n\nWe can proceed for signature. \n\nThank you !","2026-01-30T09:07:53.405Z"],["3851716","PC-4941","PC","michal.buzek@bolt.eu","Michal Buzek","Moved under the split epic.","2026-01-30T09:08:43.021Z"],["3851717","PFI-829457","PFI","inna.arutyunova@bolt.eu","Inna Arutyunova","Hello!\n\nNo, not Balance Adjustment. Could you, please, remove the debt (Cash balance) on courier account 13.11 EUR, since they paid it. \n\nThank you, \nInna\n\n","2026-01-30T09:08:49.692Z"],["3851718","LSS-60107","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Thanks [~accountid:6411c587f1b529dfa98c0e66] I will close this ticket for now, we can re-open it if we hear back from the auditors. Thanks !","2026-01-30T09:09:00.323Z"],["3851720","PFI-840650","PFI","ana.tsimakuridze@bolt.eu","Ana Tsimakuridze","!anzor.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T09:09:45.662Z"],["3851721","PFI-840650","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T09:09:48.599Z"],["3851722","FPD-1578","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","Following the methodologies applied in the backtesting ([https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1503|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FPD-1503|smart-link] ), I ran the spend optimization with the latest models (from annual FP cycle, train end date = 2025-12-31) and selected markets where we have the highest uplift while the confidence in incremental models is not poor (exception being OH as incremental data is usually of bad quality). Alongside that, these markets need to have supply incrementality modeled (e.g. they have incremental data on the supply side) and organic conversion models must not be flat (e.g. OH / SS affects base conversion).\n\nA total of 11 cities was selected with the current methodology, results are shown below:\n\n!image-20260130-090538.png|width=983,alt=\"image-20260130-090538.png\"!\n\nWe still need to understand if we should wait until we have the most recent models (data up to end of January) and if we should measure uncertainty in the optimization from OH / SS accuracy before we generate an updated list or share this one with Growth.\n\ncc [~accountid:712020:abc9fd59-ced8-4834-8627-722844558f0d] ","2026-01-30T09:09:53.845Z"],["3851723","IDC-1698","IDC","uku.soome@bolt.eu","Uku Soome","Will be done in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CAMLE-9453|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/CAMLE-9453|smart-link]  rejecting this one. ","2026-01-30T09:10:03.201Z"],["3851725","LSS-62437","LSS","kai.vainola@bolt.eu","Kai Vainola","This does not seem to be a corporate legal ticket. Please specify what the NDA is for (vertical, market, purpose) [~accountid:712020:e9966afc-8926-48fe-bacc-f9daa6118aad] ","2026-01-30T09:10:27.265Z"],["3851726","LSS-62444","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi ! Would you be possible to issued the document attached to the main ticket for signature from Ahto please? Thank you !","2026-01-30T09:10:36.475Z"],["3851728","DO-5841","DO","kaarel.nummert@bolt.eu","Kaarel Nummert","{{ng_financial_modeling_sensitive_spark}} is a fairly old database. Despite its name, the data for its tables is stored in the {{bolt-delta-lake}} S3 bucket. Some legacy instance profiles do have access to it (for example the groups created from terraform). This is already addressed in Data Platform Authorisation, and we will most likely get rid of most of legacy profiles during Unity Catalog migration (i.e., Q1 2026). That said, if you want to ensure security right now, we could migrate the tables to the {{bolt-delta-lake-sensitive}} S3 bucket, which doesn’t have any legacy instance profiles with access to it.\n\nRegardless, if you want to grant additional access to individual tables or a whole data lake database, then you can use [Data Platform Authorisation|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DATA/pages/6021087382/Data+Platform+Authorisation].","2026-01-30T09:10:46.926Z"],["3851736","PFI-829457","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","As Partner Payment operations, we can handle manual payouts of the courier balance, reallocate the payment to another client, refund the payment back to sender. \nIf this payment was allocated to C balance, would it not have been paid out to them?\nIf there are different balances for earning and cash payments, then I think only billing team can make those adjustments. ","2026-01-30T09:11:54.195Z"],["3851738","GS-71","GS","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nIntegration with Admin-panel finished.\nWorking on: Walking Polyline refinement.\n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\n- :done: done implementation \"Alternative #2: Pickup directions per search_category_group\" . Released.\n- :done: done: integration with admin-panel: new UI fields to support editing of directions with search_category_group  => Example https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/pickup-dropoff-areas/areas/64/location/90?tab=directions (Tallinn Airport)\n- :loading: GS-421 Walking Polyline refinement. Details: moving walking polyline from \"area_location\" table to a separate table \"area_pickup_directions\" containing polyline per category_group. Purpose is to have a detailed polyline instead of concatenating instructions locations.","2026-01-30T09:12:06.811Z"],["3851743","PFI-840651","PFI","amina.hemed@bolt.eu","Amina Juma Hemed","!WhatsApp Image 2026-01-30 at 12.11.32.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T09:12:50.998Z"],["3851745","LSS-62425","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[^Bolt Operations & Rocsys BV NDA (Mutual) (1).docx]\n\nHi Legal Ops \n\nPlease send for signing by Ahto and counterparty ","2026-01-30T09:13:04.716Z"],["3851747","CSP-451","CSP","quentin.legrand@bolt.eu","Quentin Émile N. Legrand","26W5\n\nI added a couple of features to the model, and I have now achieved a bit better performance. I now plan to log my results in Confluence and meet with Hugo to discuss a bit UX around that feature. That will inform the next steps.\n\nI am also wondering if, given the [prioritisation scheme of queues|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C030ME1919R/p1768474021061509], if it wouldn’t make more sense to model / predict all response times, not only first responses. There is nothing specific about FRT regarding responses. I may explore that after.","2026-01-30T09:13:20.513Z"],["3851750","MARTECH3-1565","MARTECH3","anette.tiitus@bolt.eu","Anette Tiitus","I created a [Content Block Anette Test|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/message-cms/rider/email/content-blocks/edit/240001?tab=basic_info] and an [Email Template Anette Test.|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/message-cms/rider/email/templates/edit/180002?tab=basic_info]\n\nIt’s really nice to see the update of the Translation Languages block. Now it’s much clearer and smoother to use. 🙏 However, I noticed Bulgarian was missing from the list. Maybe it’s intentional and will be added later. \n\nEmail Template\n\n* How does it work – in what condition can I edit the content after it has been sent to localisation?\n\nI created different variants in the Email template and tried to send a test message to the email that has the Bolt accounts. But I got an error. Would be great to understand why it went to error and what I can fix in my setup.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 10.58.03.png|width=1044,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 10.58.03.png\"!\n\nAfter the error, I activated all my Variants and still nothing. Still getting the error.\n\nAfter I added my user ID, I was able to send the test email. I hope that in the future we can send based on the email only as well. Tested out different User Context values and all worked as expected. ","2026-01-30T09:13:38.805Z"],["3851753","LSS-62425","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:c43a3f02-a108-4c7a-8b5b-9f4d3b47124f] do we have email of the other party ? {{Crijn BOUMAN}}","2026-01-30T09:14:08.402Z"],["3851754","LSS-61673","LSS","philippine.huret@bolt.eu","Philippine Huret","Hi [~accountid:5f5f26b5f4571b006a51732b], please could you reply with the following:\n\n \n\nBonjour Monsieur Michel,\n\nSuite à votre email concernant Monsieur Abdelmonaim TALEB, nous vous confirmons que nous n’avons pas reçu le formulaire de demande de réactivation. Néanmoins, nous vous informons que, conformément à nos procédures internes, une période de 6 mois à compter de la date du blocage, le 28 août 2025 dans le cas de Monsieur Abdelmonaim TALEB, doit s’écouler avant que la demande de réactivation puisse être examinée.\n\nNous vous invitons à revenir vers nous à compter du 28 février 2026 pour effectuer la demande de réactivation du compte.\n\nConformément au cadre applicable au dialogue social dans le secteur des VTC, nous vous informons que les coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants figurent ci-dessous, si votre client souhaite les contacter.\n\n|h2. [+*Coordonnées des organisations représentatives des travailleurs indépendants du secteur des VTC*+|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/#h2-2]|\n|h3. *ACIL : Association des Chauffeurs Indépendants Lyonnais*\n* [Site internet |http://www.acilvtclyon.fr/]\n* Coordonnées *:* [acilvtclyon@gmail.com|https://www.arpe.gouv.fr/les-organisations-representatives-des-travailleurs-independants/acilvtclyon@gmail.com]|\n|h3. *FO : Force Ouvrière*\n* [Site internet |https://www.force-ouvriere.fr/travailleurs-des-plateformes-avec-fo-pour-gagner-des-droits]\n* Coordonnées *:* [+sg@force-ouvriere.fr+|mailto:sg@force-ouvriere.fr] |\n|h3. *UD - VTC SUD : Union des VTC 06/83*\n* Page [Facebook|https://www.facebook.com/p/UNION-DES-VTC-0683-100088991093162/] \n* Coordonnées :  [+uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com+|mailto:uniondesvtc0683@gmail.com] \n* Représentants :  \n** Houari BEN ALI | 06 01 64 77 79  | [+houari3120@live.fr+|mailto:houari3120@live.fr]  \n** Sabrina SABENA | 07 68 25 41 16 | [+lilisab1930@gmail.com+|mailto:lilisab1930@gmail.com]  \n** Florian RUBELI MAROVELLI | 06 06 44 38 09 | [+florian.rubeli@gmail.com+|mailto:florian.rubeli@gmail.com] |\n|h3. *UNION - Indépendants*\n* [Site internet |https://www.union-independants.fr/]\n* Coordonnées : [contact@union-independants.fr|mailto:contact@union-independants.fr] \n* Représentants : \n** Adel DE SOUSA | [+syndic.occitanie@gmail.com+|mailto:syndic.occitanie@gmail.com]\n** li LEMMOUCHI | [+ali197393@hotmail.com+|mailto:ali197393@hotmail.com]\n** Fabian TOSOLINI | [+fabian@union-independants.fr+|mailto:fabian@union-independants.fr]  |\n\nCordialement,\n\n[Nom & Fonction]\n\nBolt\n\n \n\ncc. [~accountid:5d4d47a42be2120ce3e60fca]","2026-01-30T09:14:31.921Z"],["3851756","RCE-388","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769764490660609]*{color}:\nReleased. it should not trigger new comms if the document status is not changed\n{quote}","2026-01-30T09:15:05.179Z"],["3851760","SCM-836","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","Shared the reminder on #micromobility-ops about the upcoming deadline.","2026-01-30T09:16:25.797Z"],["3851765","WFM-10216","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:9bdd162b-aea1-4903-ac52-7df6be2941f7].\r\n\r\nQueue priorities changed.\r\n\r\nHave a wonderful day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T09:17:39.057Z"],["3851769","PFA-573","PFA","ach.rozie@bolt.eu","Achmad Rozie","[https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29920|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/29920]","2026-01-30T09:18:08.368Z"],["3851771","PFI-829216","PFI","johannamaria.kask@bolt-outsource.eu","Johanna-Maria Käsk","Hey! \n\nNo I don’t see anything being paid back, but by this point the courier has been naturally compensated for the overpayment by receiving lesser debt from cash orders, no work necessary.","2026-01-30T09:18:20.159Z"],["3851772","CLIENTAPP-38781","CLIENTAPP","ios.ci.robot@bolt.eu","ios.ci robot","UI tests execution has been completed. Test cycle created: \"https://taxify.atlassian.net/projects/CLIENTAPP?selectedItem=com.atlassian.plugins.atlassian-connect-plugin%3Acom.kanoah.test-manager__main-project-page#!/testPlayer/CLIENTAPP-R3023\"","2026-01-30T09:18:21.266Z"],["3851773","PFI-829216","PFI","johannamaria.kask@bolt-outsource.eu","Johanna-Maria Käsk","I don’t see anything being paid back, but by this point the courier has been naturally compensated for the overpayment by receiving lesser debt from cash orders, no work necessary.","2026-01-30T09:18:33.042Z"],["3851774","LSS-61680","LSS","miriam.hamam@bolt.eu","Miriam Hamam","Thank you Thale! I am aware of the case and glad to see that the legal assessment is confirming my assumption that there is no ground whatsoever for the requests made by the customer. ","2026-01-30T09:18:40.804Z"],["3851775","FX-3673","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Jana Lutus [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769764736622579]*{color}:\nHeyy <@U02TPHQNARF> <@U09B111L8G1>, thanks for reaching out. Unfortunately, search categories are not owned by us. Please reach out to the Marketplace team via <#C02LWCMELDD>, I'm sure they'll be able to help you :meow_flowers:\n{quote}","2026-01-30T09:19:11.195Z"],["3851776","CRC-2196","CRC","cesar.echeverria@bolt.eu","César Orellana Echeverría","[update] UI change to be released on Feb.03. After this, ready to A/B test in Romania and rollout.","2026-01-30T09:19:11.958Z"],["3851780","HS-29553","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hei [~accountid:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nKui sul ei ole aega, et sellega tegelede, let me know 💚  \n\nAll the best,\n\nKerilin","2026-01-30T09:20:45.493Z"],["3851784","RDXENG-4244","RDXENG","mustafa.ogun@bolt.eu","Mustafa Ogün Öztürk","[~accountid:625fb496efc8a5006a5557e5] great! let’s take care of it next week then. Thanks 🙏 ","2026-01-30T09:21:01.071Z"],["3851786","DMB-1729","DMB","raj.parekh@bolt.eu","Raj Parekh","Impact \n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 11.21.13.png|width=774,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 11.21.13.png\"!","2026-01-30T09:21:34.636Z"],["3851789","DISC-3788","DISC","arsenii.zubkovskii