360","DPM","hanno.narvik@bolt.eu","Hanno Narvik","Verified matching prices with the same file on the latest deploy in prelive:\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 09.11.24.png|width=795,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 09.11.24.png\"!","2026-01-30T09:23:30.365Z"],["3851835","RCE-388","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Anneli Tammesson [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769765022272779]*{color}:\nthank you\n{quote}","2026-01-30T09:23:55.572Z"],["3851836","LSS-62431","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:c43a3f02-a108-4c7a-8b5b-9f4d3b47124f] \n\nChanges accepted. \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SR2Frchbddu2p7H6Wayqq0AqsguasuRy/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SR2Frchbddu2p7H6Wayqq0AqsguasuRy/edit|smart-link]  \n\nIn order to sign the NDA we need full name of the company, their signing details. \n\nPlease ask them to fill the empty spaces and send NDA to us again. ","2026-01-30T09:25:09.575Z"],["3851837","WFM-10225","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","[https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601897|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/601897]","2026-01-30T09:25:23.228Z"],["3851841","PAW-15289","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was merged\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162588\nStatus: merged\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-30 09:26:22 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-30T09:26:22.587Z"],["3851844","WFM-10225","WFM","jose.acevedo@bolt.eu","Jose Acevedo","Role created: CS - Spain Driver Block\n\nRequest to add permission is now pending permission owner approval.\n\n[~accountid:5e3d437d9749d00c924cb0f5] FYI: I will add all agents assigned to 01 RH_Spain_T1 and 06 RH_Spain_T2 ","2026-01-30T09:27:36.501Z"],["3851845","CSDA-309","CSDA","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","Okay, cool. Let me try to build the test version and get back to you. I would expect it to be ready next week, but will keep you posted. \n\n\n\n# Not yet. With utilization, the situation is the same as with QA: uncertainty with Assembled, so we are not building anything on top of their data. Also, this metric will not work without actually logged schedules in Assembled or some other tool if we end up using one. So if in the future you’d like to see this metric, it is important to understand that scheduled time will need to be logged in the tool that is used for scheduling. \n# Aligned\n# Could you please share a couple of examples of those tier 1 agents? I want to see if we can somehow differentiate them in data currently. \n# ✅ \n# Aligned. This will only be possible with old explores for now, as we are not yet building anything on top of ZendeskQA in new explores.\n# ✅ \n# ✅ \n# ✅ \n# ✅ \n# ✅ \n# Aligned. ","2026-01-30T09:28:04.074Z"],["3851846","SRED-1114","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","{noformat}71:72:\nc7g.large -> c6g.large\n\n125:126:\nc7g.large -> c6g.large{noformat}\n\ndownscaled like before the NYE","2026-01-30T09:28:13.130Z"],["3851847","WFM-10222","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Market request: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571950|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571950]\n\nRole request: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571951|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/571951]","2026-01-30T09:28:37.132Z"],["3851852","DO-5834","DO","ionut.danila@bolt.eu","Ionuț Dănilă","Hi, [~accountid:712020:3bcdd959-6456-4648-918e-4a25bb1a646e] ,\n\nWe did not perform any backfil on that table. It is a very old table, without any changes.\n\nIs there any way to prevent duplication of these fields?","2026-01-30T09:31:28.822Z"],["3851856","PFI-840659","PFI","jutathip.songcharoen@bolt-outsource.eu","Jutathip Songcharoen","!image-20260130-092839.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260130-092852.png|thumbnail!\n\n!image-20260130-092911.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T09:32:04.886Z"],["3851857","CMP-24","CMP","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162602","2026-01-30T09:32:13.199Z"],["3851859","WD-22727","WD","deepak.chaturvedi@bolt.eu","Deepak Chaturvedi","Hey [~accountid:712020:fa8a842c-b8b9-4555-a3d9-2647acf081ec] ,\n\nThanks for your help!\n\nNow I am able to see manual as payment type in settlement run. You may close the ticket. \n\nRegards,\n\nDeepak","2026-01-30T09:32:22.337Z"],["3851864","HS-28685","HS","kristin.runnel@bolt.eu","Kristin Runnel","no tax form needed, new system via Madison app, sent the instructions to employee","2026-01-30T09:33:08.525Z"],["3851865","WFM-10219","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:712020:2069522b-e792-4f63-bbb9-a4a5c62d4e3f].\r\n\r\n*05 BU_Global_Business_English* queue removed.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T09:33:19.147Z"],["3851866","FPD-1416","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","First EDA results:\n\nh3. Suggestion\n\n* Start with SS/AR, and with: {{n_weekend_days}}\n** {{n_holidays}} not as consistent, and it's anyways captured by special events\n** Also, we can do another EDA on Holidays happening during the week and change the event itself to e.g. christmas_week, christmas_weekend\n* OH/AR not as consistent, but once we have {{n_weekend_days}} in SS/AR, it will be pretty fast to quickly backtest\n* Conversion models might be helped as well, I would test that after SS/AR.\n** Main reason is that I struggle to understand why would there be an impact.\n** We will also have to compute differently the features because of train weekly/inference monthly","2026-01-30T09:33:42.863Z"],["3851867","BDMCD-34","BDMCD","mercedes.ramirezmolina@bolt.eu","Mercedes Ramírez Molina","We received 20€ on 29.01","2026-01-30T09:33:48.659Z"],["3851868","HS-29549","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Task sent back on Workday","2026-01-30T09:34:12.596Z"],["3851869","FRAUD-5762","FRAUD","ivan.honchar@bolt.eu","Ivan Honchar","I realized that it would be good to add new column into CDC to replicate it into Data Lake\nCan be done here\n[https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/blob/a562499574ff90e86e3f9e632a18105ad29238dd/src/ingestion_config/ng/live/2023_Nov.json#L1183-L1287|https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/blob/a562499574ff90e86e3f9e632a18105ad29238dd/src/ingestion_config/ng/live/2023_Nov.json#L1183-L1287] ","2026-01-30T09:34:42.294Z"],["3851870","PFI-831415","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, I see the Customer has used the Work Profile, not a Business Account. Can you, please, delete existing Work Profile: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-billing-profile/profiles/edit/9201493|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/user-billing-profile/profiles/edit/9201493]\n\nGoing forward, we have stricter validations on the Work Profile usage, and we can guarantee that the amount is being charged from the Personal Payment method not to Company.","2026-01-30T09:34:42.447Z"],["3851871","SUPX-2337","SUPX","pranav.dineshkumar@bolt.eu","Pranav Dinesh Kumar","[~accountid:712020:eba3c46d-5b67-4363-896f-8bc6e1642c6f] I spoke to Fred about this. We can remove the SSAT for these as well.","2026-01-30T09:34:45.971Z"],["3851872","DO-5834","DO","ionut.danila@bolt.eu","Ionuț Dănilă","Also, is there any way to cleanup these duplicate entries?","2026-01-30T09:35:00.823Z"],["3851873","LSS-62295","LSS","roger.bjorkbacka@bolt.eu","Roger Björkbacka","Indeed [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] will do and we will no start  the process of discussing  with them ","2026-01-30T09:35:05.598Z"],["3851877","PFI-838784","PFI","carlo.mizzon@bolt.eu","Carlo Mizzon","Hi [~accountid:62026399c4e2c9006ae5fb59] this is not resolved and [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] and others agents have already issued the same refund due to city closure in Italy, please, kindly assist, TY","2026-01-30T09:35:40.814Z"],["3851878","PFI-840661","PFI","sakina.khalilova@bolt.eu","Sakina Khalilova","[^AZ Business Company VAT Payments - Missing payments.csv]","2026-01-30T09:36:10.108Z"],["3851881","LSS-62448","LSS","domantas.dabrukas@bolt.eu","Domantas Dabrukas","[^Lietuvos_Respublikos_generaline__prokuratu_ra._Specialiosios_sa_lygos._Bolt_Business.adoc] _(219 kB)_","2026-01-30T09:36:38.462Z"],["3851882","LSS-60535","LSS","ksenia.korolkova@bolt.eu","Ksenia Korolkova","[^Bolt Letter of Confirmation 2025.asice]\n\n[~accountid:712020:11b028d0-a65b-4db4-93f7-938b14e353e9]  please find attached signed version of the confirmation letter.","2026-01-30T09:37:28.751Z"],["3851883","PFI-839117","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03NBHZ6NKC/p1769765841679759|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C03NBHZ6NKC/p1769765841679759|smart-card]","2026-01-30T09:37:40.275Z"],["3851888","PFI-839117","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe have forwarded the refund request to the payment service provider and will let you know once the refund is completed.","2026-01-30T09:38:48.692Z"],["3851894","MKP-9901","MKP","nicholas.p.smith@bolt.eu","Nick Smith","Hey [@artjom.brehhunov|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:987e0719-a08b-4a9e-9349-ae881aeaf688] [@iaroslav.melnichuk|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/712020:d88f5976-1e33-47f5-acb2-a9c422493f69] - can you please let me know when you expect this task to be completed pls :pray::skin-tone-2:","2026-01-30T09:39:55.790Z"],["3851900","PAR-3866","PAR","volodymyr.hadomskyi@bolt.eu","Volodymyr Hadomskyi","!Screen Recording 2026-01-30 at 10.33.00 (d2d41190-e717-4204-a5b4-553365175dd8).mov|width=650,alt=\"Screen Recording 2026-01-30 at 10.33.00.mov\"!","2026-01-30T09:41:29.817Z"],["3851901","LSS-62288","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","Hi! I have made a copy of the confirmation of personal address and edited it accordingly. \n\nWe just need the group chart signed and certified copies of the ID’s. They need the certifications to be issued in the last 3 months max.\n\nThanks. ","2026-01-30T09:41:37.824Z"],["3851902","FX-3766","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Jana Lutus [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769766101650469]*{color}:\nheyy <@UCVT712UR>, just to double-check, is getOrders API being compared with the *Ride History* page on FOP?\n{quote}","2026-01-30T09:41:54.394Z"],["3851907","PFI-835518","PFI","karlo.masnjak@bolt.eu","Karlo Masnjak","[~accountid:712020:5c8bc485-83b5-47c2-ba7a-e8927f399b6f] Hi, I checked the receipt using the fiscal number (JIR) *d914e054-da35-4f6c-8c0e-ec4580d9f17d*, and the message I received is:\n_“The receipt is not recorded in the Tax Administration system. The relevant verification period is 48 hours from the moment the receipt is issued. If it is still not recorded after that, please submit it to the Tax Administration office.”_\n\nIt might be worth checking this? \n\n","2026-01-30T09:42:59.413Z"],["3851912","SREDESK-7484","SREDESK","maciej.knichal@bolt.eu","Maciej Knichał","Investigating","2026-01-30T09:43:41.086Z"],["3851914","HS-29138","HS","marilin.allak@bolt.eu","Marilin Allak","Hi [~accountid:712020:255e9251-2a80-4b03-82b7-1ebc3abacf51] ! \n\nChecking in, did You get answers to Your questions? \n\nKind regards\n\nMarilin","2026-01-30T09:43:48.113Z"],["3851915","PFI-838733","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, pending the deeper investigation the results are the following: \n\n* We issue Invoice Payment Receipts only when the invoice becomes paid via the bank transfer or the one-off credit card payment in case of postpaid companies.\n* For the month of November, on the 19 Dec the payment was done for the amount of 4166.04 which is lower than amount owed and hence invoice wasn’t considered paid.\n* Invoice became paid only on 31 December, when the withholding tax was applied\n* As per the point 1, we don’t issue receipts in such cases.\n\nNow, whether we have to or don’t have to issue Invoice Payment Receipts when the source of marking invoice as Paid was different than Bank Transfer or Credit Card requires a broader alignment with Tax, which we will do, but will take longer","2026-01-30T09:44:00.750Z"],["3851917","LSS-60738","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hey [~accountid:712020:60da7793-200e-4a92-a78d-1705c6e5cdf8], I have reviewed this amendment, please go ahead and collect the signatures as you mentioned via Slack 😉 \nFor archiving purposes please shared signed version of the amendment in the comments,  thanks 🙏 ","2026-01-30T09:44:04.427Z"],["3851919","CSP-315","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","26W05: PoC for courier new UX completed. Engineering research for the feature to start next week.","2026-01-30T09:44:20.957Z"],["3851922","PFI-835518","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, thanks! Will check in more details and get back","2026-01-30T09:45:34.184Z"],["3851925","WEB-9377","WEB","aleksandr.komolov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Komolov","Hey [~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] the only small suggestion from my side is that it might make sense to show the initial publication date when a modified date is displayed, so that when both dates exist, we show the original publication date as well as when the article was updated.","2026-01-30T09:45:45.201Z"],["3851926","DO-5824","DO","przemyslaw.gumula@bolt.eu","Przemysław Gumuła","[~accountid:5a91321e646c8a4475ece436] , while we wait for the fix, I can grant you access to the bucket manually. It would be best if you provided me with a group name (so that all relevant people have access to the schema).\nI’ll create an access request to the path of the schema, on behalf of the group","2026-01-30T09:45:49.410Z"],["3851927","CSP-79","CSP","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","26W05: Feature enabled for 100% of ridehailing orders (in new UX). A/B test for rentals (MM, carsharing) running. Copy update for delivery completed, awaiting translations; A/B test planned next week. Bolt Balance payment support on our side completed, on commerce side support for charges has been added, support for refunds is pending.","2026-01-30T09:45:59.740Z"],["3851930","PFI-835091","PFI","ricardo.dias@bolt-outsource.eu","Ricardo Vieira Dias","Hello, \n\nIs there an update regarding the situation, or any additional information we can provide to the rider? ","2026-01-30T09:46:28.026Z"],["3851931","SUPX-2337","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","[~accountid:712020:33002f0b-c802-4f83-911e-b96c405eae99] I will create a separate task for that, since this one is already completed","2026-01-30T09:46:38.916Z"],["3851934","WEB-9377","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:712020:c9a5e707-0d6d-488a-bafd-1418ebf8e556] We already have it for all blog articles, but we should add the label to the publication date + add the last edit labal + date and time. ","2026-01-30T09:47:23.357Z"],["3851935","MARTECH3-1588","MARTECH3","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","PS I did not have time to test the nodes on my user ID this week. Please find comments on the Canvas UI below. Questions are highlighted with {color:#ff991f}orange{color}, improvement ideas are in {color:#0747a6}*bold blue.*{color}\n\nCanvas setup:\n\n*Basic info*:\n\n* {color:#ff991f}What happens if you choose a date that’s in the past?{color} {color:#0747a6}*Nice to have:*{color} Show a warning if the date is in the past.\n* If the “End” time box is left empty, {color:#ff991f}I assume the canvas will run until it’s stopped?{color} {color:#0747a6}*Nice to have:*{color} Show a disclaimer if the end date box is left empty.\n* You can’t proceed to the next section unless you save the basic info one - {color:#0747a6}*nice to have:*{color} show a warning about this.\n\n*Enrollment settings*:\n\n* End dates in the test - we don’t usually have an end date for autocomms. {color:#ff991f}Would it be possible to leave this empty?{color}\n\n*Goals*:\n\n* We don’t always want to kick out the user if they perform the conversion event. {color:#0747a6}*Must have*{color}: Separate selections for conversion event and exit criteria \n\n*Canvas Builder*:\n\n* Different nodes:\n** The setup of the different nodes was a bit confusing for me. I think it’s mostly the fact that everything looks super blended in the editor (grey buttons on white bg, fields also grey, multiple green buttons). I think Braze solved this nicely by adding frames around sections, assigning clear colours to different nodes etc.\n*** {color:#0747a6}*Should have*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color} I got an error while trying to save my Action Path. However, it does not tell me what is wrong (Gives generic “Failed to update the node”). {color:#bf2600}I was unable to test the action path because of this.{color}\n*** {color:#0747a6}*Nice to have:*{color} Action path could have numbers before the groups. Similarly to Braze 👇 This makes it super easy to identify how many groups you have. \n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 11.06.41.png|width=188,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 11.06.41.png\"!\n*** For all nodes: the “everyone else“ group turns into “default” on the canvas builder view. It’s not really the same thing in my opinion and could cause some confusion (it does not always lead to a 'default' variant) TLDR: {color:#0747a6}*Should have:*{color} “everyone else“ should be called “everyone else“ in the canvas builder view as well.\n* {color:#0747a6}*Must have:*{color} message nodes cannot be deleted after you add one. \n* {color:#0747a6}*Must have*{color}{color:#0747a6}:{color} delay nodes cannot be deleted after you add one.\n* {color:#0747a6}*Should have:*{color} the canvas builder section should also have a save button.","2026-01-30T09:47:42.097Z"],["3851941","SUPX-2337","SUPX","krzysztof.szlachetka@bolt.eu","Krzysztof Szlachetka","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2371|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SUPX-2371|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T09:48:57.623Z"],["3851944","PFI-830758","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, we don’t issue Payment receipts on Billing side; \n\nThe service fee invoice: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5819127531|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/5819127531]","2026-01-30T09:49:37.041Z"],["3851947","WFM-10217","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello, [~accountid:712020:3a3742eb-3298-4df7-a8af-c0fd7279bf95]!\r\n\r\nThis data should be accessible now.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T09:50:01.150Z"],["3851948","PFI-813837","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hello, unfortunately no. The invoice is still pending the engineering input.","2026-01-30T09:50:09.854Z"],["3851949","HS-29138","HS","valentin.descas@bolt.eu","Valentin Descas","Hey [~accountid:712020:58704fb5-3b31-40a0-896f-1d862e6e1fd9],\nAligned with Louisa yesterday. Thanks for the feedback!\nRegards,\n\nValentin \n\n","2026-01-30T09:50:17.701Z"],["3851950","WFM-10107","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Thank you for sharing! Blocking reasons were approved, pending approval for car_block now","2026-01-30T09:50:27.941Z"],["3851952","PFI-828222","PFI","zuzanna.stanislawiak@bolt-outsource.eu","Zuzanna Stanisławiak","??","2026-01-30T09:50:44.610Z"],["3851955","PFI-813837","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BB-2221|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/BB-2221|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T09:51:05.433Z"],["3851958","WFM-10077","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Hello! I will close this ticket, please reply or open a new one if needed","2026-01-30T09:51:42.325Z"],["3851959","RLONE-836","RLONE","anton.berggren@bolt.eu","Anton Berggren","Discussed with [~accountid:712020:2f0ea547-67d9-460b-98f3-2216cf603c7c] Waiting for current AB-test to be finalised before deciding way forward. Expecting a timeline during beginning of next week.","2026-01-30T09:51:46.177Z"],["3851960","FPD-1435","FPD","rodrigo.ponzetto@bolt.eu","Rodrigo Étore Evangelista Ponzetto","*Weekly updates:*\n\n* What moved this week: \n** Created methodology to assess overall confidence / uncertainty level of models and added these to the optimization backtesting results\n** Looked into a simulation to understand how accuracy in OH and SS metrics forecasts impacts the optimization curve\n** Shared first view of results and methodology with Growth\n* Next week focus:\n** Share initial list of cities / optimal splits with Growth + any additional actionable from our side to put this in production\n** Add a quantification of uncertainty uplift curves driven by the performance error in OH and SS forecasts\n** Write a document on methodology / results of this backtest and first analysis\n* Help needed:\n** Need some feedback on current evaluation methodology in order to further improve it before generating / sharing the split recommendations ","2026-01-30T09:52:00.779Z"],["3851963","LSS-62403","LSS","edik.davtian@bolt.eu","Edik Davtian","Hello, I drafted the 1-pager in GPT, please have a look\n\n\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TGOrs0j_5SW3m6JvMiy3baQtxY4VCsGK8gg7RdbG09Q/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TGOrs0j_5SW3m6JvMiy3baQtxY4VCsGK8gg7RdbG09Q/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T09:52:22.145Z"],["3851964","RDXENG-3950","RDXENG","anastasiya.sviatokha@bolt.eu","Anastasiya Sviatokha","Fixed in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4778|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RDXENG-4778|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T09:52:28.049Z"],["3851965","LSS-56938","LSS","alon.alkalay@bolt.eu","Alon Alkalay","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656] - in this case, we can close and indicate that: \n\n{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}\nSupport has been provided, agreement finalised and Doc is being submitted for signature\n{panel}","2026-01-30T09:52:30.727Z"],["3851968","PFI-832308","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","Hey, we calculate the service fee, not as a % of Total amount, but rather as a % of each individual record (Ride, coupon, etc), and then round it to two digits immediately. This may create small rounding discrepancies.\n\nCurrent approach is when the amounts don’t match and clients complain - just to issue apology credits, usually difference would be few cents.","2026-01-30T09:53:05.514Z"],["3851970","HS-29565","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Richard,\n\nThanks for your request! We’ve moved your request to the correct People Services Support Desk so it can be handled by the right team.\n\nYou can view and track your request(s) here:\n [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/26/REL-1138|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/26/REL-1138|smart-link]\n\nBest regards,\nPeople Services Team","2026-01-30T09:53:38.531Z"],["3851971","LSS-62407","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:6169660ebfa2c1006b56c18f] \n\nPlease find reviewed NDA\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hEfIhljcvMoUrsfSyQFoMju8pM_Nc93C/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hEfIhljcvMoUrsfSyQFoMju8pM_Nc93C/edit|smart-link] \n\n* We pushed back to Luxembourg law and offered FR law\n* We pushed back to 30 days negotiations before having possibility to use injunctive relief, if there is breach of confidentiality Bolt needs to have the right to act immediately \n* Please share with the other party and ask them to sign if accepted","2026-01-30T09:53:55.892Z"],["3851974","GUM-85","GUM","brindusa.niculae@bolt.eu","Brîndușa Niculae","After further discussions, we agreed on a different solution that has a roadmap item: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/GEORM/ideas/view/8453940?selectedIssue=GEORM-506|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/polaris/projects/GEORM/ideas/view/8453940?selectedIssue=GEORM-506|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T09:55:00.756Z"],["3851977","LSS-60715","LSS","silvia.plochanbenova@bolt.eu","Silvia Plocháň Beňová","I’ve no idea, my understanding is that client added those closes wanting to cover some additional information to make sure all is covered. Can we or can we not accept them in Special terms, if not please comment. ","2026-01-30T09:56:22.687Z"],["3851978","DSR-4235","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T09:56:25.378Z"],["3851979","LSS-62295","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","Status: TO be updated by business","2026-01-30T09:56:32.029Z"],["3851980","MKP-9961","MKP","peter.yeremenko@bolt.eu","Peter Eremenko","Hi team, is it possible to add the 'Driver Accepted' coordinates as a field to export in the [Order Export page|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/export?tz=Europe%2FTallinn&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22start_timestamp%22%3A1769724000%2C%22end_timestamp%22%3A1769810399.999%2C%22all_order_try_states%22%3Atrue%7D%7D]?","2026-01-30T09:56:46.844Z"],["3851981","MKP-9961","MKP",null,"Slack","[Peter Eremenko|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/people/63184a3e62fe1e6eac6dbbf0] synced this conversation thread with the Slack thread [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1769766134159739?thread_ts=1769766134.159739&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04SLV3GT5K/p1769766134159739?thread_ts=1769766134.159739&cid=C04SLV3GT5K|smart-link]. Replies in synced threads will automatically update across both Slack and Jira.","2026-01-30T09:56:47.816Z"],["3851982","MKP-9961","MKP","peter.yeremenko@bolt.eu","Peter Eremenko","Does it work if it's added as separate fields:\n• Driver accepted latitude\n• Driver accepted longitude\nThat's how it works for pickup location, for example","2026-01-30T09:56:48.339Z"],["3851983","MKP-9961","MKP","maksim.baitsov@bolt.eu","Maksim Baitsov","Yes, that'd be perfect!","2026-01-30T09:56:49.199Z"],["3851987","PFI-839922","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","hey, adding the link to the slack message [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0198U511UJ/p1769616237125939|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0198U511UJ/p1769616237125939|smart-link]  that has the explanation. \n\nbut also writing it out here, the ride price VAT is calculated when the supplier is VAT liable. in [this|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/billing-document/invoices/6120877438] case, ride price with VAT is 86,71 GBP.  The receipt shows the full cost to the company, which for resale model is calculated as {{final ride price with VAT + local VAT}} . Calculation is the same whether service is ordered from the app or from ride booker. Since the driver sells the ride to Bolt, this VAT can be claimed back by Bolt. VAT from Bolt to Business company (will be visible on the monthly aggregate invoice that is generated in the beginning of the month) can be claimed back by the company.","2026-01-30T09:57:47.470Z"],["3851990","MVRT-1458","MVRT","tiffany.irianto@bolt.eu","Tiffany Ainnurrahmi Irianto","Heyy [~accountid:6101032e0b454a0068b57bef] added the print as a task here, link to logo is on the main epic (FYI for later if needed). Will add more details once I get them here as well","2026-01-30T09:59:51.309Z"],["3851993","DO-5824","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","People Analytics (GROUP ID: 660003)","2026-01-30T10:00:06.401Z"],["3851998","LSS-62208","LSS","mikk.vachtmeister@bolt.eu","Mikk Vachtmeister","{quote} I can draft an email you could send them, explaining why the switch is necessary, and will share the Bolt DPA template with you as well.{quote}\n\nThat would be nice","2026-01-30T10:01:32.810Z"],["3851999","PFI-830758","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","Hello team!\n\nArtem the ticket can be closed - my apologies it was created in the first place. There has been some sort of misunderstanding of the clients issue. \n\nCS - they payment is the Service Fee - explain:\n\n# Where to find the Service Fee invoice in the Company Dashboard. \n# That the Service Fee is withheld on the basis of registration and agreement to the T&C of BB. Point 1.9 [https://bolt.eu/lv-lv/legal/terms-for-bolt-business-new/?category=boltBusiness|https://bolt.eu/lv-lv/legal/terms-for-bolt-business-new/?category=boltBusiness|smart-link]  \n\nIf anything is needed - please escalate in the Slack Onboarding channel.\n\n\n","2026-01-30T10:01:37.833Z"],["3852003","PFI-830570","PFI","katrin.voloditsev@bolt.eu","Katrin Voloditšev","Hi!\nIs there an update on this? ","2026-01-30T10:01:58.708Z"],["3852004","DRAG-668","DRAG","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:712020:7636318d-11ba-448e-8ae7-b935370c0640] I did the review and added my comments into the document.","2026-01-30T10:02:03.507Z"],["3852007","PFI-834334","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/COMM/pages/6803423312/Romania+E-invoicing+Escalations+and+troubleshooting|smart-link]  here is the RO specific guide. If you don’t have the necessary permissions, please first escalate to your team lead who can then assess if they can take the necessary action or it will need to be escalated to local operations. ","2026-01-30T10:02:46.766Z"],["3852009","WD-22602","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hello [~accountid:637f4716de5cdaba3a67c532] ! I see that we are already late to fix the issue before January closing , I see that Period Close process has alredy been initiated. but I hope we will fix this by next period close ))\n\n\n\nHello [~accountid:6131df23b1894f00718e9faa] ,\n\nI am currently testing security settings to restrict the \"Start Period Close\" process for companies in the *Region 6* hierarchy (where all companies except CL are inactive).\n\nCurrently, My understanding is that wen you run the task Start Period Close you chose  “Bolt Group\" and it triggers the process for every company in the group—including inactive ones—which creates unnecessary work for the accountants assigned to inactive companies. To prevent this, I can configure the permissions in one of two ways:\n\n# *Restrict Permissions to Regions 1–5:* I can grant you permission to initiate the period close only for hierarchies Region 1 through Region 5. You would be able to select only these hierarchies, but you would have to run the task five separate times (once for each region).\n\n!image-20260130-095423.png|width=839,alt=\"image-20260130-095423.png\"!\n\n# *Create a Dedicated Hierarchy:* I can create a separate company hierarchy specifically for the period close process that includes all active companies ( this hierarchy won’t be included to Bolt Group).  This would allow you to start the process for all active companies in a single step.\n\n!image-20260130-095607.png|width=839,alt=\"image-20260130-095607.png\"!\n\nLet me know which approach you prefer.","2026-01-30T10:03:10.132Z"],["3852010","WEB-9376","WEB","aleksandr.komolov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Komolov","Everything is great! One important moment I would like to pay attention to: \n\nI’d like to make a suggestion that may be slightly more complex to implement, but has deeper potential. What if we added a small author section to each article with one additional feature? \n\nWhere the section exists in the article, it would include only the author’s name, role, and photo. \n\nAddition: The *author’s name would be a clickable link* leading to a *dedicated author page* containing the author’s name, role, photo, *+* *a short bio* (around 60 words), *and a list of other articles* written by that author.\n\nThis approach could strengthen internal linking and help build author authority in line with E-E-A-T principles. ","2026-01-30T10:03:09.739Z"],["3852012","PAW-15291","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-30T10:03:56.238Z"],["3852014","WEB-9376","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:712020:c9a5e707-0d6d-488a-bafd-1418ebf8e556] Would be great to do this, but as the part of the second iteration, but maybe we can squeeze it all when we will be doing this! I would love to create separate single-author pages as well! ","2026-01-30T10:04:36.636Z"],["3852016","PFI-833286","PFI","aisma.austruma@bolt.eu","Aisma Austruma","[~accountid:712020:f2473ea6-a01f-4207-919c-160dbe10a686] - as reply to the Slack thread-  I’m posting you here. \nThe cilent was unnecessarily debited 10cents. Can we add apology credits to resolve this issue? Asking as Apology credits are owned by the Local Business team, not CS. ","2026-01-30T10:04:46.018Z"],["3852017","WD-22657","WD","mariliis.palo@bolt.eu","Mariliis Palo","Hei! I see the change that NL001 is marked as “inactive”. I can not RF the entity - super! Just to be sure, currently when I`m doing Jan 2026 month-end closing, I see NL001 under the period 2026 meaning I can open/close periods in 2026. Can we block this as well?","2026-01-30T10:04:56.980Z"],["3852018","PFI-840642","PFI","grzegorz.zabrzecki@bolt-outsource.eu","Grzegorz Zabrzecki","Automated message does not solve this.","2026-01-30T10:05:05.895Z"],["3852019","LSS-60122","LSS","iryna.bielykh@bolt.eu","Iryna Bielykh","[^Unit Holdings Am.Contract 6 (2026-2029).pdf]\n\nHello,\n\nHere is the signed scan of Amendment Contract #6","2026-01-30T10:05:06.937Z"],["3852020","WEB-9377","WEB","aleksandr.komolov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Komolov","[~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] ok, great! But time may be shown only in code, but not on the page itself, right?","2026-01-30T10:05:58.499Z"],["3852021","LSS-58768","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] ,\n\nCoachHub came back with the following:\n\n{quote}Our legal team has reviewed the proposed wording on clause 6.3, and we are able to accept it with some minor tweaks (see the part in BOLD). Please find the modified version below:\n\n“_In the event that CoachHub intends to implement an update that would result in a material decrease in the overall protection of Customer Personal Data, CoachHub shall notify Customer in writing at least sixty (60) days in advance of the intended change._\n\n_Any such material decrease shall be subject to Customer’s prior written agreement . If Customer does not agree to the proposed update_ *_within_* *_fourteen (14) days after the receipt of the notice from CoachHub_* *_and it is established that the grounds for the_* *_disagreement is such that would be reasonably expected of customers procuring similar services in the industry_*_, Customer shall have the right to terminate the Agreement (or the affected services) with immediate effect, and CoachHub shall refund any prepaid fees on a pro-rata basis for the unused portion of the services._\n\n_This termination right shall apply notwithstanding any contrary termination provisions in the Agreement._”{quote}\n\nPlease let me know your feedback.\n\nThanks ","2026-01-30T10:06:16.526Z"],["3852026","PASD-179","PASD","sohail.nikouzad@bolt.eu","Sohail Nikouzad","Hi Mihuț, the access has been granted. You can log in to OneModel from the Okta page.","2026-01-30T10:06:35.664Z"],["3852027","WEB-9377","WEB","roberts.calijs@bolt.eu","Robert Chaliy","[~accountid:712020:c9a5e707-0d6d-488a-bafd-1418ebf8e556] Wdyt, better go without time? ","2026-01-30T10:06:41.211Z"],["3852028","FPD-1500","FPD","matteo.casolari@bolt.eu","Matteo Casolari","h1. End of the Week Summary\n\n*What was achieved this week:*\n\n* Ran backtesting for special events and computed accuracy metrics.\n* Created a Google Sheet to compare baseline vs new special-events results and analyzed portfolio and city-level impact.\n* Conducted EDA on temporal features and identified SS/AR and {{n_weekend_days}} as the most promising additions.\n\n*Next week focus:*\n\n* Backtest SS/AR with {{n_weekend_days}}, including:\n** Modifying the codebase accordingly.\n** Running the full backtesting pipeline.\n\n*Scope change:*\n\n* None.\n\n*Risk, blocking:*\n\n* New special events improve finished orders but worsen ASP, resulting in inconsistent GMV impact.\n* No GMV improvement observed, even in cities where special events were added.\n\n*Help needed:*\n\n* None.","2026-01-30T10:06:48.170Z"],["3852029","PFI-836618","PFI","sandra.davidsson@bolt.eu","Sandra Davidsson","Hello Afiba, user says it seems the issue is solved now, so you can close this ticket, thank you! 🙂 ","2026-01-30T10:06:48.814Z"],["3852032","WD-22602","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","documentation of security set up [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/edit-v2/7472447719?draftShareId=7f5d5910-93c5-4a19-a097-cd800bb1aef2|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/WDFTECH/pages/edit-v2/7472447719?draftShareId=7f5d5910-93c5-4a19-a097-cd800bb1aef2|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:07:01.273Z"],["3852033","PFI-840644","PFI","kristina.balazova@bolt-outsource.eu","Kristina Balazova","I am sorry but we still need help. The invoice for this period 1.1.2026 - 19.1.2026 is missing","2026-01-30T10:07:03.990Z"],["3852035","WEB-9376","WEB","aleksandr.komolov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Komolov","[~accountid:63874527f6c85b343c0b7f4b] Gotcha! Let’s see how it goes 👍 ","2026-01-30T10:07:35.943Z"],["3852039","LSS-61798","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","Hi [~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] I see the one in [our folder |https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1JBrRZidgoTOyhBd2N1Rud-KO9SZf9NNk]is from 2023. I have requested an up to date version from the company secretary and will share once received. ","2026-01-30T10:07:48.545Z"],["3852041","INT-94","INT","oleksii.kulbako@bolt.eu","Oleksii Kulbako","26W05 Update:\n\n* Release is blocked by the DriverX team.  Waiting for QA resources to proceed with testing. Aprox estimate from their side is 1 week\n* Released the recalculation mechanism for referral links\n* *Next steps:* Waiting for the green light from the DriverX team\n\n26W04 Update:\n\n* Helped DriverX analysts with A/B test preparation\n* Tested the new design for legacy referral campaigns\n* Working on the recalculation flow for the referral links\n* *Next steps:* Preparations for design release + releasing recalculation flow","2026-01-30T10:08:08.214Z"],["3852045","LSS-62452","LSS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","[^NCA Mutual Agreement - Loi Nguyen.pdf] _(158 kB)_\n\n[^Mutual Agreement on Termination - Loi Nguyen.pdf] _(298 kB)_","2026-01-30T10:09:09.388Z"],["3852046","LSS-62452","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hi,\nBerit Mustonen has identified that there is a data protection / data privacy consideration for this piece of work. \n\nPlease review the ticket and if needed, then please create a sub-ticket for the Privacy team.","2026-01-30T10:09:10.922Z"],["3852047","PFI-840675","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T10:09:37.769Z"],["3852048","LSS-58645","LSS","sumaila.ali@bolt.eu","Sumaila Ali","Ticket raised. \n\nThanks for the nudge. ","2026-01-30T10:09:45.298Z"],["3852052","BDB-1528","BDB","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","Here’s the Expo logo in black [^230624_GGB-Expo-Schriftzug ohne Claim.pdf] ","2026-01-30T10:11:21.764Z"],["3852053","WD-22735","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Hi [~accountid:712020:722e9198-6351-4ae6-8622-13b71b1833f6] \n\nUnfortunately I’m not able to provide you the access because I don’t have it either.\n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga","2026-01-30T10:11:40.617Z"],["3852057","LSS-61941","LSS","ieva.jatulyte@bolt.eu","Ieva Jatulyté","Prašome susipažinti su keleivio pateikta žinute dėl įvykio:\n\n{quote}Incidentas įvyko „Bolt“ platformoje užsakytos ir teiktos paslaugos metu, o vairuotojas buvo parinktas ir pasiūlytas per „Bolt“ sistemą. Smurtiniai veiksmai, ašarinių dujų panaudojimas ir kilusi žala yra tiesiogiai susiję su paslaugos teikimu ir jos saugumo neužtikrinimu.\n\nAtkreipiu dėmesį:\n\n* Dėl įvykio pradėtas ikiteisminis tyrimas.\n* Pateikti medicininiai dokumentai, patvirtinantys sveikatos sutrikdymą.\n* Žala padaryta keleiviui „Bolt“ kelionės metu.\n\nLaikau, kad vien sutartinių sąlygų nuostatų citavimas *nepašalina „Bolt“ pareigos* užtikrinti, kad per platformą teikiamos paslaugos būtų saugios vartotojams.{quote}\n\nPrašau įvertinti ir patarti dėl tolimesnių veiksmų.","2026-01-30T10:12:11.587Z"],["3852058","CMP-27","CMP","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-30T10:12:13.313Z"],["3852064","BDRIV-7","BDRIV","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","[~accountid:712020:688b8f24-a27c-4c40-b5ff-4a0e76cbd371]We do not have to implement all functionality at once, I just listed different possibilities what a “smart” charger will possibly enable. We can just use chargers, which can be adjusted by a dip switch, knob or something like that and just rely on OPS feedback.\n\n[~accountid:712020:e77ef51b-4584-479b-bc00-b172e7475d2e] Can tell more about business parameters I think based on the DE example, in my opinion running a trial and getting real data/feedback from one warehouse would help to provide better understanding of the problem. ","2026-01-30T10:13:35.503Z"],["3852066","CLIENTAPP-38788","CLIENTAPP","taxifyqa@bolt.eu","QA Testing","PR comment for QA:\nNothing to test","2026-01-30T10:13:43.141Z"],["3852070","RLONE-589","RLONE","anton.berggren@bolt.eu","Anton Berggren","Survey respondents increased to max from 200  to 320 weekly.","2026-01-30T10:13:59.826Z"],["3852073","INT-799","INT","oleksii.kulbako@bolt.eu","Oleksii Kulbako","26W05 Update:\n\n* Had a productive meeting with the Driver team regarding streak redesign + backend-driven UI discussions for supply campaigns\n* I'm working on a document that will help designers get a high-level understanding of supply campaigns.\n* I’m working on the admin component for streak campaigns\n","2026-01-30T10:14:51.929Z"],["3852074","GC-3171","GC","radu.vasiliu@bolt.eu","Radu Vasiliu","ETA: 2026-01-30\nStatus: Implementation\n\nSummary: \nRevived the last silent-live test:\n• :done: Recomputed tolls by EdgeDetection for the last silent-live test records.\n• :loading: MapOPs team is analysing the accuracy of Internal EdgeDetection vs TollGuru \n\nBlockers: \n\n\nDetails:\n• :done: implementation complete, last PR was merged this week.\n•  :done: Run silent-live test for comparing EdgeDetection vs TollGuru,  in Thailand.\n•  :done: Extract silent-live results\n•  :done: Map OPs team found some bugs while analysing the last silent-live test: EdgeDetection vs TollGuru in  Thailand).\n•  :done: Tooling: Admin-panel page for testing our internal solution: Route-Tolls\n•  :done: Analysed the bugs found by Map OPs team on the last silent-live test => none was reproducible. Possibly the errors were due to OSRM map-matching failure. In the meanwhile the OSRM was updated a few times, and works correctly.\n•  :done: Revived the last silent-live test:\n    ◦ :done:  Recomputed tolls by EdgeDetection for the last silent-live test records.\n    ◦ :loading:  MapOPs team is analysing the accuracy of Internal EdgeDetection vs TollGuru","2026-01-30T10:14:59.865Z"],["3852076","MVRT-1530","MVRT","kyrylo.matiupatenko@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Matiupatenko","[~accountid:6358f0a501c2ff842c182ef2] fixed that ✅","2026-01-30T10:15:49.666Z"],["3852078","SRED-1114","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","{noformat}7:8:\nLeft as is, there are bw out spikes up to 3 Kp/s, older generation can actually make it worse \n\n23:24:\nLeft as is, there are bw out spikes up to 2 Kp/s, older generation can actually make it worse \n\n25:26:\nLeft as is, there are bw out spikes up to 3 Kp/s, older generation can actually make it worse \n\n29:30:\nLeft as is, there are bw out spikes up to 3 Kp/s, older generation can actually make it worse \n\n31:32:\nLeft as is, there are bw out spikes up to 2-2.5 Kp/s, older generation can actually make it worse \n\n87:88:\nLeft as is, there are bw out spikes up to 5-6 Kp/s, older generation can actually make it worse \n\n89:90:\nm7g.large -> m6g.large\n\n119:120:\nm7g.large -> m6g.large{noformat}","2026-01-30T10:16:20.095Z"],["3852082","PFI-840676","PFI","austin.fagbolagun@bolt-outsource.eu","Austin Fagbolagun","!IMG_1379.jpeg|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T10:16:38.979Z"],["3852084","LSS-58668","LSS","stefano.roggiero@bolt.eu","Stefano Roggiero","[^Confirmation re personal address_ VP and AK.pdf]\n[^Incorporation certificate_Bolt Services RO Srl.pdf]\n[^2025.05.05 Bolt Services RO S.R.L.  AoA.pdf]\n[^2025.09.05 Registration certificate Bolt Services RO S.R.L.pdf]\n[^UBO statement - RO 25.10.2021]\n\nHere you go [~accountid:712020:c152e340-503c-4822-bf8e-89c9f6cffb24] \n\nFinancial statements we need to request from Finance. Please make a ticket for them [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/28/group/101/create/589]. Clarify which years you need. No licence to operate is needed. \n\n[^RO-Bolt Group structure chart - Bolt Technology OU.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-30T10:17:00.031Z"],["3852086","LSS-61751","LSS","aleksandr.parshikov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Parshikov","Hello! When do you think it is going to be signed, [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] ? ","2026-01-30T10:17:49.804Z"],["3852088","XP-3111","XP","garret.oconnell@bolt.eu","Garret O'Connell","* 2 types of marts:\n** one built on metric flow - that has assigned ownership - in semantic layer in configuration in dbt repo\n** one built on sql - there has to be clear \n*** we can find in datahub the owners of marts, e.g. Ansh owns \n*** but Silja owns mart city rides, which needs to be re-assigned\n*** lets ensure at least 1 AE and 1 DA owning each mart","2026-01-30T10:18:05.052Z"],["3852089","LSS-61751","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hi team!\nCan you please check if this document has reached Ahto for signatures. Please note that MasterCard has initiated the signature process. ","2026-01-30T10:19:27.735Z"],["3852091","LSS-61406","LSS","andrei.ivanov@bolt.eu","Andrei Ivanov","Hey team, \ncould you pls advise if it’s been sent to the Provider? yesterday they told me that it’s not there yet ","2026-01-30T10:20:06.762Z"],["3852097","WD-22736","WD","dominika.bednarczyk@bolt.eu","Dominika Bednarczyk","Also information about my sick live from November is still missing there.","2026-01-30T10:21:21.113Z"],["3852099","FRAUD-5762","FRAUD","liisi.laasik@bolt.eu","Liisi Dovbnja","CDC PR: [https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/pull/4762|https://github.com/bolteu/change-data-capture/pull/4762|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:21:33.855Z"],["3852103","LSS-60715","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","Thanks, [~accountid:712020:89527d4a-ea9c-40dc-b6fd-9e0779096af2] ! Basically, we can accept these Special Terms but before that we need to make sure that invoicing rules they proposed to us in the invoicing agreement are doable for Billing Team (Bolt). I worked on machine translation into EN so here are the most crucial clauses from this agreement that provisions that may deviate from our Special T&C. Please advise what you think 😉 \n\n*Special Terms:*\n\n# The service fee is 10% of the fee for Bolt Services.\n# Subsequent payments are payments for Bolt Services used by the Customer.\n# A monthly invoice is submitted to the Customer for the Service Fee under Section 2.1 and for Bolt Services used by Users during the previous calendar month.{color:#ff5630} Invoices will be available to the Customer on the Business Portal by the 14th day of the following calendar month.{color}\n# The Customer shall make payment according to the invoice within *60* days of the date of receipt of the invoice by the Customer. If payment is not received by the due date, all subsequent requests by Users for Bolt Services will be rejected.\n# If the Customer fails to make payment by the due date specified in the invoice, they shall be obliged to pay interest at a rate of 5% per annum on the total amount overdue. The Customer is obliged to compensate Bolt for all reasonable expenses, including all administrative, legal and other costs incurred in recovering any late payment\n\n*Invoicing Agreement*\n\n# _The Supplier is obliged to deliver invoices to SE exclusively electronically, i.e. by e-mail to the following SE e-mail address:_ [*_e-invoice@seas.sk_*|mailto:e-invoice@seas.sk] _,_ *_e_*{color:#ff5630}*_xclusively from the e-mail address. The Supplier specified in the header of this Agreement_* {color}_and, in the event that the Supplier's email address for electronic delivery of invoices is changed in accordance with the procedure specified below in this Agreement, from the changed email address._\n\n_5. Invoices delivered electronically to an email address other than that specified in the previous point, or from an email address other than that specified in the previous point, shall not be considered delivered, and SE shall not be obliged to pay such invoices to the Supplier._","2026-01-30T10:22:17.602Z"],["3852104","SREP-928","SREP","kirill.kuznetsov@bolt.eu","Kirill Kuznetsov","Checked statistic, unfortunately we have such services which are killed after graceTermination period in majority these are only GEO services. \n\n!image-20260130-102146.png|width=766,alt=\"image-20260130-102146.png\"!\n\n\n\nSo this is not global issue, but overall for NJSC service we use a common configuration [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/e6f2662fbd581a40dbe161b46b26c004a584cfc4/deploy/k8s/server.yaml#L37|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/e6f2662fbd581a40dbe161b46b26c004a584cfc4/deploy/k8s/server.yaml#L37]  together with preStop hook and increased graceTermination shudown to 45s. (default 30).\n\nIn such scenario, there is no golden parameters which fit for everyone, so let’s focus now on improvement for vector only, because vector now has quite short graceTerminationPeriod\n\n{noformat}kubectl  -n vector get daemonsets -o custom-columns=\"NAME:.metadata.name,GRACE_PERIOD:.spec.template.spec.terminationGracePeriodSeconds\"\nNAME         GRACE_PERIOD\nvector-k8s   5\n{noformat}\n\nWhich also is conflicting with config {{VECTOR_GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN_LIMIT_SECS}}Which pass in vector configuration:\n\n{noformat}            - name: VECTOR_GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN_LIMIT_SECS\n              value: \"10\"\n{noformat}\n\nAlso as Igor highlighted for such thing better fit preStop hook for vector DS, but we already have in use internal vector mechanism to processing SIGTERM, so adjusting this now, to mitigate it. ","2026-01-30T10:22:23.781Z"],["3852108","HS-29568","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Hi [~accountid:62d7b457807cf6f78ca9d117],\n\nPlease initiate the offboarding in Workday and ensure all approvals are completed by 4:00 PM today. You can see the instructions [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BMP/pages/4609048899/Contract+Contingent+Workers+in+Workday#End-Contingent-Worker-Contract].\n\nAdding [~accountid:712020:950de065-187c-4170-babd-e5aa814bdb19] for visibility.\n\nAll the best, \n\nKerilin ","2026-01-30T10:23:46.978Z"],["3852109","CSDA-314","CSDA","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","FYI [~accountid:6220fed259c0740069d878cc] ","2026-01-30T10:23:57.173Z"],["3852112","TA-158","TA","jorick.polderman@bolt.eu","Jorick Thijs Polderman","[~accountid:712020:a7f24c35-13af-47c1-b146-05c4a36324d4] , the Teams feature from Atlassian offers agents, including automating a job listing agent, you can brows them from the team page: [https://home.atlassian.com/o/d3799b7c-d294-40ed-8a3f-ae8d7891558e/people/team/89434a35-1705-49ee-bbe6-1f2475408bf5?cloudId=1eb99fa2-4cbc-4ca4-b378-38b339f46f0b|https://home.atlassian.com/o/d3799b7c-d294-40ed-8a3f-ae8d7891558e/people/team/89434a35-1705-49ee-bbe6-1f2475408bf5?cloudId=1eb99fa2-4cbc-4ca4-b378-38b339f46f0b|smart-link]  and then basically look at the Add Agent feature, haven’t tried it but maybe worth exploring. CC [~accountid:712020:5f494197-2d0e-454f-918b-48f52a220ab9] / [~accountid:712020:c2e979f7-9494-4395-9718-36c7ffc96e53] ","2026-01-30T10:24:24.549Z"],["3852113","CSDA-314","CSDA","lisanna.lomp@bolt.eu","Lisanna Lomp","Added [~accountid:5d3ff51eb7f3ac0da80c815c] and [~accountid:712020:29d8b602-d17f-40cd-9cae-5653bc2c54b7] for visibility","2026-01-30T10:25:02.453Z"],["3852114","PAW-15290","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 Auto-closed: PR was approved by @bolt-juri-gavshin\n\nPR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162570\nStatus: open\nAuto-closed at: 2026-01-30 10:25:12 UTC\n\nIf this ticket was closed incorrectly, you can reopen it manually.","2026-01-30T10:25:12.251Z"],["3852121","FPD-1277","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","Status update for this week:\n\n* the last part of the epic – moving the budget logic to {{financial-planning-input-based-model}} from {{investment-modeling}} is almost done; two PRs were already merged and there is one that is still pending code review:\n** [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-data-science-libraries/pull/253|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-data-science-libraries/pull/253] - merged\n** [https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/822|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/822|smart-link] - merged\n** [https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/826|https://github.com/bolteu/data-science-databricks/pull/826|smart-link] - needs code review\n* after the last PR is merged, the only thing left to do is to update the job settings in databricks to make sure that the moved budget scripts can still be executed ","2026-01-30T10:27:01.460Z"],["3852122","MKP-9901","MKP","iaroslav.melnichuk@bolt.eu","Iaroslav Melnichuk","will be back with info today","2026-01-30T10:27:01.968Z"],["3852123","PFI-840679","PFI","carlo.mizzon@bolt.eu","Carlo Mizzon","!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 11.28.17.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T10:28:26.034Z"],["3852128","WD-22735","WD","filip.bederski@bolt.eu","Filip Bederski","Hello Darja,\n\nThank you for your reply. Do you know who can or how I need to proceed\nfurther ?\n\nBest Regards, Cordialement, Met vriendelijke groeten, Mit freundlichen\nGrüßen, Pozdrawiam,\n\nFilip Bederski\nOperations Manager Maintenance | Belgium\n\n\nfilip.bederski@bolt.eu <loredana.panait@bolt.eu>\nblog.bolt.eu <https://bolt.eu/>","2026-01-30T10:29:44.486Z"],["3852130","COP-1912","COP","rok.fortuna@bolt.eu","Rok Fortuna","Postponing until new supply data marts are available.","2026-01-30T10:30:04.774Z"],["3852131","PFI-816884","PFI","maria.hanuschi@bolt-outsource.eu","Maria Narcisa Hanuschi","The Rider is waiting for our response. Can you help us with an answer in this case, please?","2026-01-30T10:30:10.023Z"],["3852136","LSS-61606","LSS","beatrice.krasenko@bolt.eu","Beatričė Krašenko","sent","2026-01-30T10:31:39.971Z"],["3852138","WFM-10197","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:63ff08ef15d668edd8ed70fb].\r\n\r\nAs we discussed earlier, I assigned \t\r\nDocument data extraction - LIVE - Mandarin script & \t\r\nDocument data extraction - QC - Mandarin script queues.\r\n\r\nIf any additional help needed, just ask or raise a new ticket.\r\n\r\nHave a wonderful day,\r\nArtiur","2026-01-30T10:32:08.079Z"],["3852139","CMP-27","CMP","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162619","2026-01-30T10:32:13.028Z"],["3852142","INT-854","INT","shubham.chodankar@bolt.eu","Shubham Tukaram Chodankar","26W05 Update:\n\n* Done\n** Backfill of data and backend support for dynamic holdout label\n* Next\n** drop usages of hardcoded values\n** admin panel integration","2026-01-30T10:32:48.850Z"],["3852143","WFM-10107","WFM","ruxandra.dumitrescu@bolt.eu","Ruxandra-Elena Dumitrescu","Please ask agents to check now","2026-01-30T10:33:21.566Z"],["3852144","LSS-61406","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hi team can you please take the attached document forward for signatures. [^Bolt - Credits System_08012026 (2).docx] \n\nSignatory details:  [+Xavier.Segalie@nielseniq.com+|mailto:Xavier.Segalie@nielseniq.com], please cc [+nihan.fisek@nielseniq.com+|mailto:nihan.fisek@nielseniq.com]","2026-01-30T10:33:31.871Z"],["3852146","LSS-62152","LSS","jolanta.prystupa@bolt.eu","Jolanta Prystupa","hello, any updates here?","2026-01-30T10:34:01.272Z"],["3852150","PFI-823728","PFI","erik.semet@bolt-outsource.eu","Erik Šemet","Hello, any update in this case?","2026-01-30T10:35:33.451Z"],["3852154","LSS-62021","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Hello team,\n[~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] thanks for the overview! \n[~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17] [~accountid:712020:a7dc00bc-9eb8-4c76-ad4a-4fd81a639553] I have [drafted a direct claim to Etransport|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l2WpvZDujFS27CUAFScsaSul8URl8WU-/edit], please have a look, thanks! ","2026-01-30T10:36:13.572Z"],["3852164","HS-29572","HS","anastasia.orfanidou@bolt.eu","Anastasia Orfanidou","[^BoltEuCyprusPayroll_31-01-2026_Payslip_AnastasiaOrfanidou(E010918) (1).pdf]\n\n[^BoltEuCyprusPayroll_31-12-2025_Payslip_AnastasiaOrfanidou(E010918).pdf]","2026-01-30T10:38:06.173Z"],["3852166","CNT-466","CNT","kristjan.konsap@bolt.eu","Kristjan-Johannes Konsap","[~accountid:712020:c9a5e707-0d6d-488a-bafd-1418ebf8e556] What was the newest decision, are we duplicating content in our blog and Medium?","2026-01-30T10:38:23.187Z"],["3852171","INT-878","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-30T10:39:11.055Z"],["3852176","DRX-16433","DRX","mariia.nazarenko@bolt.eu","Mariia Nazarenko","Seems like issue fixed already, please retest it","2026-01-30T10:39:58.049Z"],["3852177","LSS-55962","LSS","felix.antwi@bolt.eu","Felix Antwi","Hi [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] \n\nDijo will take over this ticket going forward, thanks!","2026-01-30T10:40:03.409Z"],["3852180","LSS-47809","LSS","felix.antwi@bolt.eu","Felix Antwi","Hi [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] \n\nDijo will take over this ticket going forward, thanks!","2026-01-30T10:40:40.103Z"],["3852183","LSS-58081","LSS","felix.antwi@bolt.eu","Felix Antwi","Hi [~accountid:712020:c190ab8b-4add-4eb3-bd6e-ab39d6c1cd0c] \n\nDijo will take over this ticket going forward, thanks!","2026-01-30T10:41:06.615Z"],["3852186","LSS-62343","LSS","laura.newton@bolt.eu","Laura Newton","Thanks [~accountid:61fd40abc224b80069c9d6cf], here is a editable version attached for the records, but will send the proposed changes to the landlord.\n\n[^GF 22 Gas Street BOLT 290126.pages]\n\n","2026-01-30T10:42:20.280Z"],["3852187","INT-879","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-30T10:42:27.808Z"],["3852188","CMP-36","CMP","lukasz.wolodkiewicz@bolt.eu","Łukasz Wołodkiewicz","Issue is caused by users accessing PDE without an email address set.","2026-01-30T10:42:43.836Z"],["3852189","FX-3766","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Ernests Rudzītis [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769769754980169]*{color}:\nYes\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:42:48.930Z"],["3852190","LSS-61941","LSS","beatrice.grize@bolt.eu","Beatričė Grižė","Sveiki, [~accountid:712020:7a0eb594-fb3b-4988-9715-b614bae4a6fb], dėkui.\n\nDalinuosi galimu atsakymu:\n\nSveiki, _(vardas),_\n\nSuprantame Jūsų poziciją ir pabrėžiame, kad bet kokie smurtiniai veiksmai yra visiškai nepriimtini. Kartu pažymime, jog „Bolt“ rimtai vertina saugumo klausimus ir, gavusi informaciją apie tokio pobūdžio incidentus, imasi priemonių platformos naudotojų saugumui užtikrinti (įskaitant vidinį incidento vertinimą ir bendradarbiavimą su kompetentingomis institucijomis).\n\nVis dėlto teisiniu požiūriu „Bolt“ nėra pavežėjimo paslaugų teikėjas ir nedalyvauja kaip šalis keleivio ir nepriklausomo vairuotojo teisiniuose santykiuose, todėl atsakomybė už konkretaus nepriklausomo vairuotojo veiksmus ir dėl jų kilusią žalą tenka pačiam vairuotojui. Ši pozicija išlieka nepakitusi, nepaisant to, kad kelionė buvo užsakyta per „Bolt“ platformą.\n\nAtsižvelgiant į tai, klausimai dėl žalos atlyginimo sprendžiami teisės aktų nustatyta tvarka tarp nukentėjusio asmens ir atsakingo asmens, taip pat vykstant ikiteisminiam tyrimui.\n\nDar kartą apgailestaujame dėl patirtos situacijos ir linkime, kad ji būtų kuo greičiau išspręsta.\n\nPagarbiai\nBolt komanda","2026-01-30T10:42:52.208Z"],["3852192","HS-29540","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Confirming Job Description","2026-01-30T10:43:02.977Z"],["3852197","INT-831","INT","ilya.vrubleuski@bolt.eu","Ilya Vrubleuski","26W05 Update:\n\n* All event campaigns were migrated (Including CS campaigns). We already see successful usages of newly added campaigns.\n* Only cleanup from migration code is left (task is in progress)\n* We did not receive Source Code for the script using by CS team so we took some risks during the migration. Indirect pointers and team knowledge highlighted the correctness of our suggestions. We have to carefully monitor CS requests but there is 95% chance everything should work as expected.","2026-01-30T10:43:50.418Z"],["3852198","FX-3765","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Jana Lutus [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769769827575589]*{color}:\nduplicate. already being handled in [this ticket|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3744]\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:44:00.123Z"],["3852199","SRED-1114","SRED","artem.timchenko@bolt.eu","Artem Timchenko","{noformat}19:20:\nc6gn.large -> c6g.large{noformat}\n\nSince traffic dropped significantly ","2026-01-30T10:44:02.936Z"],["3852202","FX-3765","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769769853318479]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3765 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:44:25.510Z"],["3852206","FX-3764","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769769898030849]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3764 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:45:10.369Z"],["3852208","FX-3765","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769769893431089]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3765 successfully transitioned to state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:45:24.944Z"],["3852211","FX-3744","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769769927828419]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3744 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:45:39.763Z"],["3852212","LSS-62456","LSS","edik.davtian@bolt.eu","Edik Davtian","[^BANK DETAILS (4).pdf] _(131 kB)_","2026-01-30T10:45:56.473Z"],["3852214","FX-3743","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769769960723629]*{color}:\nIssue FX-3743 is already in the state 'Rejected'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:46:14.777Z"],["3852216","LSS-62456","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-30T10:46:25.621Z"],["3852220","MM-993","MM",null,"Automation for Jira","||Readiness Criteria||Rating||Rationale||\n|Completeness|🔴|No description or requirements provided; insufficient information for development.|\n|Clarity|🔴|No content to assess clarity; summary alone is vague and lacks detail.|\n|Auditability|🔴|No links or references to supporting documentation or sources.|\n|Estimated|🔴|No time estimate or original estimate field provided.|\n\nSuggestions:\n\n* Add a detailed description, requirements, and acceptance criteria.\n* Clarify the scope and objectives in simple language.\n* Link to any relevant documentation or designs.\n* Provide a time estimate.","2026-01-30T10:46:53.864Z"],["3852221","PFI-838733","PFI","sikarin.seepol@bolt.eu","Sikarin Seepol","Just to confirm, in this scenario the client will not receive an Invoice Payment Receipt for the amount paid. Is that correct?","2026-01-30T10:46:54.840Z"],["3852222","PFI-826411","PFI","fahmin.mikayilov@bolt.eu","Fahmin Mikayilov","[~accountid:616ff0d6702bd0006a685f65] , hey. If there is only iban belongs to another subject imo the payout could not be finished. Are you sure about the payout has not be stopped by ABB? \nWe have faced a number of cases like that. The payout send back us by our bank due to invalid bank details and we reject the payout.\n[~accountid:712020:db5b1201-8d10-4d36-ba7f-c3ddac5e909e] can you please have a look?","2026-01-30T10:46:56.908Z"],["3852223","PFI-840540","PFI","fiona.achieng@bolt-outsource.eu","Fiona Achieng","[~accountid:626a69abb31e6f0068634a56] , the driver’s claim is that the report is showing his earnings from January, but claims it should show from April instead, as that is when their year is calculated from. How do I proceed in advising them?","2026-01-30T10:47:05.830Z"],["3852224","PFI-840540","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋  Thank you for the response. Looks like this ticket is already resolved. \n\nIf the issue persists, please feel free to reopen your request via our service desk https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1 or reach out through #commerce-support-billing.\n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T10:47:09.382Z"],["3852225","RISK2-3300","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*30.01*\n\n* {{Entity}} will be a linkable record on OR-Instance\n* Access to view and link it must be restricted via a new *Entity Role*. The role would be later granted to Finance (PayCo) and Legal (Reclass) teams, in addition to Admins.\n** [@Sujith|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03UQBS230B] please create a repository and ability to link Entities to OR-Instance, I’ve attached the document to this message.","2026-01-30T10:47:12.353Z"],["3852226","LSS-62456","LSS","edik.davtian@bolt.eu","Edik Davtian","UPD: \n\n\n\nIn terms of the main contract - Bolt shared in November of the last year our Special Terms for Bolt Food - Delivery vertical - for Merchants & we are awaiting for Partner comments - if any to be received ","2026-01-30T10:47:14.988Z"],["3852229","PFI-835503","PFI","maret@bolt.eu","Maret Kukk","Hey, I have received a reply from Fonoa support, also asked [~accountid:610279973900e60070a3495c] to review whether we should take action based on the advice received. Let us know when you get more details from the FO while we’re reviewing 🙂 ","2026-01-30T10:47:43.650Z"],["3852231","WFM-10221","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:5dbbe92cb87a410db33f7faa].\r\n\r\nCould you please clarify if you want me to change the Market access to ZA only?\r\nCurrently, I see active queues for Canada and USA. Would you like me to unassign her from these queues? \r\n\r\nWaiting for you response,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T10:47:51.749Z"],["3852235","LSS-60958","LSS","daniela.capatana@bolt-outsource.eu","Daniela Căpățână","Hi! Regarding this case, the necessary measures have already been taken, so the issue has been resolved. Thank you!","2026-01-30T10:48:30.886Z"],["3852237","LSS-62316","LSS","ankita.dhabu@bolt.eu","Ankita Chandrashekhar Dhabu","Hi [~accountid:6151832899b4b8006a366830] Request you to please start the correct workflow in Jira for Fleet deal agreements and provide all the commercial information. Thank you. \n","2026-01-30T10:48:41.151Z"],["3852243","RISK2-3303","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*30.01. Update - Shared with LogicGate:*\n\n*The new Risk Type field in OR-Instance for prompting SCF section*\n\n* Remove the standalone {{Risk Type}} field and condition which includes drop-down options for {{operational}} and {{security}}.\n* Instead, implement a role-based access, adding both {{SCF}} and {{Assets}} to InfoSec Role, so only their role is able to see those sections.","2026-01-30T10:50:04.959Z"],["3852244","HS-29476","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:58704fb5-3b31-40a0-896f-1d862e6e1fd9],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-30T10:50:18.736Z"],["3852246","CMO-12987","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","26.01 - 72% completed training [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1o2Mo4x9tJpNYXG_UUpeozeHzm8clG-hX/edit?gid=1974767367#gid=1974767367|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1o2Mo4x9tJpNYXG_UUpeozeHzm8clG-hX/edit?gid=1974767367#gid=1974767367|smart-link] \n\n[https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04LWD26QNM/p1769434993644459?thread_ts=1767859835.793789&cid=C04LWD26QNM|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04LWD26QNM/p1769434993644459?thread_ts=1767859835.793789&cid=C04LWD26QNM|smart-link] \n\n\n\nNext and final check 02.02","2026-01-30T10:50:41.433Z"],["3852248","WFM-10222","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:64182443b05b4e3e7daa195b]!\r\n\r\nQueues assigned.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T10:50:43.146Z"],["3852249","LSS-61459","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:a9500cde-28bc-4a8e-95d6-7818a2252cf8] \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hk9c6RsYiAZifBnZm0txPfSljhw89dWa/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hk9c6RsYiAZifBnZm0txPfSljhw89dWa/edit|smart-link]  - please share updated SOW with Apple  \n\nPlease also request reviewed T&C for customers that we shared with Apple because we need to add their data in empty spaces ","2026-01-30T10:50:44.375Z"],["3852250","DSR-4237","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T10:51:08.551Z"],["3852251","DMB-1731","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Resolved as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:52:00.300Z"],["3852254","DMB-1735","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Resolved as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:52:43.374Z"],["3852255","PFI-829457","PFI","inna.arutyunova@bolt.eu","Inna Arutyunova","Thank you for reply, \n\nWe always send such reports to this channel. Like [this one|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-770918].\nWhen courier pays the debt and it is not added to account we created ticke to Food Collection and colleagues add the payment to the courier's account. \n\n","2026-01-30T10:52:50.260Z"],["3852257","DMB-1736","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Resolved as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:52:58.186Z"],["3852258","DMB-1738","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Resolved as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:53:09.522Z"],["3852259","LSS-49536","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hi [~accountid:5f0c30effe23000022252e68] !\n\nHaving in consideration what we wrote in our last comment and the fact that the testing showed that there isn’t, in fact, ant advantage in keeping the feature, we don’t have objections in disabling the feature, if this what the business wants.\n\nThank you for seeking our confirmation!\n\n\n\ncc: [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1] ","2026-01-30T10:53:15.757Z"],["3852260","DMB-1742","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Resolved as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:53:18.702Z"],["3852261","FPD-1532","FPD","anastasia.serebryannikova@bolt.eu","Nastya Serebryannikova","Status update:\n\n* the ingestion of cycle metadata, city dataset metadata and scenario metrics forecast is now possible\n* there is a confluence page with initial information on how to query these tables\n\nStill to do for these three tables:\n\n* make sure that the access to the data is restricted and it’s being treated as sensitive (right now it’s unfortunately not the case)\n* update the ingestion configs to account for the changes in the folder structure in s3\n* ingest the data that we already have (from this cycle and recent cycles) into these tables\n* add info to confluence on the technical setup \n\nNext steps:\n\n* enable ingestion for adjustments and selected scenarios\n* enable ingestion for model metadata and comments\n* delete unused code in the {{data_layer/}} folder","2026-01-30T10:53:31.972Z"],["3852262","CMO-13009","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","W5 - had 2 meetings\n\n* general tool intro, with focus on Articulate\n* adult learning theories session","2026-01-30T10:53:40.369Z"],["3852263","RISK2-3248","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","To keep the risk assessment process *simple and scalable for wider teams*, while still enabling *country-level tracking where required* (e.g. Reclassification, Safety), we introduced a mandatory scope related question or Operational Risk page, which affects the Operational Risk Instance layout.\n\nThe {{Scope}} section, if chosen as {{Globally}}, hides the basic details section, leaving only Country, Controls, Assessments, KRIs, Entity, and Assets visible.\n\n* Section: {{Scope}}\n** {{How is this risk tracked?}}\n* drop-down options:\n** {{Globally}}\n** {{Country level}}","2026-01-30T10:53:52.152Z"],["3852264","DMB-1741","DMB","rachit.dua@bolt.eu","Rachit Dua","Should have been resolved as part of [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DLP-1739|smart-link] \nHowever would require re-testing. [~accountid:712020:d0b05abd-21c2-4eb5-a2e6-6a1f8aff10e2] ","2026-01-30T10:53:52.510Z"],["3852266","RS-1988","RS","liisa.aavik@bolt.eu","Liisa Aavik","Hi team, here’s my initial response about the status of those claims and what actions will be needed onwards:\n\n| |{color:#ffffff}*Sustainability claim* {color}|{color:#ffffff}*Advice*{color}|{color:#ffffff}*Action needed*{color}|\n|{color:#ffffff}*1*{color}|_It’s another step towards helping make cities for people, not cars, by reducing car dependency in companies and improving businesses’ access to urban transportation._|*Status*: ✅ _Low risk_\n*Why*: value-driven messaging, no direct environmental or social claim.|-|\n|{color:#ffffff}2{color}|_Businesses are increasingly under pressure to ensure sustainability is at the heart of their business strategies and practices._|*Status*: ⚠️ Currently, the pressure has lowered, so we need to update this a bit. The statement is true in long–term, but a bit vague and not grounded in data.|Find a new credible source to reference and reword.|\n|{color:#ffffff}3{color}|_Employee travel is one of the greatest contributors to carbon emissions for businesses (_[+_World Economic Forum_+|https://www.weforum.org/agenda/2021/09/business-travel-wont-be-more-sustainable-post-covid-unless-companies-take-action/]_)._|*Status*: ⚠️ The source added is from 2021, but I couldn't verify any research or graphs it references. It feels like a random, unreliable source, which also reflects poorly on the World Economic Forum. The source mainly discusses air travel, only briefly mentioning car travel, lacking nuance and relevance to our activities.|Find a new credible source to reference.|\n|{color:#ffffff}4{color}|_Only_[ |https://news.na.chubb.com/blog-2022-10-05-The-Return-of-Business-Travel-Understanding-Risks-and-Coverage][+_7% of business travel is over 1,000 miles_+|https://news.na.chubb.com/blog-2022-10-05-The-Return-of-Business-Travel-Understanding-Risks-and-Coverage]_, and most trips are under 250 miles._|*Status*: ⚠️This claim refers only to [+US research about flights+|https://www.stratosjets.com/blog/business-travel-statistics/#:~:text=Only%207%25%20of%20trips%20fly%20further%20than%201%2C000%20miles], so it doesn't support a global view on employee travel.|Find a new credible source to reference and likely a different claim. |\n|{color:#ffffff}5{color}|_Multimodal urban transportation can efficiently cut personal car use and passenger transportation emissions. This is proven by a recent modelling on the multimodality impact in Berlin, which concluded that by 2030 the German capital could cut private car use by 20% and_[ |https://www.oliverwyman.com/content/dam/oliver-wyman/v2/publications/2023/nov/2023-oliver-wyman-shared-mobility-report][+_passenger transport emissions_+|https://www.oliverwyman.com/content/dam/oliver-wyman/v2/publications/2023/nov/2023-oliver-wyman-shared-mobility-report] _by up to 40%._|*Status*: ⚠️ Generally strong, but I would reword. We cite one research we commissioned, not all research meta-analytically. So, there's room to argue. Let's focus on this one study. It may not be flashy marketing-wise, but in sustainability, modesty is key.|*Rewording:*\n[+Modelling of Berlin’s transport system+|https://www.oliverwyman.com/content/dam/oliver-wyman/v2/publications/2023/nov/2023-oliver-wyman-shared-mobility-report] shows that expanding multimodal urban mobility could reduce private car use by 20% and lower passenger transport emissions by up to 40% by 2030. This highlights the potential of integrated transport solutions to significantly decrease urban car dependency and emissions.|\n|{color:#ffffff}6{color}|_Scooters emit 3+ times less CO2 than private internal combustion engine (ICE) vehicles even considering the full life-cycle emissions_|*Status*: ⚠️ What is the source? Life-cycle assessment? |* Cite data source. \n* Share that emission figures are based on the lifesycle, not just tailpipe. \n* State that it’s “compared to private ICE cars per passenger-km” or similar|\n|{color:#ffffff}7{color}|_e-bikes are 2,5 times better than private ICE vehicles_|*Status*: ⚠️ Better how? What metric? What is the source?|Reword, add metric and source of the claim. |\n|{color:#ffffff}8{color}|_EVs have zero tailpipe emissions, and depending on the grid’s energy mix, their lifetime emissions can be as much as 75% lower than those of ICE (UK comparison) (source_[ |https://about.bnef.com/blog/no-doubt-about-it-evs-really-are-cleaner-than-gas-cars/?utm_source=Email&utm_campaign=863036&utm_medium=Newsletter&utm_content=BNEFNewsletterMar&tactic=863036&pchash=][+_1_+|https://about.bnef.com/blog/no-doubt-about-it-evs-really-are-cleaner-than-gas-cars/?utm_source=Email&utm_campaign=863036&utm_medium=Newsletter&utm_content=BNEFNewsletterMar&tactic=863036&pchash=]_;_[ +_2_+|https://about.bnef.com/insights/clean-transport/no-doubt-about-it-evs-really-are-cleaner-than-gas-cars/?utm_source=Email&utm_campaign=863036&utm_medium=Newsletter&utm_content=BNEFNewsletterMar&tactic=863036&pchash=#:~:text=27%2D71%25%20lower%20than%20those%20of%20equivalent%20ICE%20vehicles.]_)._|*Status*: ⚠️ Pretty good, but change the % and remove “UK” (let’s not cite the source from internal Slack).|*Change:*\n_EVs have zero tailpipe emissions, and depending on the grid’s energy mix, their lifetime emissions can be_ [+_up to 71% lower_+|https://about.bnef.com/insights/clean-transport/no-doubt-about-it-evs-really-are-cleaner-than-gas-cars/?utm_source=Email&utm_campaign=863036&utm_medium=Newsletter&utm_content=BNEFNewsletterMar&tactic=863036&pchash=#:~:text=27%2D71%25%20lower%20than%20those%20of%20equivalent%20ICE%20vehicles.] _than those of ICE._|\n\n\n\n*Next steps:*\n\n* Actions 5, 8 can be done by [~accountid:5e8f2bde2c0eff0b8fc1313f]. \n* Actions 2,  3, 4 can be done by [~accountid:712020:81ed6d45-d7b2-45d4-89cd-030f00488538]  and confirmed with [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257]. \n* Actions 6, 7 should be checked by [~accountid:712020:d4341386-14a0-42a7-b596-cca29c4c7257] .\n\n\n\n[~accountid:5e8f2bde2c0eff0b8fc1313f], as this research is extra work, do you have a deadline for this?  ","2026-01-30T10:54:22.955Z"],["3852267","CMO-13003","CMO","taisiia.nahorna@bolt.eu","Taisiia Nahorna","29.01 - shared the lesson for review - [https://360.articulate.com/review/content/a645794f-7aaa-482d-bf1a-77ef4f152f3f/review|https://360.articulate.com/review/content/a645794f-7aaa-482d-bf1a-77ef4f152f3f/review|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T10:54:43.912Z"],["3852269","SREDESK-7476","SREDESK","aleksei.getman@bolt.eu","Aleksei Getman","[~accountid:712020:469c4639-7443-4548-87bf-64c61cd29052] \n1. I’ve contacted [~accountid:5de0e6d8be6c1f0d07202403] and she told me she will get back in this ticket or someone from her team will to greenlight this.\n2. I don’t think I do\n3. Honestly I think no special retention policy is needed now. We expect new releases of our sdk be fairly rare (a few per year)","2026-01-30T10:55:03.979Z"],["3852270","RCE-402","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769770487698559]*{color}:\nHey <@UDQ0ZU37T>! We own and manage the suspension system, but the part about scheduled order lifecycle is outside of our scope. Not something we'd be able to help you with, unfortunately.\n\nI cant really point at who owns the scheduled rides as a feature from product side, but looks like <#C06FKQ4F7RC> could be a good place to start.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:55:04.406Z"],["3852271","LSS-53738","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (30.01) - Brightflag*+\n\n* KVDL onboarding being handled on [+LSS-62458+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/issue/LSS-62458]","2026-01-30T10:55:23.734Z"],["3852273","RCE-389","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769770523555709]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-389 is already in the state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:55:35.650Z"],["3852274","CSDT-990","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","New report shared with owner: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/47470|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/47470]","2026-01-30T10:55:38.957Z"],["3852276","RCE-384","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769770538332279]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-384 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:55:52.892Z"],["3852279","CNT-466","CNT","aleksandr.komolov@bolt.eu","Aleksandr Komolov","[~accountid:621c92ba4160640069c52776] Ideally, we slightly change articles that publish to Medium in case if these are duplicates of what we have in our Blog. I would not publish the same copy to both resources. ","2026-01-30T10:56:15.595Z"],["3852280","RCE-402","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Maria Temmo [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769770569456809]*{color}:\nThank you! Will turn to them :pray:\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:56:21.773Z"],["3852282","DSR-4239","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T10:56:29.257Z"],["3852283","LSS-58352","LSS","natalia.szurnicka-dmoch@bolt.eu","Natalia Szurnicka-Dmoch","Thank you [~accountid:712020:62d2d09a-02e2-437d-abbd-86f5be2b5737] ! I closed all the resolved comments. The agreement can be shared with Novitus again [~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] - there are still few points for them to respond/accept.\n\n[~accountid:712020:62d2d09a-02e2-437d-abbd-86f5be2b5737] I don’t have any comments to Annex 5, we may proceed with signing it. I suggest you submit a separate ticket so that we can proceed straight to sining.","2026-01-30T10:56:30.957Z"],["3852286","PFI-838893","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","They can stay with both accounts, you can request deletion only in case they are no longer using it ","2026-01-30T10:56:48.635Z"],["3852287","CSDT-932","CSDT","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","Built and validated {{outsourced_support_case_metrics_v3}} table for outsource partner reporting.\n\n*Key design decisions:*\n\n* *Row-per-company pattern*: One row per {{(support_case_id, agent_company_handled)}} to support multi-tenant access control\n\n* *PII masking*: Agent details (email, name, team lead) are masked using {{IFF()}} conditions — each company only sees their own agents\n\n* *Metrics split*: Both total case metrics and company-specific (outsource) metrics included for benchmarking\n\n*Bug fix in v3:*\n\n* Fixed cross-product issue in {{case_handling_time}} and {{agent_replies}} CTEs\n\n* Added {{agent_company_handled}} to GROUP BY to prevent metric inflation when multiple companies work on the same case\n\n* Validated fix by comparing v2 vs v3 results\n\n*Columns included:*\n\n* Case attributes (timestamps, state, tier, vertical, language, etc.)\n\n* Agent info for: first solved, last solved, first response, CSAT agents\n\n* Handling time metrics (total + outsource-specific)\n\n* Agent replies metrics (total + outsource-specific)\n\n* CSAT and FRT SLO data\n\n\n\n*Tables created:*\n\n* {{dbt_roman_trohhalev.outsourced_support_case_metrics_v3}}\n\n*Next steps:*\n\n* Convert to dbt model","2026-01-30T10:56:55.172Z"],["3852291","MM-993","MM","eugene.lazutin@bolt.eu","Yauheni Lazutsin","Ideas: \n\nPlaybook editor is variant with Rentals data. Their config is more complex (discount, duration, target group distr.). Clicking each cell opens the modal window with the config form. \nThe second option is simpler, it has only a discount. In this case, we can use inline inputs without a modal.\n\nVertical and horizontal highlighting to help user read the data. Minimalistic data in a table to emphasise only important data and not overload UI with symbols.\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.08-20260129-141017.png|width=781,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.08-20260129-141017.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.24-20260129-141030.png|width=702,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.24-20260129-141030.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.34-20260129-141039.png|width=752,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.34-20260129-141039.png\"!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.41-20260129-141047.png|width=559,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-29 at 15.10.41-20260129-141047.png\"!","2026-01-30T10:57:44.422Z"],["3852292","WD-22717","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","If bolt technology ou is removed here WD allows recording the payment \n\n!image-20260130-105754.png|width=1076,alt=\"image-20260130-105754.png\"!\n\n\n\n\n\n!image-20260130-125938.png|width=692,alt=\"image-20260130-125938.png\"!\n\n\n\n!image-20260130-125956.png|width=692,alt=\"image-20260130-125956.png\"!\n\n!image-20260130-130019.png|width=692,alt=\"image-20260130-130019.png\"!\n\n!image-20260130-130037.png|width=692,alt=\"image-20260130-130037.png\"!","2026-01-30T10:57:57.633Z"],["3852295","LSS-62459","LSS","dammian.kivuva@bolt.eu","Dammian Kivuva","!image.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T10:58:22.635Z"],["3852303","RCE-402","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Divyansh Kumar [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769770778187449]*{color}:\nFound a related thread, [https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C04S1P7U4E7/p1762251799499419]. Maybe follow up in the same thread/channel\n\nLinked messages:\n[November 4th, 2025 2:23 AM] philipp.rokov: Hey team, we received a [ticket|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/660881499] from a [driver |https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/fleet/drivers/edit/7636767?tab=profile&amp;filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&amp;tz=Europe%2FZagreb]where he complains that he lost his SR on the 5th of Oct. by taking a look into this [look|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/36218?toggle=fil&amp;qid=0Z4cA3jmdUEMylPnRvkZu8] I can see that orders that counted towards unfulfilled are the following:\n• [28th of Jul|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2104899433/334?orderTryId=2610999195] - missed_scheduled_ride_go_online_deadline\n• [5th of Aug|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2108669911/334?orderTryId=2618211607] - missed_scheduled_ride_go_online_deadline\n• [4th of Oct|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/ride-hailing-order/orders/order/2195919469/334?orderTryId=2764493427] - scheduled_order_significantly_changed\n2 questions:\n• why was the last one counted as unfullfileed as the reason is scheduled_order_significantly_changed?\n• Even if these 3 were unfulfiled driver should get SR back as of 20th of Oct (28th of July + 12W)?\n{quote}","2026-01-30T10:59:54.298Z"],["3852304","CSDT-922","CSDT","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","I confirm that I have completed all points in this checklist during previous on-duty cycle.\nI independently handled incoming Jira Service Desk tickets, monitored and responded to requests in *#cs-looker*, applied the correct escalation paths when needed, and maintained SLA and communication standards throughout.\nI’m confident in covering the on-duty responsibilities reliably going forward","2026-01-30T11:00:05.646Z"],["3852306","PFI-839869","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! This is due to a new payout system that prevents the balance from going negative. Since the fleet had two cash orders on 12.01 before the payout was processed, the cash order commission was already deducted from the payout. This is intentional. If you have more questions about this system and how it works, kindly reach out to Partner Payments team. Thanks! ","2026-01-30T11:00:31.821Z"],["3852310","LSS-62460","LSS",null,"Automation for Jira","Thanks for your ticket! For the lucky ones with access to Flank-supported channels (#legal-agent-) — why not ask your legal AI assistant first on Slack — Flank might already have the answer.","2026-01-30T11:01:07.595Z"],["3852311","DBRE-8768","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","Resolved in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7478|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/SREDESK-7478|smart-link] / [https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5621|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5621].\n\nTime spent: 2h – research, PR review, testing.","2026-01-30T11:01:13.669Z"],["3852312","LSS-62460","LSS","alberta.gedzia@bolt.eu","Alberta Kafui Dziedzom Gedzia","[https://docs.google.com/document/d/15rPe4zJA9PwLArwgM9CcKKg0_NUVCHSWGKR1wxFZfKM/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/15rPe4zJA9PwLArwgM9CcKKg0_NUVCHSWGKR1wxFZfKM/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T11:01:18.630Z"],["3852314","RCE-401","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769770516355519]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-401 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T11:01:55.832Z"],["3852315","RCE-388","RCE","maksim.shashkov@bolt.eu","Max Shashkov","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Compliance triage [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C01PT0B6D70/p1769770908573649]*{color}:\nIssue RCE-388 successfully transitioned to state 'Done'.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T11:02:22.948Z"],["3852316","CSDT-931","CSDT","roman.trohhalev@bolt.eu","Roman Trohhalev","I have completed the review of the existing Supplier Looker folder and went through all legacy dashboards (Agent CSAT, Combined Deep Dives, First Interactions Deep Dive, etc).\n\nTried to build and replicate these reports using existing explores and identified missing metrics and data availability.\nI also mapped out the key metrics, filters, joins, and dashboard-level dependencies to understand how they connect to the underlying explores and views.","2026-01-30T11:03:03.194Z"],["3852317","WD-22735","WD","darja.netjaga@bolt.eu","Darja Netjaga","Have you tried to request  the access from here?\n\n!image-20260130-110036.png|width=630,alt=\"image-20260130-110036.png\"!\n\nKind regards,\n\nDarja Netjaga","2026-01-30T11:03:08.767Z"],["3852318","PFI-840697","PFI","elmar.agabeyov@bolt.eu","Elmar Agabeyov","[^Manual payout's W5 (file 3).csv]","2026-01-30T11:03:20.257Z"],["3852320","RISK2-3305","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*27.01. Shared with LG*","2026-01-30T11:03:47.501Z"],["3852328","PFI-840700","PFI","viktorija.valinskaite@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktorija Valinskaitė","!Screenshot_20260130_085205_Bolt.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T11:04:58.414Z"],["3852329","LSS-56386","LSS","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","hey! [~accountid:712020:663f2145-dfc6-459e-9619-14aca983f77c] we got the answer from Lidl\n\n\n\nAgata,\n\nwith reference to the ongoing discussions regarding the campaign carried out under the Benefit Plus Partner Program, I would like to clarify the matter of the contract effective date and the resulting implications for the order documentation.\n\nIn line with the parties’ arrangements and the course of cooperation, *the agreement was concluded and became effective on 5 December 2025*. As of that date, there was a mutual and consistent intent of the parties as to the terms of cooperation, and the campaign was in fact executed starting from mid-December. The electronic signatures applied later — including the signature dated 30 December 2025 — were of a purely formal nature and served only to confirm arrangements that had already been agreed and were being performed.\n\nFrom a legal perspective:\n\n* the agreement could be validly concluded also in an implied manner (Article 60 of the Polish Civil Code),\n* the actual performance of the services and operational correspondence constitute clear evidence that the agreement was effective as of 5 December 2025,\n* the electronic signatures merely recorded and formalised an arrangement that was already binding.\n\nFor this reason, *the order must refer exclusively to 5 December 2025 as the contract conclusion date*, and no reference should be made in any documents to the date of 30 December 2025, as this would hinder the ability to demonstrate that the agreement was binding earlier and would complicate the proper settlement of the cooperation (including barter settlement).\n\nAt the same time, I would like to address your proposal to remove certain marketing services from the order. In our view, the non-performance of these services is not a fair situation — approximately 1.5 months were allocated for their execution, and Lidl has fulfilled all of its marketing obligations towards Bolt. However, we understand that due to the campaign nearing its end, there is no longer a realistic opportunity to make up for these activities. Therefore, we may agree to remove these provisions from the order *provided that the annex confirming the correct effective date of the agreement is signed promptly*.\n\nThe annex will be prepared today by Lidl’s legal counsel. It will be forwarded to Bolt next week via Nais (either by myself or by Tomasz Masal). Its key provision will be as follows:\n\n“The Parties confirm that the cooperation between them was established and performed as of 5 December 2025, and that this Agreement constitutes a written confirmation and record of the cooperation terms agreed earlier. The Agreement shall be effective as of 5 December 2025.”\n\nOur objective is to close this matter in a legally secure and transparent manner for both parties. We count on your cooperation and the swift execution of the annex, which will allow us to properly finalise the documentation and settlement of the campaign.\n\nPlease feel free to contact me should you have any questions.","2026-01-30T11:05:14.768Z"],["3852330","LSS-29559","LSS","maja.matuszak@bolt.eu","Maja Matuszak","Hi, here are the screenshots of all the internal communication between me and accounting, before I sent BTH a demand for payment, when I was confirming I stayed in touch with them, and they were promising a refund\n\n[https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1tRpXityQTkT3tPF3KIvEC4_ltrgFZUaQ|https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1tRpXityQTkT3tPF3KIvEC4_ltrgFZUaQ|smart-link] \nTo have it all in one place, what has already been confirmed with Jolanta: \n\n* We became aware of the incorrect transfer only on May 29, 2023, i.e. more than a year after the incident. Moreover, during telephone conversations, BTH repeatedly assured us throughout 2023 that a refund would be issued. *We want to try to use this as an argument that the claim has not become time-barred.*\n* During a telephone conversation (which is also confirmed by the screenshot), BTH informed me that the matter was being handled by their accountant, who was considering how to execute the transfer correctly in order to avoid any tax consequences. *If possible, we may attempt to use this accountant as a witness in the case.*\n* Unfortunately, I do not have access to SMS or call billing records, as my mobile operator is only able to retrieve them for up to one year retrospectively. For earlier periods, obtaining such records may be possible only upon a court order. Now, I am the only witness to the conversations between myself and BTH, which is corroborated by the conversations attached as screenshots.\n\n","2026-01-30T11:05:43.636Z"],["3852331","LSS-29559","LSS","maja.matuszak@bolt.eu","Maja Matuszak","[~accountid:712020:b971e044-987e-4f04-8fbe-2c3b651e5a0f] ","2026-01-30T11:05:53.541Z"],["3852334","PFI-839469","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Let me know if you can access this Looker view: [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/24690?toggle=fil&qid=Eyg0I7lA83KuAN0uFXGvVy|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/24690?toggle=fil&qid=Eyg0I7lA83KuAN0uFXGvVy]\n\n\n\nThis should have the balances. ","2026-01-30T11:06:23.060Z"],["3852337","PFI-830479","PFI","karan.gaikwad@bolt.eu","Karan Rajesh Gaikwad","Raised this with the bank again !","2026-01-30T11:06:59.841Z"],["3852339","MLC-3906","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 5*\n\n* *Context of the project/initiative:* Multiple initiatives to support the expansion and growth of the Bolt Plus membership.\n* *Status / Milestone:*\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n** *Uplift validation: Experiment on Plus-ready modals*\n*** [+Confluence page+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/7018905601/2025-11+Bolt+Plus+Plus-ready+modal+experiment]\n*** *Status:* {color:#36B37E}*[ EXPERIMENT RUNNING ]*{color}, {color:#ff5630}*relaunched*{color}\n*** *New tentative ETA:* February / mid-March\n*** *Context:* There was a misalignment within MarTech on the experiment setup, which resulted in the modal being shown to significantly fewer users than expected and needed to draw conclusions.\n** *Hopp Plus launch*\n*** *Ad-hoc template*\n**** Changes required, [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] informed \n**** *Jira task:* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4026|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4026|smart-link] \n*** *Automations*\n**** *Jira task:* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4035|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4035|smart-link] \n**** All of the necessary info added to the sub-task for Nida (/) \n** *Annual discount*\n*** *Update:* We’ll support additional testing with ad-hoc comms\n*** *Potential markets:* SE, RO\n*** *Timeline:* TBC\n*** *Further data and input from Growth:* [+Slack thread+|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C0A2VPCAHS9/p1769176188060459?thread_ts=1768222206.249989&cid=C0A2VPCAHS9]\n** *NZ priorit pickup launch (ad-hoc)*\n*** Coordinated by Vertical Marketing, supported by [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] with my help\n*** *Jira task:* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4106|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4106|smart-link] \n*** *Channels:* push, modal\n*** *Target groups:* members, non-members\n*Annual discount*\n** *Bi-weekly synch with Vertical Marketing*\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Hopp Plus launch*\n*** Align with [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] on setting up the automated comms.\n*** Test 1—2 events once the comms are set up (just to ensure everything’s correctly triggered).\n*** Share the ad-hoc comms setup with Vertical Marketing once the visuals are finalised.\n*** Start setting up in-app comms.\n** *Uplift validation: Experiment on Plus-ready modals*\n*** Keep an eye on the enrolments.\n** *Quality improvements: Churn flow*\n*** Go through the copies written by the Content team (deadline for them: 4 February)","2026-01-30T11:07:18.539Z"],["3852340","DINE-989","DINE","simona.andries@bolt.eu","Simona Andries","Issue should be fixed now. Customer wil be prompted to the payments screen, to select a payment method.","2026-01-30T11:07:35.856Z"],["3852341","XP-3039","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","h2. Results [[PR|https://github.com/bolteu/data-experimentation/pull/1120]]\n\nImplemented the V4.1 flows architecture using *Template + Factory + Strategy* pattern with stateless stages.\n\nHere is a [+Databricks notebook+|https://bolt-datascience.cloud.databricks.com/editor/notebooks/3599265223934881?o=3829506390716583] with some *use cases and examples* (do not mistake it for ABU as ABU will use the provide functionality inside).\n\nh3. Changes\n\n*Core (*{{v4/flows/core/}}*)*\n\n* {{Flow}} - Template method orchestrating 3 stages: activity → aggregation → write\n* {{FlowFactory}} - Factory methods for pre-configured flows ({{targeting_user}}, {{calculator}})\n* {{protocols.py}} - Strategy interfaces for all components\n\n*Models (*{{v4/flows/models/}}*)*\n\n* {{FlowContext}} - Immutable Pydantic config passed through stages\n* {{stage_artifacts.py}} - Immutable stage results ({{ActivityStageResult}}, {{AggregationStageResult}})\n* {{semantic.py}} - YAML artifact models ({{EnrollmentArtifact}}, {{TableSource}})\n\n*Strategies (*{{v4/flows/strategies/}}*)*\n\n* {{TargetingEnrollmentBuilder}} - Dynamic YAML artifact loading with context-based filtering\n* {{TargetingActivityComposer}} - Vertical join pattern + enrichment pipeline\n* {{TargetingAggregationBuilder}} - SQL generation with capping/CUPED support\n* {{ScorecardArtifactWriter}}, {{CalculatorResultWriter}} - Result output\n* {{CappingActivityEnrichment}}, {{DSTSlicerEnrichment}} - Activity enrichments","2026-01-30T11:07:46.454Z"],["3852343","PFI-840652","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:08:09.097Z"],["3852344","HS-29557","HS","kerilin.mand@bolt.eu","Kerilin Mänd","Confirming salary info as it is not changing with the position change ","2026-01-30T11:09:03.356Z"],["3852348","WFM-10177","WFM","viktoriia.mazanik@bolt-outsource.eu","Viktoriia Mazanik","Hi [~accountid:5b31360d7b8c14625a47e4f5] is there any updates on the permission access?\n\n","2026-01-30T11:09:53.197Z"],["3852350","RISK2-3262","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*30.01 Control Effectiveness Score & how it affects residual risk*\n\n[@Sujith|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03UQBS230B] and[ @Bobby|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/team/U03UQEYULF4] please see the proposed formula outlining how to set up the logic. Could you also let us know what you have seen as the market standard so far, and how other companies typically manage this calculation?\n\nControl Effectiveness formula: *Residual likelihood* of a risk should equal the *inherent likelihood* minus the *Control Effectiveness* of the MAX control:\n\n* A reduction of 0 for control effectiveness 1–2,\n* A reduction of 1 for control effectiveness 3\n* A reduction of 2 for control effectiveness 4\n* A reduction of 3 for control effectiveness 5\n* The Residual likelihood should have a MIN of 1.\n\n*Final result:*\n\n* *Residual likelihood = maximum(1, inherent likelihood − maximum(0, control effectiveness − 2)).*","2026-01-30T11:10:18.141Z"],["3852352","FDBT-4891","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2 fails on 2026-01-30 10:33:10.158135+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task execute failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'SystemExit: 11', 'run_id': 1075390652383242, 'task_key': 'execute'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_pigment_aggregation_integration_v2/grid?dag_run_id=manual__2026-01-30T10%3A33%3A10.158135%2B00%3A00&task_id=finance_model_ledger_aggr_pigment.finance_model_ledger_aggr_pigment&base_date=2026-01-30T10%3A33%3A10.158135%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-30T11:11:22.052Z"],["3852353","CRC-2332","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Business: LHV VAs testing in progress","2026-01-30T11:11:23.239Z"],["3852354","PFI-840603","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Please reach out to customer payments team for this. Thanks! ","2026-01-30T11:11:28.457Z"],["3852355","CRC-2337","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Citi account opening in progress for Rides collection","2026-01-30T11:11:32.013Z"],["3852356","PFI-840700","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nNew cards must be used for a personal ride before they can be added to your Family Profile. Kindly advise the user to take a ride with this card first, then try again.","2026-01-30T11:11:35.771Z"],["3852357","PFI-840603","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting this ticket!\n\nLooks like you've selected invalid Request Type which isn't handled by this team. Create a new ticket for the correct team! 🚗\n\nPayments\n- [Customer Payments] Driver/Fleet payment didn't reflect : https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/311\n- [Partner Payments] Manual payout request to Payments team: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/432\n- [Partner Payments] Driver/Fleet payout issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/312\n- [Customer Payments] Rider payment/charge issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/307\n\nTech Support\n- Driver/Fleet Campaign and Bonus issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/597\n- Driver app/backend/earning screen issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66\n- Rider app/backend issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/103\n- Wrong price calculation for the order: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/2/group/66/create/354\n\nFraud\n- Fraud related issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57/create/308\n\nBilling\n- Driver/Fleet Balance Disputes: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet Invoicing and Reports Disputes:https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/57\n- Driver/Fleet/Rider Fiscalization (e.g. Missing QR, SAF-T) issues: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/5247\n- Commission Changes, invoice issuer changes, feature requests, general configurations: https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/61/create/301\n\nCheers\nCommerce Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T11:11:38.144Z"],["3852359","CRC-2313","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Waiting local team to share bank formats for payment initiation","2026-01-30T11:11:46.932Z"],["3852361","XP-2343","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","[~accountid:712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] It is relevant, but it has to be moved to the new [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/XP-3058|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/XP-3058|smart-link] epic.","2026-01-30T11:12:22.641Z"],["3852363","CRC-2316","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] Payout testing blocked due to Citi error. Franchise teem to contact Citi","2026-01-30T11:12:56.774Z"],["3852364","RISK2-3194","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*28.01. Update - internal meeting, needs alignment internally*\n\nReduce: will lead to the user logging an Action\n\nAccept: will lead to the user logging an Acceptance justification (i.e fill out a text box for justifying the decision to accept the risk)\n\nTransfer: will lead to the user filling out two text box fields:  Which entity/to whom will the risk be transferred to? and Justification  (i.e fill out a description box to explain why the risk is being transferred)\n\nAvoid: will lead to the user filling out a Description  (i.e fill out the description box of how the activity causing the risk has been stopped or discontinued) and a non-mandatory Evidence Upload field to document that the activity was stopped.","2026-01-30T11:13:18.179Z"],["3852365","MLC-186","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 5*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* Dropping email Open Rates\n* *Status update:*\n** *26Q1 planning*\n*** Reviewing the plan with [~accountid:6270f0bd807e0000691b79bb] \n** *Testing the email builder + first email template*\n*** Monitoring the A/B tests (old non-storytelling template vs. optimised storytelling).\n*** Logging the results and deep-diving into data to understand all of the trends.\n*** *Overall result:*\n**** *The old non-storytelling template and the optimised storytelling template are performing at the same level across all markets where we tested.* With an optimised storytelling template slightly ahead.\n**** Given these are the highest-volume comms we tested on + we rolled back these templates in December (meaning, OR also recovered), it looks promising.\n**** We’re seeing some odd patterns in a few of the other tests (i.e. not User Campaigns). In some cases, both A/B versions are below the benchmark, and in one case, the old non-storytelling template OR looks unusually low.\n***** Assumption: This is more likely a negative impact the initial storytelling HTML caused, not an inbox issue.\n*** *Next steps:*\n**** Move forward with implementing the template in one non-incentive use case (Airport Fares).\n**** Once it's rolled out, we'll continue closely monitoring the numbers to ensure things are moving in the right direction.\n** *Localisation estimations*\n*** Finalising the initial calculations → aligning within the team on the logic and potential effort.\n**** [File|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1GfYwSJnFNffjyWe0j6Mh799FFASBWHL2UMtd5gBRn8A/edit?gid=706459080#gid=706459080]\n** *Converting copies with Poe*\n*** Converting the next batch of copies (higher-volume use cases) to convert all of our comms to the storytelling format.\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Rolling out the first use case (Airport Fares)*\n*** Monitor the progress and data, support the team with QA.\n** *Converting the copies with Poe*\n*** Aiming to finalise, including finishing up with the QA.","2026-01-30T11:13:35.177Z"],["3852366","LSS-62461","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","[~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] can you please look into this one?","2026-01-30T11:13:48.558Z"],["3852367","CRC-2395","CRC","jaak.kaljula@bolt.eu","Jaak Kaljula","[update] No progress due to engineering unavailability. Payout flow (including AML checks) to be tested next week","2026-01-30T11:13:54.593Z"],["3852368","DMC-384","DMC","razvan.nastase@bolt.eu","Răzvan Năstase","cc. [~accountid:5d15daceb8c82e0c0ff146c9]  - task that we just discussed during the meeting.","2026-01-30T11:13:55.176Z"],["3852371","PAW-15295","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-30T11:15:09.060Z"],["3852372","PFI-828407","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-30T11:15:15.137Z"],["3852374","DO-5834","DO","kaarel.nummert@bolt.eu","Kaarel Nummert","{quote}Is there any way to prevent duplication of these fields?{quote}\n\nYes, define a unique key for the data lake table. The reason I copied the backfillability comment is that it looks like the table was intentionally configured without a unique key to have it serve as an event log of all updates/versions of the source table’s rows. Unfortunately, I don’t know if anyone is still relying on this setup.\n\n\n\n{quote}Also, is there any way to cleanup these duplicate entries?{quote}\n\nYes, once the unique key is defined, I can deduplicate the existing records.","2026-01-30T11:15:52.651Z"],["3852375","WFM-10203","WFM","artur.naago@bolt.eu","Artur Näägo","Hello [~accountid:61d2a784e763790068e85541]!\r\n\r\nQueues assigned.\r\n\r\nHave a nice day,\r\nArtur","2026-01-30T11:15:58.580Z"],["3852376","RISK2-3240","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","we will not inherit the description, as it technically is not possible. ","2026-01-30T11:16:10.265Z"],["3852379","PFI-838733","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","I will discuss with the Tax Team, whether we have to issue Invoice Payment Receipt in such case and if we have to than it will take some development time to do so.","2026-01-30T11:16:25.711Z"],["3852380","LSS-60958","LSS","estelle.herbiet@bolt.eu","Estelle Herbiet","Hi [~accountid:712020:d74efb91-e36e-4885-b4a9-d3e39fa06548] , thanks for the update. Could you please clarify which measures have been taken? The account [+189319811+|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/189319811/overview] is still not archived, from what I can see.","2026-01-30T11:16:31.652Z"],["3852381","PFI-827557","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-30T11:17:04.784Z"],["3852383","PFI-840679","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nWe do not have access to issue refund to Bolt balance. There is a possibility to issue a refund from our end but there has to be an existing card payment and the refund amount should be the full amount, we can’t complete partial refunds to card from our end.","2026-01-30T11:18:13.064Z"],["3852386","LSS-58941","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*UPDATE (30.01)*+\n\n* Tat/Lev/Ema have been asked about what the rider verification flow looks like (re biometric consents) [here|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C07S3ULEKBQ/p1769771742730789].\n* If biometric flow is missing, I should talk to Mikk Vachtmeister (PM) to ask to bring it back.\n** Gab believes that the original advice was just to trigger normal rider verification for WfW (include biometric consent flow), and then add gender field extraction on top. Gab said she will find the ticket - “_Likely that we advised separate flow, but Product wanted to use the same flow / tie it to safety_”.","2026-01-30T11:18:50.942Z"],["3852387","PFI-840110","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hello [~accountid:712020:aa9c35d8-f4bc-43fd-80fd-584fe896e9f8],\n\nThank you for the escalation. Given some of the fraud rules we have in place - seems like some of these suspicious requests does not pass anyway. I will have another look if we can find more suspicious activity around these users. Thank you.\n\nBest Regards,\nNigar Alizada","2026-01-30T11:18:53.621Z"],["3852388","PFI-826688","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Duplicate ticket for [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-830043|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/PFI-830043|smart-link]  \nClosing this one.","2026-01-30T11:18:56.858Z"],["3852390","PFI-840287","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","I think local ops may be the best case scenario, but I briefly checked before and neither of the people who applied/approved the adjustment work at Bolt anymore, so idk what the chances are that anyone knows/remembers. ","2026-01-30T11:19:21.222Z"],["3852394","HS-29577","HS","adam.graffy@bolt.eu","Adam Graffy","[^Stadt.pdf]","2026-01-30T11:20:26.100Z"],["3852395","PFI-840678","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nCould you confirm if this is the correct user ID? The account attached here is a Ukrainian one where the charges are made in UAH.","2026-01-30T11:20:35.111Z"],["3852396","PFI-839419","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Do they want to enter company details into the work profile? The rider does not need to indicate that, the VAT liability is based on the seller. ","2026-01-30T11:20:50.631Z"],["3852399","PFI-840676","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","\n\n\n\nHello Team!\n\nI completely understand why this might look like a double charge, but I can assure you that the user was only charged once. This is a common part of how card payments are processed. Here's what happens:\n\n# When the user first makes a payment, the bank temporarily ‘reserves' the funds and this is just the bank setting aside the amount for the transaction. The user’s account balance might show less amount but the payment hasn’t actually been taken out by the bank yet.\n# Later, when the payment is fully processed, that reserved amount is now “officially” debited from the user’s account. At that point, some banks send a second notification, which can make it seem like a second charge.\n\n\nThe refund is successfully completed. I would advise the user to check their final account balance or statement, where they can confirm that only one payment was actually withdrawn. The earlier “pending” amount will either drop off or convert into the final charge.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:21:50.417Z"],["3852400","DO-5842","DO","przemyslaw.gumula@bolt.eu","Przemysław Gumuła","Hi! It’s already the case. Is there a problem?","2026-01-30T11:21:54.456Z"],["3852401","LSS-60621","LSS","tom.bishop@bolt.eu","Tom Bishop","Thanks Julia. Requested access to do the doc, but are you saying we’re good to proceed with the changes you’ve made? Your first sentence says otherwise! If we’re not:\n\n11.1 - can we have it better distinguished between the type of software the type of rides that are intermediated?\nWith Bolt it is our own marketplace. With GS they operate a marketplace of companies with owned and operated rides.\n\n11.2 - i had agreed with them that we are in the US in ride hailing and will inform them if we go into the black car/chauffeur space in the US. They agreed.\n\n11.3 Agreed\n\n11.4 Agreed\n\nAddendum - will review","2026-01-30T11:22:02.760Z"],["3852402","L10N-31106","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31104](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31104)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-30T11:22:20.907Z"],["3852403","L10N-31108","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31104](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31104)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-30T11:22:22.278Z"],["3852404","L10N-31110","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31104](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31104)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-30T11:22:23.089Z"],["3852405","L10