vahl@bolt.eu","Kristi Liina Vahl","Waiting for PQ.","2026-01-30T11:22:36.699Z"],["3852412","MLC-2432","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 5*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n** Mapping LCM-stage level coverage status (/) \n** Mapping market-level coverage status (/) \n** [Confluence page|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MP/pages/6726254599/Rider+Lifecycle+communication+coverage+analysis+and+action+items]\n*** Focus areas:\n**** Top 10 GMV markets first. Also went through other higher-importance markets (GMV-prio) with coverage needs improvement.\n**** Activation and Never Active communications (both currently under Activation in Rider LCM): the highest-priority segment for us due to the lowest coverage\n** Support-task for [~accountid:712020:07449b81-9129-47a7-bd23-f01775b97cff] created: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4110|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/MLC-4110|smart-link] \n*** Doing a QA to the plan on Monday, after which Nida can proceed with setting live missing automated communications.\n*** Also, comparing MoM trends for additional validation.\n* *Next steps:*\n** *Setting live missing automations:* Assigning more specific sub-tasks to Nida + assisting with prios.\n** *Sync with* [~accountid:628b4f089c617b006a6c6efb]*:* Aligning on projects with the shared goal + action items.\n** *Further investigation:* \n*** Potential flow optimisations\n*** Technical reasons for low coverage\n*** Potential new communications + channels\n** *Clarity updates:* Update Jira with clear deliverables and potential timelines","2026-01-30T11:22:39.846Z"],["3852417","RNP-242","RNP","nikita.popov@bolt.eu","Nikita Popov","[~accountid:610279a2ec92ab00707f6b23] Thank you for looking into it! No worries about a blocker. I’m not expecting expo updates to freeze an app because this is at least a part of an expo itself and didn’t do any restarts on arriving to device. So it’s flow is a bit different than what you did with app restart from admin panel.","2026-01-30T11:23:34.986Z"],["3852419","FDBT-4885","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-30T11:24:03.486Z"],["3852422","PFI-839297","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","სალამი,  \n\n  \n\n[@Mira Tsotsoria|mailto:MiTsotsoria@Tbcbank.ge] როგორ მოვიქცეთ ? მომხმარებელი ელოდება უკუკავშირს \n\n   \n\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *პატივისცემით*{color}* \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *Sincerely*{color}* \n{color:#0093D3}{color}\n----\n{color:#0093D3}{color}  \n\n *{color:#0093D3} *მზიკო დანელია*{color}**{color:#0093D3} */*{color}*  *{color:#0093D3} *Mziko Danelia*{color}* \n\n{color:#1F497D}ბარათების{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}მენეჯერი{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color} {color:#1F497D}Card Manager{color} \n\n{color:#1F497D}მომხმარებელთა{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}მხარდაჭერის{color}{color:#1F497D}{color} {color:#1F497D}განყოფილება{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color} {color:#1F497D}Customer Support Department{color}{color:#595959}{color}{color:#2F5496}{color} \n\n  \n\n  \n\n *{color:#333399} *Tel:*{color}* {color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 27 27 37 (*4){color} \n\n *{color:#333399} *Fax:*{color}* {color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 77 27 74{color} \n\n[{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}|https://urldefense.com/v3/__http:/www.tbcbank.ge/__;!\\!P1qVsL2A!JjZp3RvKmPyFPpMib2WSUCp6PkWNjFswW63tExjK8iJPWNwDfHIlD8kZT1rjOdXXWJZHtiNk2GquYRKhfMLnN1yk4Lcm6hI$] \n\n  \n\n!image001.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T11:24:25.700Z"],["3852423","PFI-837559","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hi! Seems like the driver profile is incomplete 8probably missing an address). Please reach out to local ops to have them add it and resend the invoices to fiscalization.","2026-01-30T11:24:32.117Z"],["3852424","PFI-840706","PFI","elvira.jamalova@bolt.eu","Elvira Camalova Seyidbayli","!p1.jpg|thumbnail!\n\n!p2.jpg|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T11:24:32.560Z"],["3852426","WAVE-256","WAVE","artur.luik@bolt.eu","Artur Luik","Provided answers to Kaakrel Kook, so he can polish it for PR","2026-01-30T11:25:15.480Z"],["3852427","RNP-242","RNP","tanel.koha@bolt.eu","Tanel Koha","[~accountid:62e147f78cc02d0b34bd89a4] Well, the reason I’m making note of this is that while working on this, I learned that both Expo’s own restart mechanism and Expo Update’s specific restart mechanism caused the freeze 😄\n\nMy worry is whether Expo Updates uses that mechanism as it applies patches 🤔 \n\nBut if it doesn’t, then we are OK.","2026-01-30T11:25:15.945Z"],["3852430","PFI-826667","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Made and exception here and credited the funds to courier account instead of returning them. ","2026-01-30T11:25:47.466Z"],["3852433","PFI-839297","PFI","support@flitt.com","support@flitt.com","<\\!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN\"> \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nგამარჯობა,\n\nრით შეგვიძლია დაგეხმაროთ?\n\nპატივისცემით,\n\nNino Pachulia\n\n{color:#1d1c1d}Support Specialist{color}\n\n\n\n{color:#222222}+995 325 00 01 02{color}\n\n[npachulia@flitt.com|mailto:npachulia@flitt.com] | [LinkedIn|https://www.linkedin.com/in/nino-pachulia/] | [www.flitt.com|https://flitt.com/]{color:#202124}{color}{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n\n\n!https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdesUJg1p54UqXLenrFQFanpvXuj_umTqEFnw1W5JR9LBf8O3m6bGImWLGpg2ulKBMgaF3p6b25v6bmXHIHIZutpHE-jvRov39TlA4JBIsOA1TnvQv9Hi1Pl6DSaGos3E_cDDVNa_WgN0NWjc5AHd9dzQAW?key=gAVmix1twk-tFXoz-xQXqA!{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n---- on Fri, 30 Jan 2026 15:25:06 +0400  *\"pfi\"<pfi@taxify.atlassian.net>*  wrote ---- \n\n\n{quote}\n\n\n\n{color:#333333}{color}{color:#999999} —-—-—-—{color} {color:#333333}\n{color}{color:#999999} Reply above this line.{color} {color:#333333}\n\n\nchargeback_reports commented:\n\nსალამი,{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}@Mira Tsotsoria{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.netmailto:MiTsotsoria@Tbcbank.ge]{color:#333333} როგორ მოვიქცეთ ? მომხმარებელი ელოდება უკუკავშირს\n\n {color}{color:#0093D3} *პატივისცემით*{color}{color:#333333} \n\n {color}{color:#0093D3} *Sincerely*{color}{color:#333333} \n{color}\n----\n{color:#333333} \n\n\n\n {color}{color:#0093D3} *მზიკო დანელია*{color}{color:#333333}  {color}{color:#0093D3} */*{color}{color:#333333}   {color}{color:#0093D3} *Mziko Danelia*{color}{color:#333333} \n\n{color}{color:#1F497D}ბარათების{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#1F497D}მენეჯერი{color}{color:#333333}{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#1F497D}Card Manager{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#1F497D}მომხმარებელთა{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#1F497D}მხარდაჭერის{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#1F497D}განყოფილება{color}{color:#333333}{color}{color:#1F497D} /{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#1F497D}Customer Support Department{color}{color:#333333}\n\n {color}{color:#333399} *Tel:*{color}{color:#333333}  {color}{color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 27 27 37 (*4){color}{color:#333333}\n\n {color}{color:#333399} *Fax:*{color}{color:#333333}  {color}{color:#333399}+(995 32) 2 77 27 74{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#333333}{color}|https://urldefense.com/v3/__http:/www.tbcbank.ge/__;!\\!P1qVsL2A!JjZp3RvKmPyFPpMib2WSUCp6PkWNjFswW63tExjK8iJPWNwDfHIlD8kZT1rjOdXXWJZHtiNk2GquYRKhfMLnN1yk4Lcm6hI$]{color:#333333}{color}\n\n{color:#333333}{color} !1769772384126000_1933234790.png|thumbnail!{color:#333333}  <[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/request/3024810/attachment/1125336]>{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}View request{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-839297?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjBlMGM4NmIxOTdhYmI0NjhkNTZmNmNjMTU2OTcxOTVlZWVkNmJhYWVhODIyMTVlMzJjZjhhOTRmNWIyNTc1OGEiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNTM4MDYiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IlBGSS04MzkyOTcifSwiZXhwIjoxNzcyMTkxNTA1LCJpYXQiOjE3Njk3NzIzMDV9.qOCPWVYQZdJG5LDcazzlDdZsJQcuAQh7uBdt3h4kGw8&sda_source=notification-email]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333} ·{color} [{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}Turn off this request's notifications{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-839297/unsubscribe?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..wMIEs_Y39X3KYtT5GI10kzfgpd4xj_Kcwk0v75e6vAg]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#707070}This is shared with chargeback_reports, Joel Süldre, and{color} [{color:#707070}support@flitt.com{color}|mailto:support@flitt.com]{color:#707070}.{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#707070}Powered by Jira Service Management{color}|https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira/service-desk/powered-by?utm_medium=jira-in-product&utm_source=jira_service_desk_email_footer&utm_content=taxify]{color:#707070}{color}{color:#333333}\n Sent on January 30, 2026 1:25:05 PM EET{color} \n!http://usw2-track.atlassian.com/CI0/0101019c0ea651ab-b0096296-df55-4825-aa85-9e5a10e2bf54-000000/1CxNUQ5MDIWXrsOBQvuAKVmckiwEv7ZI0hoR3xgFAGY=442!{color:#333333}{color} {quote}","2026-01-30T11:26:34.327Z"],["3852434","FX-3767","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769772391068399]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@chantel.rowe>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3767] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T11:26:45.230Z"],["3852435","FX-3767","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*Chantel Rowe [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769772402029799]*{color}:\n\n\nLinked files:\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 13.25.02.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ACTL8RB32/screenshot_2026-01-30_at_13.25.02.png]\n\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 13.25.12.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ABXA1Q8NS/screenshot_2026-01-30_at_13.25.12.png]\n\n* [Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 13.26.30.png|https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T049H2DT1QQ-F0ABXA2T08N/screenshot_2026-01-30_at_13.26.30.png]\n{quote}","2026-01-30T11:26:55.896Z"],["3852436","MP-2916","MP","mirkamal.gasimov@bolt.eu","Mirkamal Gasimov","Actually, I think there is no need to reset dark mode after a logout. iOS does not do it either. So I removed the theme cleanup logic in my [pr|https://github.com/bolteu/android-app-client/pull/17943] [~accountid:6401d565314f508813822b2e] fyi","2026-01-30T11:26:57.199Z"],["3852437","HS-29478","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-30T11:27:05.492Z"],["3852440","XP-2344","XP","yaroslav.morozevych@bolt.eu","Yaroslav Morozevych","[~accountid:712020:3f46b943-bb22-4289-83f6-326f708a1f24] For now, the lowest priority. We can decide if we want or don’t want to do it closer to the full v3 deprecation.","2026-01-30T11:27:33.691Z"],["3852441","BDB-1593","BDB","britt.peet@bolt.eu","Bo Britt Peet","[~accountid:621fa8978a4bb60068f1fe09] [Link to tab NO Oslo Airport 20.02|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1lehHeLxczVkTW5xDbqeL0_cWnsS1g4DHp8UdQK2kMl8/edit?gid=1106086052#gid=1106086052]","2026-01-30T11:28:01.303Z"],["3852443","INT-880","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-30T11:28:22.182Z"],["3852444","LSS-62456","LSS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","# Share a copy of the current draft of the Special Terms\n# Contracting entity here will be Bolt Operations OU. Same as contracting entity for Platform Services Agreement.\n# If the team can configure daily payment option it is preferable to do this and it guarantees payment (reduces Naivas exposure) with the option to Naivas to go offline if daily payments are not made at the designated time each day and to terminate if there is repeated failure by Bolt to make payments on time at least [x] times in a quarter.  ","2026-01-30T11:28:58.005Z"],["3852445","PFI-829457","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","This case is different, yes we do manage matching payments in no-client state as well in addition to the other topics I shared.\nIn this case, the payment was allocated correctly to their balance already, so there is no other option for us - it is either matched to client balance or not.  ","2026-01-30T11:29:03.960Z"],["3852446","PFI-840539","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-30T11:29:05.105Z"],["3852450","LSS-62441","LSS","thiago.delbel@bolt.eu","Thiago Del Bel","Hi [~accountid:712020:7f47c2af-14e1-4206-a795-ac87cb906276] , I hope you’re well.\n\nI read the POAs and the legal acts referred to in them and they seem indeed pretty standard for customs agents to carry out customs duties and activities on behalf of importers/exporters.\n\nHowever, since these are your markets (NO and SE), I’d like to check with you if there are any objections or points of attention before Bolt signs the POAs.\n\nThank you!\n\nThiago","2026-01-30T11:29:51.426Z"],["3852452","HS-29480","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:9d22087b-9bd3-42c9-944c-2112fcfa004e],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-30T11:30:16.570Z"],["3852453","LSS-61798","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[^20250121 CoR39 Certificate Director Amendments.pdf]\n[^COR44 Auditor Changes.pdf]\n\n[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] ","2026-01-30T11:30:26.417Z"],["3852455","MLC-3683","MLC","mariann.kapanen@bolt.eu","Mariann Kapanen","h3. *Week 5*\n\n* *Status / Milestone:* in progress\n* *Blockers:*\n* *Status update:*\n** *Aligning with Growth:* Got in touch to understand how we can validate the users we’ll re-enrol to incentive emails will be enrolled to incentives.\n*** *Status:* Waiting for their reply\n** *Person ID and duplicated accounts*\n*** Looked into the definition of person ID logic they shared with us, and whether it could be useful for us in any way.\n*** In short, not something for us → it helps them *not* to re-enrol existing users to _signup_ discounts again (a fraud scheme many use), but in LCM, we shouldn’t block new signups in any way and rely more on activity.\n*** [Confluence page|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4825547095/2024-01+-+Person+ID+-+DS+Design+Document#Executive-Summary]\n** *Next steps:*\n*** *Following up with Growth*\n*** *Planning the experiment* based on their input to launch this as soon as possible.","2026-01-30T11:31:07.393Z"],["3852456","PFI-840532","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nUnfairly, we can’t provide a bank account information to the customer to make a transfer to clear the debt. Kindly advise the user to ensure there are no restrictions on their payment method with their bank and retry completing the payment via the App.","2026-01-30T11:31:26.371Z"],["3852457","PFI-840241","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hello [~accountid:712020:b7055121-ece8-42fc-9500-0c6f8cb7256b],\n\nWe have not initially rejecting the log in requests, but started to reject once the courier reached a certain threshold of OTP volume. Lately this has been issue in LV market - couriers log out and log back in too often leading to this problem. \n\nWe did whitelist this number but please inform the courier that such frequent log outs/in might still lead a same issue. Thank you.\n\nBest Regards,\nNigar Alizada ","2026-01-30T11:31:28.824Z"],["3852458","FX-3768","FX","meruzhan.kerobyan@bolt.eu","Meruzhan Kerobyan","^#sync^ {quote}\n{color:red}*FleetX reports [wrote|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/C02FP2YL06L/p1769772692641329]*{color}:\nThank you for the report, <@uns>!\n\nOur team duty champion will review [your request|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/FX-3768] soon.\n{quote}","2026-01-30T11:31:44.567Z"],["3852459","LSS-60621","LSS","tom.bishop@bolt.eu","Tom Bishop","Addendum is fine by me. I’ll look to push down the booking costs, but let’s get this over the line and do that after","2026-01-30T11:32:04.674Z"],["3852460","PAW-15300","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-30T11:32:09.594Z"],["3852461","PAW-15299","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-30T11:32:11.821Z"],["3852463","BDRIV-7","BDRIV","martin.luts@bolt.eu","Martin Luts","Update from TWS regarding cells:\n\n* EVE Energy- TWS have projects which use EVE 4695 cell for production. EVE have 3 types of 46 cells in mass production.\n\nhe 46XX cell is under development, not in mass production.\n\n# BAK Battery\n# Gotion High-Tech\n# SVOLT\n\nCustomer customized products are in mass production, not for sale to other customers.\n\n# LG\n# Samsung SDI\n# CATL\n# Envision AESC\n\nTWS are not familiar with these company’s cell status.\n\n# Leawat-Power\n# CALB\n\n_To upgrade your next generation batteries, the opinion from us is researching 21700 cells to see any better options for D1/EB1 batteries  which can meet your improve requirements._\n\nNext steps from TWS:\n\n* They make a comparison between the 21700 cells to see whether anything new or better is available. (I do not have high hopes because we did the same during EB1 battery research phase which was ~1year ago). They will provide input of 21700 cells by {{2026-02-03}} \n* TWS will make a comparison of the 3 different 46xx cells available by EVE and provide their input by {{2026-02-03}} \n\nI also remembered that we have a direct contact to BAK. I will ask them directly about 46xx cells.","2026-01-30T11:32:37.681Z"],["3852464","PFI-840400","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:33:00.920Z"],["3852468","PFI-826498","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Hey, the payment has been linked to courier balance [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75602063|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/75602063] \nI believe in that case there is no refund required and has been adjusted by their cash orders. ","2026-01-30T11:34:16.908Z"],["3852471","LSS-61486","LSS","ignacio.vrtal@bolt.eu","Ignacio Agustin Vrtal","Hi [~accountid:712020:65ceddf5-ffa6-4723-b2a7-eb44b8e9e656],\n\nSorry this got lost in my email somehow. I’ll fill out the cognito regarding this. Thank you for your help!","2026-01-30T11:34:54.525Z"],["3852472","PFI-830137","PFI","artem.lishchuk@bolt.eu","Artem Lishchuk","The problem: the company overpaid 490 CZK; it was then refunded back, but balance didn’t update;\n\n490 refund in thhe November isn’t registered on the Invoice\n\nbut is registered on Balance?","2026-01-30T11:35:06.945Z"],["3852473","PFI-822463","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","This request has been raised previously and has been resolved already. ","2026-01-30T11:35:17.962Z"],["3852474","PFI-840658","PFI","wiktoria.wawryszuk@bolt.eu","Wiktoria Wawryszuk","Hey -When will it be visible in admin? ","2026-01-30T11:35:21.441Z"],["3852475","PFI-830137","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Thank you for submitting a ticket to Billing! \n\nLooks like this issue needs input from our developers. The issue has been flagged to them & they are investigating. We will keep you posted with any updates! \n\nCheers\nBilling Team Jira Bot","2026-01-30T11:35:35.629Z"],["3852476","PFI-840394","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:35:36.474Z"],["3852477","PFI-840392","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nThanks for reaching out! The Customer Payments team doesn't handle promotion or discount codes. For assistance with those, please reach out to the *Campaigns and Incentives team* (technical support). They'll be able to assist you with any questions you have.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:36:02.308Z"],["3852478","SCM-1112","SCM","zuzanna.jurkitewicz@bolt.eu","Zuzanna Jurkitewicz","I discussed this topic with Marko and he added additional column to the [Bolt Rentals - Locations report|https://wd3.myworkday.com/bolt/d/gateway.htmld?reloadToken=6f4f0eb69a725bc96066f5323b6afc63c3161cf8c918db463f843a377b41c922] (the last column - _Created Moment_) - basically this column says when the new warehouse location was created in WD, so with using filters it will be easy to know which locations were opened during the specific period of time and export it to excel. I’m waiting for the Insurance Team feedback if this is sufficient for them.","2026-01-30T11:36:38.171Z"],["3852480","PFI-840676","PFI","austin.fagbolagun@bolt-outsource.eu","Austin Fagbolagun","I completely understand your perspective. The user's concern here was not the pre-authorization, but that a refund was initiated [here|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/729938782] on the 25th of January, 2026, for an order that was never delivered, then the same amount was recalled from the user's account on the 27th of January, hence the reason for the duplicate where the customer is insisting on gettin a refund since the initial refund was charged back.\n\n\nThe refund could have been re-nintiated but that wouldn’t be possible since the initial refund was accepted by the customer. Please review.\n\nI await your response,\n\nAustin\n\n","2026-01-30T11:36:58.383Z"],["3852482","LSS-61580","LSS","stanislaw.staniszewski@bolt.eu","Stanisław Staniszewski","Hi, I received an answer form the LL. \n\nHere is the message provided by him: \n”In fact, I have suspended my business activity, as I mentioned previously. I issue invoices as a natural person (Wiesław Kietliński) who is a VAT payer.\nI regularly pay VAT 7 and PIT 28 to the tax office.”  \n\nOrginal in PL:\n”W istocie mam zawieszoną działalność gospodarczą o czym kiedyś  informowałem.    Faktury wystawiam jako osoba fizyczna  ( Wiesław Kietliński ) pozostająca płatnikiem podatku VAT. \n\nDo urzędu skarbowego odprowadzam systematycznie podatek VAT 7 oraz PiT 28.”\n\nAdditionally to that, I checked our latest invoices received from him, and In place of his details, we can see the tax identification number (NIP) of a suspended business. Sharing the invoices below. \n\n[^Faktura za media styczeń 2026 r .pdf]\n[^Faktura czynszowa za styczeń   2026 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-30T11:37:56.059Z"],["3852484","RISK2-3256","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis"," LG removed Country Prioritisation Score column from Linkable Records: Country, so a default value is no longer needed.\n\nWe aim to separate the Country Prioritisation Score from the Risk Assessment completely, as they are standalone things and it does not affect the risk score. We will create two separate views in the table report - one based on risk assessment, and the second being the country prioritisation score which is static and due for an update annually.","2026-01-30T11:38:15.347Z"],["3852490","HS-29481","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:4888de6c-ac03-4e7d-85c8-91ac19352650],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-30T11:40:19.556Z"],["3852492","LSS-62463","LSS","brendanasomah.stahl@bolt.eu","Brendan Asomah Stahl","[^Luxury Drive GmbH - Bolt Cooperation Agreement - Germany.docx (1).pdf] _(482 kB)_","2026-01-30T11:40:41.854Z"],["3852495","LSS-62240","LSS","julia.maal@bolt.eu","Julia Maal","Hey [~accountid:712020:bc3e1151-2459-4765-92b8-897f743d8296] and [~accountid:712020:652fd966-97db-4de3-b20d-d6644848128c]! I compared our NDA template with the attached file and Rolzo LTD just filled the blanks. Hence, all good to sign this for Bolt Chaffeur related discussions.\n\nCan you share the email of the signatory with me please in order for us to proceed with signing?","2026-01-30T11:41:30.173Z"],["3852496","MP-2916","MP","mustafa.ogun@bolt.eu","Mustafa Ogün Öztürk","Can’t remember the full context but i think this report came from the duty quite some time ago. Therefore, it might be outdated by now. Maybe it was already fixed under the dark mode efforts.","2026-01-30T11:41:39.702Z"],["3852501","LSS-58941","LSS","gabriele.kaveckyte@bolt.eu","Gabrielė Kaveckytė","Hey [~accountid:712020:13033e65-435c-4794-a380-e007eba7615a] , check out these pages:\n\n* [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_mQpcfXqla3NPq33HZO14EQiTRptho9UzHPFot7aBPA/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_mQpcfXqla3NPq33HZO14EQiTRptho9UzHPFot7aBPA/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] \n* [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PRODWIKI/pages/5737709569/WIP+Gender+field+check|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PRODWIKI/pages/5737709569/WIP+Gender+field+check|smart-link] \n\n\n\nUnfortunately can’t find the tickets from the past, so we’ll need to consult Mikk, and we can add the position/overview to a Confluence page.","2026-01-30T11:42:16.956Z"],["3852502","LSS-62464","LSS","izabela.adamiec@bolt.eu","Izabela Rosińska","[^Annex 5 (1).pdf] _(60 kB)_","2026-01-30T11:42:17.488Z"],["3852503","PFI-840387","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba","2026-01-30T11:42:19.151Z"],["3852504","DO-5824","DO","przemyslaw.gumula@bolt.eu","Przemysław Gumuła","ok, you’re set","2026-01-30T11:42:24.479Z"],["3852505","PFI-840711","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:43:07.036Z"],["3852506","BDB-1600","BDB","adega.murbe@bolt.eu","Adega Murbe-Onyango","Hey [~accountid:621fa8978a4bb60068f1fe09] \nFind [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1lehHeLxczVkTW5xDbqeL0_cWnsS1g4DHp8UdQK2kMl8/edit?gid=1814651184#gid=1814651184] Media plan & brief for the TZ:Arusha Airport digital screen ads.\ncc: [~accountid:6012ba328fb6ea014a8294ce] [~accountid:6290ab2fab91fe00709a0d7c] ","2026-01-30T11:43:15.110Z"],["3852508","LSS-58970","LSS","thalemarie.bo@bolt.eu","Thale Marie Bø","[~accountid:619cad8cb43d5b006af304cc] I don’t have any objections to proceeding with the UGC campaign from a legal standpoint, so long as:\n\n* Each creator signs the UGC contract with us, and potential drivers involved sign a Driver contract as shared below.\n* The marketing team reviews every UGC video before it’s posted.\n** As part of the review, ensures that any drivers involved in the videos do not make statements indicating that they represent Bolt or have an employment-like relationship with Bolt. This is especially important as the current script encourages creators to include a driver where possible.\n* Any benchmarks shown in the videos, such as average ratings in the app, are real and accurate for the market that the videos will be targeting. ","2026-01-30T11:43:36.003Z"],["3852509","WFM-10227","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Delivery role has been [granted|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/admin-access-request/access-requests/view/541942] ","2026-01-30T11:44:04.171Z"],["3852510","LSS-62456","LSS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","[~accountid:712020:7d2c0ae5-7247-4c64-bc22-4fc4f2e8a7a1] use this [page|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/7470219433/Bolt+Food+Sign-Up+Bonus+deals#:green:-Core-Addendum-(mandatory)] for some guidance on clauses to use for the deposit (payment guarantee). What he has drafted is not bad but just put in more checks for us e.g \n\n# after a period of time (e.g 1 year) and payments have been consistent, we can have the deposit released as we have guaranteed payment; \n# Is the expectation that the funds will be put in an interest bearing account? and if so, is there an expectation for Naivas to account for interest?\n# Naivas cannot draw down from the deposit unless payment is outstanding for 7 days from the payment date.\n# Withdrawals should be limited to only Goods Price as Partner still owes Bolt commission (Agency Fee)\n# We will not be required to top up the deposit if Naivas draws down on it. \n# If Naivas gives us notice that the deposit has been drawn down for the relevant period-we will withhold payment for that period as it has been recovered from the deposit. Note that payment to Partner is due less commission so there should be an allowance for us to set off the amounts.\n# Specifics of the determination of actual funds due. Our statement should be proof of funds due to Naivas and if Naivas have drawn down on the deposit but there is a disagreement about the amount; then include a short dispute resolution window (2 weeks); otherwise final determination of amount due shall be based on our statement of accounts. \n# Check Practical Law on Payments and Guarantees, Security to see if you can find any useful clauses. \n# Also speak with tax team and FinReg team to review and flag if any issues. ","2026-01-30T11:44:05.545Z"],["3852511","PFI-840678","PFI","filip.kieronczyk@bolt-outsource.eu","Filip Kieronczyk","ID: 212343771\nUSER: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/212343771|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/identity/consumers/rider/212343771]\nPAYMENTS: [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments?userId=212343771&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw&filter={\"limit\"%3A25%2C\"offset\"%3A0%2C\"filter\"%3A{\"userType\"%3A\"user\"%2C\"from\"%3A1753833600.741%2C\"to\"%3A1769817599.741%2C\"userId\"%3A212343771}}|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments?userId=212343771&tz=Europe%2FWarsaw&filter=%7B%22limit%22%3A25%2C%22offset%22%3A0%2C%22filter%22%3A%7B%22userType%22%3A%22user%22%2C%22from%22%3A1753833600.741%2C%22to%22%3A1769817599.741%2C%22userId%22%3A212343771%7D%7D]","2026-01-30T11:44:28.697Z"],["3852514","PFI-839419","PFI","milosz.jasinski@bolt-outsource.eu","Milosz Jasinski","Next to Yes/No, there is a note saying “required,” and the rider claims that the application does not respond when clicking on one of the options.","2026-01-30T11:44:58.667Z"],["3852516","LSS-62461","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","+*BACKGROUND*+\n\n* On 22 January 2026, we received an email from [pmbell@gmail.com|mailto:pmbell@gmail.com], asking for invoices ([link|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/728411265]).\n** Request was for invoices for various transactions made with a credit card ending in 8689.\n** This is re-sending a previous request (previously sent to CS), now from an email address registered to their Bolt account.\n** In response on the same day, outsourced CS (Emanuel Corado) responded flagging that the above email is not associated with a Bolt account. CS then stated “_However, the contact information you provided leads us to the following email address:_ [_contabilidade@lisbonlounge.com_|mailto:contabilidade@lisbonlounge.com]”. No response since then.\n* I can see that on 24 January, the same request was then submitted from the email [contabilidade@lisbonlounge.com|mailto:contabilidade@lisbonlounge.com] ([link|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/case/728135156]).\n** “_I did not receive any communication at my email address_ [_contibilidade@lisbonlounge.com_|mailto:contibilidade@lisbonlounge.com]_, but I am sending a reply from here to confirm that it is mine_”\n** Case was closed as the user apparently did not reply to the webform.\n* CS has escalated this as a personal data incident ticket as “_the email registered to the rider’s account was shared. Since the user contacted us from an email address that was not registered on our system, the agent should not have shared the email associated with the profile or the name linked to it_”.\n\n+*ANALYSIS*+\n\n* It looks like the user at-issue owns both email addresses. As such, there has been no disclosure to any third parties here, and so I have not seen anything to suggest that a personal data incident had occurred.\n* Nevertheless, this is because we got lucky - as a mitigation step, we should still ensure that the agent is told not to share email addresses going forward.\n\n+*NEXT STEPS*+\n\n* QUESTIONS:\n** Confirm understanding of the facts.\n** Has the DSAR been properly escalated via DSAR channel?\n* ADVICE:\n** No data breach here. Train the relevant CS agent.","2026-01-30T11:45:26.838Z"],["3852519","PFI-821965","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-30T11:45:49.823Z"],["3852523","LSS-62456","LSS","kerubo.ombati@bolt.eu","Kerubo Ombati","Just FYI. I know Naivas is a major Partner and would be a big win for us but Supermarkets have come under scrutiny & been penalised of the competition authority in Kenya for abusing their dominance and market power by requiring suppliers to agree to terms that are unfair. ","2026-01-30T11:47:02.974Z"],["3852524","DINE-989","DINE","prasheel.soni@bolt.eu","Prasheel Soni","Thanks for the quick action Simona :raised_hands:","2026-01-30T11:47:08.071Z"],["3852525","SREDESK-7486","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","Why you need access to k8s cluster? ","2026-01-30T11:47:17.754Z"],["3852526","LSS-56585","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}\nSupport has been provided, agreement finalised and Doc is being submitted for signature.\n{panel}","2026-01-30T11:47:31.330Z"],["3852528","MLC-3181","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 30th*+\n\n* *Decision:* Reverting to old strategy\n** Data here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Ea_q9uOFfQRQUidat63MGALZ1NdpMP6W7XpWUh1_xY0/edit?gid=1333149813#gid=1333149813|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Ea_q9uOFfQRQUidat63MGALZ1NdpMP6W7XpWUh1_xY0/edit?gid=1333149813#gid=1333149813|smart-link] \n** Current data shows negative impact on performance or at the very least is not reliable due to date of changes.There is relative 12% drop from the previous conversion rate.\n** There was a similar trend last year where the December to January period showed a 7% drop, however, during January numbers should normalize / start rising. This trend is not seen in the current year.\n** There is an impact of an approximately 500 conversions loss for the period (or 100 conversions per week) if we estimate the numbers by using the old conversion rate.\n** Although there are some signs on normalization on top affected markets, only 7 markets out of 16 exhibit this behaviour. All CEE markets are also underperfroming and not showing signs of normalization.\n* *Next Steps:* Will revert to initial strategy by EOD Monday.","2026-01-30T11:48:02.652Z"],["3852530","PAW-15436","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline started.","2026-01-30T11:48:38.968Z"],["3852531","PFI-839297","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","{color:#172B4D}{color}   \n\n  Greeting \n\n   \n\n   \n\n We kindly request that you provide your official position along with the relevant supporting documentation immediately, but no later than within one (1) business day. \n\n Upon expiration of the aforementioned deadline, the bank will proceed with initiating a chargeback to refund the amount to the customer, and the respective sum will be debited from your company’s account without acceptance. \n\n Thank you for your cooperation. \n\n   \n\n[{color:#172B4D}{color}|]{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color} \n\n   \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image002.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-30T11:48:43.973Z"],["3852532","SREDESK-7486","SREDESK","shahmir.wahid@bolt.eu","Shahmir Bin Wahid","AFAIR, SREDO is owning runners infrastructure and k8s access is only within SRE teams.","2026-01-30T11:48:44.770Z"],["3852533","C2-463","C2","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Due to the reasons mentioned below the research will be done at Eledrive. \n\nWe will arrive to Eledriveco on {{2026-02-03}} early in the morning. We will spend the whole day at Eledrive factory doing the research + making sure the local team understands the process so that they can continue whatever we can not accomplish in one day.\n\nin addition to ~200 batteries sent to be repaired I asked Warsaw LM to pack 50pcs if random C1/C2 mix and deliver to Eledrive so we can also have a selection of “still good” batteries to examine.","2026-01-30T11:48:45.624Z"],["3852537","DRAG101-287","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","[~accountid:63d0ecd1d73cd1e44e22078f] please help answering the question about the wear rate/puncture proofing/cost ratio 🙏 ","2026-01-30T11:49:44.996Z"],["3852538","LSS-61075","LSS","catarina.faria@bolt.eu","Catarina Faria","Hey team,\n\nClosing this ticket since Dr. Thomas Bugeja went to court, provided the information and everything went well.\n\nThank you all!","2026-01-30T11:49:50.945Z"],["3852539","MLC-2962","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 30th*+\n\n* *No Updates this week* - Pending HVO results\n* *Next Steps:*\n** *Relaunch of Card BINs*\n** Will work on rebuilding and relaunch templates next week.\n** Will do a multi-variate test: DnD vs optimized template to get results sooner. Volumes for these automations should give us insights in 1-2 days max.","2026-01-30T11:50:08.042Z"],["3852540","GROWTH-757","GROWTH","mohd.goh@bolt.eu","Ameer Goh","[~accountid:621f255f59c0740069d7a613] [~accountid:712020:1901f25b-6521-4b4b-b25c-d836d7218739] I’ve created this idea for Dubai investment case specifically. Please link the relevant epics here.\n\ncc [~accountid:5dc535abb8eb490c677a579c] [~accountid:63f5cbedd6722987749da196] ","2026-01-30T11:50:23.177Z"],["3852541","LSS-59633","LSS","anna.kalabska@bolt.eu","Anna Kalabska","[~accountid:712020:b33fa9fc-2e0e-4ab0-a8b3-85f9683a7c93] hey, the finalized version from our side is below. I also left comments for landlord to address outstanding issues and receive their confirmation on clauses they did not confirm internally. All other agreed changes were accepted.\n\nFurther, clauses 11.9 and 11.10 were added to provide for a limitation on further lease to third parties for the provision of the same type of services. \n\nPlease download this document and send it to the partner for review and confirmations.\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r0In0YedhIFb7y8JV0Vu0qBCZMyb8JZc/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r0In0YedhIFb7y8JV0Vu0qBCZMyb8JZc/edit|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T11:50:36.323Z"],["3852543","PFI-839297","PFI","chargeback_reports@bolt.eu","chargeback_reports","მზიკო, \n\n  \n\nგავუგზავნე შეტყობინება, თუ პასუხს არ გაგვცემენ, ხვალ შეასრულეთ.{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}{color:#172B4D}{color}  \n\n  \n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    \n\n   \n\n პატივისცემით \n\n +Best Regards+ \n\n  \n\n{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#595959} -{color} {color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color} {color:#595959}Mira{color} {color:#595959} tsotsoria{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color} \n\n{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#595959}{color} \n\n[{color:#595959}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#595959}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#595959}{color}{color:#595959}{color}\n !image002.png|thumbnail!{color:#595959}{color}","2026-01-30T11:50:50.817Z"],["3852544","DSR-4241","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T11:51:05.443Z"],["3852547","LSS-62461","LSS","thomas.harper@bolt.eu","Thomas Harper","Hi [~accountid:712020:56888f59-a122-4004-bf1d-ae9e6ea1fe8c] - thanks for escalating this. Questions are in blue below, together with my thoughts.\n\nSo just to confirm my understanding, {color:#4c9aff}*does the same person own both email addresses*{color} here (i.e., [+pmbell@gmail.com+|mailto:pmbell@gmail.com] and [+contabilidade@lisbonlounge.com+|mailto:contabilidade@lisbonlounge.com])? If so, then technically we have not shared the email address with any third parties, and so a personal data incident has not occurred ✅ \n\nHowever, this is more due to luck than anything else, and so we should make sure that this does not happen again in the future. As such, in terms of mitigation steps, please make sure that the Outsourced CS (Emanuel Corado) if instructed not to share email addresses in this way going forward. {color:#4c9aff}*Do we know if they were following any CS guidance that told them to do so*{color}? If so then we may want to consider whether this needs updating.\n\nFinally, I see that the underlying request is technically a DSAR. As such, {color:#4c9aff}*has this been escalated to the DSAR team*{color} (via Jira)? If not, could you please do so?","2026-01-30T11:51:19.417Z"],["3852548","HS-29484","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey [~accountId:712020:b794ab88-0428-44ea-9340-6e77bef078db],\n\nThis ticket will breach its SLA in 8 hours. You should action or reassign it as soon as possible.\n\nCheers,\nYour friendly automation bot","2026-01-30T11:51:39.727Z"],["3852549","PFI-840385","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:51:47.018Z"],["3852550","PFI-839297","PFI","support@flitt.com","support@flitt.com","გამარჯობა,\n\nრით შეგვიძლია დაგეხმაროთ?\n\nპატივისცემით,\n\nNino Pachulia\n\n{color:#1d1c1d}Support Specialist{color}\n\n\n\n{color:#222222}+995 325 00 01 02{color}\n\n[npachulia@flitt.com|mailto:npachulia@flitt.com] | [LinkedIn|https://www.linkedin.com/in/nino-pachulia/] | [www.flitt.com|https://flitt.com/]{color:#202124}{color}{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n\n\n!https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdesUJg1p54UqXLenrFQFanpvXuj_umTqEFnw1W5JR9LBf8O3m6bGImWLGpg2ulKBMgaF3p6b25v6bmXHIHIZutpHE-jvRov39TlA4JBIsOA1TnvQv9Hi1Pl6DSaGos3E_cDDVNa_WgN0NWjc5AHd9dzQAW?key=gAVmix1twk-tFXoz-xQXqA!{color:#202124}{color}\n\n\n---- on Fri, 30 Jan 2026 15:51:03 +0400  *\"pfi\"<pfi@taxify.atlassian.net>*  wrote ---- \n\n\n{quote}\n\n\n\n{color:#333333}{color}{color:#999999} —-—-—-—{color} {color:#333333}\n{color}{color:#999999} Reply above this line.{color} {color:#333333}\n\n\nchargeback_reports commented:\n\nმზიკო,\n\nგავუგზავნე შეტყობინება, თუ პასუხს არ გაგვცემენ, ხვალ შეასრულეთ.\n\nპატივისცემით\n\n +Best Regards+\n\n{color}{color:#595959}მირანდა{color}{color:#333333}{color}{color:#595959} -{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959}მირა წოწორია / Miranda{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959}Mira{color}{color:#333333} {color}{color:#595959} tsotsoria{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#595959}Customer Journey Expert{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#595959}Payments Development Tribe{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:blue}www.tbcbank.ge{color}{color:#333333}{color}|http://www.tbcbank.ge/]{color:#333333}{color}\n {color:#333333}{color} !1769773906173000_1392046965.png|thumbnail!{color:#333333}  <[https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/request/3024810/attachment/1122766]>{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}View request{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-839297?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJ0Z3QiOiJhbm9ueW1vdXMtbGluayIsInFzaCI6IjBlMGM4NmIxOTdhYmI0NjhkNTZmNmNjMTU2OTcxOTVlZWVkNmJhYWVhODIyMTVlMzJjZjhhOTRmNWIyNTc1OGEiLCJpc3MiOiJzZXJ2aWNlZGVzay1qd3QtdG9rZW4taXNzdWVyIiwiY29udGV4dCI6eyJ1c2VyIjoiNTM4MDYiLCJpc3N1ZSI6IlBGSS04MzkyOTcifSwiZXhwIjoxNzcyMTkzMDYxLCJpYXQiOjE3Njk3NzM4NjF9.KzlArS_LPVLNyfG5f_728XPjE2FL_PDodwBerE0PrlA&sda_source=notification-email]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333} ·{color} [{color:#333333}{color}{color:#3572b0}Turn off this request's notifications{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/PFI-839297/unsubscribe?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..zpM_eWT28XWuwAmyF0UQHcWdttJUDiy_fbJWWiPY_5A]{color:#3572b0}{color}{color:#333333}\n\n{color}{color:#707070}This is shared with chargeback_reports, Joel Süldre, and{color} [{color:#707070}support@flitt.com{color}|mailto:support@flitt.com]{color:#707070}.{color}{color:#333333}{color}\n\n[{color:#333333}{color}{color:#707070}Powered by Jira Service Management{color}|https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira/service-desk/powered-by?utm_medium=jira-in-product&utm_source=jira_service_desk_email_footer&utm_content=taxify]{color:#707070}{color}{color:#333333}\n Sent on January 30, 2026 1:51:01 PM EET{color} \n!http://usw2-track.atlassian.com/CI0/0101019c0ebe1219-142c9625-2165-4e16-9a42-30a032982544-000000/agKCjIoywVhcW8jKCgL6ljCquuBjw4w887zqY1y8TPc=442!{color:#333333}{color} {quote}","2026-01-30T11:51:57.997Z"],["3852551","PFI-840679","PFI","marten.martinson@bolt.eu","Marten Martinson","Hi [~accountid:6131df23dae0a20071abba9c] \n\nThe user has a balance of 7.45 EUR. \nI have issued a refund to the OPM for the same amount. Please find the proof of refund attached. \n\nPlease note we are not able to adjust the users currently balance and they would keep their funds. \n\n\n[^Refund_Letter_PJTVB29C282F9SD3_CKK3JNVP2XQ5CQD3.pdf]\n\nCheers, \nMarten","2026-01-30T11:52:36.157Z"],["3852552","HS-29580","HS","berit.mustonen@bolt.eu","Berit Mustonen","!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 13.45.25.png|thumbnail!\n\n!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 13.47.14.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T11:52:45.835Z"],["3852553","MLC-2749","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 30th*+\n\n* Changed entry point for T4 moved from Day 20 to Day 24, according to query vetted by Mostafa here.\n* T2/T3 will stay at Day 17. Initially wanted to move to day 7, but that would result in significant overlaps with High Value Order. So we will keep this as a sweep automation for long churned upper tier companies.\n* +*Next steps*+\n** Clone out for the rest of the markets and push live \n** Adding PL to the mix by Monday EOD\n** Redo templates after confirmation on working template.\n** Implement for CEE markets - then move of to rest of markets","2026-01-30T11:52:48.795Z"],["3852554","LSS-60580","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:0f7a089b-3b06-423b-844c-6e5ac370aa1e] please share reviewed agreement with Singular [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1R0V3ubJzLL92aIT8cjy8kpEdHSwF1hCC/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1R0V3ubJzLL92aIT8cjy8kpEdHSwF1hCC/edit|smart-link] \n\n* Did InfoSec provide the feedback in infosec ticket ? Please link infosec ticket here ","2026-01-30T11:52:49.018Z"],["3852555","PFI-840365","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:53:06.422Z"],["3852556","WFM-10221","WFM","keoagile.malakalaka@bolt.eu","Keoagile Malakalaka","Hi there, please unassign her from Canada and USA and only have ZA as her market.\n\nThank you.","2026-01-30T11:53:10.495Z"],["3852557","LSS-61555","LSS","matiss.panga@bolt.eu","Matīss Panga","Hello everyone!\n\nThank you for your reviews, \n[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] I went over your suggestions and left my comments in necessary places, could you affirm that we can move forward with documents signing or is additional information necessary from Ignitis side?\n\n[NDA|https://docs.google.com/document/d/175Sco-gXEXq3adGRiFQCG9GQt2l1p-uS/edit]\n\n[Agreement|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1R9gJfTMbRW84-BU0bDSd_vnylbgd7u5y/edit]\n\nThank you!","2026-01-30T11:53:20.754Z"],["3852558","LSS-55517","LSS","lisa.shein@bolt.eu","Lisa Shein","[~accountid:712020:240e5e60-baab-4e72-a388-591f4f4ec6a2] please see clean version and PDF for signature. \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BhaQIi28DthixGv_Rn9nRf_qKkyoc0Zx/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BhaQIi28DthixGv_Rn9nRf_qKkyoc0Zx/edit|smart-link] \n\n[^2026.01 Bolt Support KE Limited_ Rescue.co Membership (final draft) clean.docx.pdf]\n\n","2026-01-30T11:53:34.309Z"],["3852560","LSS-56585","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Thank you for an update!\n\nSince the agreement is finalized and Doc is ready to be submitted for signature - I will go ahead and close the sub-ticket.\nIf anything privacy-related comes up, please feel free to reach out and tag me. ","2026-01-30T11:53:41.936Z"],["3852565","GRWA-1579","GRWA","zunair.butt@bolt.eu","Muhammad Zunair Butt","Very low effort, gpt script\n\n{code:sql}%sql\nWITH base AS (\n  SELECT\n    d.driver_id,\n    CASE\n      WHEN lower(r.name) LIKE '%pattaya%' THEN 'Pattaya'\n      WHEN lower(r.name) LIKE '%bangkok%' THEN 'Bangkok'\n      ELSE 'Other'\n    END AS region_group,\n    SUM(d.finished_rides) AS rides\n  FROM ng_public_spark.etl_category_kpi_by_driver d\n  LEFT JOIN core_models_spark.dim_city c\n    ON d.city_id = c.city_id\n  LEFT JOIN ng_public_spark.admin_system_region r\n    ON d.region_id = r.id\n  WHERE c.city_name = 'Bangkok'\n    AND (lower(r.name) LIKE '%bangkok%' OR lower(r.name) LIKE '%pattaya%')\n    AND d.created_date_local >= date'2025-01-01'\n    AND d.created_date_local <= date'2025-02-01'\n  GROUP BY 1,2\n),\n\npivoted AS (\n  SELECT\n    driver_id,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN region_group = 'Pattaya' THEN rides ELSE 0 END) AS pattaya_rides,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN region_group = 'Bangkok' THEN rides ELSE 0 END)  AS bangkok_rides,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN region_group IN ('Pattaya','Bangkok') THEN rides ELSE 0 END) AS total_rides\n  FROM base\n  WHERE region_group IN ('Pattaya','Bangkok')\n  GROUP BY 1\n),\n\nclassified AS (\n  SELECT\n    *,\n    CASE\n      WHEN pattaya_rides > 0 AND bangkok_rides = 0 THEN 'only_pattaya'\n      WHEN bangkok_rides > 0 AND pattaya_rides = 0 THEN 'only_bangkok'\n      WHEN pattaya_rides > 0 AND bangkok_rides > 0 THEN 'shared'\n      ELSE 'no_rides'\n    END AS driver_type,\n    CASE WHEN total_rides > 0 THEN (pattaya_rides * 1.0) / total_rides END AS pattaya_share\n  FROM pivoted\n)\n\nSELECT\n  COUNT(*) AS drivers_total,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN driver_type = 'only_pattaya' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS drivers_only_pattaya,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN driver_type = 'only_bangkok' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS drivers_only_bangkok,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN driver_type = 'shared' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS drivers_shared,\n\n  SUM(CASE WHEN driver_type = 'shared' AND pattaya_share >= 0.75 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)\n    AS shared_drivers_pattaya_75plus,\n\n  CASE\n    WHEN SUM(CASE WHEN driver_type = 'shared' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) = 0 THEN NULL\n    ELSE\n      (SUM(CASE WHEN driver_type = 'shared' AND pattaya_share >= 0.75 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) * 1.0)\n      / (SUM(CASE WHEN driver_type = 'shared' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END))\n  END AS pct_of_shared_pattaya_75plus\nFROM classified;\n{code}","2026-01-30T11:54:05.404Z"],["3852566","PFI-840362","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nCould you check with the Technical Support team regarding this issue? They might be able to support you better.","2026-01-30T11:54:10.739Z"],["3852567","CSDT-994","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","* Template created here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1EdTTWpfg57N6abVmh36yJp4gpyU3032ay6LFzH8NwWY/edit?gid=952078046#gid=952078046|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1EdTTWpfg57N6abVmh36yJp4gpyU3032ay6LFzH8NwWY/edit?gid=952078046#gid=952078046|smart-link] \n* Pending discussion with JZ regarding market level scorecards","2026-01-30T11:54:24.523Z"],["3852568","INT-881","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-30T11:54:32.373Z"],["3852570","PFI-840326","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T11:54:37.036Z"],["3852572","HS-29580","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Berit,\n\nThanks for your request! We’ve moved your request to the correct People Services Support Desk so it can be handled by the right team.\n\nYou can view and track your request(s) here:\nnull\n\nBest regards,\nPeople Services Team","2026-01-30T11:54:42.352Z"],["3852575","DRAG101-498","DRAG101","hendrik.vorno@bolt.eu","Hendrik Võrno","Prograss (extremely slow 🐌) so far:\n\n* FAKT is yet to give a specific answer whether we need to do any additional physical tests in Switzerland or are our test reports sufficient.\n* I have currently forwarded paperwork of regular D1 + explanations/drawings about modifications compared to D1 to FAKT for evaluation of the above ⬆️ \n* D3 EN17128 will be completed before CNY ","2026-01-30T11:55:11.707Z"],["3852576","RISK2-3305","RISK2","anni.faltis@bolt.eu","Anni Faltis","*30.01 Checked - ok*","2026-01-30T11:55:21.887Z"],["3852577","PFI-815878","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","This request has been raised previously and has been resolved already. ","2026-01-30T11:55:46.605Z"],["3852578","INT-882","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-30T11:56:44.977Z"],["3852579","LSS-60580","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey [~accountid:712020:548c71a6-d1f4-404d-9c5e-482bc0de371a] ,\n\nThank you very much. I’ll share this with Singular and will keep you updated on their feedback.\n\nHere is the InfoSec ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ISS-1148|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/ISS-1148|smart-link] \n\nWe’ve received the green light from Tarmo.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-30T11:56:48.933Z"],["3852581","LSS-62412","LSS","veera.pikkov@bolt.eu","Veera Pikkov","Hi Ping! \nPlease see below an overview of the key considerations, followed by a more detailed explanation below. I also address the potential Google Maps routing future addition that we discussed briefly, at the end. \n\n*Summary*\n\n* *_Do we need to credit OSM?_* Yes. Attribution to OpenStreetMap is mandatory whenever OSM data is displayed to users.\n* *Main implementation decision:* how and where attribution is shown, which depends on whether the map is considered interactive.\n* *Penalties:* not clearly defined and enforcement is typically informal; the main risk is reputational rather than financial.\n* Additional OSM policies (tiles, geocoding, editing) may apply depending on technical implementation.\n* Combining Google Maps for routing: possible from OSM perspective but compliance with Google’s own terms may be {color:#ff5630}tricky, if not impossible.{color} \n\n# *Attribution* - [https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Licence/Attribution_Guidelines|https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Licence/Attribution_Guidelines|smart-link] \n\nOpenStreetMap data is licensed under the Open Data Commons Open Database License (ODbL).\nWhenever OpenStreetMap data is displayed to users (including on an on-vehicle display), attribution is mandatory.\n\nMinimum requirement:\n\n* Attribution to *“OpenStreetMap”* (historically “© OpenStreetMap” is acceptable)\n* Clear indication that the data is available under the *ODbL* (typically via a link to [http://openstreetmap.org/copyright|http://openstreetmap.org/copyright|smart-link]  or an equivalent “About / Info” screen)\n\nThis obligation applies regardless of how the map tiles are sourced (OSM, self-hosted, or third-party).\n\n# *How attribution is shown (interactive vs non-interactive)*\n\nOSM distinguishes mainly between interactive (browsable) maps - i.e. maps where the user can change what they see (such as panning, zooming, clicking, or the map moving in response to interaction) and other map displays. \n\nFor interactive maps:\n\n* attribution should normally appear on the map (in any corner), but it may alternatively be shown adjacent to the map or via a splash screen or pop-up at application startup. \n* Attribution may be dismissed, faded, or automatically hidden after user interaction or a short time.\n*  If attribution is hidden, users must still be able to access licence information later (e.g. via an Info or About option). \n* Attribution shown at startup does not need to be repeated on every subsequent interaction.\n\n*3. Compliance and penalties*\n\nThere are no defined penalties for non-compliance with OSM attribution.\n\nPractical risks include:\n\n* Informal requests from the OSM Foundation or community to correct attribution\n* Reputational exposure if attribution is missing\n* Service restrictions only if OSM infrastructure (tiles, Nominatim) is misused\n\n → A competitor check may be useful. \n\n# *Other OSM Policies to be aware of:*\n\nDepending on the technical setup, additional OSM policies may apply. Please indicate if you think they may be applicable: \n\n* Tile Usage Policy - only if loading map tiles directly from OSM servers [https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/|https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/|smart-link]  \n* Nominatim Usage Policy - only if using OSM’s search/geocoding service [https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/|https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/|smart-link] \n* Editing API Policy - only if writing data back to OSM [https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/api/|https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/api/|smart-link] \n\n# *Routing using Google Maps on top of OSM -* [https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Licence/Attribution_Guidelines|https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Licence/Attribution_Guidelines|smart-link] \n\nFrom an OSM perspective:\n\n* Routing engines that use OSM data must credit OSM\n* Applications incorporating such routing must credit OSM\n* Individual routing instructions do not need attribution if they are not a derivative database\n\nHowever, from Google’s side things are a bit more tricky:\n\n* Google Maps Platform Terms of Service generally restrict customers from using Google Maps Platform content (routing not explicitly included but presumed), in conjunction with non-Google maps ([https://cloud.google.com/maps-platform/terms|https://cloud.google.com/maps-platform/terms|smart-link])\n* If Customer uses the Services with third-party products or services in its Customer Application, Customer is responsible for making it clear to the End User what is Google Maps Content and what content is not from Google → we must make clear which elements come from OSM vs Google ([https://cloud.google.com/terms/maps-platform/eea/maps-service-terms|https://cloud.google.com/terms/maps-platform/eea/maps-service-terms|smart-link] )\n* Google requires attribution always (can’t be faded, collapsed, like OSM). \n* Once again, it would be helpful here to check competitor approaches to map attribution and routing integration. Using a native map and routing stack from the same provider would materially simplify compliance.\n\nThank you and let me know if you have any additional questions or if you’d like to hop on a call to discuss!\n\nVeera ","2026-01-30T11:57:31.150Z"],["3852582","LSS-62349","LSS","aleksis.anijarv@bolt.eu","Aleksis Anijärv","[~accountid:712020:52cfdad6-7e7c-4e24-b869-dd2ab87c9432] we think that there might not even be a contract between all 3 parties. \nBut we still need to find a contract which states that Bolt has a *liability to cover* 14 cars *rental payments* *to ABC Rent* if Fleet fails to do so.  \nThere were total of 14 cars in this project, we have this contract for 4 cars  [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jGbg_9hpVeW4h5eMeR7chNcfWv2iSVefqF_koqHpgY4/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jGbg_9hpVeW4h5eMeR7chNcfWv2iSVefqF_koqHpgY4/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] , but we need to find the one for the rest of the 10 cars. ","2026-01-30T11:57:45.105Z"],["3852583","WFM-10227","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Hello, [~accountid:641484b72cee496759eb1c5e], please let me know if the agent will continue working on Ride-hailing vertical or I can remove this permission.","2026-01-30T11:58:26.216Z"],["3852585","PAW-15436","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","BACA: Pipeline completed successfully. PR: https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/pull/162639","2026-01-30T11:58:39.004Z"],["3852586","LSS-62365","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:4afbd60d-276d-4d8c-8d4c-5669fd772468] just heads up that we received your request and we’re on it ","2026-01-30T11:58:42.137Z"],["3852593","LSS-58970","LSS","sandra.bergstrom@bolt.eu","Sandra Bergström","Well noted, thank you [~accountid:712020:a5138bac-89ac-4e8d-8ec1-5cefe090c9a3]!","2026-01-30T11:59:19.025Z"],["3852595","LSS-61894","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:60d6dd5e9469280070403d08] just heads up that we received your request and we’re on it ","2026-01-30T11:59:29.975Z"],["3852596","LSS-61691","LSS","catherine.stiff@bolt.eu","Cathy Stiff","Please can I have an update?","2026-01-30T11:59:31.943Z"],["3852597","LSS-58352","LSS","rachael.irimu@bolt.eu","Rachael Irimu","Thanks [~accountid:712020:338dfd87-ef5d-40bb-b10d-871b880aa66d] - shared the comments with Novitus. \n\nOn the annex - I suggest having it as part of this agreement as they are related. ","2026-01-30T11:59:35.011Z"],["3852602","MLC-3472","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","h3. Week 5\n\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n** Added comms engagement metrics (measured against last 3M engagement benchmarks for ad-hocs) to the [results summary|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gbaur2SK9jBzTRgMkNFWtsyVr-aTZ4LRzKEHGciW-cI/edit?tab=t.i808357h8xpf].\n** *Key takeaways from the results:*\n**# Comms approved by test markets had better conversion rates and unsubscribe rates compared to global ad-hocs, but performed worse in terms of OR and CTR.\n**# We can generally trust local teams to create good setups without incidents, but they still struggle with email template/content quality.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Expanding the test to more markets with an increased control group size - ETA TBD.","2026-01-30T12:00:48.678Z"],["3852603","MLC-3605","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","Week 5:\n\n* Egypt, Zimbawe, Uganda, USA - all WP stages cloned in Braze, pushing live in week 6.\n* Slovenia - localisation due date 6.Feb.","2026-01-30T12:00:51.198Z"],["3852604","CSCC-35","CSCC","cheila.aniceto@bolt.eu","Cheila Aniceto","New issue tags went live on the 2nd Sept 25","2026-01-30T12:01:08.662Z"],["3852605","LSS-60879","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hi[~accountid:617175f026a540007141ae5c] - thank you for the information provided.\nPlease tag me in case of any updates.\n","2026-01-30T12:01:13.590Z"],["3852609","BDB-1562","BDB","britt.peet@bolt.eu","Bo Britt Peet","Thank you! [~accountid:712020:c7e5b826-6f9d-454b-83a6-a7755ef1ff9c], please take a look. ","2026-01-30T12:02:16.673Z"],["3852611","PFI-840302","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payment state in Admin has been adjusted to match the state from the customer’s PayPal account.","2026-01-30T12:02:31.376Z"],["3852612","CSENP-49","CSENP","warwie.sanjuan@bolt.eu","Warwie San Juan","We have built a scheduling review process for the current BPOs. As soon as we have more context on which tool Cognizant will use and how they do staffing analysis, it would be easier for us to standardize scheduling frameworks. For now we made a simple scheduling review process in [*confluence*|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CS/pages/7440466552/Schedule+Reviews]. ","2026-01-30T12:02:50.361Z"],["3852613","WD-22737","WD","iryna.stepanko@bolt.eu","Iryna Stepanko","Hello [~accountid:5e843508e57b6c0c1e6c703f] !\n\n\n\nIf have adjusted validations, if you use book code statutory adjustment validation won’t be triggered and you will be able to post journals. ","2026-01-30T12:02:54.512Z"],["3852614","PFI-840688","PFI","nigar.alizada@bolt.eu","Nigar Alizada","Hello [~accountid:712020:ebc35d95-9563-46b2-a110-5f27dd0318c8],\n\nThe issue should be solved for the user in about an hour after additional reviews are completed.\n\nBest Regards,\nNigar Alizada","2026-01-30T12:04:15.059Z"],["3852618","PFI-813850","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Both payments matched to C account, please remind them to put the payment reference in the description field not the Viitenumber/Reference number field in their bank then in the future they would not have this issue. ","2026-01-30T12:04:27.568Z"],["3852621","PFI-840722","PFI",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey 👋\nThanks for opening a ticket to Billing. Our specialists will take a look at this ASAP.\nFor a faster response, please check our self-help FAQs. Most likely, your question is already answered there.\n\nRide-Hailing ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=564964225\n\nWork Profile ➡️ https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1P6YLwjKO7fS9OusUGnMX36NCvJUo3fQU8kSqRsbAt74/edit#gid=1631784415","2026-01-30T12:04:55.626Z"],["3852622","LOC-5333","LOC","agata.bieniek@bolt.eu","Agata Bieniek","Waiting for the offer from Ops","2026-01-30T12:04:56.024Z"],["3852623","LSS-61486","LSS","maksym.padalka@bolt.eu","Maksym Padalka","Hey [~accountid:712020:d4fea1a1-04d3-411a-82fc-435abbd538e3] \nIn this ticket, there’s no need for a cognito link to be shared from your side - I’ve found it myself.\nThank you! 🙏 ","2026-01-30T12:05:25.522Z"],["3852624","INT-883","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-30T12:05:47.130Z"],["3852625","PFI-840269","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe total order was PLN 80.31 [https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4002207132|https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/commerce-payment/payments/4002207132] but only PLN 56.41 were charged from the customer’s card and the remaining amount was charged as a debt in the balance. This is why there is a debt in the customer’s account.","2026-01-30T12:05:51.799Z"],["3852626","PFI-840723","PFI","darren.seruwagi@bolt.eu","Darren Mbigiridde Seruwagi","!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 13.05.32.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T12:05:59.082Z"],["3852627","WD-22114","WD","tuuli.poldma@bolt.eu","Tuuli Põldma","Hi [~accountid:62b2cf37566f3e7b0a8fa9b4] I pulled the latest supplier invoices and the attachments are all separate, but at least now I can open all the documents and attachments. Will this solution be only applicable to Portugal or for other entities as well? I am wondering if and how this update would affect others. For PT I can inform local partner that separate documents starting with same number relate to one invoice, but if for other entities it is important that there would be one document per invoice, then I am afraid it will might be an issue.\n\n","2026-01-30T12:05:59.796Z"],["3852628","PFI-840257","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nThanks for reaching out! The Customer Payments team doesn't handle promotion or discount codes. For assistance with those, please reach out to the *Campaigns and Incentives team* (technical support). They'll be able to assist you with any questions you have.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T12:06:25.985Z"],["3852629","LSS-61691","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","hi [~accountid:712020:e7c4988a-ccaf-44c1-8546-2d01d1217937] before signing Transition plan firstly we need to sign the extension. \n\nWe’re drafting additional agreement and we can sign it next week. \n\nI will share the draft here. ","2026-01-30T12:07:09.430Z"],["3852630","WFM-10227","WFM","eva.pavliskova@bolt-outsource.eu","Eva Pavliskova","Hello, you can remove Ride-hailing permissions, she won’t use them. \n\nThank you","2026-01-30T12:07:50.327Z"],["3852632","DSR-3557","DSR","jens.zarelius@bolt.eu","Jens Zarelius","Hi [~accountid:712020:eb9cd4dd-46ca-47c8-a985-9f940495724a] \nThe user have return asking for:\n”User is asking to provide the full legal name and registered address of the company processing his personal data. It is a formal request under the GDPR as the user will report this matter to the relevant GDPR supervisory authority”.","2026-01-30T12:08:04.477Z"],["3852633","DBRE-8184","DBRE","marat.saddarov@bolt.eu","Marat Saddarov","Reassigned to [~accountid:712020:33a9f9af-afcf-458f-9564-a94507323704]  to happen next sprint if engineering is ready to support the timeline. [~accountid:604aad6558aa8d00722fb03f]  fyi","2026-01-30T12:08:30.225Z"],["3852637","MLC-3171","MLC","marian.keller@bolt.eu","Marian Keller","* BU - Promo codes - one string needs translations and proofreading.\n* BU - HVO - needs proofreading.","2026-01-30T12:08:52.662Z"],["3852638","WD-22114","WD","tuuli.poldma@bolt.eu","Tuuli Põldma","I can of course check from accountants channel if it would be an issue for accountants sharing supplier invoices, if not possible to separate the entities\n\n","2026-01-30T12:09:06.241Z"],["3852639","DBRE-8748","DBRE","juri.hudolejev@bolt.eu","Juri Hudolejev","[https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5620|https://github.com/bolteu/taxify-ansible/pull/5620] is in review, nothing left to be done here.","2026-01-30T12:09:07.157Z"],["3852641","MLC-4127","MLC","meiti.pind@bolt.eu","Meiti Pind","||*Email example*||*Push example*||\n|!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 14.07.23.png|width=825,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 14.07.23.png\"!|!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 14.06.21.png|width=528,alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 14.06.21.png\"!|","2026-01-30T12:09:22.993Z"],["3852642","PFI-840679","PFI","carlo.mizzon@bolt.eu","Carlo Mizzon","Namaste 🙏 ","2026-01-30T12:09:30.196Z"],["3852644","MLC-3104","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 5: \n\n* Final emails went out on 30.01 - too early to pull numbers.\n* Results from last weeks Emails (DnD)\n** CZ - 30,612 / 18.93%\n** PL - 28,066 / 14.67%\n** RO - 27,173 / 25.00%\n** SK - 27,603 / 21.11%\n* Compile a full report next week and share with the Growth team.","2026-01-30T12:10:23.237Z"],["3852646","FDBT-4876","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","Task succeeded. Closing the issue.","2026-01-30T12:10:29.981Z"],["3852648","PFI-840203","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,Could you advise the user to check if the have active cards linked to their Google wallet on their phone? If no active cards are added to the wallet, the user might not be able to see the option to use Google Pay in the Bolt App.","2026-01-30T12:10:40.253Z"],["3852650","PFI-838011","PFI","ketlin.peldes@bolt.eu","Ketlin Peldes","Hey! Based on my knowledge, positive balance won’t be transferred, but rather the balance will be paid out from the old account. ","2026-01-30T12:10:55.123Z"],["3852651","DSR-4243","DSR",null,"Automation for Jira","We've received your request. Our team is working on two-week sprints. Your request would be evaluated based on legal deadlines and complexity and included in the relevant sprint.\n\nOnce we assess the sprint dates for your request (not later than 2 weeks from the request), the assignee would notify you in this ticket.\n\nPlease check 🌍 [User: Data requests|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/58951] to see if your request needs to be escalated to the Privacy Legal Team. If not, let us know in the ticket to cancel the request.\n\nFor urgent requests (legal deadline for responding to the user is shorter than 2 weeks), please tag Tatsiana Sivukha in this ticket.","2026-01-30T12:11:19.666Z"],["3852652","MLC-3755","MLC","roman.cole@bolt.eu","Roman Cole","h3. Week 5\n\n* *Blockers:* None.\n* *Status update:*\n** {color:#36B37E}*[ TESTS FULLY ROLLED OUT ]*{color} → Reactivating Premium Users, Reactivating Comfort Users, Basic to Bolt. \n** {color:#FF991F}*[ ROLLOUT IN PROGRESS ]*{color}  → Bolt to XL, Basic to Women for Women. Will be finished by EOW.\n** {color:#97A0AF}*[ PENDING ROLLOUT ]*{color} → Bolt to Premium, Bolt to Comfort (to be picked up after Storytelling template A/B tests are finished).\n** We received a [report from Pavel|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/G015CPW5WGY/p1769596241244139] re: missing frequency caps in Reactivating Premium Users email - fixed this in the setup.\n* *Next steps:*\n** Finishing the rollout for Bolt to Premium/Comfort once we’ve resolved the Storytelling issues.\n** Start collecting initial results of the first A/B tests next week.","2026-01-30T12:11:22.139Z"],["3852653","LSS-61886","LSS","margarita.karamysheva@bolt.eu","Margarita Karamysheva","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] Thank you very much. At this stage, I don’t have any questions regarding the draft and I’m happy to confirm the points above.\n\nI’ll now share this with the partner for their review, and I’ll follow up here if any questions come up from their side.\n\nThanks!","2026-01-30T12:11:22.236Z"],["3852656","WD-22737","WD","siret.saks@bolt.eu","Siret Saks","Thank you!\n\nJournals are posted. \n\nKind regards,\n\nSiret","2026-01-30T12:12:06.247Z"],["3852659","DO-5775","DO","volha.anishchanka@bolt.eu","Volha Anishchanka","Then I don’t understand why at all service principal is needed if what is needed is a new service account in Looker (to use his credentials) that won’t be disabled if a user who set up the job with his personal credentials resigns from Bolt 😅 Ok, can we wait last time for Wednesday for Pawel back, I’ll just ask him directly?","2026-01-30T12:12:47.267Z"],["3852661","PFI-811830","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment was sent wrongly to our payout account. \nWe will prepare for the funds to be returned in a week.","2026-01-30T12:13:19.957Z"],["3852662","LSS-50610","LSS","viktoriia.voskolup@bolt.eu","Viktoriia Voskolup","[~accountid:712020:3f74544f-f771-4a1f-bbd9-8a60d6141880] please support with this Estonian ticket for IT team \n\nOur ISO audit will soon start, so we need to sign the agreement \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WjKTwxM7lBzBPY0nTqKRPnPCNrC0LnnY/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WjKTwxM7lBzBPY0nTqKRPnPCNrC0LnnY/edit|smart-link]  - Google Drive Link to the agreement for the review  \n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_nlp4P1j4pV_xfaBTZqfSQLX-w0vtqjlF2ts7QXAsxg/edit?tab=t.0|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_nlp4P1j4pV_xfaBTZqfSQLX-w0vtqjlF2ts7QXAsxg/edit?tab=t.0|smart-link] - this is analysis that our intern did during summer with proposals \n\n*If all good with current version of the agreement we can reply that it’s good to be signed* ","2026-01-30T12:13:25.616Z"],["3852668","HS-29576","HS",null,"Automation for Jira","Hey Łukasz,\n\nThanks for your request! We’ve moved your request to the correct People Services Support Desk so it can be handled by the right team.\n\nYou can view and track your request(s) here:\n [https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/26/WD-22739|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/26/WD-22739|smart-link]\n\nBest regards,\nPeople Services Team","2026-01-30T12:14:30.166Z"],["3852670","PFI-811807","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Did I not resolve it with the other ticket already on 16th December?\nHope we can close this ticket as duplicate","2026-01-30T12:15:00.478Z"],["3852671","LSS-59827","LSS","margarita.karamysheva@bolt.eu","Margarita Karamysheva","Hi [~accountid:712020:5960c3dd-0f70-4ba3-bd49-119c42bd10e5] thank you! All good from my side, I will share with the partner for their review and let you know once it’s ready to be signed.\n\nThanks! ","2026-01-30T12:15:08.719Z"],["3852672","DAEN-1406","DAEN","amruth.anand@bolt.eu","Amruth Anand","We have decided to go forward with stable id ","2026-01-30T12:15:08.708Z"],["3852673","CSDT-994","CSDT","boris.pavlov@bolt.eu","Boris Pavlov","There could be a template per vertical which PMs can use. \n\n\nIF we are forced to do market level scorecards in sheets, then\n\n* Need to schedule key customer support metrics dashboard with different filters per country to arrive in Google Drive\n* Use google apps script to unpack each file, depending on the country name\n* Drop everything into one tab in cs scorecard\n* Use formulas to populate the rest\n\n\n\n* Doable, but don’t want to do it in Google sheets. Why did we create new metrics and dashboards? What is the point? \n* Manual metrics will not be added by our team. If they are automated, then why not have everything in Looker then? ","2026-01-30T12:16:00.378Z"],["3852674","BDB-1528","BDB","alexsandra.kruusberg@bolt.eu","Alexsandra Kruusberg","Hey!\n\nHere are two proposals for the car branding (link below): [https://www.figma.com/design/RSzokktYVmlMvEQxNpN7dc/Ride-Hailing-Car-Branding?node-id=16304-2&t=54rk7IlixktJaneW-1|https://www.figma.com/design/RSzokktYVmlMvEQxNpN7dc/Ride-Hailing-Car-Branding?node-id=16304-2&t=54rk7IlixktJaneW-1|smart-link] \n\nAfter discussing with Kaarel, we feel the current tagline may be confusing for people seeing the cars on the street for the first time. Instead, we suggest focusing on a clearer, more recognisable approach using the Bolt logo + Expo logo + disclaimer.\n\n*Option 1*\nMost cost-effective. We can use the existing fleet and only rebrand the back doors.\n\n*Option 2*\nRequires rebranding both doors and would incorporate the colours of the 17 UN Sustainable Development Goals.\n\nPlease let me know which option you prefer. Thanks!\n\nAlex ","2026-01-30T12:16:10.567Z"],["3852676","PFI-840184","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nThe payments states adjustment has now been requested and once completed the debt will be cleared. We are sorry for the inconvenience caused to the customer.","2026-01-30T12:16:16.960Z"],["3852678","FINDATA-4110","FINDATA","ismayil.aghahasanli@bolt.eu","Ismayil Aghahasanli","[~accountid:712020:251b4304-5c21-495c-9f4a-55bd4fe62861] [~accountid:712020:9980ae13-5dd9-4982-a9c1-da0e1b3a22c2] As we discussed, that would be nice if you could add some snapshot or file as a sample, how you see the data as of now and how you wanna see with new approach. \nThat will definitely help me to speed up the dev and clear out any possible misunderstanding. \n\nAnd would be nice to define these average types a bit more to align (or confirm if I get it correctly), below I share how I understand:\n\n* current_planning_rate -CPR. Such rates are fixed as avg of the last month before quarter start. So today, 12th of Dec it would be average of September.\n** I believe we agreed on this definitions a little bit differently - CPR= average of previous quarter’s month end rates. Ex; Nov 10 , and CPR= average of EOMs of September, August, July.\n* previous_planning_rate (perhaps PPR), see above. Today it would be avg of June. \n** The same as above just moving back in time (ex: 10th of Nov - PPR =average of  June, MAY, April(EOM)\n* PPR-1, see above\n** same above- PPR-1= average of March, FEB,Jan (EOM)\n* PPR-2, see above\n** PPR-2 = average of Dec,Nov,Oct\n* prior_year_same_month_rate. Today, 12th of Dec 2025, it would be avg rate of Dec 2024.\n** This will be like , Nov 10 then average of Nov last year so on..\n\n\n\n\nThanks in advance!\n\n","2026-01-30T12:16:36.400Z"],["3852680","SAI-1293","SAI","anton.belski@bolt.eu","Anton Belski","On {{2026-01-06}}we had a [SEV|https://taxify.slack.com/archives/CGLJZE1SA/p1767694680965509] on pricing side (could not set price to orders), which resulted in a spike of CS tickets created from drivers.\n\nDuring this time number of sqs messages support-bot processed increased from 100 msg per minute to 700 msg/min ([link|https://nodemonitor.boltint.net/graph/d/000000043/mq-subscribers?orgId=1&var-team=support-automation&var-team=support-experience-backend&var-type=All&var-host=All&var-shard=All&var-service=support-bot&var-interval=$__auto_interval_interval&var-event_type=All&var-name=All&from=1767676907072&to=1767726954044&var-release_track=All&viewPanel=8]). We were able to successfully handle this load with *stable* *message avg age* and no degradation in automation.\n\n!image-20260130-110414.png|width=1043,alt=\"image-20260130-110414.png\"!\n\n!image-20260130-110739.png|width=1048,alt=\"image-20260130-110739.png\"!\n\n!image-20260130-111021.png|width=1060,alt=\"image-20260130-111021.png\"!\n\nAlso, if we look at _batch size_, _message processed per_ second and _batch load duration_, we can see that under regular load the _avg batch size_ is  <1 and _loading duration_ is somewhere ~8-10s. It means that each instance waits for about 8-10 second till a single message added to the queue. \nWith 7x load, _batch loading duration_ dropped to 1s, but the _avg batch size_ did not change (still 1). *It means that with 700 msg/min load we are within 1 message per second processing time (~15s per msg pod throughput).* Because our hard SLO is 60s to start processing support case (otherwise escalated), 700 msg/min is basically our ceiling. (we need to process 12 msg/s to not grow the queue, having 12 instances and 1 msg/sec we can achieve it). \n\n\nAs for CPU, during CPU utilization [spiked|https://monitor.boltint.net/d/k8s_views_node_ns/kubernetes-node-namespace-view?orgId=1&var-cluster=live-euc-1-charlie&var-cluster=live-euc-1-delta&var-namespace=tools-workflows&var-resolution=$__auto_interval_resolution&var-deployment=support-bot&var-datasource=PA11421A75E8A2F15&from=1767684541779&to=1767706993262&viewPanel=73] to 40% during the incident. Which is still far away from HPA target (65%).\n\n!image-20260130-111733.png|width=1060,alt=\"image-20260130-111733.png\"!\n\nTo summarize the throughput per pod can be calculated with the following formula:\n\n{noformat}throughput per pod ≈ parallel_messages / T {noformat}\n\n_where avg processing time T = 15s (calculated empirically)._ \n\n* At *15 parallel*: 60msg/min per pod ~700/min total\n* At *25 parallel*: 100msg/min per pod → ~1200/min total (same number of pods)\n\nIf we want horizontal autoscaling start working, we need to find a balance between cpu/parallel_messages/pods. Currently the cpu utilization target is 65%. We’ve seen that with 700 msg/min CPU utilization was 40%. So we need 65/40 = 1.625 more “work per pod”. \n\nThe cleanest way is to scale parallel_messages and reduce number of pods by roughly the same factor:\n\n* parallel_messages: 15*1,67 = 25 \n* pods: 12 / 1.625 = 8\n\n*So we can try to increase parallel_messages to 25 and reduce min replica size to 8.*","2026-01-30T12:16:44.524Z"],["3852681","PC-4935","PC","devanshi.bansal@bolt.eu","Devanshi Bansal","Abhilekh is looking into it further. But these are our observations until now:\n1. use_balance = false, so bolt credit not added in booking line item. \n2. Booking line item just has card payment instrument which failed authorisation.\n\n# The refund is failing because getPayment returns card and bolt-credit both in booking_items. So even if the DB has only the card {{booking_item}}, the response includes a Bolt Credit line item created by {{getMissingBalanceBookingItemIfPaymentFailedOrCancelled(...)}} : [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/6d0a7c9b2859c2ba42c56507fcd49dcafd507c4c/src/platform/commerce/balance_user/main/service/BookingResponseBuilder.ts#L534|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/6d0a7c9b2859c2ba42c56507fcd49dcafd507c4c/src/platform/commerce/balance_user/main/service/BookingResponseBuilder.ts#L534] \n# But the amount against bolt credit line item is 0, it doesn't reflect the actual debt amount. Code ref for debt calculation: [https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/c5e5762e6580973d96f290745bf24f3735ef23e4/src/platform/commerce/balance_user/main/service/BookingResponseBuilder.ts#L890|https://github.com/bolteu/bolt-server/blob/c5e5762e6580973d96f290745bf24f3735ef23e4/src/platform/commerce/balance_user/main/service/BookingResponseBuilder.ts#L890] \n# So amount against card is 0 because auth failed and against bolt_credit is also 0 as actual debt not reflected. Hence refund doesn't know what to refund exactly.","2026-01-30T12:16:43.643Z"],["3852682","PFI-840170","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T12:16:48.197Z"],["3852683","PFI-806249","PFI","kaisa.kamarik@bolt.eu","Kaisa Kamarik","Payment matched to client https://admin-panel.bolt.eu/partner-payments-payment/payments/41330809 ","2026-01-30T12:16:52.324Z"],["3852687","DELIVERY-1043","DELIVERY","tiberiu.vasile@bolt.eu","Constantin-Tiberiu Vasile","26W4: \n\n* *Done* - Update multiplier query to include ad-hoc overrides\n** Returns Effective multipliers for the current week by merging live multipliers with active ad hoc overrides.\n** Logic:\n*** Fetch live multipliers for a given source (city/zone/zone_group)\n*** Retrieve ad hoc overrides active within the current ISO week (Monday-Sunday)\n*** Splits live intervals where ad hoc overrides partially overlap\n*** Applies ad hoc changes: INCREASE (additive), DECREASE (subtractive, clamped to min 1.0), ABSOLUTE_VALUE (replacement with min 1.0 check)\n*** Only base multipliers (pickup, dropoff, km_unit) are affected\n** Fallback Behavior:\n*** Returns null if no live multipliers exist\n*** Returns live multipliers unchanged if timezone lookup fails or no active ad hoc exists\n* *Done* - Replicate DB table to data warehouse\n** Started replication of the *courier_earning_multipliers_adhoc* table to data warehouse\n** Backfill not necessary as the table isn’t used in live yet\n* *In Progress* - Create ad-hoc multiplier component in Admin Panel\n** Working on the UI component that will allow OPS to add date specific overrides to live multipliers(reason options *pending*)","2026-01-30T12:17:23.160Z"],["3852688","DAEN-1374","DAEN","amruth.anand@bolt.eu","Amruth Anand","We have had 40 PR’s reviewed from 19th Jan to Jan 30. ","2026-01-30T12:17:26.326Z"],["3852690","PFI-840169","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T12:17:42.951Z"],["3852691","LSS-50232","LSS","polina.novikova@bolt.eu","Polina Novikova","Hey hey,\nThis ticket could be closed, as the project got deprioritized.\nThanks for your support!","2026-01-30T12:17:52.883Z"],["3852692","DAEN-1415","DAEN","amruth.anand@bolt.eu","Amruth Anand","[https://www.figma.com/board/oOdASngXU8sHoqkZuTOKCq/Delivery-Data-Modeling?node-id=0-1&p=f&t=Kk8y4IezrdNXgFyp-0|https://www.figma.com/board/oOdASngXU8sHoqkZuTOKCq/Delivery-Data-Modeling?node-id=0-1&p=f&t=Kk8y4IezrdNXgFyp-0|smart-link] ","2026-01-30T12:18:02.757Z"],["3852695","PFI-840136","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T12:18:20.922Z"],["3852696","RS-1986","RS","narmin.ahmadova@bolt.eu","Narmin Ahmadova","Hey [~accountid:712020:957e19aa-4314-41d8-99a8-c9926f72db88] , please review my previous comment and take action accordingly. We can provide data regarding revenue but not include personal data, since there is no legal basis to justify it.","2026-01-30T12:18:21.587Z"],["3852698","PFI-840731","PFI","iduvu.brighstone@bolt-outsource.eu","Iduvu Brighstone","!Screenshot_20260130-143451.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T12:18:25.686Z"],["3852699","MLC-3710","MLC","tudor.toma@bolt.eu","Tudor Toma","+*Week of Jan 30th*+\n\n* Finalized queries and coverage. Summary here: [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1V31VhV2ylgW23HAGCtpJ3LPdVY-2oLvsveQcxmtYplY/edit?gid=2034208863#gid=2034208863|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1V31VhV2ylgW23HAGCtpJ3LPdVY-2oLvsveQcxmtYplY/edit?gid=2034208863#gid=2034208863|smart-link] \n\nh2. *TL;DR: Lifecycle Comms Coverage Audit*\n\nWe’ve identified several data mismatches across our messaging stages. While *Acquisition (Work Profile)* is highly accurate, other segments are firing messages to ineligible users due to data lag or status changes.\n\n----\n\nh3. *Key Insights (The \"Why\")*\n\n* *Acquisition Mismatches:* High for Riders (17%) and Activation (14%).\n** *Rider Issue:* 73% of errors are caused by *generic emails* that shouldn't be targeted.\n** *Existing Users:* Many \"prospects\" are already Business Users/Admins but haven't been filtered out.\n* *Activation Issues:* 67% of mistargeted users had *already placed an order* before the message arrived (Self-activation).\n* *Onboarding/Churn:* \"Hidden\" account statuses aren't syncing fast enough, and 82% of \"churned\" users actually ordered right before the message sent.\n\n----\n\nh3. *Completed Fixes*\n\n* *Logic Updates:* Added \"Zero Order\" filters to prevent targeting active companies.\n* *Cool-off Period:* Implemented a *60-day buffer* to stop users from getting trapped in multiple journeys simultaneously.\n* *Regex Refinement:* Cleaned up Rider acquisition filters to catch outliers.\n\n----\n\nh3. *What’s Next?*\n\n* *Martech Sync:* Investigate \"New vs. Carry-over\" audiences to find the source of data gaps.\n* *Data Deep Dive:* Audit why specific attributes (Status, Business Order Finished, Admin/User flags) aren't passing correctly from the backend to the comms tools.\n\n----\n\n+*In Depth*+\n\n* We noticed multiple mismatches across all stages. Core reasons are:\n** Best Alignment: Acquisition - WP has the highest precision, with only 2.51% of contacted users falling outside the addressable base.\n** Highest Mismatch: Acquisition - Rider and Activation show higher mismatch rates at 17.14% and 14.06% respectively.\n*** For Rider and Work Profile (WP) segments, mismatches are primarily driven by users who are already deep in the ecosystem or possess ineligible credentials.\n*** Generic Emails (Rider Only): This is the largest single driver for Rider mismatches, accounting for 72.82% of mistargeted riders (6,306 users).\n*** Existing Business Status: A significant portion of \"prospects\" were already Business Users or Admins, making them ineligible for an acquisition nudge.\n*** Historical Eligibility: Many users became \"addressable\" before our observation month, suggesting a delay in removing them from the prospect pool.\n** Activation: The \"Non-Zero Order\" Conflict\n*** The Activation stage is meant to target users who have set up an account but haven't used it.\n*** Premature Ordering: 67.02% of Activation mismatches occur because the company has a non-zero Order Count. These users have already self-activated before the message was sent.\n*** Legacy Activations: 21.31% of mismatches are due to companies having an old Activation date, meaning they were not part of the current fresh cohort we intended to target.\n** Onboarding & Churn: State Changes\n*** Hidden Status: In Onboarding, 51.36% of mismatches involve companies with a \"Hidden\" status. This suggests a sync issue where internal account flags are not suppressing external comms fast enough.\n*** Re-Engagement (Churn): In the Churn segment, 82.52% of mismatches are \"happy accidents\" where the company ordered again before the churn message fired. While these users are no longer \"Addressable\" for churn, they were likely mid-transaction when the data was queried.\n* *Already Fixed:*\n** Fix 0 Orders to remove cases where companies reactivate and get re-enrolled in the journey - Done by adding a business_order_count = 0 or blank to segment\n** Fix BA Acquisition to remove cases where users change user type and get enrolled into both journeys - Fixed by adding 60 day cool-off period between automation\n** Deepdive regex condition and fix the outlier cases for BA Acquisition Riders - Fixed by adjusting regex condition to grab all cases where users would pass through the filter\n* *Next Steps:*\n** Work with Martech on New vs Carry-over audience to better understand where gaps are coming from\n** Identify gaps and reasons for it\n** Deepdive status custom attribute and understand if there are issues where data is not being passed\n** Deepdive Business Account Activated & Business Order Finished and understand if there are issues where data is not being passed\n** Deepdive is_business_user & is_business_admin custom attributes and understand if there are issues where data is not being passed","2026-01-30T12:18:57.769Z"],["3852700","INT-883","INT","alexander.tsyba@bolt.eu","Alexander Tsyba","[~accountid:5f23e70bb7a35e002a73ef5d] Can you please take a look and estimate? I’ve currently placed it on April, but maybe those improvements are simplier and we can take them earlier to improve our output metrics performance. ","2026-01-30T12:18:58.725Z"],["3852701","LSS-61798","LSS","freek.engel@bolt.eu","Freek van den Engel","Thank you, this suffices I believe. Only remaining is now the Memorandum of Incorporation signed by Ahto","2026-01-30T12:19:01.509Z"],["3852702","WFM-10227","WFM","kyrylo.yefimov@bolt.eu","Kyrylo Yefimov","Good, then access was provided from our side","2026-01-30T12:19:04.574Z"],["3852703","PFI-840098","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hi Team,\n\nI've reviewed the case and everything is correct on Bolt's end. The preauthorisation was successfully released, and there is no further action required from us.\n\nPlease follow the steps in this Knowledge Base article to advise the customer: [https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/7109163016850?country=global&language=en]\n\nAdvise the customer to *check with their bank* to confirm the release of the preauthorisation. Banks handle these releases differently, and while some are immediate, others may process it as a temporary charge that is then refunded. Sometimes, the payment is reversed without the bank sending a reversal notification to the customer, which might lead the user to think that the reversal has not been made.\n\nThe reversal can take up to *30 days* to complete, as pending authorisations typically expire after that time on banks end.\n\nUnfortunately, we don't have full visibility into all the parties involved in the payment processing beyond our payment partner. Therefore, we can't track the exact status of the preauthorisation release once it has been sent.\n\nThank you,\n\nAfiba\n\n","2026-01-30T12:19:09.712Z"],["3852704","INT-884","INT",null,"Automation for Jira","Comment template for weekly updates\n\n26Www\n\nWhat moved this week:\n\n- ...\n\nNext week focus:\n\n- ...\n\nScope change :\n\n- ...\n\nRisk, blocking:\n\n- ...\n\nHelp needed:\n\n- ... ","2026-01-30T12:19:27.082Z"],["3852705","PFI-840732","PFI","onyinye.osuagwu@bolt.eu","Onyinyechukwu Osuagwu","!Screenshot 2026-01-30 at 13.17.58.png|thumbnail!","2026-01-30T12:19:29.812Z"],["3852706","CSP-401","CSP","przemyslaw.burczyk@bolt.eu","Przemysław Burczyk","26W05: Implementation of showing other possible actions and the ability to reset the state is done, will be released on Monday. Datapoints exposing pending implementation from Automations still. PEX team is to roll-out V2 version of the routine next week. In the meanwhile we will use V1 + steps for agents for visualisation in Beehive. PEX team is to discuss with CS teams the approach for structural granularity of the routines.","2026-01-30T12:20:10.187Z"],["3852707","DAEN-1394","DAEN","amruth.anand@bolt.eu","Amruth Anand","[figma.com/board/oOdASngXU8sHoqkZuTOKCq/Delivery-Data-Modeling|http://figma.com/board/oOdASngXU8sHoqkZuTOKCq/Delivery-Data-Modeling]","2026-01-30T12:20:16.008Z"],["3852708","PFI-840097","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello,\n\nKindly check with the Technical Support team regarding this issue.","2026-01-30T12:20:35.383Z"],["3852709","INT-829","INT","giammarco.pavan@bolt.eu","Giammarco Pavan","*26W05*\n+_What moved this week_+:\n\n* Finalised [+2026 Planning+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1n9GxhqMxX5pTqwc7EZH4Cl1aR8K4qx_-5aHeUdItddE/edit?tab=t.etwkz53f08xl#heading=h.4mg1k1svnsbp], including details for 2-weeks sprint for the next 2 months\n* Continued Discovery: finalised a proposal on [+Pricing success+|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1b7tWaaxtrw9DNsPpP-nVCwmN4KhKzVC0iStQhG_EoHs/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.i1eit2slrexd], continued brainstorming on solution approach: (1) pricing & commission change logic (commission fee levels vs marketplace states), (2) additional guardrails to avoid greedy weekly GMV maximisation\n* Outlined a [+simplified solution for MVP development+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PRODWIKI/pages/7439974480/Ongoing+Dynamic+Pricing+Commission+System+DPCS+core+logic+and+architecture]\n* Started Concept Validation on mocked data to validate directional behaviour of joint pricing, earnings and commission decisions.\n\n+_Next week focus_+:\n\n* Finalise the Discovery: close the success metrics definition, finalise solution principles (PRD), provide overview on driver earnings screen risk / dependency \n* Share preliminary results on Concept Validation on mocked data \n* Start Concept Validation with real data","2026-01-30T12:20:47.461Z"],["3852710","DO-5824","DO","kristo.sarnets@bolt.eu","Kristo Sarnets","Thank you.\nJust tested it in Databricks and with my own cluster in a notebook I was able to query the tables.\n\nAlthough in SQL Editor it still gives me Unauthorized access error.\n\nSo it is good for now as I can access and see the data and start working on it.","2026-01-30T12:20:57.800Z"],["3852711","FDBT-4876","FDBT","karl.ruudi@bolt.eu","Karl Ruudi","DAG commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments fails on 2026-01-29 02:30:00+00:00.\n\n        Exception:\n        Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 282, in _run_raw_task\n    TaskInstance._execute_task_with_callbacks(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3184, in _execute_task_with_callbacks\n    result = self._execute_task(context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 3208, in _execute_task\n    return _execute_task(self, context, task_orig)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 776, in _execute_task\n    result = _execute_callable(context=context, **execute_callable_kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/taskinstance.py\", line 742, in _execute_callable\n    return ExecutionCallableRunner(\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/utils/operator_helpers.py\", line 252, in run\n    return self.func(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/models/baseoperator.py\", line 1816, in resume_execution\n    return execute_callable(context)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 45, in execute_complete\n    raise e\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/bolt/airflow/databricks/operators/job/__init__.py\", line 37, in execute_complete\n    return super(DatabricksRunNowByNameOperator, self).execute_complete(context, event)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 958, in execute_complete\n    _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion(event, self.log)\n  File \"/home/airflow/.local/lib/python3.9/site-packages/airflow/providers/databricks/operators/databricks.py\", line 248, in _handle_deferrable_databricks_operator_completion\n    raise AirflowException(error_message)\nairflow.exceptions.AirflowException: Job run failed with terminal state: {'life_cycle_state': 'INTERNAL_ERROR', 'result_state': 'FAILED', 'state_message': 'Task load_items_to_workday failed with message: Workload failed, see run output for details.'} and with the errors [{'error': 'ValueError: can not infer schema from empty dataset', 'run_id': 147444572169184, 'task_key': 'load_items_to_workday'}]\n\n        Log URL: https://airflow-commerce.data.boltint.net/dags/commerce_finance_pipeline_bank_payments/grid?dag_run_id=scheduled__2026-01-29T02%3A30%3A00%2B00%3A00&task_id=partner_payout_currency_clearing.partner_payout_currency_clearing_ledger_aggr_to_workday_integration&base_date=2026-01-29T02%3A30%3A00.000000%2B0000&tab=logs\n        ","2026-01-30T12:21:21.218Z"],["3852712","PAW-15154","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Labels added automatically: pint-bucket-platform, pint-component-admin-panel-automations, pint-product-workflow-and-automation-platform, pint-capability-process-automation\n\nIf you think the labels are incorrect, please remove the suggested labels and add the correct ones.","2026-01-30T12:21:24.810Z"],["3852713","PFI-840035","PFI","afiba.toulassi@bolt.eu","Afiba Marylise-Lolita Toulassi","Hello Team!\n\nWe can confirm that the refund has been successfully completed and sent to the user's account.\n\nThe refund should appear on the user's statement within *10 business days or more*, depending on their bank's processing times. For PawaPay transactions, the refund should reflect within *48 hours*.\n\nWe understand the delay can be frustrating, and we apologize for any inconvenience this has caused. We recommend the user track the refund with their bank or mobile service provider using the transaction date, time, and amount.\n\nCheers,\nAfiba\n\n[^Refund_Letter_XSPFQD8X6CBBGQP9_FBFL52672JH2GGX3 (1).pdf]\n\n","2026-01-30T12:21:35.849Z"],["3852714","PAW-15302","PAW","token.atlassianpint@bolt.eu","Token Atlassian PINT","🤖 AI Analysis: Component label added automatically.\n\nIf you think the component label is incorrect, please remove the suggested label and add the correct one.If you was assigned to this issue, unassign yourself and add the correct label.\n\n","2026-01-30T12:21:48.340Z"],["3852716","MLC-1549","MLC","karl.maasen@bolt.eu","Karl Maasen","Week 5:\n\n* Tests with HTML\n** Replicated the Rider’s approach and re-launched Poland on 30.01\n*** 3h after send OR is 0.5%, but the plan is to let this run for a week to see whether OR increases over time based on Dovainis' suggestion.\n** Re-launched *Business User* Bolt to Comfort with an A/B test to compare Old HTML to Storytelling. Volumes are too low to see whether the low OR issue is fixed, but the storytelling email is performing better than the old one. \n*** RO:\n**** Old - 18.87%\n**** Storytelling - 20.88%\n*** PL: \n**** Old - 18.29%\n**** Storytelling - 25.84%\n* Results from last week's DnD run for PT and RO\n** RO: 14,860 / 20.05%\n** PT: 11,167 / 23.92%\n* Sync with Dovainis to do an inbox placement test & reputation","2026-01-30T12:21:53.128Z"],["3852718","INT-821","INT","giammarco.pavan@bolt.eu","Giammarco Pavan","*26W05*\n+_What moved this week_+:\n\n* (Feature Lead on holiday)\n\n+_Next week focus_+:\n\n* Start researching required streaming features for S2O, O2F models \n* Revamp the previous S2O model used for MDC, check on accuracy metrics (avg error, variance, signal-to-noise ratio)","2026-01-30T12:22:03.251Z"],["3852719","L10N-31122","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main ticket above this one).\n\n💬 Keeping the conversation in one place ensures that:\n- All linguists working on the project are aligned\n- The content owner can answer all queries at once\n- We avoid fragmented or duplicate discussions\n\n📌 While we aim to keep individual language tasks updated, the **Epic acts as the main source of truth**. It’s where you’ll find the latest context, updates, and team-wide communication.\n\n🔗 You can find the parent Epic here: [L10N-31121](https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/L10N-31121)\n\nThanks for collaborating!","2026-01-30T12:22:22.425Z"],["3852720","L10N-31125","L10N",null,"Automation for Jira","👋 Hi ,\n\nThanks for picking up this task!  \nPlease note that **all comments, questions, and discussions should be added under the parent Epic** (the main 